hadiths[2898]{hadithnumber,text}:
"8100","Abd al-Razzaq ibn Hammam narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, he said: This is what Abu Hurayrah narrated to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: We are the last, the foremost on the Day of Resurrection, except they were given the Book before us and we were given it after them; this is their day which Allah obligated upon them, and they differed in it, so Allah guided us to it; so they follow us in it: the Jews tomorrow and the Christians the day after."
"8101","And Abul Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My likeness and the likeness of the prophets before me is like a man who built houses and made them good and complete and beautiful except for the place of a brick in a corner of its corners, so people began to go around and the building pleased them, and they would say: Why did you not place a brick here so your building would be complete? So Muhammad the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So I was the brick."
"8102","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My likeness is like a man who kindled a fire, and when it lit up what was around it, moths and these creatures that fall into fire began to fall into it, and he began to hold them back and they overcame him so they plunged into it. He said: So that is my likeness and your likeness. I am holding you by your waist-wraps away from the Fire: Come away from the Fire, come away from the Fire, come, but you overcome me and plunge into it."
"8103","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the most false of speech, and do not envy one another, and do not compete against one another, and do not hate one another, and do not turn your backs on one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers."
"8104","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On Friday there is an hour no Muslim coincides with while asking his Lord for something except He gives it to him."
"8105","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels succeed one another among you, angels by night and angels by day, and he said: They gather at the Fajr prayer and the Asr prayer, then those who spent the night among you ascend to Him, and He asks them, and He knows best: How did you leave My servants? So they say: We left them while they were praying, and we came to them while they were praying."
"8106","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels invoke blessings upon one of you as long as he remains in his prayer place in which he prayed, as long as he does not break his ablution: O Allah, forgive him, O Allah, have mercy on him."
"8107","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you says Amin and the angels in heaven say Amin, and one of them coincides with the other, he is forgiven what preceded of his sin."
"8108","And he said: While a man was driving a garlanded sacrificial camel, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Woe to you, ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Woe to you, ride it."
"8109","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, if you knew what I know you would laugh little and weep much."
"8110","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you fights, let him avoid the face."
"8111","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This fire of yours, what the sons of Adam kindle, is one part of seventy parts of the heat of Hell. They said: By Allah, it would have been sufficient, O Messenger of Allah. He said: It was favored over it by sixty-nine parts, all of them like its heat."
"8112","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah decreed creation, He wrote a book, and it is with Him above the Throne: My mercy overcame My anger."
"8113","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting is a shield, so when one of you is on a day fasting, let him not act ignorantly nor speak obscenely, and if a man fights him or insults him, let him say: I am fasting, I am fasting."
"8114","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the changed breath of the mouth of the fasting person is better with Allah than the scent of musk. He leaves his desire and his food and his drink for My sake, so fasting is for Me and I reward for it."
"8115","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prophet from the prophets alighted under a tree, and an ant bit him, so he ordered his baggage to be removed from beneath it, and he ordered fire and it was burned in the fire. He said: So Allah revealed to him: Why not one ant?"
"8116","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, were it not that I would cause hardship for the believers, I would not have stayed behind any expedition going out in the path of Allah, but I do not find means to carry them, and they do not find means to follow me, and their souls would not be content to stay behind after me."
"8117","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For every prophet there is a supplication answered for him, and I intend, if Allah wills, to delay my supplication as intercession for my nation on the Day of Resurrection."
"8118","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves meeting Allah, Allah loves meeting him, and whoever does not love meeting Allah, Allah does not love meeting him."
"8119","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah, and whoever obeys the commander has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys the commander has disobeyed me."
"8120","And the Messenger of Allah said: The Hour will not come until wealth becomes abundant among you and overflows, until the owner of wealth is concerned about who will accept his charity from him, and he said: And knowledge will be taken away, and time will draw near, and tribulations will appear, and harj will increase. They said: What is harj, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Killing, killing."
"8121","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until two great factions fight, between them a great slaughter, and their claim is one."
"8122","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until impostor liars emerge, close to thirty, each of them claiming he is the Messenger of Allah."
"8123","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until the sun rises from its west. When it rises and people see it, they will all believe, and that is when no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good in its faith."
"8124","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the call is made for prayer, Satan turns away and he has wind so he does not hear the adhan, and when the adhan is finished he comes forward, until when the iqamah is made he turns away, until when the iqamah is finished he comes forward, until he comes between a man and himself, and says to him: Remember such, remember such, of what he did not remember before, until the man remains not knowing how he prayed."
"8125","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The right hand of Allah is full, expenditure does not diminish it, bountiful night and day. Have you seen what He spent since He created the heavens and the earth? It did not diminish what is in His right hand. He said: And His Throne is upon the water, and in His other Hand is grasping: He raises and lowers."
"8126","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, there will surely come upon one of you a day when to see me, then to see me, will be more beloved to him than his family and his wealth and the like of them with them."
"8127","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kisra has perished, then there will be no Kisra after him, and Qaysar will surely perish, then there will be no Qaysar after him, and you will surely divide their treasures in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"8128","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen and no ear has heard and what has not occurred to the heart of a human."
"8129","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave me as I have left you, for those before you were only destroyed by their questioning and their differing against their prophets. So when I forbid you from something, avoid it, and when I command you with a matter, follow it as much as you are able."
"8130","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the call is made for prayer, the dawn prayer, and one of you is in major impurity, let him not fast that day."
"8131","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has ninety-nine names, one hundred minus one. Whoever enumerates them will enter Paradise. He is Odd and loves the odd."
"8132","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you looks at one favored over him in wealth and appearance, let him look at one below him among those he is favored over."
"8133","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The purification of the vessel of one of you when the dog laps in it is to wash it seven times."
"8134","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, I intended to command my youths to prepare bundles of firewood for me, then command a man to lead people in prayer, then burn houses down upon those in them."
"8135","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was aided with terror, and I was given the comprehensive words."
"8136","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the strap of the sandal of one of you breaks, or its thong, let him not walk in one of them with a sandal and the other barefoot. Let him take them both off, or let him wear them both."
"8137","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah said: The vow does not bring the son of Adam anything I had not decreed for him, but the vow meets him with what I decreed for him, by which is extracted from the miser: he gives Me for it what he would not have given Me before."
"8138","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said to me: Spend, I will spend on you. And he named war as deception."
"8139","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Isa son of Maryam, peace be upon him, saw a man stealing, so Isa said to him: You stole. He said: No, by the One besides Whom there is no god. Isa said: I believed in Allah and disbelieved my eyes."
"8140","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, I do not give you anything nor withhold it from you. I am only a treasurer; I place where I am commanded."
"8141","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam was only appointed to be followed, so do not differ against him. When he says takbir, say takbir, and when he bows, bow, and when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise, and when he prostrates, prostrate, and when he prays sitting, pray all sitting."
"8142","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten the row in prayer, for straightening the row is part of the excellence of prayer."
"8143","And with his chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adam and Musa argued, so Musa said to him: You are Adam who misled people and brought them out of Paradise to the earth. So Adam said to him: You are Musa to whom Allah gave knowledge of all things and chose you over people with His messages. He said: Yes. He said: Do you blame me for a matter that was written upon me to do before I was created? He said: So Adam overcame Musa, peace and blessings of Allah be upon them both."
"8144","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While Ayyub was bathing naked, locusts of gold fell upon him, so Ayyub began to gather into his garment, so his Lord called him: O Ayyub, had I not enriched you from what you see? He said: Yes, O Lord, but I cannot do without Your blessing."
"8145","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recitation was made light for Dawud, peace be upon him, and he would order his mount to be saddled, and he would recite the Quran before his mount was saddled, and he would eat only from the work of his hands."
"8146","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream of the righteous man is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"8147","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the young greet the old, and the passerby greet the seated, and the few greet the many."
"8148","And with his chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will continue to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah. When they say: There is no god but Allah, they have protected their wealth and themselves from me except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"8149","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise and Hell argued, so Hell said: I was favored with the arrogant and the tyrants. And Paradise said: What is with me that none enters me except the weak of people, their lowly and their simple? So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said to Paradise: You are only My mercy, I have mercy with you upon whom I will of My servants. And He said to Hell: You are only My punishment, I punish with you whom I will of My servants. And for each one of you both is its fill. As for Hell, it will not be filled until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, places His foot, so it says: Enough, enough, enough, meaning sufficient for me. There it will be filled, and part of it will be folded to part, and Allah does not wrong any of His creation. And as for Paradise, Allah will create for it a creation."
"8150","And the Messenger of Allah said: When one of you cleans with stones, let him make it odd."
"8151","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah said: When My servant speaks of doing a good deed, I write it for him as a good deed as long as he does not do it. When he does it, I write it for him as ten like it. And when he speaks of doing an evil deed, I forgive it as long as he does not do it. When he does it, I write it for him as one like it."
"8152","And with his chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The space of the whip of one of you in Paradise is better than what is between heaven and earth."
"8153","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lowest place of one of you in Paradise is that it is said: Wish, and he wishes, and it is said to him: Have you wished? He says: Yes. It is said to him: So for you is what you wished and the like of it with it."
"8154","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for the Hijrah, I would have been a man from the Ansar, and if people stream into a ravine or a valley and the Ansar stream into a ravine, I would stream into theirs."
"8155","And with his chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for the Children of Israil, meat would not have spoiled, and were it not for Hawwa, no female would ever have betrayed her husband."
"8156","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created Adam upon his image, his length sixty cubits. When He created him, He said to him: Go and greet those people, and they were a group of angels sitting, and listen to what they answer you, for it is your greeting and the greeting of your offspring. He said: So he went and said: Peace be upon you. They said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. So they added to him: And the mercy of Allah. He said: So everyone who enters Paradise is upon the image of Adam, and his length sixty cubits. Creation continued to decrease after that until now."
"8157","And with his chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angel of death came to Musa, peace be upon him, and said to him: Answer your Lord. He said: So Musa struck the eye of the angel of death and gouged it. He said: So the angel returned to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and said: You sent me to a servant of Yours who does not want death, and he gouged my eye. He said: So Allah restored his eye and said: Return to My servant and say: Do you want life? If you want life, place your hand on the back of a bull, and whatever your hand covers of hair, you will live by it a year. He said: Then what? He said: Then you die. He said: Then now, from near. He said: Lord, bring me near the sacred land a stone's throw. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, if I were with him I would have shown you his grave beside the road at the red mound."
"8158","And with his chain he said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Children of Israil used to bathe naked, some of them looking at the nakedness of others, and Musa, peace be upon him, used to bathe alone. They said: By Allah, nothing prevents Musa from bathing with us except that he has a hernia. He said: So he went once to bathe and placed his garment on a stone, so the stone fled with the garment of Musa. He said: So Musa rushed after it, saying: My garment, stone, my garment, stone, until the Children of Israil looked at the nakedness of Musa and said: By Allah, there is nothing wrong with Musa. So the stone stood after that until he looked at it, so he took his garment and began beating the stone. Abu Hurayrah said: By Allah, there are on the stone six or seven marks, the beating of Musa on the stone."
"8159","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Richness is not from abundance of goods, but richness is richness of the soul."
"8160","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of wrongdoing is the delay of the rich, and when one of you is transferred to a solvent debtor, let him follow."
"8161","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most hateful man to Allah on the Day of Resurrection and the most wicked and most hateful to Him is a man who was named king of kings. There is no king but Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"8162","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While a man was strutting in two cloaks, and his soul had pleased him, the earth swallowed him, and he is sinking in it until the Day of Resurrection."
"8163","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: I am at the opinion of My servant of Me."
"8164","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no newborn born except upon this fitrah, then his parents make him Jewish and make him Christian, as you produce camels: do you find among them any with cropped ears, until you are the ones who crop them? They said: O Messenger of Allah, what about one who dies while young? He said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"8165","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In man there is a bone that the earth never eats; in it he is composed on the Day of Resurrection. They said: Which bone is it? He said: The tailbone."
"8166","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of wisal, beware of wisal. They said: You practice wisal, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I am not like you in that. I spend the night, my Lord feeds me and gives me drink. So burden yourselves of deeds what you have capacity for."
"8167","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes from his sleep, let him not put his hand into ablution water until he washes it. One of you does not know where his hand spent the night."
"8168","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every joint of people has charity upon it each day the sun rises. He said: You reconcile between two is charity, and you help a man with his mount, carrying him on it or lifting his goods for him on it, is charity, and he said: The good word is charity, and he said: Every step he walks to prayer is charity, and you remove harm from the road is charity."
"8169","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the owner of livestock does not give its right, they are set upon him on the Day of Resurrection, striking his face with their hooves."
"8170","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The treasure of one of you will be on the Day of Resurrection a bald serpent. He said: And its owner will flee from it, and it will seek him and say: I am your treasure. He said: By Allah, it will continue to seek him until he stretches his hand, and it puts it into its mouth."
"8171","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not urinate in standing water that does not flow, then bathe from it."
"8172","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The needy is not this wanderer who goes around people, whom a morsel and two morsels and a date and two dates turn away. The needy is only one who finds no wealth to suffice him, and is shy to ask people, and is not noticed so charity is given to him."
"8173","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman does not fast while her husband is present except with his permission, and she does not permit in his house while he is present except with his permission, and what she spends from his earnings without his order, half its reward is for him."
"8174","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you wish for death nor supplicate for it before it comes to him. When one of you dies, his deed is cut off, and the life of the believer only increases him in good."
"8175","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you call grapes karam. Karam is only the Muslim man."
"8176","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man bought from a man a property of his, so the man who bought the property found in his property a jar with gold in it. So the one who bought the property said: Take your gold from me. I only bought the land from you and did not buy the gold from you. And the one who sold the land said: I only sold you the land and what is in it. He said: So they sought judgment from a man. So the one they sought judgment from said: Do you have children? One of them said: I have a boy. And the other said: I have a girl. He said: Marry the boy to the girl, and spend on yourselves from it, and give charity."
"8177","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does one of you rejoice at his mount when it strays from him then he finds it? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, Allah is more intense in joy at the repentance of His servant when he repents than one of you at his mount when he finds it."
"8178","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: When My servant meets Me with a handspan, I meet him with a forearm, and when he meets Me with a forearm, I meet him with an armspan, and when he meets Me with an armspan, I come to him with haste."
"8179","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you performs ablution, let him draw water into his nostrils, then blow it out."
"8180","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, if Uhud were gold with me, I would love that three nights not pass over me while I have of it a dinar with me for which I find one to accept it from me, except something I set aside for a debt upon me."
"8181","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the worker brings you your food, having sufficed you the toil of its heat and its smoke, invite him to eat with you, and if not, feed him a morsel in his hand."
"8182","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say: Give drink to your lord, feed your lord, perform ablution for your lord, and let none of you say: My lord, but let him say: My master and my patron, and let none of you say: My slave and my slave-girl, but let him say: My youth, my young woman, and my servant."
"8183","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first group to enter Paradise, their image upon the image of the moon on the night of full moon. They do not spit in it, nor blow their noses in it, nor blow mucus in it, nor defecate in it. Their vessels and their combs are gold and silver, and their censers are aloeswood, and their sweat is musk. And for each one of them two wives, the marrow of their shins seen from behind the flesh, from beauty. No disagreement among them nor hatred. Their hearts upon one heart. They glorify Allah morning and evening."
"8184","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I take with You a covenant You will never break for me: I am only a human, so whichever believer I harm or insult or flog or curse, make it for him prayer and purification and nearness by which You bring him near on the Day of Resurrection."
"8185","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spoils were not lawful for those before us; that is because Allah saw our weakness and incapacity, so He made them good for us."
"8186","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman entered the Fire because of a cat of hers she tied up: she neither fed it, nor let it go to eat from the vermin of the earth, until it died emaciated."
"8187","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A thief does not steal when he steals while he is a believer, and a fornicator does not fornicate when he fornicates while he is a believer, and a drinker does not drink when he drinks while he is a believer, meaning wine, and by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, none of you plunders a plunder of honor to which the believers raise their eyes while he is a believer when he plunders it, and none of you misappropriates spoils when he misappropriates while he is a believer. So beware, beware."
"8188","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, no one of this nation hears of me, neither Jew nor Christian, and dies without believing in what I was sent with, except he will be among the companions of the Fire."
"8189","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glorification is for the men, and clapping is for the women, in prayer."
"8190","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every wound a Muslim is wounded in the path of Allah, then it will be on the Day of Resurrection as its form when it was pierced, gushing blood: the color is the color of blood, and the scent is the scent of musk. My father said: Meaning by arf, fragrance."
"8191","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I return to my family and find a date fallen on my bed or in my house, so I lift it to eat it, then I fear it may be charity, so I throw it and do not eat it."
"8192","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will continue asking until one of you says: This is Allah who created creation, so who created Allah, Mighty and Majestic?"
"8193","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, for one of you to persist in his oath concerning his family is more sinful for him with Allah than to give his expiation which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, imposed."
"8194","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two are compelled to an oath and both desire it, let them draw lots upon it."
"8195","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you buys a milch camel with withheld milk or a sheep with withheld milk, he has the better of the two views after milking it: either he is content, or let him return it with a sa of dates."
"8196","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The old man remains upon love of two things: long life and much wealth."
"8197","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you walk to his brother with a weapon, for none of you knows: perhaps Satan may pull in his hand, so he falls into a pit of Fire."
"8198","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The anger of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, intensified against a people who did this to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was then pointing to his front teeth, and he said: The anger of Allah intensified against a man whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kills in the path of Allah."
"8199","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was written upon the son of Adam his share of fornication, which he will inevitably meet: the eye, its fornication is looking, and turning away confirms it, and the tongue, its fornication is speech, and the heart wishes, and the private part confirms what is there and denies."
"8200","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever village you come to and settle in it, your share is in it, and whatever village disobeys Allah and His Messenger, its fifth is for Allah and His Messenger, then it is for you."
"8201","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you perfects his Islam, every good deed he does is recorded as ten like it up to seven hundred times over, and every evil deed he does is recorded for him as one like it, until he meets Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"8202","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you stands to lead the people, let him lighten the prayer, for among them are the old, and among them are the weak, and among them are the sick; and when he stands alone, let him lengthen his prayer as he wishes."
"8203","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels said: Lord, that servant of Yours wants to do an evil deed, and He sees him better. So He said: Watch him; if he does it, record it for him as one like it, and if he leaves it, record it for him as a good deed, for he left it only for My sake."
"8204","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: My servant denied Me, and he had no right to do that, and he insulted Me, and he had no right to do that. His denial of Me is his saying: He will never return us as He began us. And as for his insulting Me, it is his saying: Allah has taken a son, while I am al-Samad, who did not beget and was not begotten, and there is none like unto Me."
"8205","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cool down from the heat for the prayer, for the intensity of heat is from the blast of Hell."
"8206","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not accept the prayer of one of you when he breaks wind until he performs ablution."
"8207","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the call to prayer is made, come to it walking, with calm upon you; what you catch, pray, and what you miss, complete."
"8208","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah laughs at two men, one of whom kills the other, and both enter Paradise. They said: How, O Messenger of Allah? He said: This one kills him and enters Paradise, then Allah turns to the other and guides him to Islam, then he strives in the way of Allah and is martyred."
"8209","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you sell over the sale of his brother, nor let one of you propose over the proposal of his brother."
"8210","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, and the believer eats in one intestine. Abd Allah narrated: I heard my father saying: I said to Abd al-Razzaq: O Abu Bakr, do you prefer, meaning this hadith, as if he was impressed by the excellence of this hadith and its quality. He said: Yes."
"8211","Abd al-Razzaq ibn Hammam narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Hammam, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He was not named Khadir except that he sat upon a white fleece, and it shook green. Al-farwah is white herbage and what resembles it. Abd Allah said: I think this is an explanation from Abd al-Razzaq."
"8212","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah does not look at the one who drags his garment on the Day of Resurrection."
"8213","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It was said to Bani Israil: Enter the gate prostrating and say: Hittah, We will forgive you your sins. But they changed, so they entered the gate crawling upon their buttocks, and they said: A grain in a hair."
"8214","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you stands at night and the Quran becomes tangled upon his tongue and he does not know what he says, let him lie down."
"8215","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not the son of Adam say: O failure of time. Indeed I am time; I send the night and the day, and when I wish I withhold them."
"8216","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What a good thing for the slave is to die upon excellent worship of Allah and companionship of his master. How good is that for him."
"8217","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you stands in prayer, let him not spit in front of him, for he is conversing with Allah as long as he is in his place of prayer, nor to his right, for there is an angel to his right; but let him spit to his left or beneath his foot and bury it."
"8218","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you say to the people: Be silent, while they are speaking, you have nullified your own reward."
"8219","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the closest of people to the believers in the Book of Allah. Whichever of you leaves a debt or a dependent, call me, for I am his guardian; and whichever of you leaves wealth, his male relatives, whoever they are, shall inherit his wealth."
"8220","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say: O Allah, forgive me if You wish, and have mercy on me if You wish, and provide for me. Let him be firm in asking, for He does what He wills; there is none to compel Him."
"8221","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prophet among the prophets raided, and he said to his people: Let no man follow me who has taken possession of a woman and wants to consummate with her but has not consummated, nor anyone who has built a building and has not yet raised its roof, nor anyone who has bought sheep or pregnant camels and awaits their offspring. So he raided and drew near the town at the time of Asr prayer or near that, and he said to the sun: You are commanded and I am commanded. O Allah, hold it back for me a little. So it was held back for him until Allah granted him victory. They gathered the spoils, and fire came to consume it but refused to taste it. He said: There is misappropriation among you, so let a man from every tribe pledge to me. They pledged to him, and the hand of a man stuck to his hand. He said: The misappropriation is among you, so let your tribe pledge to me. His tribe pledged to him. He said: Then the hands of two or three men stuck to his hand. He said: The misappropriation is among you; you misappropriated. So they brought out for him something like the head of a cow of gold. He said: They placed it in the wealth while it was on the open ground, and fire came and consumed it. Spoils were not lawful for anyone before us; that is because Allah, Mighty and Majestic, saw our weakness and incapacity, so He made it wholesome for us."
"8222","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was sleeping, I saw that I was drawing water at my basin, giving the people to drink. Abu Bakr came to me and took the bucket from my hand to ease it for me, until he drew one or two buckets, and in his drawing there was weakness. He said: Then Ibn al-Khattab came to me, may Allah forgive him, and took it from me, and no man drew like him until the people left and the basin was gushing."
"8223","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until you fight Khuz and Kirman, peoples among the non-Arabs, red-faced, flat-nosed, small-eyed, as if their faces were hammered shields."
"8224","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until you fight peoples whose sandals are hair."
"8225","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Arrogance and pride are among the people of horses and camels, and calm is among the people of sheep."
"8226","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People follow Quraysh in this matter; their Muslims follow their Muslims, and their disbelievers follow their disbelievers."
"8227","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best women who rode camels are the women of Quraysh, the most affectionate to a child in his childhood and the most caring for a husband in his property."
"8228","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The evil eye is true, and he forbade tattooing."
"8229","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of you remains in prayer as long as the prayer detains him; nothing prevents him except waiting for it."
"8230","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support."
"8231","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the closest of people to Isa ibn Maryam in this world and the Hereafter. They said: How, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The prophets are brothers from one father by different mothers; their mothers are different and their religion is one, and there is no prophet between us."
"8232","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was sleeping, I was brought the treasures of the earth, and two gold bracelets were placed in my hands. They weighed heavily upon me and troubled me, so it was revealed to me to blow upon them. I blew upon them and they vanished. I interpreted them as the two liars between whom I am: the man of Sanaa and the man of al-Yamamah."
"8233","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one will be saved by his deed, but be upright and draw near. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, except that Allah envelops me from Him with mercy and bounty."
"8234","And he said: He forbade two sales and two garments: that one of you sits with his knees drawn up in a single garment with nothing of it over his private part, and that one wraps himself in his waistcloth when he prays unless he crosses its two ends over his shoulder; and he forbade touching and najsh."
"8235","And he said: The injury of a stray beast is void, and the well is void, and the mine is void, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"8236","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I am the most like you in prayer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he said: Allah hears him who praises Him, said: Our Lord, and to You is praise; and he would say takbir when he bowed, and when he raised his head, and when he stood from the two prostrations he said: Allah is Most Great."
"8237","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Ajlan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every child born among Bani Adam, Satan touches him with his finger, except Maryam and her son."
"8238","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in whose hand is my soul, I see what is behind me as I see what is before me; so straighten your rows and perfect your bowing and prostration."
"8239","And with his isnad, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Men around the mosque who do not attend Isha shall desist, or I shall surely burn around their houses with bundles of firewood."
"8240","Hashim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Aswad ibn al-Ala al-Thaqafi, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: From the time one of you leaves his house to his mosque, one foot records a good deed and the other erases an evil deed."
"8241","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Hamzah, meaning al-Zayyat, narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Then he calls out with that: Indeed for you is to live and never die, and indeed for you is to be healthy and never be ill, and indeed for you is to be young and never grow old, and indeed for you is to enjoy and never suffer. He said: They call out with these four."
"8242","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abu Kathir narrated to me, Abu Hurayrah narrated to me, and he said to us: By Allah, Allah has not created a believer who hears of me nor sees me except that he loved me. I said: What is your knowledge of that, O Abu Hurayrah? He said: My mother was a polytheist woman, and I used to call her to Islam, and she would refuse me. One day I called her and she made me hear about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what I dislike. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) weeping, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I used to call my mother to Islam and she would refuse me, and today I called her and she made me hear about you what I dislike. Supplicate Allah to guide the mother of Abu Hurayrah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, guide the mother of Abu Hurayrah. So I went out running to give her glad tidings of the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When I came to the door, it was ajar, and I heard the splashing of water and heard the shuffling of a foot, meaning its sound. She said: O Abu Hurayrah, stay where you are. Then she opened the door, having put on her chemise and hastened without her headscarf, and she said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) weeping from joy as I had wept from sorrow, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, rejoice, for Allah has answered your supplication and guided the mother of Abu Hurayrah. Then I said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me and my mother beloved to His believing servants and to make them beloved to us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make this little servant of Yours and his mother beloved to Your believing servants and make them beloved to them. So Allah has not created a believer who hears of me nor sees me, or sees my mother, except that he loves me."
"8243","Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywah and Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad, the orphan of Urwah, narrated to us, that he heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrating from Marwan ibn al-Hakam, that he asked Abu Hurayrah: Did you pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the fear prayer? Abu Hurayrah said: Yes. He said: When? He said: In the year of the raid of Najd. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for Asr prayer, and a group stood with him, and another group faced the enemy, their backs to the qiblah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said takbir, and they all said takbir, those with him and those facing the enemy. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed one bow, then the group next to him bowed with him, then he prostrated and the group next to him prostrated, while the others stood facing the enemy. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, and the group with him stood, and they went to the enemy and faced them, and the group that had been facing the enemy came forward, and they bowed and prostrated while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood as he was. Then they stood, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed another bow, and they bowed with him and prostrated with him. Then the group that had been facing the enemy came forward, and they bowed and prostrated while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat, and those who followed him. Then came the taslim, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam and they all gave salam. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had two rakas, and for each man of the two groups, two rakas, two rakas."
"8244","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Abu Hani informed us, that Abu Said al-Ghifari informed him, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would follow silk in garments and remove it."
"8245","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to me, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever reaches sixty years, Allah has left him no excuse in age."
"8246","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Musa, meaning Ibn Ali, narrated to us, I heard my father narrating from Abd al-Aziz ibn Marwan ibn al-Hakam, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worst in a man is anxious greed and cowardice that unstrings."
"8247","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Jafar narrated to me, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is offered perfume, let him not refuse it, for it is light to carry and pleasant in scent."
"8248","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Hubayrah, from Abu Tamim al-Jayshani, who said: Abd Allah ibn Hurmuz, a freedman among the people of Madinah, wrote to me, mentioning from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever follows a funeral and carries from its upper part and carries in its grave and sits until he is permitted, returns with two qirats of reward, each qirat like Uhud."
"8249","Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from his book, narrated to us, he said: Said, meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to us, Bakr ibn Amr al-Maafiri narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Nuaymah, from Abu Uthman Muslim ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever falsely attributes to me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire; and whoever his Muslim brother consults him and he advises him without right guidance has betrayed him; and whoever is given a fatwa that is not firm, its sin is upon the one who gave him the fatwa."
"8250","Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Said narrated to us, Abu Hani Humayd ibn Hani al-Khawlani narrated to me, from Abu Uthman Muslim ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There will be at the end of time people from my ummah who narrate to you what neither you nor your fathers heard; beware of them."
"8251","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said narrated to us, Jafar ibn Rabiah narrated to me, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When you hear the voices of roosters, they have seen an angel, so ask Allah and desire Him; and when you hear the braying of donkeys, they have seen a devil, so seek refuge with Allah from the evil of what it saw."
"8252","Shuayb ibn Harb Abu Salih narrated to us, Layth ibn Said narrated to us, Jafar ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, and he mentioned its meaning."
"8253","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Sulayman informed me, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shoots at us by night is not of us."
"8254","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Ibn Hujayrah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The right of the believer upon the believer is six traits: to greet him when he meets him, and to say Yarhamuk Allah when he sneezes, and if he invites him to answer him, and when he is ill to visit him, and when he dies to attend him, and when he is absent to advise him."
"8255","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Ibn Hujayrah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised Salman al-Khayr. He said: The Prophet of Allah, upon him be peace, wants to grant you words with which you ask al-Rahman, desire Him in them, and supplicate with them night and day. He said: O Allah, I ask You for soundness of faith, and faith in good character, and success followed by prosperity, meaning, and mercy from You, and health, and forgiveness from You, and pleasure. My father said: And they are raised in the book: success followed by prosperity, and mercy from You, and health, and forgiveness from You, and pleasure."
"8256","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever finds means and does not sacrifice, let him not approach our place of prayer."
"8257","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from al-Qaqa, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There will remain for this affair, or over this affair, a group upon the truth, and the opposition of those who oppose them will not harm them until the command of Allah comes to them."
"8258","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said narrated to us, Abu Khayrah narrated to me, from Musa ibn Wardan, Abu Khayrah said: I know only that he said: from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among the males of my ummah believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waistcloth; and whoever among the females of my ummah believes in Allah and the Last Day, let her not enter the bathhouse."
"8259","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad and Ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abbas al-Jushami, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a surah of the Quran of thirty verses interceded for a man until he was forgiven, and it is: Blessed is He in whose hand is dominion."
"8260","Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Yunus ibn Yusuf narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, who said: The people moved away from Abu Hurayrah, and Natil al-Shami said to him: O shaykh, narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The first of people to be judged on the Day of Resurrection are three: a man martyred, so he is brought and He makes him know His blessings, and he knows them. He says: What did you do in them? He says: I fought in You until I was killed. He says: You lied, but you fought that it be said: He is bold, and it was said. Then He commands him, and he is dragged upon his face until he is thrown into the Fire. And a man who learned knowledge and taught it and recited the Quran, so he is brought to make him know His blessings, and he knows them. He says: What did you do in them? He says: I learned knowledge in You and taught it, and recited the Quran in You. He says: You lied, but you learned that it be said: He is learned, and it was said, and you recited the Quran that it be said: He is a reciter, and it was said. Then He commands him, and he is dragged upon his face until he is thrown into the Fire. And a man whom Allah enriched and gave all kinds of wealth, so he is brought and He makes him know His blessings, and he knows them. He says: What did you do in them? He says: I left no path You love to be spent in except I spent in it for You. He says: You lied, but you did that that it be said: He is generous, and it was said. Then He commands him, and he is dragged upon his face until he is thrown into the Fire."
"8261","Ali ibn Hafs narrated to us, Warqa narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Our dwelling tomorrow, if Allah wills, when Allah opens, is al-Khayf, where they swore upon disbelief."
"8262","Ali ibn Hafs narrated to us, Warqa informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah forgive Lut; he sought refuge in a strong support."
"8263","Ali ibn Hafs narrated to us, Warqa informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While two women with their two sons, a wolf came and took one of the two sons. They sought judgment from Dawud, and he judged for the elder. They went out, and Sulayman called them and said: Bring the knife; I shall cut him between you. The younger said: May Allah have mercy on you, he is her son, do not cut him. So he judged for the younger. Abu Hurayrah said: By Allah, we did not know what the knife was except that day, and we used to say only al-mudyah."
"8264","Ali ibn Hafs narrated to us, Warqa informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ibrahim, the friend of al-Rahman, was circumcised after eighty years had passed over him, and he was circumcised with al-Qadum, with lightening."
"8265","Ali ibn Hafs narrated to us, Warqa informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man said: I shall surely give charity tonight. He brought out his charity and placed it in the hand of an adulteress. In the morning they talked: Charity was given tonight to an adulteress. And he said: I shall surely give charity tonight. He brought out his charity and placed it in the hand of a thief. In the morning they talked: Charity was given tonight to a thief. Then he said: I shall surely give charity tonight. He brought out the charity and placed it in the hand of a rich man. In the morning they talked: Charity was given tonight to a rich man. He said: Praise be to Allah for a thief, and for an adulteress, and for a rich man. He said: Then he was visited and it was said to him: As for your charity, it has been accepted. As for the adulteress, perhaps she will thereby abstain, and as for the thief, perhaps he will thereby become independent, and as for the rich man, perhaps he will take heed and spend from what Allah gave him."
"8266","Ali ibn Hafs narrated to us, Warqa informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The earth consumes every son of Adam except the tailbone, for from it he was created and from it he is composed."
"8267","Ali ibn Hafs narrated to us, Warqa informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Umar for charity, and it was said: Ibn Jamil, and Khalid ibn al-Walid, and al-Abbas, the uncle of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), withheld. The Prophet said: Ibn Jamil resents only that he was poor and Allah enriched him. As for Khalid, you wrong Khalid, for he has reserved his coats of mail in the way of Allah. As for al-Abbas, it is upon me and the like of it. Then he said: Do you not know that the uncle of a man is like his father."
"8268","Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"8269","Abu Amir narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Muhammad, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No one goes out, meaning from his house, except in his hand are two banners: a banner in the hand of an angel, and a banner in the hand of a devil. If he goes out for what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves, the angel follows him with his banner, and he remains under the banner of the angel until he returns to his house; and if he goes out for what angers Allah, the devil follows him with his banner, and he remains under the banner of the devil until he returns to his house."
"8270","Abu Amir narrated to us, Abd Allah narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Muhammad, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah cursed the muhill and the one for whom it is done."
"8271","Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rights shall surely be given to their owners, until the hornless sheep is retaliated from the horned sheep on the Day of Resurrection."
"8272","Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The world is the prison of the believer and the paradise of the disbeliever."
"8273","Abu Amir narrated to us, Ali, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, from Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, from Ibn Yaqub, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The mufarridun have gone ahead. They said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the mufarridun? He said: Those who are absorbed in the remembrance of Allah."
"8274","Abu Amir narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from Musa ibn Abi Uthman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created Adam upon his image. And in the book of my father: And his length is sixty cubits. I do not know whether he narrated it to us or not."
"8275","Abu Amir narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Damdam ibn Jaws al-Yamami, who said: Abu Hurayrah said to me: O Yamami, do not ever say to a man: By Allah, Allah will not forgive you, or: Allah will never admit you to Paradise. I said: O Abu Hurayrah, this is a word one of us says to his brother and companion when angry. He said: Do not say it, for I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There were among Bani Israil two men; one of them was striving in worship, and the other was extravagant against himself, and they were two brothers. The striving one would always see the other upon a sin and say: O you, desist. He would say: Leave me and my Lord; were you sent over me as a watcher. He said: Until one day he saw him upon a sin he deemed grave, and said to him: Woe to you, desist. He said: Leave me and my Lord; were you sent over me as a watcher. He said: Then he said: By Allah, Allah will not forgive you, or: Allah will never admit you to Paradise. One of them said: Then Allah sent to them an angel who took their souls, and they gathered. He said to the sinner: Go and enter Paradise by My mercy. And He said to the other: Were you knowing of Me, were you a keeper over what is in My hand. Take him to the Fire. He said: By Him in whose hand is the soul of Abu al-Qasim, he spoke a word that ruined his world and his Hereafter."
"8276","Abu Amir narrated to us, Aflah ibn Said al-Ansari, among the people of Quba, narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Rafi, the freedman of Umm Salamah, narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: If a long time passes over you, you are about to see people who go out in the anger of Allah and return in the curse of Allah, in their hands like the tails of cows."
"8277","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from Abd al-Malik, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is offered something without asking for it, let him accept it, for it is only provision Allah drove to him."
"8278","Affan and Abd al-Samad said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Maymunah, from Abu Hurayrah, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: When I see you my soul is pleased and my eye is cooled, so inform me about everything. He said: Everything Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created is from water. He said: Inform me of a matter which if I take it I shall enter Paradise. He said: Spread peace, and feed food, and join ties of kinship, and pray while people sleep, then enter Paradise in peace. Abd al-Samad said: And inform me about everything."
"8279","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Maymunah, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When I see you my soul is pleased and my eye is cooled, so inform me about everything, and he mentioned its meaning."
"8280","Abu Amir narrated to us, Abu Mawdud narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hadrad al-Aslami narrated to me, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters this mosque and spits, or clears his throat, or hawks, let him dig in it and distance it and bury it; if he does not do so, then in his garment, then let him go out with it."
"8281","Abu Amir narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has his wealth sought unjustly and is killed, he is a martyr."
"8282","Abu Amir narrated to us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Muslim, narrated to us, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me some dates, and I placed them in a basket of ours and hung it in the roof of the house. We kept eating from it until its last was when the people of Sham seized it when they raided Madinah."
"8283","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Habib, meaning al-Muallim, narrated to us, Amr ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The flogged adulterer marries only his like."
"8284","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, who said: I stayed in Madinah with Abu Hurayrah for a year, and one day he said to me, while we were at the chamber of Aishah: You saw us with no garments except torn cloaks, and days would come upon one of us when he found no food to straighten his back, until one of us would take a stone and press it upon the hollow of his stomach, then tie it with his garment to straighten his back. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day distributed dates among us, and each man of us received seven dates, among them a dry one. Nothing would delight me that I have a good date in its place. He said: I said: Why. He said: It strengthens me for chewing. He said: Then he said to me: From where have you come. I said: From Sham. He said: Then he said to me: Did you see the stone of Musa. I said: What is the stone of Musa. He said: Bani Israil said about Musa a saying beneath his garments about his private parts. He said: He placed his garments upon a rock while bathing. He said: His garments hastened. He said: He followed them in their track, saying: O stone, cast my garments, until it brought him to Bani Israil, and they saw him level, excellent in form. He struck it three strikes. By Him in whose hand is the soul of Abu Hurayrah, had I looked, I would have seen the marks of Musa in it."
"8285","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Farqad narrated to us, from Abu al-Ala, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most lying of people are the goldsmiths and the dyers."
"8286","Abd al-Samad and Affan said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Ziyad ibn Riyah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasten with deeds six: the rising of the sun from its west, and al-Dajjal, and the smoke, and the beast of the earth, and the private affair of one of you, and the general affair. Affan said in his hadith: And Qatadah, when he said: And the general affair, said: And the affair of the Hour."
"8287","Rawh narrated to us, Abu Umayyah Amr ibn Yahya ibn Said ibn Amr ibn Said ibn al-As narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Said ibn Amr ibn Said informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The destruction of my ummah is at the hands of youths from Quraysh. Marwan said, while he was with us in the circle, before he held anything: May the curse of Allah be upon them as youths. He said: And by Allah, if I wished to say: Banu so-and-so and Banu so-and-so, I would do so. He said: Then I got up to go out, I with my father and my grandfather, to Marwan after they were made kings, and they were pledging allegiance to the boys among them and to whom allegiance is pledged for him while he is in a rag. He said to us: Perhaps these companions of yours are those whom I heard Abu Hurayrah mentioning that these kings resemble one another."
"8288","Rawh narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Sumayy, the freedman of Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salih al-Samman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The martyrs are five: the plague-stricken, and the one with abdominal illness, and the drowned, and the one under demolition, and the martyr in the way of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"8289","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Numan ibn Rashid informed me, from Ibn Shihab, that Ibn Shihab informed him, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When one of you eats, let him eat with his right, for Satan eats with his left and drinks with his left."
"8290","Rawh narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to them while they mentioned truffles, and some said: The smallpox of the earth. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Truffles are from manna, and their water is healing for the eye, and ajwah is from Paradise, and it is healing from poison."
"8291","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until my ummah takes what the nations and centuries before it took, a span by a span and a cubit by a cubit. They said: O Messenger of Allah, as Persia and Rome did. He said: Are people but those."
"8292","Abu Amir and Abu Salamah said: Sulayman, meaning Ibn Bilal, narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the man who wears the clothing of a woman and the woman who wears the clothing of a man."
"8293","Rawh narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanting travel, and said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: I advise you with fear of Allah and takbir upon every elevation. When the man turned away, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, fold the earth for him and ease travel for him."
"8294","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah, from Said ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from poverty, and scarcity, and humiliation, and I seek refuge in You from wronging or being wronged."
"8295","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ziyad informed me, that Thabit, the freedman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd, informed him, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the rider greet the walker, and the walker the sitter, and the few the many."
"8296","Rawh and Abu al-Mundhir said: Malik narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from Zufar ibn Sasaa ibn Malik, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he turned from the dawn prayer, would say: Did any of you see a dream tonight. Nothing remains after me of prophethood except the righteous dream."
"8297","Rawh narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abi Labid narrated to me, from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril commanded me to raise the voice in tahlil, for it is among the rites of Hajj."
"8298","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr informed us, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun was never held back for a man except for Yusha, the nights he marched to Bayt al-Maqdis."
"8299","Al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr informed us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever travels a path seeking knowledge in it, Allah eases for him a path to Paradise."
"8300","Al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to me, from Hisham, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered a camel, and the people plundered it. His caller called: Allah and His Messenger forbid you from plunder. The people came with what they took, and he divided it among them."
"8301","Al-Aswad narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr informed us, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not to have direct bodily contact with another woman, nor a man with another man."
"8302","Al-Aswad narrated to us, he said: Kamil, meaning Abu al-Ala, informed us, he said: I heard Abu Salih, a caller to prayer who used to call to prayer for them, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Seek refuge with Allah from the beginning of seventy and from the rule of boys."
"8303","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Kamil Abu al-Ala narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek refuge with Allah from the beginning of seventy and from the rule of boys. And he said: The world will not pass away until it belongs to Luka ibn Luka."
"8304","Al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Kamil informed us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: It was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do you not feel jealousy. He said: By Allah, I do feel jealousy, and Allah is more jealous than me, and out of His jealousy He forbade foul deeds."
"8305","Al-Aswad ibn Amir and Abu al-Mundhir Ismail ibn Umar narrated to us, they said: Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world will not pass away until it belongs to Luka. Ismail ibn Umar said: Until it belongs to Luka ibn Luka. And Ibn Abi Bukayr said: To Lukay ibn Lukay. And Aswad said: Meaning the disreputable son of the disreputable."
"8306","Al-Aswad narrated to us, Kamil narrated to us, Abu Salih narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The wealthy hoarders are the lowest, except one who says thus and thus and thus. Kamil said with his hand to his right and to his left and before him."
"8307","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Ata ibn Qurrah, from Abdullah ibn Damrah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as far as I know - Musa expressed doubt - he said: The offspring of the Muslims are in Paradise; Ibrahim (peace be upon him) looks after them."
"8308","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Uthman ibn Abi Sawdah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a Muslim visits his brother for the sake of Allah Almighty or visits him when sick, Allah Almighty says: You are blessed and you have taken a dwelling in Paradise."
"8309","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Numan narrating from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that Abdullah ibn Hudhafah al-Sahmi stood praying and raised his voice in his prayer, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ibn Hudhafah, do not make me hear, but make your Lord Almighty hear."
"8310","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Numan narrating from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one day seeking rain, and he prayed with us two rakahs without adhan and without iqamah, then he addressed us and supplicated Allah and turned his face toward the qiblah raising his hands, then he turned his cloak and put the right side upon the left and the left upon the right."
"8311","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Yunus from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are more entitled to doubt than Ibrahim (peace be upon him) when he said: My Lord, show me how You give life to the dead. He said: Have you not believed. He said: Yes, but that my heart may be at rest. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on Lut; he used to take refuge in a strong support. And had I remained in prison as long as Yusuf remained, I would have answered the caller."
"8312","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none among you whom his deed will admit to Paradise nor save him from the Fire. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Not even me, unless my Lord covers me with mercy from Him. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said with his hand thus, and Wahb gestured closing it and opening it."
"8313","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Most of the punishment of the grave is because of urine."
"8314","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Ruzayq, meaning Ibn Abi Salma, narrated to us, Abu al-Muhazzim narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the last Isha with the heaven of constellations and the heaven and the morning star."
"8315","Abu Said, freedman of Bani Hashim, narrated to us, Hammad ibn Abbad al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Muhazzim narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that the chapters of the heavens be recited in Isha."
"8316","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah disliked three things for you and is pleased with three things for you. He is pleased for you that you worship Him and do not associate anything with Him, and that you hold fast to the rope of Allah all together, and that you sincerely advise the rulers. And He disliked for you hearsay and gossip, and wasting wealth, and excessive questioning."
"8317","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to drink standing, and drinking from the mouth of the waterskin, and that a man prevent his neighbor from placing a beam in his wall."
"8318","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Shahr, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When the delegation of Abd al-Qays came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every man is accountable for himself; let every people drink in whatever vessels seem fit to them."
"8319","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell."
"8320","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two sons of al-As are believers."
"8321","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you fights his brother, let him avoid the face."
"8322","Hajjaj narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed me, Ziyad ibn Sad informed me, from Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, you will surely follow the ways of those before you handspan by handspan and cubit by cubit and fathom by fathom, until if they entered the hole of a lizard you would enter it. They said: And who are they, O Messenger of Allah, the People of the Book. He said: Then who."
"8323","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Ismail ibn Umayyah informed me, from Ayyub ibn Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Rafi, freedman of Umm Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and said: Allah created the soil on Saturday, and created the mountains therein on Sunday, and created the trees therein on Monday, and created the disliked things on Tuesday, and created light on Wednesday, and spread therein the beasts on Thursday, and created Adam (peace be upon him) after Asr on Friday, the last of creation in the last hour of the hours of Friday between Asr and the night."
"8324","Hashim narrated to us, Isa, meaning Ibn al-Musayyab, narrated to us, Abu Zurah narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit the house of some people of the Ansar with another house before theirs. He said: That was hard upon them, so they said: O Messenger of Allah, glory be to Allah, you visit the house of so-and-so and do not visit our house. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Because in your house there is a dog. They said: In their house there is a cat. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cat is a predator."
"8325","Hashim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shubrumah, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing infects anything, nothing infects anything, three times. He said: So a bedouin stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, a sore appears on the lip of a camel or on its tail and then covers the camels with mange. He said: So he was silent for a while, then he said: Who infected the first. There is no contagion and no Safar and no Hamah. Allah created every soul and wrote its life and its death and its calamities and its provision."
"8326","Hashim narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shubrumah, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is most entitled from me to good companionship. He said: Your mother. He said: Then who. He said: Then your mother. He said: Then who. He said: Then your mother. He said: Then who. He said: Your father."
"8327","Ribi ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The molar of the disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection will be like Uhud, and the breadth of his skin seventy cubits, and his thigh like Warqan, and his seat in the Fire like what is between me and al-Rabadhah."
"8328","Ribi ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Two men sneezed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), one of them nobler than the other. The noble one sneezed and did not praise Allah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not bless him. And the other sneezed and praised Allah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) blessed him. He said: So the noble one said: I sneezed before you and you did not bless me, and this one sneezed before you and you blessed him. He said: So he said: This one remembered Allah so I remembered him, and you forgot Allah so I forgot you."
"8329","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Malik ibn Zalim, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating to Marwan ibn al-Hakam, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu al-Qasim the truthful believed, saying: The ruin of my nation is at the hands of foolish young rulers from Quraysh."
"8330","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, Allah is Pure and does not accept except what is pure. And Allah commanded the believers with what He commanded the messengers, so He said: O messengers, eat of the pure things and do righteous deeds; I am Knowing of what you do. And He said: O you who believe, eat of the pure things of what We provided you. Then he mentioned a man who prolongs travel, disheveled and dusty, then stretches his hands to the heaven: O Lord, O Lord, while his food is unlawful and his drink is unlawful and his clothing is unlawful and he was nourished with the unlawful, so how can that be answered."
"8331","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Ashath ibn Sulaym, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Congregational prayer exceeds solitary prayer by twenty-seven degrees."
"8332","Abu al-Nadr and Ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Said al-Maqburi, from Said ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim man settles in the mosques for prayer and remembrance - Ibn Abi Bakr said: No Muslim man settles - but Allah rejoices with him until he leaves, as the family of an absent one rejoice at his coming when he comes to them."
"8333","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, and Ishaq ibn Sulayman said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Said ibn Saman, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating to Abu Qatadah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allegiance will be given to a man between the Corner and the Station, and none will violate the House except its people. When they violate it, ask not about the destruction of the Arabs. Then the Abyssinians will come and destroy it with a destruction after which it will never be inhabited again, and they are the ones who will extract its treasure."
"8334","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Salih, freedman of al-Tawamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that he used to describe the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: He had broad forearms, long eyelashes, wide between the shoulders, he turned all together and turned away all together. May my father and mother be ransom for him, he was not obscene nor deliberately obscene nor loud in the markets."
"8335","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, that he mentioned from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the owned slave will be judged by his prayer. If anything is lacking from it, it will be said to him: You fell short in it. So he will say: O Lord, You set over me a master who distracted me from my prayer. So He will say: I saw you stealing from his wealth for yourself, so why did you not steal for yourself from your work or his work. He said: So Allah will establish the proof against him."
"8336","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Mubarak ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I know it only from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every joint of the son of Adam is charity in the morning. That was hard upon the Muslims, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your greeting the servants of Allah is charity, and your removing harm from the road is charity, and your enjoining good is charity, and your forbidding evil is charity. And he narrated things of like this that I did not memorize."
"8337","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Only one who hopes not to wear it in the Hereafter wears silk in this world. Only one with no share wears silk. Al-Hasan said: What is with peoples to whom this reaches from their Prophet yet they put silk in their clothes and in their houses. Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, and I know it only from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The eye commits adultery and the heart commits adultery; the adultery of the eye is the gaze, and the adultery of the heart is wishful desire, and the private part confirms what is there or denies it."
"8338","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, and I know it only from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The eye commits adultery and the heart commits adultery; the adultery of the eye is the gaze, and the adultery of the heart is wishful desire, and the private part confirms what is there or denies it."
"8339","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: My close friend Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me three that I will not leave: fasting three days of every month, and not to sleep except upon witr, and ghusl on Friday."
"8340","Al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, which prayer is best after the prescribed. He said: Prayer in the middle of the night. He said: Then which fasting is best after Ramadan. He said: The month of Allah which you call Muharram."
"8341","Abu Asim narrated to us, Ibn Ajlan informed us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever bears arms against us is not of us."
"8342","Abu Asim narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty said: The most beloved of My servants to Me are the quickest of them in breaking the fast."
"8343","Abu Asim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rifah informed us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) most often fasted Mondays and Thursdays. He said: So it was said to him. He said: So he said: Deeds are presented every Monday and Thursday - or every Monday and Thursday - so Allah forgives every Muslim or every believer except two estranged ones, and He says: Delay them."
"8344","Abu Asim narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Yazid ibn Farrukh al-Damri of the people of Medina narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Salamah saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I bear witness that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no servant or maid who swears at this minbar a sinful oath, even over a moist siwak, but the Fire becomes due for him."
"8345","Abu Asim narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, Imran ibn Abi Anas narrated to me, from Umar ibn al-Hakam, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A believing man is not to hate a believing woman; if he dislikes one trait from her, he is pleased with another from her."
"8346","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Umar ibn al-Hakam al-Ansari, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The night and day will not pass until a man from the freed slaves called Jahjah rules."
"8347","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that the food notes of the traders came out, so the traders asked Marwan for permission to sell them, and he permitted them. So Abu Hurayrah entered upon him and said to him: You permitted the sale of riba, though the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade food to be bought then sold until it is fully received. Sulayman said: So I saw Marwan send the guards, and they began seizing the notes from the hands of those among them who were not scrupulous."
"8348","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said: I never saw a man whose prayer more resembled that of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than so-and-so, an imam in Medina. Sulayman ibn Yasar said: So I prayed behind him, and he used to lengthen the first two of Zuhr and lighten the last two, and lighten Asr, and recite in the first two of Maghrib with the short Mufassal, and recite in the first two of Isha from the middle Mufassal, and recite in the morning with the long Mufassal. Al-Dahhak said: And one who heard Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, saying: I never saw anyone whose prayer more resembled the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than this young man, meaning Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz. Al-Dahhak said: So I prayed behind Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, and he used to do like what Sulayman ibn Yasar said."
"8349","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Abi Muzarrid narrated to me, he said: My uncle Said Abu al-Hubab narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah Almighty created creation, the womb stood and took hold of the waist of al-Rahman. It said: This is the station of one seeking refuge from severing. He said: Will you not be pleased that I join whoever joins you and sever whoever severs you. Recite if you wish: Would you then, if you turned away, spread corruption in the earth and sever your kin. Those are the ones Allah cursed, so He deafened them and blinded their sights. Do they not ponder the Quran, or are there locks upon hearts."
"8350","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi said: Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Tamim, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the oath of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), no month has come upon the Muslims better for them than Ramadan, and no month has come upon the hypocrites worse than Ramadan. That is because the believers prepare therein strength for worship, and the hypocrites prepare therein heedlessness of people and their faults. It is spoil, and the believer profits from it and the wicked loses."
"8351","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is in prayer, Satan comes to him and cajoles him as a man cajoles his beast. When he submits to him, he breaks wind between his buttocks to confuse him about his prayer. So if one of you finds anything of that, let him not leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell, without doubt."
"8352","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is in the mosque, Satan comes to him and cajoles him as a man cajoles his beast. When he submits to him, he constricts him or bridles him. Abu Hurayrah said: So you see that. As for the constricted, you see him leaning thus, not remembering Allah. And as for the bridled, with his mouth open, not remembering Allah Almighty."
"8353","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Iyad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Sarh, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and addressed the people, then he mentioned that faith in Allah and jihad in the path of Allah are among the best deeds with Allah. So a man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, if I am killed in the path of Allah while patient and seeking reward, advancing and not retreating, will Allah expiate my sins from me. He said: Yes. So how did you say. He said: If I am killed in the path of Allah while patient and seeking reward, advancing and not retreating, will Allah expiate my sins from me. He said: Yes. How did you say. He said: If I am killed in the path of Allah while patient and seeking reward, advancing and not retreating, will Allah expiate my sins from me. He said: Yes, except debt, for Jibril told me that secretly."
"8354","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The righteous owned slave has two rewards. And by Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Abu Hurayrah, were it not for jihad in the path of Allah and hajj and kindness to my mother, I would love to die as a slave."
"8355","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, Abu Abdullah al-Qarraz narrated to us that he heard Sad ibn Malik and Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless the people of Medina in their city, and bless them in their sa and bless them in their mudd. O Allah, Ibrahim is Your servant and Your close friend, and I am Your servant and Your Messenger. Ibrahim asked You for the people of Mecca, and I ask You for the people of Medina as Ibrahim asked You for the people of Mecca, and the like with it. Medina is encircled by angels; over every pass thereof are two angels guarding it. Neither plague nor the Dajjal will enter it. Whoever intends it with evil, Allah will melt him as salt melts in water."
"8356","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Jafar, meaning al-Razi, narrated to us, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade one of us to pray with his hands upon his waist."
"8357","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Jafar narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: For the belly of one of you to be filled with pus is better for him than to be filled with poetry."
"8358","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Said, meaning al-Muaddib, narrated to us, he said: My father - and his name is Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Abi al-Waddah Abu Said al-Muaddib - he said: My father - and Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Abu Dawud and Abu Kamil narrated from him - he said: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan comes to one of you and says: Who created the heaven. So he says: Allah Almighty. So he says: Who created the earth. So he says: Allah. So he says: Who created Allah. So if one of you senses anything of this, let him say: I believe in Allah and His messengers."
"8359","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Aqil narrated to us, Abu Hayyan narrated to us, from Abu Zurah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to love the foreleg."
"8360","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Aqil narrated to us, he said: My father, his name is Abdullah ibn Aqil al-Thaqafi, trustworthy, Abdallah ibn Said narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your oath is what your companion believes you about."
"8361","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Warqa ibn Umar al-Yashkuri narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Dinar narrating from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prayer after the iqamah except the prescribed one."
"8362","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Warqa narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a market of the markets of Medina, and he left and I left with him. Then he came to the courtyard of Fatimah and called Hasan, saying: O Luka, O Luka, O Luka, saying it three times, and none answered him. He said: So he left and I left with him. He said: Then he came to the courtyard of Aishah and sat. He said: Then Hasan ibn Ali came. Abu Hurayrah said: I thought his mother kept him to put the sikhab necklace upon his neck. When he came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) embraced him and he embraced the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: O Allah, I love him, so love him and love whoever loves him, three times."
"8363","Abu al-Nadr and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Warqa narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Said ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever gives charity equal to a date from pure earnings - and only the pure ascends to Allah - Allah accepts it with His right hand, then raises it for its owner as one of you raises his foal, until it is like a mountain."
"8364","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Peoples will enter Paradise whose hearts are like the hearts of birds."
"8365","Abdullah said: My father said: Yaqub narrated it to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Salamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - Abdullah said, and it is correct, meaning he did not mention Abu Hurayrah - Peoples will enter Paradise whose hearts are like the hearts of birds."
"8366","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me with three: sleep upon witr, and ghusl on Friday, and fasting three days of every month."
"8367","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Usamah narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intending travel to bid him farewell, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I enjoin upon you fear of Allah and takbir upon every eminence. When he turned away, he said: O Allah, fold the distance for him and ease travel for him."
"8368","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Said narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that he used to say: How will you be when you collect neither dinar nor dirham. So it was said to him: And do you see that happening, O Abu Hurayrah. So he said: By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Abu Hurayrah, on the word of the truthful believed. They said: And what is that about. He said: The covenant of Allah and the covenant of His Messenger will be violated, so Allah will harden the hearts of the people of the covenant and they will withhold what is in their hands. And by Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Abu Hurayrah, it will surely happen twice."
"8369","Abu Abd al-Rahman Shadhan narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There was a man who used to lend people. He used to say to his servant: When you come to one in hardship, overlook him; perhaps Allah will overlook us. So he met Allah and He overlooked him."
"8370","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Euphrates will recede - or the Hour will not come until the Euphrates recedes from a mountain of gold, and the people fight over it. Then killed from every hundred will be ninety-nine. O my son, if you reach it, do not be among those who fight over it."
"8371","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muawiyah al-Mahri narrated to me, he said: Abu Hurayrah said to me: O Mahri, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of a dog and the earnings of a cupper and the earnings of a prostitute and the earnings from the studding of a stallion."
"8372","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Quran was revealed in seven modes: All-Knowing, Wise, Forgiving, Merciful."
"8373","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The noble son of the noble son of the noble son of the noble is Yusuf ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, the close friend of al-Rahman Almighty. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I remained in prison as Yusuf remained, then the caller came to me, I would have answered him, when the messenger came to him and he said: Return to your lord and ask him what is the case of the women who cut their hands; my Lord is Knowing of their plot. And may the mercy of Allah be upon Lut; he used to take refuge in a strong support when he said to his people: Would that I had strength against you or took refuge in a strong support. And Allah did not send after him any prophet except among the wealth of his people."
"8374","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to love the good omen and dislike bad omens."
"8375","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am only a human, and perhaps some of you are more eloquent in his plea than others. So whomever I cut for him a piece of the right of his brother, I only cut for him a piece of the Fire."
"8376","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A bedouin entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did Umm Mildam ever seize you. He said: And what is Umm Mildam. He said: Fever between the skin and the flesh. He said: I never felt this. He said: So did this headache ever seize you. He said: And what is this headache. He said: A vein that throbs in a man in his head. He said: I never felt this. When he turned away, he said: Whoever loves to look at a man of the people of the Fire, let him look at this."
"8377","And with his isnad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Jews split into seventy-one or seventy-two sects, and my nation will split into seventy-three sects."
"8378","And with his isnad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five are of the right of a Muslim over a Muslim: returning the greeting, and accepting the invitation, and attending the funeral, and visiting the sick, and blessing the sneezer when he praises Allah Almighty."
"8379","And with his isnad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah created Paradise and Hell, He sent Jibril. He said: Look at it and at what I prepared for its people therein. So he came and looked at it and at what Allah prepared for its people therein, then returned to Him. He said: By Your might, none will hear of it but will enter it. So He commanded it and it was veiled with hardships. He said: Return to it and look at it and at what I prepared for its people therein. He said: So he returned to it, and it had been veiled with hardships. So he returned to Him. He said: By Your might, I fear that none will enter it. He said: Go to the Fire and look at it and at what I prepared for its people therein. And it was heaping one part upon another. So he returned. He said: By Your might, I feared that none would hear of it and enter it. So He commanded it and it was surrounded with desires. So he said: By Your might, I fear that none will escape from it but will enter it."
"8380","And with his isnad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: There were two men from Bali of Qudaah who embraced Islam with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and one of them was martyred and the other was delayed a year. Talhah ibn Ubaydillah said: So I was shown Paradise and I saw therein the delayed of the two admitted before the martyr, and I wondered at that. In the morning I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - or that was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did he not fast Ramadan after him and pray six thousand rakahs, or so-and-so rakahs of the prayer of the year."
"8381","Yazid, meaning Ibn Harun, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Talhah ibn Ubaydillah, that two men from Bali, a clan of Qudaah, and he mentioned it."
"8382","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Kaysan narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Salamah ibn al-Azraq, he said: One of the kinswomen of Marwan died, and the people attended her and Abu Hurayrah attended her, and with her were weeping women. So Marwan ordered them off. So Abu Hurayrah said: Leave them, for a bier with weepers passed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Umar, may Allah have mercy on him, scolded them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Leave them, for the soul is afflicted and the eye is tearful and the covenant is recent."
"8383","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When Warn your nearest kin was revealed, he began calling the bellies of Quraysh one by one: O sons of so-and-so, save yourselves from the Fire, until he ended with Fatimah. So he said: O Fatimah daughter of Muhammad, save yourself from the Fire; I own nothing for you from Allah except that you have kinship which I will keep moist with its moisture."
"8384","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Abu Hayyan narrated to us, from Abu Zurah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Bilal at the Fajr prayer: O Bilal, tell me of the most hopeful deed you did of benefit in Islam, for I heard tonight the sound of your sandals before me in Paradise. He said: I never did in Islam, O Messenger of Allah, a deed more hopeful to me of benefit than that I never performed complete purification at any hour of night or day but I prayed with that purification for my Lord whatever was written for me to pray."
"8385","Yahya ibn Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik, meaning al-Nawfali, narrated to us, from his father, he mentioned it from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever touches his private part with his hand with no covering, ablution becomes obligatory upon him."
"8386","Al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from his father, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"8387","Yahya ibn Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from his father, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say often: There is no power nor strength except with Allah, for it is a treasure of the treasures of Paradise."
"8388","Yahya ibn Yazid narrated to us, from his father, from Jubayr ibn Abi Salih, and he was called Ibn Nufaylah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The price of al-jarisah is unlawful and eating it is unlawful."
"8389","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: And I see it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Peoples will surely stop raising their sights to the heaven in prayer, or their sights will surely be snatched away."
"8390","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Is there no man to take what Allah and His Messenger obligated, one word or two words or three or four or five, and put them in the edge of his cloak and learn them and teach them. Abu Hurayrah said: So I said: Me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: So spread your garment. He said: So I spread my garment, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated, then he said: Gather it to you. So I gathered my garment to my chest, and I hope I have not forgotten a hadith I heard from him after."
"8391","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar, narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The molar of the disbeliever is like Uhud, and his thigh is like al-Bayda, and his seat in the Fire is like what is between Qudayd and Mecca, and the thickness of his skin forty-two cubits by the cubit of al-Jabbar."
"8392","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A servant speaks a word of the pleasure of Allah Almighty paying no heed to it, and Allah raises him with it degrees. And a servant speaks a word of the wrath of Allah paying no heed to it, and he falls with it into Jahannam."
"8393","Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ammar Kashakish, he said: I heard Said al-Maqburi narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The best earning is the earning of the hand of a worker when he is sincere."
"8394","Abu Amir narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Nuaym ibn Abdullah al-Mujmir, that he went up to Abu Hurayrah on the back of the mosque while he was performing ablution, and he raised it to his upper arms, then he turned to me and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: My nation on the Day of Resurrection are radiant in forehead and limbs from the traces of ablution. So whoever of you can extend his radiance, let him do. Nuaym said: I do not know whether His saying: Whoever can extend his radiance let him do is from the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or from the saying of Abu Hurayrah."
"8395","Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do you know who the bankrupt is. They said: The bankrupt among us, O Messenger of Allah, is one with no dirham nor dinar nor goods. He said: The bankrupt of my nation on the Day of Resurrection is one who comes with prayer and fasting and zakat, and comes having insulted the honor of this and slandered this and consumed the wealth of this and struck this. So he is seated, and this retaliates from his good deeds and this from his good deeds. If his good deeds are exhausted before what is upon him is settled, taken from their sins and thrown upon him, then he is thrown into the Fire. And Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, said: So he retaliates. And Abd al-Rahman said: Before what is upon him is settled."
"8396","Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If the believer knew what is with Allah of punishment, none would hope for Paradise. And if the disbeliever knew what is with Allah of mercy, none would despair of Paradise. Allah created a hundred mercies and placed one mercy among His creation by which they show mercy to one another, and with Allah are ninety-nine mercies."
"8397","Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Asid ibn Abi Asid, from Nafi ibn Ayyash, freedman of Aqilah bint Talq al-Ghifari, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever loves to collar his beloved with a collar of Fire, let him collar him with a collar of gold. And whoever loves to bracelet his beloved with a bracelet of Fire, let him bracelet him with a bracelet of gold. And whoever loves to ring his beloved with a ring of Fire, let him ring him with a ring of gold. But silver is for you; play with it as you like, play with it as you like."
"8398","Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Musa ibn Wardan narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man is upon the religion of his friend, so let one of you look at whom he befriends."
"8399","Abu Amir and Surayj narrated to us, they said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no believer but I am closer to him in this world and the Hereafter. Recite if you wish: The Prophet is closer to the believers than themselves. So whichever believer perishes and leaves wealth, his kinsmen inherit it, whoever they are. And whoever leaves debt or helpless dependents, let him come to me, for I am his guardian."
"8400","Abu Amir narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever believes in Allah and His Messenger and establishes prayer and fasts Ramadan, Allah will admit him to Paradise, whether he emigrated in the path of Allah or sat in the land in which he was born. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not inform the people. He said: In Paradise are a hundred ranks which Allah Almighty prepared for the mujahids in His path; between every two ranks is as between the heaven and the earth. So when you ask Allah Almighty, ask Him al-Firdaws, for it is the middle of Paradise and the highest of Paradise, and above it is the Throne of al-Rahman Almighty, and from it the rivers of Paradise burst forth. Abu Amir doubted. Ata ibn Yasar said."
"8401","Yunus narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Ata ibn Yasar or Ibn Abi Amrah - Fulayh said: I only know it as from Ibn Abi Amrah - then he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: the rivers of Paradise gush forth, and he said: Shall we not inform the people of that? He said it alone, then he narrated it to us without doubt - meaning Fulayh [source text ends abruptly here]"
"8402","Surayj narrated it to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then he mentioned it, and he said: And above it is the Throne of the Most Merciful, and from it the rivers of Paradise burst forth."
"8403","Surayj narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The old man grows old and his body weakens, but his heart remains young in love of two things: long life and wealth."
"8404","Abu Amir and Surayj narrated to us, both said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The people of Paradise will visit one another in it - Surayj said: they will see one another in it - just as you see the eastern star and the western star disappearing on the horizon and rising, according to the difference in ranks. They said: O Messenger of Allah, those are the prophets? He said: Yes, by the One in Whose Hand is Muhammad's soul, people who believed in Allah and His Messenger and confirmed the messengers - and Surayj said: people who believed in Allah."
"8405","Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No fatigue, nor illness, nor worry, nor grief, nor sorrow, nor harm befalls the Muslim man, even the thorn he is pricked with, except that Allah expiates thereby some of his sins."
"8406","Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Amr ibn Shihab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever has three daughters and endures their hardship, their adversity and their ease, Allah will admit him to Paradise by virtue of His mercy to them. A man said: Or two, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Or two. A man said: Or one, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Or one."
"8407","Bakr ibn Isa narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Balj, from Amr ibn Maymun who said: Abu Hurayrah said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Hurayrah, shall I guide you to a word, a treasure from the treasure of Paradise beneath the Throne? I said: Yes, may my father and mother be your ransom. He said: That you say: There is no strength except through Allah. Abu Balj said: And I think he said: For Allah the Exalted says: My servant has submitted and surrendered. He said: I said it to Amr - Abu Balj said: Amr said: I said to Abu Hurayrah: There is no might nor power except through Allah, and he said: No, it is in Surat al-Kahf: And why, when you entered your garden, did you not say: What Allah wills; there is no strength except through Allah."
"8408","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a man used to sell wine on a ship and used to adulterate it with water, and with him on the ship was a monkey. It took the bag containing the dinars, climbed to the top, meaning the mast, opened the bag, and began throwing one dinar into the sea and one into the ship until nothing remained in it."
"8409","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Muslim, narrated to us, he said: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of the rows of men is the foremost, and the worst of them is the last; and the worst of the rows of women is the foremost, and the best of them is the last."
"8410","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Abi Khalid, narrated to us, from his father who said: I said to Abu Hurayrah: Is this how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray with you? He said: What did you find objectionable in my prayer? He said: I said: I wanted to ask you about that. He said: Yes, and he kept it brief. His standing was about the time it takes the muezzin to descend from the minaret and reach the row."
"8411","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A neck will emerge from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, having two eyes with which it sees, two ears with which it hears, and a tongue with which it speaks, and it will say: I have been entrusted with three: every obstinate tyrant, everyone who claimed another god besides Allah, and the image-makers."
"8412","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Nafi, the freedman of Abu Qatadah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How will you be when Isa son of Maryam descends among you and your imam is from among you?"
"8413","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, by Allah, he does not believe; no, by Allah, he does not believe; no, by Allah, he does not believe. They said: Who is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A neighbor whose neighbor is not safe from his evils. It was said: What are his evils? He said: His harm."
"8414","Uthman ibn Umar Abu Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until my nation follows the ways of the nations before it, handspan by handspan and cubit by cubit. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, as Persia and Rome did? He said: And who are the people except those?"
"8415","Abu al-Walid ibn Umar narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to me, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: A Bedouin brought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a rabbit he had roasted, with its mustard sauce and condiment, and placed it before him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) withheld and did not eat, and commanded his companions to eat, while the Bedouin withheld. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What prevents you from eating? He said: I fast three days of the month. He said: If you are fasting, then fast the bright days."
"8416","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to observe retreat in the last ten days of the month of Ramadan, but in the year in which he passed away he observed retreat for twenty days."
"8417","Umar ibn Sad, who is Abu Dawud al-Hafari, narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought food at Marr al-Zahran, and he said to Abu Bakr and Umar: Come near and eat. They said: We are fasting. He said: Saddle up for your two companions; work for your two companions."
"8418","Umar ibn Sad narrated to us, Yahya, meaning Ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah, narrated to us, from Sad ibn Tariq, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The quickest of the Arab tribes to perish is Quraysh, and it is near that a woman will pass by a sandal and say: This is the sandal of a Qurashi."
"8419","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Qutbah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We find among the worst of people before Allah the two-faced one."
"8420","Hisham ibn Said narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the slave of one of you steals, let him sell him, even for a nashsh."
"8421","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to me in the year one hundred and fifty-one: I went out with Sufyan, he said: Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys food, let him not sell it until he has taken full possession of it."
"8422","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you fights his brother, let him avoid the face."
"8423","Abd al-Samad and Affan narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you travel in fertile land, give the camels their due, and when you travel in drought, hasten the pace, and when you wish to halt for rest at night, keep away from the road - Affan said in his hadith: I am Suhayl ibn Abi Salih."
"8424","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not make your houses graveyards, for Satan flees from the house when he hears Surat al-Baqarah recited in it."
"8425","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Salim Abu Jumay narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, that Abu Hurayrah reported that Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, Utarid al-Tamimi used to offer a silk suit; if only you would buy it and wear it when the delegations of people come to you. He said: Only one who has no share wears silk."
"8426","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: By Allah, I am the closest of you in prayer to the Messenger of Allah. Abu Hurayrah used to perform supplication in the last rakah of the late evening prayer and the dawn prayer, after saying: Allah hears whoever praises Him, supplicating for the believers and cursing the disbelievers."
"8427","Mansur ibn Salamah narrated to us, Sulayman, meaning Ibn Bilal, informed us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Hasten to do deeds before six: the rising of the sun from its west, the Dajjal, the smoke, the Beast, the personal affair of one of you, and the general affair."
"8428","Mansur narrated to us, Sulayman, meaning Ibn Bilal, informed us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: It is not fitting for a truthful one to be given to cursing."
"8429","Mansur narrated to us, Sulayman informed us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Fix prices. He said: Allah the Exalted raises and lowers, but I hope to meet Allah the Exalted with no one having a claim of injustice against me."
"8430","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Awanah informed us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the women who visit graves frequently."
"8431","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Awanah informed us, and Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This Uhud loves us and we love it."
"8432","Husayn narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the slave steals, sell him, even for a nashsh, meaning half an uqiyyah."
"8433","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Awanah informed us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the women who visit graves frequently."
"8434","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, from Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Dajjal will surely descend upon Khuz and Kirman among seventy thousand, their faces like hammered shields."
"8435","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Harith, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he went out to the two festivals would return by a different road than the one by which he went out."
"8436","Yunus narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Said ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted says: Where are those who love one another for My majesty? Today I shall shade them in My shade, on a day when there is no shade except My shade."
"8437","Yunus narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The old man - Yunus said, I think he said: grows decrepit and his body weakens, but his heart remains young in love of two things: long life and love of wealth."
"8438","Yunus and Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, both said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu Tuwalah, from Said ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever learns knowledge by which the Face of Allah is sought, learning it only to attain thereby a worldly gain, will not find the fragrance of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection - Surayj said in his hadith, meaning its scent."
"8439","Yunus and Surayj narrated to us, both said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Said ibn Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Lands and cities will be opened, and men will say to their brothers: Come to the countryside, while Madinah is better for them if only they knew. No one endures its hardship and severity except that I shall be for him on the Day of Resurrection a witness or an intercessor."
"8440","Yunus and Surayj narrated to us, both said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Said ibn Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the Hour there will be deceitful years, in which the truthful will be denied and the liar believed, the trustworthy betrayed and the treacherous trusted, and the worthless will speak - Surayj said: and the worthless will opine."
"8441","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw in a dream as though there were two bracelets of gold on my hands, so I blew on them and they were lifted away, and I interpreted that one of them was Musaylimah and the other al-Ansi."
"8442","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, he said: And Bukayr narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us on an expedition and said: If you find so-and-so and so-and-so, two men of Quraysh, burn them with fire. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when we were about to depart: I had commanded you to burn so-and-so and so-and-so with fire, but none punishes with fire except Allah the Exalted; if you find them, kill them."
"8443","Yunus narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Yaqub ibn Abi Yaqub, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man should not make another man stand from his seat, but make room; Allah will make room for you."
"8444","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu al-Muhazzim, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought seven spiny-tailed lizards served with dates and clarified butter, and he said: Eat, for I find them distasteful."
"8445","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Abu al-Muhazzim narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a mangy young goat which its owners had cast out, and said: Do you see this as worthless to its owners? They said: Yes. He said: The world is more insignificant to Allah the Exalted than this is to its owners."
"8446","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when food from other than his household was brought to him would ask about it; if it was said to him: It is a gift, he ate, and if it was said: It is charity, he said: Eat, and did not eat himself."
"8447","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, that Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out after the prayer had been called and the rows straightened, until when he stood in his place of prayer and we waited for him to say the takbir, he turned away and said: Stay in your places. He entered his house, and we remained as we were until he came out to us with his head dripping, having performed the ritual bath."
"8448","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man used to lend to people, and he would say to his servant: When you come to one in hardship, pardon him; perhaps Allah will pardon us. He met Allah, and Allah pardoned him."
"8449","Fazarah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There were among the nations before you inspired men, and if there is any among this nation of mine, it is Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"8450","And Yaqub narrated it to us, my father narrated to us, from his father, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - then he mentioned it as disconnected."
"8451","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, Ibn Shihab said: Ibn al-Musayyab narrated to me that Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was asleep, I saw myself in Paradise, and there was a woman performing ablution beside a palace. I said: Whose palace is this? They said: Umar ibn al-Khattab's. I remembered your jealousy, so I turned away. And Umar, may Allah have mercy on him, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was saying that, was sitting with the people; Umar wept when he heard that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Would I be jealous of you, may my father be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah?"
"8452","Fazarah narrated to us, he said: Fulayh informed me, from Hilal, meaning Ibn Ali, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise will see one another in Paradise just as you see - or you behold - the brilliant star disappearing on the horizon and rising, according to the difference in ranks. They said: O Messenger of Allah, those are the prophets? He said: Yes, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, and people who believed in Allah and confirmed the messengers."
"8453","Fazarah narrated to us, Fulayh informed us, and Surayj said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The old man grows old and his body weakens, but his heart stays young in love of two things: long life and love of wealth - and Surayj said: love of life and love of wealth."
"8454","Yunus narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed the woman who joins hair and the one who asks for it to be joined, and the woman who tattoos and the one who asks to be tattooed."
"8455","Fazarah ibn Amr narrated to us, Fulayh informed me, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and His Messenger, establishes prayer and fasts Ramadan, it is incumbent upon Allah the Exalted to admit him to Paradise, whether he emigrates in the cause of Allah or remains in the land where he was born. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not inform the people of that? He said: In Paradise there are a hundred levels prepared for those who strive in His cause; between every two levels is like between heaven and earth. When you ask Allah the Exalted, ask Him for al-Firdaws, for it is the middle of Paradise and the highest of Paradise, and above it is the Throne of the Most Merciful the Exalted, and from it the rivers of Paradise gush forth."
"8456","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid, from Amr ibn Quhayd ibn Mutarrif al-Ghifari, from Abu Hurayrah who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what if my property is attacked? He said: Implore them by Allah. He said: If they refuse me? He said: Implore them by Allah. He said: If they refuse me? He said: Implore them by Allah. He said: If they refuse me? He said: Then fight; if you are killed you are in Paradise, and if you kill him he is in the Fire."
"8457","Qutaybah narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Amr ibn Quhayd al-Ghifari, from Abu Hurayrah, then he mentioned the hadith."
"8458","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Sumayy, the freedman of Abu Bakr, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complained to him of the hardship of prostration upon them when they were spaced apart. He said: Seek help with the knees. Ibn Ajlan said: That is, one places his elbow upon his knees when prostration is long and he grows weary."
"8459","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Have you not seen how Allah diverts from me the curse and reviling of Quraysh? They revile Mudhammam, while I am Muhammad."
"8460","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ajlan, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two will not gather in the Fire in a gathering that harms one of them: a Muslim who killed a disbeliever, then the Muslim remained upright or close to upright; dust in the cause of Allah and the smoke of Hell will not gather in a servant, nor will faith and miserliness gather in the heart of a servant."
"8461","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu al-Zinad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Two women went out with two boys, and the wolf attacked one of them. They disputed over the remaining boy and brought their dispute to Dawud, who judged him to belong to the elder of them. They passed by Sulayman the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: How did he judge for you? They told him the story. He said: Bring me a knife to cut the boy between you. The younger said: Would you cut him? He said: Yes. She said: Do not do it; my share is hers. He said: He is your son, and judged him to her."
"8462","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: I say nothing but the truth. One of his companions said: You jest with us, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I say nothing but the truth."
"8463","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Muhammad, from his father and others, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The most numerous will be the lowest on the Day of Resurrection, except one who says like this and like this."
"8464","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Muhammad, from his father al-Ajlan, from Abu Hurayrah that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which people are best? He said: I and those with me, then those upon their trail, then those upon their trail; then it was as if he rejected those who remain."
"8465","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Muhammad, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: There will never cease to be a party upon this affair, upon the truth; those who oppose them will not harm them until the command of Allah comes to them while they are upon that."
"8466","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Muhammad, from al-Qaqa, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: In one wing of the fly is disease and in the other is cure; when it falls into the vessel of one of you, let him submerge it, for it guards itself with the one carrying disease, then let him remove it."
"8467","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The best of the rows of men is the first, and the worst of them is the last; and the best of the rows of women is the last, and the worst of them is the first."
"8468","Yunus and Hajjaj narrated to us, both said: Layth narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Said narrated to me, from Abu Ubaydah, from Said ibn Yasar, that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you performs ablution, perfecting and completing it, then comes to the mosque intending only prayer therein, except that Allah the Exalted rejoices with him as the family of an absent one rejoices at his appearance."
"8469","Yunus narrated to us, from Layth, Said narrated to me, from his brother Abbad ibn Abi Said, that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from four: from knowledge that does not benefit, from a heart that does not humble itself, from a soul that is never sated, and from a supplication that is not heard."
"8470","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Said narrated to me, from his father, that Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim woman to travel a night's journey except with a man who is unmarriageable to her."
"8471","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: There is no god but Allah alone; He honored His troops, aided His servant, and defeated the confederates alone; there is nothing after Him."
"8472","Yunus and Hajjaj narrated to us, both said: Layth narrated to us - Hajjaj said in his hadith: Said ibn Abi Said narrated to me - from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and Yunus said: from Said, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prophet among the prophets except that he was given signs of such kind that men believed thereby; what I have been given is revelation which Allah the Exalted revealed to me, and I hope to be the one with the most followers on the Day of Resurrection."
"8473","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Had, from Amr, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah the Exalted says: My believing servant is with Me in the station of all good; he praises Me while I draw his soul from between his sides."
"8474","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: By Allah, I seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him in the day more than seventy times."
"8475","Abu Said, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Abbad ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from al-Hasan al-Basri, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever listens to a verse from the Book of Allah the Exalted, a multiplied good deed is written for him, and whoever recites it, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"8476","Abu Said narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Isl ibn Sufyan narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the star rises in the morning, blight is lifted."
"8477","Abu Said narrated to us, Wuhayb and Hammad narrated to us, from Isl, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade as-sadl, meaning in prayer."
"8478","Abu Said narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah who said: Part of the talbiyah of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: At Your service, God of truth."
"8479","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A Muslim man passed by a stump of thorns on the road and said: I shall surely remove these thorns from the road lest they injure a Muslim man; he was forgiven."
"8480","He said: Affan narrated it to us with this chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you eats, let him lick his fingers, for he does not know in which of them the blessing lies."
"8481","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When Allah loves a servant, He calls Jibril, peace be upon him, and says: I have loved so-and-so, so love him. Jibril loves him, then calls out in heaven: Allah has loved so-and-so, so love him. They love him, then Allah places acceptance for him on earth; and when He hates, it is likewise."
"8482","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Today there has been opened of the barrier of Yajuj and Majuj like this - and Wuhayb made a circle of ninety."
"8483","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musab ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abu Salih as-Samman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The imam is only to be followed; when he says the takbir, say the takbir, and do not say it until he says it; when he bows, bow, and do not bow until he bows; when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: Our Lord, and to You is praise; when he prostrates, prostrate, and do not prostrate until he prostrates; and if he prays sitting, pray sitting all together."
"8484","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: We are the last, the foremost on the Day of Resurrection, except that every nation was given the Book before us and we were given it after them. This is the day in which they differed, and Allah the Exalted guided us to it: tomorrow is for the Jews and the day after tomorrow for the Christians. Then he fell silent and said: It is Allah's due upon every Muslim to wash every seven days, washing his head and his body."
"8485","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the most false of speech; do not spy, do not eavesdrop, do not hate one another, do not turn away from one another, do not compete against one another, and be servants of Allah, brothers."
"8486","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever obeys the commander has obeyed me."
"8487","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid, meaning Ibn Ziyad, narrated to us, Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah mention the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The dream of the Muslim man is a part of seventy parts of prophethood."
"8488","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best prayer after the obligatory is prayer in the depth of the night, and the best fasting after the month of Ramadan is the month of Allah which you call al-Muharram."
"8489","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, my father narrated to me that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has truly seen me, for Satan does not take my likeness. Asim said: My father said: Ibn Abbas narrated it to me, and I told him I had seen him. He said: Did you see him? I said: Yes, by Allah, I saw him. He said: Then I mentioned al-Hasan ibn Ali. He said: By Allah, I described him and his gait. Ibn Abbas said: He resembled him."
"8490","Affan narrated to us, Hammad informed us, Suhayl ibn Abi Salih informed us, he said: I was sitting with my father, and a boy was with him. The boy stood, and I sat in the boy's seat. My father said to me: Stand from his seat; Abu Hurayrah informed us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you stands from his seat then returns to it, he has more right to it - except that Suhayl said: When he made me stand, I felt small in myself."
"8491","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Ajlan Abu Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The slave is entitled to his food and clothing, and he is not burdened with work beyond his capacity."
"8492","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Drought is not that there is no rain, but drought is that the sky rains and the earth does not produce."
"8493","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Safwan, meaning Ibn Sulaym, from al-Qaqa ibn al-Lajlaj, from Abu Hurayrah, and Suhayl, from al-Qaqa ibn al-Lajlaj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Miserliness and faith do not gather in the heart of a man, nor do dust in the cause of Allah and the smoke of Hell gather upon a servant - Hammad said: One of them said al-Qaqa ibn al-Lajlaj, and the other said al-Lajlaj ibn al-Qaqa."
"8494","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If there is good in any of what you treat yourselves with, it is in cupping."
"8495","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man says: The people have perished, he is the most perished of them."
"8496","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said, who is Abu Hayyan at-Taymi, narrated to us, from Abu Zurah, from Abu Hurayrah, that a Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a deed which, if I do it, I shall enter Paradise. He said: Worship Allah without associating anything with Him, establish the prescribed prayer, pay the obligatory zakat, and fast Ramadan. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is Muhammad's soul, I shall never add anything to this nor detract from it. When he turned away, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to look at a man of the people of Paradise, let him look at this one."
"8497","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Salih ibn Abi Salih as-Samman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one endures the hardship and strain of Madinah except that I shall be for him an intercessor or a witness on the Day of Resurrection."
"8498","Affan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is this black seed, for in it is healing from everything."
"8499","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Kulayb informed us, my father narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every sermon without testimony is like the leprous hand."
"8500","Affan narrated to us, Aban al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd ar-Rahman narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer feels jealousy, and Allah feels jealousy, and part of Allah's jealousy is that the believer commits what Allah has forbidden."
"8501","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was a tree that harmed the people on the road, so a man cut it and removed it from the road, so he entered Paradise."
"8502","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The poor Muslims will enter Paradise before their rich by half a day, and it is five hundred years."
"8503","Affan narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd: One who heard Abu Hurayrah narrated to me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O son of Adam, act as if you are seen, and count yourself among the dead, and beware the supplication of the oppressed."
"8504","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Aws ibn Khalid, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels on Friday are at the doors of the mosques, writing the people according to their stations: So-and-so came at such-and-such hour, so-and-so came at such-and-such hour, so-and-so came while the imam was delivering the sermon, so-and-so came and caught the prayer but did not catch the Friday prayer if he did not catch the sermon."
"8505","Affan narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The people of Paradise will enter Paradise hairless, white, curly-haired, with kohl on their eyes, aged thirty-three, upon the creation of Adam, seventy cubits by seven cubits."
"8506","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qays and Habib, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said: In every prayer there is recitation; whatever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made audible to us we made audible to you, and whatever he concealed from us we concealed from you."
"8507","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Abi Salih reported to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every son of Adam has a share of adultery: the two eyes commit adultery and their adultery is looking, the two hands commit adultery and their adultery is seizing, the two feet commit adultery and their adultery is walking, the mouth commits adultery and its adultery is kissing, the heart inclines and wishes, and the private part confirms that or denies it."
"8508","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that a Jewish funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he stood up, so it was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, it is the funeral of a Jew. He said: Death has a fright."
"8509","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The angels do not accompany a party in which there is a dog or a bell."
"8510","Affan narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none among you whom his deed will save. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even me, unless Allah covers me from Him with mercy."
"8511","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw in what the sleeper sees as if in my hand were two bracelets, so I blew on them and they were lifted, and I interpreted that one of them is Musaylimah. [source text ends here without mentioning the second]"
"8512","Affan said: Wuhayb reported to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you sleeps at night while grease is on his hand and something befalls him, let him blame no one but himself."
"8513","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Mukhallad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, does not look at a man who has intercourse with his wife in her anus."
"8514","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will bridle him with a bridle of fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"8515","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best fasting after Ramadan is the month of Allah, al-Muharram, and the best prayer after the obligatory or prescribed prayer is the night prayer."
"8516","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abu al-Zinad, from Ibn Hurmuz, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire enter the Fire, a caller will call: O people of Paradise, eternity with no death in it, and O people of the Fire, eternity with no death in it. He said: And Khalid ibn Zayd mentioned to me that he heard Abu al-Zubayr mention the like of it from Jabir and Ubayd ibn Umayr, except that he narrates from them that that is after the intercessions and those who are brought out of the Fire."
"8517","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Uthman ibn Abi Sawdah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Muslim visits his brother or calls upon him, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says: You are pure and your walk is pure, and you have taken an abode in Paradise."
"8518","Affan narrated to us, Hammad reported to us, Thabit reported to us, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the slave obeys his Lord and his master, he has two rewards. He said: So when Abu Rafi was freed he wept, and it was said to him: What makes you weep? He said: I had two rewards, then one of them has gone."
"8519","Affan narrated to us, Hammad reported to us, Thabit reported to us, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels of the night and the angels of the day gather at the Fajr prayer and the Asr prayer; when the angels of the day ascend, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says to them: From where have you come? They say: We came to You from Your servants; we came to them while they were praying and we came to You while they were praying. And when the angels of the night ascend, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says to them: From where have you come? They say: We came to You from Your servants; we came to them while they were praying and we came to You while they were praying."
"8520","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Thabit reported to us, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two eyes commit adultery, the two hands commit adultery, and the private part confirms that or denies it."
"8521","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, that Abu Husayn narrated to him, that Dhakwan narrated to him, that Abu Hurayrah narrated to him, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me a deed that equals jihad. He said: I cannot find it. He said: Can you, when the warrior goes out, enter a mosque and stand without slackening and fast without breaking? He said: I cannot. He said: Abu Hurayrah said: The horse of the warrior prances in its tether, and good deeds are written for him."
"8522","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: My grandfather through my mother, Abu Habibah, narrated to me that he entered the house while Uthman was besieged in it, and that he heard Abu Hurayrah asking Uthman for permission to speak, so he gave him permission. He stood, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: You will meet after me trial and dissension, or he said dissension and trial. A man among the people said to him: Then who is there for us, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Upon you is the trustworthy one and his companions, while he was pointing to Uthman by that."
"8523","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Yunus reported to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Each man among the people of Paradise has two wives from the wide-eyed maidens; upon each one are seventy robes, the marrow of her shin seen from behind the garments."
"8524","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man following a pigeon and said: A devil following a she-devil."
"8525","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Said ibn Kathir ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and they establish the prayer and give the zakat; then their blood and their wealth have become forbidden to me, and their reckoning is upon Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"8526","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Abu al-Jallas Uqbah ibn Yasar narrated to us, Uthman ibn Shammakh narrated to me, he said: I witnessed Marwan ask Abu Hurayrah how he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray over the funeral. He said: With what I said. He said: Yes. He said: O Allah, You are its Lord, You created it, You guided it to Islam, You took its soul, and You know best its secret and its open; we have come as intercessors, so forgive it."
"8527","Affan narrated to us, Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: I heard my father, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Beware of continuous fasting, twice. They said: But you fast continuously, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I am not like you in that; I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink, so do not burden yourselves with deeds for which you have no strength."
"8528","Affan narrated to us, Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrate from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever keeps a dog that is not a dog for crops, hunting, or livestock, a qirat is deducted from his reward every day. Sulaym said: And I think he said: And the qirat is like Uhud."
"8529","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Farqad narrated to us, from Yazid the brother of Mutarrif, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Among the most lying of people, or the most lying of people, are the dyers and the goldsmiths. And Affan once said: Among the most lying."
"8530","Affan narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Does a man pray in a single garment? He said: Do all of you find two garments?"
"8531","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: And Hammad narrated to us, he said: I heard Thabit, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fasting person has two joys: a joy in this world at his breaking the fast, and a joy in the Hereafter."
"8532","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Isl ibn Sufyan al-Tamimi informed us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade letting the garment hang down in prayer."
"8533","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Khuthaym, meaning Ibn Irak, narrated to us, from his father, that Abu Hurayrah came to Medina with a group of his people while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at Khaybar, and he had left Siba ibn Urfutah in charge of Medina. He said: I reached him while he was reciting in the Fajr prayer in the first rakah Kaf-Ha-Ya-Ayn-Sad and in the second Woe to the defrauders. He said: I said to myself: Woe to so-and-so, when he measures for himself he takes in full, and when he measures for others he gives short. He said: When he prayed he provisioned us with something until we came to Khaybar, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had already conquered Khaybar. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke to the Muslims, and they shared with us in their portions."
"8534","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Seek refuge with Allah from the evil of the settled neighbor, for the traveling neighbor, if he wishes to be removed, is removed."
"8535","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning His saying to His messenger: Ask him what is the case of the women who cut their hands. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I been there I would have hastened the answer and would not have sought the excuse."
"8536","Affan narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had ten of the rabbis of the Jews believed in me, every Jew on the face of the earth would have believed in me."
"8537","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Amir, he said: Shurayh ibn Hani said: While I was in the mosque of Medina, Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No man loves meeting Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, but Allah loves meeting him, and no man hates meeting Allah but Allah hates meeting him. So I went to Aishah and said: If what Abu Hurayrah mentioned from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is true, we have perished. She said: The perished is only one who perishes in what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said; and what is that? He said: He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No man loves meeting Allah but Allah loves meeting him, and no man hates meeting Allah but Allah hates meeting him. She said: And I bear witness that I heard him say that; but do you know why that is? When the chest rattles, the sight stares, the skin shudders, and the fingers contract, then at that moment whoever loves meeting Allah, Allah loves meeting him, and whoever hates meeting Allah, Allah hates meeting him."
"8538","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: May his nose be humbled, may his nose be humbled, may his nose be humbled: a man who reaches his parents, one of them or both, with old age at his side, and they do not admit him into Paradise."
"8539","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abd Allah al-Awdi, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, or Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should urinate in standing water and then wash from it."
"8540","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr reported to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Euphrates is about to recede from a mountain of gold over which the people will fight until nine out of every ten are killed and one remains."
"8541","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a rabbit he had roasted, along with its gravy and condiments, and placed it before him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) withheld and did not eat, and ordered his companions to eat, while the Bedouin withheld. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What prevents you from eating? He said: I fast three days of the month. He said: If you are fasting, then fast the bright days."
"8542","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Abi Salih reported to me, he said: I went out with my father to Sham, and the people of Sham would pass by the people of the hermitages and greet them. I heard my father say: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not initiate them with the greeting, and force them to its narrowest."
"8543","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qays, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no child born except upon the natural disposition, until his two parents are the ones who make him Jewish and make him Christian, just as you produce your cattle: are there among them any with slit ears, until you yourselves slit them? A man said: And where are they? He said: Allah knows best what they would have done. Qays said: I do not think that man was anything but a Qadari."
"8544","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He hears the thud of their sandals when they turn away."
"8545","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A woman should not travel a journey of three days except with a close relative."
"8546","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man freed a portion of a slave, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) validated his freeing and charged him with the remainder of his price."
"8547","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever finds his goods intact with a bankrupt person, he has the most right to them."
"8548","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Yasar said to me: What do you say about the life-grant? I said: Al-Nadr ibn Anas narrated to us, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The life-grant is valid."
"8549","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has two wives and inclines to one of them over the other will come on the Day of Resurrection with one of his sides fallen."
"8550","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There rained, or fell, upon Ayyub locusts of gold, so he began to gather them, so Allah revealed to him: O Ayyub, did I not make ample provision for you? He said: Yes, but I have no independence from Your bounty."
"8551","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays, meaning one rakah of the Fajr prayer, then the sun rises, let him pray another to it."
"8552","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, Abu Hazim narrated to me, that Abu Hurayrah said: The changed breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter, or he said more beloved, to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, than the scent of musk."
"8553","He said, and I think he said: At the right of the Throne is a caller calling in the seventh heaven: Give a spender a replacement, and give, or hasten, to a withholder a loss. [fragmentary continuation without its own chain in source]"
"8554","He said, and Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the earnings of the cupper and the earnings of the slave-girl. [fragmentary continuation without its own chain in source]"
"8555","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Wasi narrated to us, from a man called Maruf, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: My close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined me not to sleep except upon witr."
"8556","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Ayyub al-Ataki, and he is Yahya ibn Malik, and Affan once said: Abu Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you fights, let him avoid the face."
"8557","Affan narrated to us, Hammam and Aban said: Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When he sits between her four parts and exerts himself, the bath has become obligatory, whether he ejaculates or not."
"8558","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not precede Ramadan by fasting a day or two days, except a man whose fasting it was, then let him fast."
"8559","He said, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever stands the Night of Decree in faith and seeking reward will be forgiven what preceded of his sin. Affan said: And Aban narrated to us in this chain the like of it. [fragmentary continuation without its own chain in source]"
"8560","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Amir, meaning al-Ahwal, narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution: he rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water three times, washed his face three times, washed his hands three times, wiped his head, and washed his feet."
"8561","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Uthman, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"8562","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A woman does not desert her husband's bed except that the angels of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, curse her."
"8563","Affan narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Jafar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are best? He said: Faith in which there is no doubt, a campaign in which there is no misappropriation, and an accepted Hajj. And Abu Hurayrah used to say: And an accepted Hajj expiates the sins of that year."
"8564","Affan narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Three supplications are answered, about which there is no doubt: the supplication of the oppressed, the supplication of the traveler, and the supplication of the father against his child."
"8565","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said, meaning Ibn Abi Arubah, narrated to us, from Isl, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade letting the garment hang down."
"8566","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the death of the Negus reached him, prayed over him, and they formed rows behind him, and he said takbir over him four times."
"8567","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ata narrated to me that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: Delay the prayer for coolness, for the intensity of heat is from the blast of Hell."
"8568","In every prayer there is recitation; whatever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made audible to us we made audible to you, and whatever he concealed from us we concealed from you. [without chain in source]"
"8569","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever catches a rakah of the Fajr prayer before the sun rises has caught it, and whoever catches a rakah or two rakahs of the Asr prayer before the sun sets has caught it."
"8570","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes from his sleep, let him pour over his hands from his vessel three times."
"8571","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Rabiah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he mentioned that a man from the Children of Israel asked one of the Children of Israel to lend him a thousand dinars. He said: Bring me witnesses to witness them. He said: Allah suffices as a witness. He said: Bring me a guarantor. He said: Allah suffices as a guarantor. He said: You spoke the truth. So he paid it to him for a named term. He went out on the sea and fulfilled his need, then sought a ship to come upon for the term he had set, but found no ship. He took a piece of wood, hollowed it, put into it a thousand dinars and a note with it to its owner, then sealed its place, then brought it to the sea and said: O Allah, You know that I borrowed from so-and-so a thousand dinars, and he asked me for a guarantor and I said Allah suffices as a guarantor, and he was pleased with You, and he asked me for a witness and I said Allah suffices as a witness, and he was pleased with You, and I strove to find a ship to send to him what is his but found no ship, and I entrust it to You. He threw it into the sea until it entered it, then turned away looking, while seeking a ship to go out to his land. The man who had lent him went out looking, hoping a ship would come with his wealth, and there was the piece of wood in which was the wealth, so he took it for his household as firewood. When he broke it he found the wealth and the note. Then the man who had borrowed from him came, bringing a thousand dinars, and said: By Allah, I kept striving in seeking a ship to bring you your wealth, but found no ship before the one I came in. He said: Did you send anything to me? He said: Did I not tell you that I found no ship before this one I came in? He said: Allah has discharged on your behalf what you sent in the piece of wood, so go away with your thousand rightly guided."
"8572","Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Aswad say: Abu Abd Allah, the freedman of Shaddad, reported to me that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever hears a man calling out for a lost item in the mosque, let him say to him: May Allah not return it to you, for the mosques were not built for this."
"8573","Abd Allah ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi narrated to us in Mecca, al-Dahhak, meaning Ibn Uthman, narrated to me, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said to Marwan: You have permitted the sale of usury. Marwan said: I did not do it. Abu Hurayrah said: You have permitted the sale of vouchers, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of food until it is taken in full. He said: Marwan addressed the people and forbade its sale. Sulayman said: I looked at the guards of Marwan taking them from the hands of the people."
"8574","Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Numan, meaning Ibn Rashid al-Jazari, reported to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand and drink with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left and drinks with his left."
"8575","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr, meaning Ibn al-Harith, reported to me, Abu Yunus Sulaym ibn Jubayr, the freedman of Abu Hurayrah, reported to us, narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Were it not for Hawwa, no female would ever betray her husband."
"8576","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn al-Nadr, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The countrysides will be opened, so people will come to their acquaintances and go away with them, while Medina is better for them had they known. He said it twice."
"8577","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith and disbelief do not gather in the heart of a person, truthfulness and lying do not gather together, and betrayal and trustworthiness do not gather together."
"8578","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abd Rabbih ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None enters the Fire except the wretched. It was said: And who is the wretched? He said: The one who does not act in obedience and does not leave disobedience for Allah."
"8579","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr, meaning Ibn al-Harith, reported to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, that Sulayman ibn Yasar narrated to him that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I would not love that this Uhud of yours be gold with me, spending from it every day, then three pass by me while I have anything of it left, except something I reserve for a debt."
"8580","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Salman ibn Amir narrated to us, from Abu Uthman al-Asbahi, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be in my nation impostors, liars, narrating to you innovations of speech you never heard, you nor your fathers; beware of them and them, let them not mislead you."
"8581","Hasan narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu Yunus Sulaym ibn Jubayr, the freedman of Abu Hurayrah, narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Were it not for Hawwa, no female would betray her husband."
"8582","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman al-Araj narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every son of Adam has inevitably committed adultery: the eye, its adultery is looking, the hand, its adultery is touching, the soul desires and speaks, and the private part confirms that or denies it."
"8583","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman al-Araj narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until the sun rises from the west; when the sun rises from the west, all the people will believe, and that is when no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good in its faith."
"8584","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman al-Araj narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Burden yourselves with deeds you can bear, for the best deed is the most lasting, even if little."
"8585","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman al-Araj narrated to us, I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O sons of Abd al-Muttalib, ransom yourselves from Allah; O Umm al-Zubayr, aunt of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and O Fatimah daughter of Muhammad, ransom yourselves from Allah, for I own nothing for you from Allah; ask me what you wish; O sons of Abd Manaf, ransom yourselves from Allah."
"8586","And with his chain from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man from the Children of Israel said: I will surely give charity tonight with my wealth. He went out with it and placed it in the hand of an adulteress. In the morning the people talked: Charity was given to so-and-so the adulteress. Then he went out with wealth and said again, and placed it in the hand of a thief. In the morning the people of the city talked: Charity was given to so-and-so the thief. He went out with wealth again and placed it in the hand of a rich man. He said: If I wished I would say he did not know where he placed it. The man returned to himself, and he was shown in a dream that your charity has been accepted: as for the adulteress, perhaps she will abstain from her adultery, as for the thief, perhaps it will suffice him from stealing, and as for the rich, perhaps he will take heed regarding his wealth."
"8587","Hasan narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu Sakhr narrated to us, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever enters this mosque of ours to learn good or to teach it is like the warrior in the path of Allah, and whoever enters it for other than that is like one looking at what is not his."
"8588","Hasan narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu Yunus Sulaym ibn Jubayr, the freedman of Abu Hurayrah, narrated to us, that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: I never saw anything more handsome than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); it was as if the sun ran in his forehead, and I never saw anyone faster in his walk than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as if the earth were folded for him; we exert ourselves and he is unconcerned."
"8589","And from him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Give the worker from his work, for the worker of Allah does not fail. [fragmentary continuation without its own chain in source]"
"8590","And with his chain from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: May Allah have mercy on Lut, for he used to resort to a strong pillar. [fragmentary continuation without its own chain in source]"
"8591","And with his chain from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Would one of you rejoice to return to his family with two pregnant camels? They said: Yes. He said: Then two verses from the Book of Allah with which he goes out to his family are better for him than two pregnant camels. [fragmentary continuation without its own chain in source]"
"8592","And with his chain from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: None of you should wish for death nor supplicate for it before it comes to him, unless he is confident of his deeds, for when one of you dies his deed is cut off from him, and his age does not increase the believer except in good. [fragmentary continuation without its own chain in source]"
"8593","And with his chain from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Every soul has charity written upon it every day the sun rises in it; among that is that judging justly between two is charity, helping a man with his mount by mounting him upon it is charity, lifting his goods upon it is charity, removing harm from the road is charity, the good word is charity, and every step he walks to prayer is charity. [fragmentary continuation without its own chain in source]"
"8594","And with his chain from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, no one of this nation, Jew or Christian, hears of me then dies without believing in what I was sent with except that he is among the companions of the Fire. [fragmentary continuation without its own chain in source]"
"8595","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: My servant belied Me, though he had no right to belie Me, and My servant insulted Me, though he had no right to insult Me. As for his belying Me, he says: He will not return me as He began me, while the last creation being returned is not harder upon Me than its first; he has belied Me if he says it. As for his insulting Me, he says: Allah has taken a son; I am Allah, the One, the Eternal; I did not beget. [source text ends abruptly here]"
"8596","Hasan and Yahya ibn Ishaq said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you applies kohl, let him apply it an odd number of times, and when he cleans himself with stones, let him do so an odd number of times."
"8597","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you applies kohl, let him apply it an odd number of times."
"8598","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When three are together, two should not whisper apart from the third."
"8599","And with his chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of my nation will enter Paradise without reckoning. Ukkashah ibn Mihsan said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me among them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make him among them. Then another said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me among them. He said: Ukkashah has already preceded you to it. [fragmentary continuation without its own chain in source]"
"8600","And with his chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How good a people are al-Azd: pure their mouths, dutiful their oaths, clean their hearts. [fragmentary continuation without its own chain in source]"
"8601","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Abu Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Hurayra: My father said: He did not raise it [to the Prophet]. He said: The Angel of Death came to Musa and said: Answer your Lord. So Musa, peace be upon him, slapped the eye of the Angel of Death and gouged it out. So the angel returned to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and said: You sent me to a servant of Yours who does not want death, and he has gouged out my eye. He said: So Allah restored his eye to him and said: Return to My servant and say to him: Do you want life? If you want life, then place your hand on the back of a bull, and for every hair your hand covers you will live a year for it. He said: Then what? He said: Then death. He said: Then now, O Lord, from near."
"8602","Surayj narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqama, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever hoards a hoard seeking to raise prices thereby against the Muslims, then he is a wrongdoer."
"8603","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: And Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed me, from Abdurrahman ibn Mihran, from Abdurrahman ibn Sa'd, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The farther, then the farther, is greater in reward with respect to the mosque."
"8604","Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from Sa'id ibn Sam'an, that he heard Abu Hurayra informing Abu Qatada that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allegiance will be given to a man between the Corner and the Maqam, and this House will not be violated except by its own people. Then when they violate it, do not ask about the destruction of the Arabs. Then the Abyssinians will come and destroy it with a destruction after which it will never be rebuilt, and they are the ones who will extract its treasure."
"8605","Surayj, meaning Ibn an-Nu'man, narrated to us, and Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Abu Wahb, the freed slave of Abu Hurayra, from Abu Hurayra, he said: Wine was forbidden three times. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madina while they were drinking wine and consuming gambling. So they asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about them, so Allah sent down upon His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): They ask you about wine and gambling. Say: In them is great sin and benefits for people, and their sin is greater than their benefit, to the end of the verse. So the people said: It has not been forbidden to us; He only said: In them is great sin. And they continued drinking wine until one day a man from the Emigrants led his companions in Maghrib prayer and confused his recitation, so Allah sent down concerning it a verse more severe than it: O you who believe, do not approach prayer while you are intoxicated until you know what you say. And the people continued drinking until one of them would come to prayer while sober. Then a verse more severe than that was sent down: O you who believe, wine and gambling and idols and divining arrows are filth from the work of Satan, so avoid them that you may prosper. So they said: We have desisted, our Lord. Then the people said: O Messenger of Allah, people were killed in the cause of Allah or died on their beds while they used to drink wine and consume gambling, though Allah has made it filth and from the work of Satan. So Allah sent down: There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they tasted, when they fear Allah and believe, to the end of the verse. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had it been forbidden to them, they would have left it as you have left it."
"8606","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Rafi', from Abu Hurayra, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever reaches Ramadan while owing something from Ramadan that he has not made up, it will not be accepted from him. And whoever fasts voluntarily while owing something from Ramadan that he has not made up, it will not be accepted from him until he fasts it."
"8607","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Ibn al-Had narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Isa ibn Talha ibn Ubaydullah, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you performs ablution, let him blow his nose, for Satan spends the night on his nasal passages."
"8608","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Ayyash ibn Abbas al-Qitbani narrated to us, from Abu Tamim az-Zuhri, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the one that has been established."
"8609","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, and Abdullah said: And I heard it myself from Harun, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj narrated to him that Ali ibn Khalid ad-Du'ali narrated to him that an-Nadr ibn Sufyan ad-Du'ali narrated to him that he heard Abu Hurayra saying: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Tala'at al-Yaman, and Bilal stood to call, then when he fell silent, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says the like of what this one said, with certainty, will enter Paradise."
"8610","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub, from Nafi' ibn Sulayman, from Abdurrahman ibn Mihran, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who waits for prayer after prayer is like a horseman whose horse gallops with him in the cause of Allah on his flank; the angels of Allah pray upon him so long as he does not break his ablution or stand up, and he is in the greater guarding of the frontiers."
"8611","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Muthanna ibn as-Sabbah, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayra, he said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: We are in this sand and we do not find water, and among us are the menstruating, the ritually impure, and the postpartum, and four months may pass without finding water. He said: Upon you is dust, meaning tayammum."
"8612","Azhar ibn al-Qasim ar-Rasibi narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Abi Ali, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Woe to the rulers, woe to the headmen, woe to the trustees. Peoples will wish on the Day of Resurrection that their forelocks had been suspended from the Pleiades, dangling between heaven and earth, and that they had not been in charge of anything."
"8613","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from al-Muhajir, from Abu al-Aliya, from Abu Hurayra, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day with some dates, and I said: Supplicate Allah for me for blessing in them. He said: So he spread them before him, then he supplicated, then he said to me: Put them in a provision bag, and put in your hand but do not scatter them. He said: So I carried from it such and such wasqs in the cause of Allah, and we ate and fed others, and it never left my waist. Then when Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed, it was cut from my waist and fell."
"8614","Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna Abu Umar narrated to us, Abdulaziz ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Salama al-Majishun narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl, from Abdurrahman al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayra, he said: Among the talbiya of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Labbayk, God of truth."
"8615","Hujayn Abu Umar narrated to us, and Abdulaziz narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Udhayn, from Makhul, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The servant does not believe with complete faith until he leaves lying in jest and leaves argumentation even if he is truthful."
"8616","Hujayn Abu Umar narrated to us, Abdulaziz narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Abu Salih as-Samman, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to Allah. Then when he says: Praise be to Allah, his brother says to him: May Allah have mercy on you. Then when it is said to him: May Allah have mercy on you, let him say: May Allah guide you and set right your affairs."
"8617","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrima, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking from the mouth of the waterskin."
"8618","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Farrukh al-Jurayri, he said: I heard Abu Uthman an-Nahdi saying: I was a guest of Abu Hurayra for seven days, and he and his wife and his servant would take turns in the night in thirds: this one would pray then wake this one, and this one would pray then sleep and wake this one. He said: I said: O Abu Hurayra, how do you fast? He said: As for me, I fast three days from the beginning of the month, and if something happens to me, then my fasting is at the end of my month. He said: And I heard Abu Hurayra saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once distributed dates among his companions, and I received seven dates, one of them dry, and there was nothing among them more pleasing to me than it, for it strengthened my molars."
"8619","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayra, that a black woman or a man used to sweep the mosque, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed him and asked about him, and they said: He died. So he said: Why did you not inform me of him? They said: It was at night. He said: Then he said: Show me his grave. So they showed him, and he came to his grave and prayed over him."
"8620","Yunus narrated to us, Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Sa'd, narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Our stopping place tomorrow, if Allah wills, is at Khayf Bani Kinana, where they swore together upon disbelief."
"8621","Abdulwahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, that Fatima came to Abu Bakr and Umar seeking her inheritance from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they said to her: We heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I am not to be inherited from."
"8622","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A believer who kills a disbeliever and then remains upright will not be gathered together in the Fire in a gathering that harms."
"8623","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will bridle him with a bridle of fire."
"8624","Hasan and Affan said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Aws ibn Khalid, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of one who sits and hears wisdom and then narrates from its owner only the worst of what he heard is like a man who comes to a shepherd and says: O shepherd, slaughter for me a sheep from your flock. He says: Go and take the best of them by its ear. So he goes and takes the sheepdog by its ear."
"8625","Hasan and Affan, with the same meaning, said: Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, and Affan said: Hammad narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abu as-Salt, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw on the night I was taken by night, when we reached the seventh heaven, and I looked above - Affan said: above me - and there was thunder and lightning and thunderbolts. He said: Then I came upon people whose bellies were like houses, in them snakes seen from outside their bellies. I said: Who are these, O Jibril? He said: These are the consumers of usury. Then when I descended to the lowest heaven, I looked below me and there was dust and smoke and voices. So I said: What is this, O Jibril? He said: These are the devils hovering over the eyes of the sons of Adam so that they do not reflect upon the kingdom of the heavens and the earth; were it not for that, they would see wonders."
"8626","Hasan ibn Musa and Abu Kamil said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqama, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two sons of al-As are believers, meaning Hisham and Amr."
"8627","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two sons of al-As are believers."
"8628","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talha, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from poverty and lack and humiliation, and I seek refuge in You from wronging or being wronged."
"8629","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of the rows of men is the foremost, and the worst of the rows of men is the last. And the best of the rows of women is the last, and the worst of the rows of women is the foremost."
"8630","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdala, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hospitality is three days, and what is beyond that is charity."
"8631","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Abu Musa has indeed been given the flutes of Dawud."
"8632","Hasan ibn Musa and Affan said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Aws, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection in three kinds: a kind walking, a kind riding, and a kind upon their faces. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, how will they walk upon their faces? He said: The One who made them walk upon their feet is able to make them walk upon their faces. Indeed they will shield with their faces every mound and thorn."
"8633","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqama, from Abu Salama ibn Abdirrahman, from Abu Hurayra, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created Paradise, He said: O Jibril, go and look at it. So he went and looked, then he said: O Lord, by Your might, no one will hear of it except that he will enter it. Then He surrounded it with hardships, then He said: Go and look at it. So he went and looked, then he said: O Lord, by Your might, I fear that no one will enter it. Then when He created the Fire, He said: O Jibril, go and look at it. So he went and looked at it, then he said: O Lord, by Your might, no one will hear of it and enter it. So He surrounded it with desires, then He said: O Jibril, go and look at it. So he went and looked at it, then he said: O Lord, by Your might, I fear that no one will remain except that he will enter it."
"8634","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in the morning: O Allah, by You we enter morning, and by You we enter evening, and by You we live, and by You we die, and to You is the return."
"8635","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ata ibn as-Sa'ib, from Salman al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and Humayd and Thabit al-Bunani and Salih ibn Zakwan, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - concerning what he narrates from his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, that He said: Whoever remembers Me in himself, I remember him in Myself. And whoever remembers Me in an assembly of people, I remember him in an assembly greater than them and better."
"8636","Hasan and Affan said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us - Affan said in his hadith: Abu Sinan narrated to us - from Uthman ibn Abi Sawda, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Muslim visits his brother or visits him - Hasan said: for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic - Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: You are pure, and your walking is pure, and you have taken a dwelling in Paradise - Affan said: a dwelling from Paradise - Hasan said: for the sake of Allah, and Affan did not say it."
"8637","Hasan and Ahmad ibn Abdulmalik said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you dress and when you perform ablution, then begin with your right sides. And Ahmad said: With your right sides."
"8638","Hasan narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayra, he said: Our food with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was only the two black things: dates and water. By Allah, we never saw this wheat of yours nor knew what it was. And our clothing with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was only striped garments, meaning the cloaks of the Bedouins."
"8639","Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, Kamil Abu al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih claimed, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek refuge in Allah from the head of seventy and the rule of boys."
"8640","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That the belly of one of you be filled with pus that festers is better for him than that it be filled with poetry."
"8641","Hasan narrated to us, Sukayn narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Khalid narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me, from Abu Hurayra, he said: I am indeed a witness to the delegation of Abdulqays when they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So he forbade them to drink in these vessels: the hantam, the dubba, the muzaffat, and the naqir. He said: Then a man from the people stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, people have no vessels. He said: So I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as if he felt pity for the people. He said: Then he said: Drink what is good for you, and when it becomes foul, then leave it."
"8642","Al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us, from Thumama, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the fly falls in the vessel of one of you, let him dip it, for in one of its wings is disease and in the other is cure. Hammad said: And Habib ibn ash-Shahid, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"8643","He said: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may speak a word, not seeing that it will reach where it reached, by which he falls into the Fire for seventy autumns."
"8644","Hasan narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah said: Whoever kills a gecko on the first strike, for him is such and such reward. And whoever kills it on the second, for him is such and such reward. And whoever kills it on the third, for him is such and such reward. Suhayl said: The first is the greatest."
"8645","Hasan narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Balj narrated to us, that Amr ibn Maymun narrated to him, he said: Abu Hurayra said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Hurayra, shall I not guide you to a word from the treasure of Paradise? He said: I said: Yes, may my father and mother be ransomed for you. He said: Say: There is no power except through Allah."
"8646","Hasan narrated to us, Abdurrahman ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is given wealth by Allah and does not pay its zakat, his wealth will be represented to him on the Day of Resurrection as a bald serpent with two spots, seizing his jaws on the Day of Resurrection, then saying: I am your wealth, I am your treasure. Then he recited this verse: Let not those who are miserly with what Allah has given them of His bounty, to the end of the verse."
"8647","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn Ayyash, narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seclude himself in every Ramadan for ten days. Then when it was the year in which he died, he secluded himself for twenty days."
"8648","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Abdurrahman ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar al-Madini narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They pray for you; if they are correct, then for you and for them, and if they err, then for you and against them."
"8649","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever I have forbidden you, then refrain from it. And whatever I have commanded you, then take from it what you are able."
"8650","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two kinds of the people of the Fire I do not yet see: women clothed yet naked, leaning and swaying, upon their heads like the humps of leaning Bactrian camels; they will not see Paradise nor find its scent. And men with whips like the tails of cows with which they beat people."
"8651","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Ibrahim Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a leaning wall and hastened his walk. So it was said to him, and he said: I dislike sudden death."
"8652","Aswad narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Ibrahim Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from dying of grief or sorrow, or dying by drowning, or that Satan strike me down at death, or that I die stung."
"8653","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The ajwa date is from Paradise, and it is a cure from poison. And the truffle is from manna, and its water is a cure for the eye."
"8654","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Abu al-Halbas, from Abu Hurayra, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The deprived is one who is deprived of the war booty of Kalb."
"8655","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed women who frequently visit graves."
"8656","Hisham ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the slave of one of you steals, then sell him, even for a nash."
"8657","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave the beards, and trim the mustaches, and change your white hair, and do not resemble the Jews and the Christians."
"8658","Aswad ibn Amir and Muhammad ibn Sabiq said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the closest of people to themselves. Whoever leaves property, then for the freed allies of his tribe. And whoever leaves debts or dependents, then I am his guardian, and none shall call for him."
"8659","And Aswad said with this chain: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is the fasting day of one of you, let him not speak obscenely nor act disobediently nor act ignorantly. Then if ignorance is shown to him, let him say: I am a fasting man."
"8660","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three, all of them a duty upon every Muslim: visiting the sick, attending the funeral, and blessing the sneezer when he praises Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"8661","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a informed us, and Ishaq ibn Isa said: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Lahi'a ibn Uqba, from Abu al-Ward - Ishaq said: al-Mazini - from Abu Hurayra, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Beware of piebald horses, for if they meet they flee, and if they gain spoils they misappropriate."
"8662","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'a informed us, from Abu Yunus, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you applies kohl, let him apply it an odd number of times. And when he cleans himself with stones, let him do so an odd number of times."
"8663","Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu Yunus, from Abu Hurayra, that a Bedouin raided with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Khaybar and received from its share two dinars. So the Bedouin took them and placed them in his cloak and stitched over them and wrapped them. Then the Bedouin died, and they found the two dinars, and they mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Two brandings."
"8664","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a informed us, al-A'raj narrated to us, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The takbir in the two Eids is seven before the recitation and five after the recitation."
"8665","Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a informed us, from Abu Yunus, from Abu Hurayra, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The sweat of the people of Paradise is musk, and their fuel is aloes. He said: I said to Ibn Lahi'a: O Abu Abdirrahman, what is aloes? He said: Fine Indian oud."
"8666","He said: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Aban, meaning Ibn Yazid al-Attar, narrated to us, from Qatada, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayra, that the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned truffles and said: They are the smallpox of the earth, and we do not see eating them as proper. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: The truffle is from manna, and its water is a cure for the eye. And the ajwa date is from Paradise, and it is a cure from poison."
"8667","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Isma'il, meaning Ibn Ja'far, narrated to us, he said: al-Ala informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - and Ubayy read to him the Mother of the Quran - and he said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, nothing like it has been sent down in the Torah nor in the Gospel nor in the Psalms nor in the Furqan. It is the Seven Oft-Repeated and the Mighty Quran which I have been given."
"8668","Sulayman narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ja'far informed us, Muhammad ibn Abi Harmala informed us, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu ad-Darda, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while narrating upon the pulpit: And for whoever fears the standing of his Lord are two gardens. So I said: Even if he commits adultery and steals, O Messenger of Allah? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said a second time: And for whoever fears the standing of his Lord are two gardens. So I said a second time: Even if he commits adultery and steals, O Messenger of Allah? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said a third time: And for whoever fears the standing of his Lord are two gardens. So I said a third time: Even if he commits adultery and steals, O Messenger of Allah? So he said: Yes, even if the nose of Abu ad-Darda is rubbed in dust."
"8669","Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Isma'il informed us, Abu Suhayl Nafi' ibn Malik ibn Abi Amir informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Ramadan comes, the gates of Paradise are opened, and the gates of the Fire are closed, and the devils are chained."
"8670","Sulayman narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, Abu Suhayl Nafi' ibn Malik ibn Abi Amir informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sign of the hypocrite is three: When he speaks he lies, and when he promises he breaks, and when he is trusted he betrays."
"8671","Sulayman narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to me, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no life-grant. So whoever is granted something for life, then it is his."
"8672","Sulayman narrated to us, Isma'il informed me, Muhammad informed me that he heard Abu Abdullah al-Qarraz shouting in the mosque, saying: Abu Hurayra informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever intends the people of Madina with evil, Allah will melt him as salt melts in water."
"8673","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three, all of them a duty upon every Muslim: visiting the sick, following funerals, and blessing the sneezer when he praises Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"8674","Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to me, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wishes, let him consider what he wishes, for he does not know what will be written for him of his wish."
"8675","Ishaq narrated to us, Abdurrahman ibn Zayd narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salih as-Samman, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts a day in the cause of Allah, Allah will distance him from Hell for seventy autumns."
"8676","Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ammar, the muezzin of the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to us, he said: I heard Sa'id al-Maqburi saying: I heard Abu Hurayra saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of earning is the earning of the hands of a worker when he is sincere."
"8677","Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, I heard Isma'il ibn Umayya narrating from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: Three, I am their opponent on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever I oppose, I defeat him: A man who gives by Me then betrays, and a man who sells a free man and consumes his price, and a man who hires a worker and takes his full due from him but does not fulfill his wage to him."
"8678","Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, he said: I asked Sulayman ibn Yasar about racing, so he said: Abu Salih narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayra, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no racing except in camel or hoof."
"8679","Ishaq informed us, Ibn Lahi'a informed us, from al-Hasan ibn Thawban, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he bade farewell to someone, said: I entrust to Allah your religion and your trust and the final outcomes of your deeds."
"8680","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr narrated to us, Aban, meaning Ibn Abdullah al-Bajali, narrated to us, a freed slave of Abu Hurayra narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayra saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution for me. So I brought him water for ablution, and he cleaned himself, then he put his hand in dust and wiped it, then washed it, then performed ablution and wiped over his khuffs. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, your feet, you did not wash them. He said: I entered them while they were pure."
"8681","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Imran, meaning Ibn Za'ida ibn Nashit, narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Khalid, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: O son of Adam, devote yourself to My worship, I will fill your chest with richness and close your poverty. And if you do not do so, I will fill your chest with busyness and not close your poverty."
"8682","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Kamil narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world will not end until it belongs to Luka' ibn Luka'."
"8683","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Kamil narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The wealthy, meaning they are the fewest, except one who says: thus and thus and thus."
"8684","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn Abi az-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayra, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The heart of the old man is young in love of two things: long life and abundance of wealth."
"8685","Husayn narrated to us, Ibn Abi az-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayra, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When Allah decreed creation, He wrote in a book, and it is with Him above the Throne: My mercy overcomes My anger."
"8686","Yunus narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Husayn, from Abdullah ibn Subayha, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of charity is the loaned milch animal; it goes in the morning with reward and returns with reward. And the loan of a camel is like the freeing of a red one, and the loan of a sheep is like the freeing of a black one."
"8687","Hujayn narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Yahya ibn Ja'da, from Abu Hurayra, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, which charity is best? He said: The effort of the poor, and begin with those you support."
"8688","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Drought is not that you are not rained upon, but drought is that you are rained upon and then rained upon, yet the earth grows nothing."
"8689","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has extra angels who follow the gatherings of remembrance. They gather at remembrance, and when they pass by a gathering, some of them rise above others until they reach the Throne. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says to them, and He knows best: From where have you come? So they say: From servants of Yours asking You for Paradise and seeking refuge in You from the Fire and seeking Your forgiveness. So He says: They ask Me for My Paradise; have they seen it? Then how if they had seen it? And they seek refuge from the fire of Hell; then how if they had seen it? For I have forgiven them. So they say: Our Lord, among them is Your sinful servant so-and-so who passed by them for a need of his and sat with them. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Those are companions by whom their sitter is not wretched."
"8690","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has traveling extra angels seeking the gatherings of remembrance. Then he mentioned the like of it."
"8691","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Salih, the freed slave of at-Taw'ama, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wrapped his izar, the muscle of his calf could be seen from beneath his izar."
"8692","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: I asked my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and He promised me to admit from my nation seventy thousand upon the image of the moon on the night of full moon. So I sought increase, and He increased me with every thousand seventy thousand. So I said: O Lord, if these are not the emigrants of my nation? He said: Then I will complete them for you from the Bedouins."
"8693","Sulayman ibn Dawud, meaning at-Tayalisi, narrated to us, Sadaqa ibn Musa as-Sulami ad-Daqiqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Wasi' narrated to us, from Shutayr ibn Nahar, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, said: Had My servants obeyed Me, I would have given them rain by night and brought the sun upon them by day, and would not have made them hear the sound of thunder."
"8694","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good opinion of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is part of the good worship of Allah."
"8695","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Renew your faith. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how do we renew our faith? He said: Increase in saying: There is no god but Allah."
"8696","Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship or remits for him, Allah will shade him in the shade of His Throne on the Day of Resurrection."
"8697","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Qurra ibn Abdirrahman, from az-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every speech or important matter not opened with the remembrance of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, then it is cut off. Or he said: Severed."
"8698","Abu Ja'far al-Mada'ini narrated to us, Abdussamad ibn Habib al-Azdi informed us, from his father Habib ibn Abdullah, from Shubayl ibn Awf, from Abu Hurayra, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to Thawban: How will you be, O Thawban, when the nations summon one another against you as you summon one another to a dish of food, taking from it? Thawban said: By my father and mother, O Messenger of Allah, is it from fewness in us? He said: No, you on that day are many, but weakness will be cast into your hearts. They said: And what is weakness, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Your love of the world and your hatred of fighting."
"8699","Abu Ja'far informed us, Abbad informed us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to accept the gift and not accept charity."
"8700","Abu Ja'far informed us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam informed us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The five prayers and Friday to Friday are expiations for what is between them, so long as major sins are avoided."
"8701","Abu Jafar narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Habib al-Azdi narrated to us, from his father Habib ibn Abd Allah, from Shubayl, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was fasting on the day of Ashura, and he said to his Companions: Whoever among you began the morning fasting, let him complete his fast, and whoever has partaken of his family morning meal, let him complete the rest of his day."
"8702","Abu Jafar narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, from his father, from Shubayl, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by some Jews who had fasted the day of Ashura, and he said: What is this fast? They said: This is the day in which Allah saved Musa and the Children of Israel from drowning, and drowned Pharaoh therein, and this is the day in which the Ark settled upon al-Judi, so Nuh and Musa fasted it in thanks to Allah the Exalted. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am more entitled to Musa and more entitled to fast this day, so he commanded his Companions to fast."
"8703","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, is pleased for you with three and dislikes for you three. He is pleased for you that you worship Him and do not associate anything with Him, and that you sincerely advise those whom Allah has placed in charge of your affairs, and that you hold fast all together to the rope of Allah and do not divide. And He dislikes for you idle talk, excessive questioning, and wasting wealth."
"8704","Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd Allah, meaning Ibn Said, narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things competent, whoever says it ten times when he enters the morning, there will be recorded for him thereby one hundred good deeds, and one hundred evil deeds will be erased from him thereby, and it will be for him equal to freeing a slave, and he will be protected thereby that day until evening. And whoever says the like of that when he enters the evening, there will be for him the like of that."
"8705","Makki narrated to us, Hashim ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Kinanah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until when we were beneath the pass of Lift, Khalid ibn al-Walid came upon us from the pass, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Hurayrah: See who this is. Abu Hurayrah said: Khalid ibn al-Walid. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What an excellent servant of Allah this is."
"8706","Makki narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Said narrated to us, from Abd al-Majid ibn Suhayl ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This minbar of mine is upon a stream from the streams of Paradise."
"8707","Ismail ibn Umar and Abu Nuaym said, Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, Abu Said, freed slave of Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Kurayz, narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not engage in najsh, do not hate one another, do not turn your backs on one another, do not envy one another, and let none of you sell over the sale of another, and be servants of Allah, brothers. The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim: he does not wrong him, he does not despise him, he does not forsake him. All of the Muslim is inviolable to the Muslim: his blood, Ismail said in his hadith: and his wealth and his honor. Taqwa is here, taqwa is here, pointing to his chest three times. It is enough of evil for a man to despise his Muslim brother."
"8708","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, you joke with us? He said: Indeed I speak nothing but the truth."
"8709","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Ibn Mutarrif al-Ghifari, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what if my property is attacked? He said: Implore them by Allah. If they refuse, then fight. If you are killed, then you are in Paradise, and if you kill, then he is in the Fire."
"8710","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you cleans himself with stones, let him make it odd, and when the dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times. And let him not withhold surplus water so as to withhold thereby pasture. And among the rights of camels is that they be milked at the water on the day they are brought to drink."
"8711","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said, Zaidah narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When this verse was revealed: And warn your nearest kindred, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Quraysh, addressing them generally and specifically, and said: O company of Quraysh, save yourselves from the Fire. O company of Banu Kab ibn Luayy, save yourselves from the Fire. O company of Banu Abd Manaf, save yourselves from the Fire. O company of Banu Hashim, save yourselves from the Fire. O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, save yourselves from the Fire. O Fatimah bint Muhammad, save yourself from the Fire. For by Allah, I possess nothing for you against Allah except that you have kinship, which I shall keep moist with its due moisture."
"8712","Husayn narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When this verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: For I do not possess for you against Allah any harm nor any benefit, meaning Fatimah, peace be upon her."
"8713","Yunus and Surayj said, Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All my Ummah will enter Paradise on the Day of Resurrection except whoever refuses. They said: And who would refuse, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Whoever obeys me will enter Paradise, and whoever disobeys me has refused."
"8714","Yunus and Surayj said, Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting narrating to the people in his gathering, a Bedouin came and said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued narrating. Some of the people said: He heard but disliked what he said, and some said: Rather he did not hear. Until when he finished his narration, he said: Where is the one asking about the Hour? He said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: When trust is lost, then await the Hour. He said: O Messenger of Allah, how, or he said: what is its loss? He said: When authority is entrusted to other than its rightful people, then await the Hour."
"8715","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Indeed a man who never did any good at all used to lend to people, and he would say to his agent: Take what is easy and leave what is difficult, and overlook, perhaps Allah will overlook us. Then when he perished, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said to him: Did you ever do any good at all? He said: No, except that I had a servant boy, and I used to lend to people, and when I sent him to collect, I would say to him: Take what is easy and leave what is difficult, and overlook, perhaps Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will overlook us. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: I have overlooked you."
"8716","Abu Salamah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi informed us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: Indeed the believer is to Me in the station of all good: he praises Me, while I take his soul from between his sides."
"8717","Abu Salamah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Abu al-Ghayth, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who strives for the widow and the poor is like the mujahid in the cause of Allah, or like the one who stands the night and fasts the day."
"8718","Abu Salamah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Abu al-Ghayth, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes people wealth intending to repay it, Allah will repay it on his behalf, and whoever takes it intending to destroy it, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will destroy him."
"8719","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said, Malik informed us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath and then sees something else better than it, let him expiate for his oath and do that which is better."
"8720","Abu Salamah narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Said ibn Salamah, of the family of Ibn al-Azraq, that al-Mughirah ibn Abi Burdah, who is of Banu Abd al-Dar, informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: We ride the sea and carry with us little water. If we perform ablution with it, we will thirst. So may we perform ablution from seawater? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Its water is purifying, its dead are lawful."
"8721","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has removed from you the arrogance of Jahiliyyah and its boasting of forefathers: a God-fearing believer and a wretched sinner. People are the children of Adam, and Adam is from dust. Peoples shall surely cease their boasting of men, or they shall surely be more insignificant to Allah than the numerous dung beetles that push filth with their noses."
"8722","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Baqiyyah informed us, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever meets Allah not associating anything with Him, and pays the zakat of his wealth with a content soul seeking reward, and hears and obeys, then for him is Paradise, or he will enter Paradise. And five things have no expiation: associating partners with Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, killing a soul without right, or plundering a believer, or fleeing on the day of battle, or a binding oath by which one wrongfully cuts off wealth."
"8723","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ibn Mubarak informed us, from Isa ibn Yazid, from Jarir ibn Yazid, from Abu Zurah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A legal punishment carried out in the land is better for people than that they be rained upon for thirty or forty mornings."
"8724","Harun, he is Ibn Maruf, narrated to us, he said, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yunus narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah narrated to me, that Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you not seen what your Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, said? He said: Whatever blessing I bestow upon My servants, a group of them become thereby disbelievers in the morning, saying: It is the star, and by the star."
"8725","A man he had named, and he is Abd Allah ibn Yazid, narrated to us, he said, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you urinate in standing water and then bathe from it."
"8726","He said, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said, Zaidah narrated to us, from Layth, from Kab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed you are the radiant, white-marked on the Day of Resurrection from the traces of purification. So whoever of you is able to lengthen his radiance, let him do so."
"8727","Abu Said, freed slave of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Abbad ibn Rashid narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, Abu Hurayrah narrated to us then, while we were in Madinah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Deeds will come on the Day of Resurrection. Prayer will come and say: O Lord, I am prayer. And He will say: You are upon good. Then charity will come and say: O Lord, I am charity. And He will say: You are upon good. Then fasting will come and say: O Lord, I am fasting. And He will say: You are upon good. Then deeds will come in that manner, and Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will say: You are upon good. Then Islam will come and say: O Lord, You are peace, and I am Islam. And Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will say: You are upon good. By you today I take, and by you I give. Then Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said in His Book: And whoever seeks other than Islam as religion, it will never be accepted from him, and he in the Hereafter is among the losers. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abbad ibn Rashid is trustworthy, but al-Hasan did not hear from Abu Hurayrah."
"8728","Zayd ibn Yahya al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, he said, I heard al-Qasim, freed slave of Yazid, saying, Abu Hurayrah narrated to me that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says: O son of Adam, if you give surplus, it is better for you, and if you withhold it, it is evil for you. Begin with those you support. Allah does not blame for sufficiency. And the upper hand is better for you than the lower hand."
"8729","And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Command me with something, and do not make it much upon me so that I may comprehend it. He said: Do not become angry. Then he repeated to him, and he repeated to him. He said: Do not become angry."
"8730","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah cursed the Jews: fats were forbidden to them, so they sold them and consumed their prices."
"8731","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Miraya, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels do not invoke blessings upon a wailing woman nor upon one who shrieks."
"8732","Sulayman ibn Dawud, and he is Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi, narrated to us, Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Ala ibn Ziyad al-Adawi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The structure of Paradise is a brick of gold and a brick of silver."
"8733","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is nothing more noble to Allah than supplication."
"8734","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said, Damdam ibn Jaws al-Hiffani narrated to us, he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There were among the Children of Israel two men, one of them diligent in worship and the other excessive against himself, and they were as brothers. The diligent one would continually see sin upon the other, and say: Woe to you, desist. The sinner would say: Leave me and my Lord. Then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Abu Amir."
"8735","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If ten of the rabbis of the Jews believed, all of them would believe in me."
"8736","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu al-Jallas Uqbah ibn Sayyar narrated to me, he said, Ali ibn Shammakh narrated to me, he said: I witnessed Marwan asking Abu Hurayrah: How did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicating over the funeral? Abu Hurayrah said: O Allah, You are its Lord, You created it, You guided it to Islam, You took its soul, and You know best its secret and its open. We have come as intercessors, so forgive it."
"8737","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Extinguish the lamps, close the doors, and cover food and drink."
"8738","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Balj, he said, I heard Amr ibn Maymun narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Shall I not guide you to a word from the treasure of Paradise, from beneath the Throne: There is no power except through Allah."
"8739","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Drought is not that there be no rain, but drought is that the sky rains and the earth does not produce."
"8740","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Aws ibn Khalid, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will be gathered in three categories: a category walking, a category riding, and a category upon their faces. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how will they walk upon their faces? He said: Indeed the One who made them walk upon their feet is able to make them walk upon their faces. Indeed they will shield themselves with every hill and thorn. Affan said: They will shield with their faces every hill and thorn."
"8741","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Wasil, from Yahya ibn Uqayl, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The creation will exact retribution, some from others, even the hornless from the horned, and even the atom from the atom."
"8742","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu al-Salt, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I ended at the seventh heaven, and I looked, and behold above me thunder and lightning. Then I came upon a people whose bellies were like houses, in them snakes seen from outside their bellies. I said: Who are these? He said: These are the eaters of riba. Then when I descended and reached the lowest heaven, behold I was met with dust, smoke, and sounds. I said: Who are these? He said: The devils who confuse the eyes of the children of Adam so that they do not reflect upon the dominion of the heavens and the earth. Were it not for that, they would see wonders."
"8743","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The qintar is twelve thousand ounces, each ounce better than what is between heaven and earth."
"8744","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Umar ibn Rashid narrated to us, Abu Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that fruit be sold until its soundness appears."
"8745","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Hakam, guide of Said ibn Abi Arubah, narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman al-Asamm narrated to us, he said, I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he followed a funeral, would say: Spread out with it, and do not creep as the Jews creep with their funerals."
"8746","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said, Abu Maryam narrated to me that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sovereignty is in Quraysh, judgment is among the Ansar, the call to prayer is among the Abyssinians, and swiftness is in Yemen. And Zayd once said, as he remembers it: And trustworthiness is in al-Azd."
"8747","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ibn Thawban narrated to us, he said, Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl narrated to me, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing ablution twice, twice."
"8748","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Umar ibn Said narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I saw my head struck, and I saw it rolling. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled, then said: Satan comes to one of you at night and frightens him, then he goes in the morning informing people."
"8749","Shuayb ibn Harb Abu Salih, at Makkah, narrated to us, he said, Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, Jafar ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you hear the braying of donkeys at night, seek refuge with Allah from their evil, for they have seen a devil. And when you hear the crowing of roosters at night, ask Allah of His bounty, for they have seen an angel."
"8750","Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, he said, Abu al-Muhazzim narrated to us, he said, I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a Hajj or Umrah, and a swarm of locusts met us. We began striking them with our sticks and whips. Then we regretted what we had done, and we said: What have we done while we are in ihram? So we asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, and he said: There is no harm in sea game."
"8751","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Udhayn, from Makhul, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The servant does not believe with complete faith until he abandons lying in jest and argumentation even if he is truthful."
"8752","Musa ibn Dawud al-Dabbi narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Jafar, from Isa ibn Talhah, from Abu Hurayrah, that Khawlah bint Yasar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a Hajj or Umrah and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have only one garment, and I menstruate in it. He said: When you become pure, wash the place of blood, then pray in it. She said: O Messenger of Allah, if its stain does not come out? He said: Water suffices you, and its trace will not harm you."
"8753","Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar al-Madini narrated to us, and that was before the trial, Abd Allah said: And my father did not narrate from him after the trial anything, he said, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid, meaning al-Thaqafi, narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast."
"8754","Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Said ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Indeed the dead is attended by the angels. If it is the righteous man, they say: Come out, O good soul that was in the good body, come out praiseworthy, and receive glad tidings of rest and sweet scent and a Lord not angry. He said: That will continue to be said to it until it comes out. Then it is taken up to heaven, and it is asked to be opened for, and it is said: Who is this? And it is said: So-and-so. And they say: Welcome to the good soul that was in the good body, enter praiseworthy, and receive glad tidings of rest and sweet scent and a Lord not angry. He said: That will continue to be said to it until it is brought to the heaven in which is Allah, the Mighty and Majestic. And if it is the evil man, they say: Come out, O wicked soul that was in the wicked body, come out blameworthy, and receive glad tidings of scalding water and pus and other of its kind in pairs. It will continue until it comes out. Then it is taken up to heaven, and it is asked to be opened for, and it is said: Who is this? And it is said: So-and-so. And it is said: No welcome to the wicked soul that was in the wicked body, return blameworthy, for the gates of heaven will not be opened for you. So it is sent from heaven, then it returns to the grave. Then the righteous man is seated, and there is said to him the like of what was said to him in the first hadith. And the evil man is seated, and there is said to him the like of what was said in the first hadith."
"8755","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Layth, from Kab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Invoke blessings upon me, for it is purification for you. And ask Allah for me al-Wasilah, for it is a rank in the highest Paradise that none attains except one man, and I hope that I am he."
"8756","Husayn narrated to us, he said, Sufyan, meaning Ibn Uyaynah, narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, in narration, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you see my qiblah here? Nothing of your humility nor your bowing is hidden from me."
"8757","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said, Zaidah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu al-Awbar, he said: A man came to Abu Hurayrah and said: Are you the one who forbids people to pray with their sandals on them? He said: No, but by the Lord of this Sanctuary, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying toward this station with his sandals on him, and he departed with them on him. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting on Friday unless it is among other days."
"8758","Muawiyah ibn Amr, in meaning, narrated to us, he said, Zaidah narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Karim, from the freed slave of Abu Ruhm, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Any woman who perfumes herself for the mosque, no prayer is accepted from her until she washes it from herself as she washes from janabah."
"8759","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muslim, meaning Ibn Khalid, narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: A man nobility is his religion, his manliness is his intellect, and his lineage is his character."
"8760","Yahya ibn Ghaylan and Qutaybah ibn Said said, Rashdin ibn Sad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ghaylan said in his hadith, he said, Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Qabisah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There will emerge from Khurasan black banners which nothing will repel until they are set up in Iliya."
"8761","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said, Rashdin narrated to us, Bakr ibn Amr narrated to me, from Amr ibn Abi Nuaymah, from Abu Uthman, companion of Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever says of me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire. Whoever is given a fatwa without knowledge, the sin thereof is upon whoever gave him the fatwa. And whoever consults his brother and he advises him of a matter while he sees right guidance in other than that, he has betrayed him."
"8762","Al-Khuzai Abu Salamah said, Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us, from Uthman ibn Muhammad al-Akhnasi, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is made a judge among people has been slaughtered without a knife."
"8763","And after that he narrated to us, meaning al-Khuzai, he said, Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us, he said, Uthman ibn Muhammad informed us, from al-Araj and al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah."
"8764","Mansur ibn Salamah Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Trim the mustaches and leave the beards."
"8765","Al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said, Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Said, from his brother Abbad, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: O Allah, I seek refuge with You from four: from knowledge that does not benefit, from a heart that does not humble itself, from a soul that is never satisfied, and from a supplication that is not heard."
"8766","Al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The lowest of my Ummah grants protection."
"8767","Al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said, Ibn Bilal informed us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Ubayd Allah ibn Salman al-Agharr, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not fitting for the two-faced one to be trustworthy."
"8768","Al-Khuzai narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It is not fitting for the truthful one to be a curser."
"8769","Al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said, Sulayman informed us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The bell is the flute of Satan."
"8770","Al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Reconciliation is permissible among Muslims."
"8771","Al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Trim the mustaches, leave the beards, and oppose the Magians."
"8772","Al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When sight has entered, there is no permission."
"8773","Al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said, Layth ibn Sad informed us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Ibn Shihab, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I saw Amr ibn Amir dragging his intestines in the Fire, and he was the first who set free the saibah and dedicated the bahirah."
"8774","Al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said, Layth informed us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Ibn Shihab, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah cursed the Jews: they took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"8775","Muawiyah narrated to us, he said, Zaidah narrated to us, he said, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar every fanged beast of prey, and the animal used as a target, and the domestic donkey."
"8776","Muawiyah narrated to us, he said, Abu Ishaq, meaning al-Fazari, narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever spends a pair, or he said: two pairs, of his wealth, I think he said: in the cause of Allah, the keepers of Paradise will call him: O Muslim, this is good, come to it. Abu Bakr said: This is a man who will suffer no loss. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No wealth ever benefited me except the wealth of Abu Bakr. Then Abu Bakr wept and said: And has Allah benefited me except through you, and has Allah benefited me except through you, and has Allah benefited me except through you."
"8777","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said, Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Rabiah, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The strong believer is better, more excellent, and more beloved to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, than the weak believer, and in each is good. Strive for what benefits you and do not be helpless. If a matter overcomes you, say: Allah decreed, and what He willed, He did. And beware of if, for if opens the work of Satan."
"8778","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People shall surely abandon their boasting of Jahiliyyah, or they shall surely be more hateful to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, than beetles."
"8779","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abbas, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Yazid ibn Mikraz, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, a man intends jihad in the cause of Allah while seeking worldly gain? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no reward for him. People deemed that grave, and they said to the man: Return to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), perhaps he did not understand. So he repeated that to him three times, each time saying: There is no reward for him."
"8780","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A Bedouin passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whose health and strength impressed him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and said: When did you last feel Umm Mildam? He said: And what is Umm Mildam? He said: Fever. He said: And what is fever? He said: Heat that occurs between skin and bones. He said: I have never had that. He said: When did you last feel headache? He said: And what is headache? He said: A throbbing that occurs in the temples and head. He said: I have never had that. Then when the Bedouin turned away, he said: Whoever is pleased to look at a man of the people of the Fire, let him look at him."
"8781","Khalaf narrated to us, he said, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The supplication of the oppressed is answered, even if he is sinful, for his sinfulness is upon himself."
"8782","Khalaf narrated to us, he said, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for what is in houses of women and offspring, I would establish the prayer, the Isha prayer, and command my youths to burn what is in the houses with fire."
"8783","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Abu al-Walid, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I would not love to have Uhud as gold with me while three pass by me and I have of it a dinar, except something I set aside for my creditor."
"8784","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said, Khalid ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best rows of men are the first of them and the worst are the last of them. And the best rows of women are the last of them and the worst are the first of them."
"8785","Khalaf narrated to us, he said, Khalid narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah is pleased for you with three and angry with you for three. He is pleased for you that you worship Him and do not associate anything with Him, and that you hold fast to the rope of Allah all together and do not divide, and that you advise sincerely those whom Allah has placed in charge of your affairs. And He is angry with you for idle talk, wasting wealth, and excessive questioning."
"8786","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said, Khalid narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to cover ablution water, and to tie the mouth of the waterskin, and to turn over the vessel."
"8787","Khalaf narrated to us, he said, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let me not know one of you to whom a hadith comes from me while he is reclining on his couch, and he says: Recite to me of Quran. Whatever comes to you from me of good, whether I said it or I did not say it, I do say it. And whatever comes to you from me of evil, I do not say evil."
"8788","Khalaf narrated to us, he said, al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said, and I think he mentioned the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Peoples who raise their sights to the sky in prayer shall surely cease, or Allah will surely snatch their sights."
"8789","Surayj narrated to us, he said, Abd Allah ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to me, from Salih, freed slave of al-Tawamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man sat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: From where are you? He said: A Berber. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Stand from me, he said, with his elbow like this. Then when he stood from him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to us and said: Indeed faith does not pass their throats."
"8790","Surayj narrated to us, he said, Abd Allah ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not take my grave as a festival, and do not make your houses graves. And wherever you are, invoke blessings upon me, for your blessings reach me."
"8791","Surayj narrated to us, he said, Abd Allah ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until my Ummah follows the ways of the nations and generations before it, handspan by handspan and cubit by cubit. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, as Persia and Rome did? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And are people other than those?"
"8792","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, meaning the like of it."
"8793","Ismail ibn Umar narrated to us, he said, Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Our dowry when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among us was ten ounces, and he folded with his hands, and that is four hundred."
"8794","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said, Zaidah narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I saw myself upon a well drawing with a bucket. Then Abu Bakr took it and drew a bucket or two, in them was weakness, and Allah have mercy on him. Then Umar took it, and he continued drawing until it turned into a large bucket. Then it struck the trough. I never saw the drawing of a master more excellent than the drawing of Umar."
"8795","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said, Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed over the funeral, would say: O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, our present and our absent, our young and our old, our male and our female. O Allah, whomever of us You keep alive, keep him alive upon Islam, and whomever of us You cause to die, cause him to die upon faith."
"8796","Muawiyah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed Satan has despaired of being worshipped in this land of yours, but he is content with what you deem insignificant."
"8797","Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, he said, Rashdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you not seen what your Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, said: Whatever blessing I bestow upon My servants, a group of them become disbelievers in the morning, saying: The star, and by the star."
"8798","Haytham narrated to us, Hafs ibn Maysarah, meaning al-Sanani, narrated to us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood over some people sitting and said: Shall I not inform you of the best of you from the worst of you? The people fell silent. He repeated it three times. A man from the people said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The best of you is he whose good is hoped and whose evil is safe from. And the worst of you is he whose good is not hoped and whose evil is not safe from."
"8799","Haytham narrated to us, Hafs ibn Maysarah informed us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The servant says: My wealth, my wealth. Yet he has of his wealth only three: what he ate and consumed, or what he wore and wore out, or what he gave and stored. What is besides that is going and he leaves it to people."
"8800","Haytham narrated to us, Rashdin narrated to us, from Amr, from Bukayr, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man shall lie with a woman while her pregnancy is another."
"8801","Haytham narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Maysara narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every human whom his mother bears, Satan pricks him in his flanks, except what was the case of Maryam and her son. Have you not seen the infant when he drops, how he cries. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: That is when Satan pricks him in his flanks."
"8802","Haytham narrated to us: Hafs ibn Maysara informed us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A disbeliever and his killer among the Muslims will never be gathered together in the Fire ever."
"8803","Haytham narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Maysara narrated to us, from al-Ala, and Qutayba narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection on a single plain, then the Lord of the worlds will appear to them, then it will be said: Will not every nation follow what they used to worship. So the cross will appear to the owner of the cross, his cross, and images to the owner of images, his images, and fire to the owner of fire, his fire, so they will follow what they used to worship, and the Muslims will remain. Then the Lord of the worlds will appear to them and say: Will you not follow the people. They will say: We seek refuge with Allah from you, Allah is our Lord, and this is our place until we see our Lord, and He is commanding them and making them firm. Then He will withdraw, then appear and say: Will you not follow the people. They will say: We seek refuge with Allah from you, we seek refuge with Allah from you, Allah is our Lord, and this is our place until we see our Lord, and He is commanding them and making them firm. They said: And will we see Him, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And are you harmed in seeing the moon on the night of full moon. They said: No. He said: Then you will not be harmed in seeing Him at that hour. Then He will withdraw, then appear and make Himself known to them: I am your Lord, so they will say: You are our Lord, follow me. So the Muslims will rise and the Sirat will be placed, and they will be upon it like excellent horses and mounts, and their saying upon it will be: Spare, spare. And the people of the Fire will remain, so a group of them will be cast into it, and it will be said: Are you filled, and it will say: Is there any more. Then a group will be cast into it, and it will be said: Are you filled, and it will say: Is there any more, until when they are all contained in it, the Most Merciful, mighty and majestic, will place His foot in it and draw part of it together to part, then it will say: Enough, enough, enough. And when the people of Paradise are settled in Paradise and the people of the Fire in the Fire, death will be brought seized by its forelock and made to stand upon the wall between the people of the Fire and the people of Paradise, then it will be said: O people of Paradise, so they will look out fearfully, then it will be said: O people of the Fire, so they will look out rejoicing, hoping for intercession, then it will be said to the people of Paradise and the people of the Fire: Do you know this. So these and these will say: We have known him, he is death which was entrusted with us. So he will be laid down and slaughtered with slaughter upon the wall, then it will be said: O people of Paradise, eternity without death, and O people of the Fire, eternity without death. And Qutayba said in his hadith: And part of it will be drawn together to part, then he said: Enough, it said: Enough, enough."
"8804","Haytham narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The expiation of gatherings is for the servant to say: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise, I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You."
"8805","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Husayn narrated to us, from Yahya, he said: I heard Abu Salama say: Abu Hurayra reported from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The righteous dream is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"8806","Rawh narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsa narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard Abdullah ibn Qays reciting, so he said: This one has indeed been given from the psalms of the family of Dawud, the Prophet, peace be upon him."
"8807","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: al-Bara ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the people of Paradise. They are the weak and the oppressed. Shall I not inform you of the people of the Fire. Every harsh swaggering coarse one."
"8808","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: al-Bara narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Shaqiq narrated to me, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of your worst. So he said: They are the babblers, those who affect eloquence with their mouths. Shall I not inform you of your best. The best of you in character."
"8809","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: al-Bara narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayra, he said: My truthful intimate friend, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me that he said: There will be in this nation an expedition to al-Sind and al-Hind. If I live to see it and am martyred, then so be it, and if I - and he mentioned a word - return, and I am Abu Hurayra the freed, He has freed me from the Fire."
"8810","Ali ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Warqa informed us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will surely come while their two garments are between them, they will neither fold them nor trade them, and the Hour will surely come after he has milked his milch camel and will not taste it, and the Hour will surely come after he has raised his morsel to his mouth and will not taste it, and the Hour will surely come while a man is plastering his basin and will not give drink from it."
"8811","Ali ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Warqa informed us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you not wonder how the reviling of Quraysh is turned away from me. They revile Mudhammam, and I am Muhammad, and they curse Mudhammam, and I am Muhammad."
"8812","Ali narrated to us, he said: Warqa informed us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose hand is my soul, Aslam and Ghifar and Juhayna, and whoever was of Muzayna, or Muzayna and whoever was of Juhayna, are better with Allah on the Day of Resurrection than Asad and Tayyi and Ghatafan."
"8813","Yahya ibn Ishaq informed us: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Thabit, from Abi Rafi, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters Paradise will enjoy bliss and will not despair, and his garments will not wear out, and his youth will not perish. In Paradise is what no eye has seen, and no ear has heard, and has not occurred to a human heart."
"8814","Surayj narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayra, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a cloud passed, so he said: Do you know what this is. He said: We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The clouds and the water-carriers of the earth, Allah drives it to those of His servants who do not thank Him and do not supplicate Him. Do you know what this is above you. We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The firmament, a restrained wave and a guarded roof. Do you know how much is between you and it. We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: A journey of five hundred years. He said: Do you know what is above it. We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Another heaven. Do you know how much is between you and it. We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: A journey of five hundred years, until he counted seven heavens. Then he said: Do you know what is above that. We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The Throne. He said: Do you know how much is between you and the seventh heaven. We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: A journey of five hundred years. Then he said: Do you know what this is beneath you. We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Earth. Do you know what is beneath it. We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Another earth. Do you know how much is between it and it. We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: A journey of five hundred years, until he counted seven earths. Then he said: By Allah, if you were to lower one of you with a rope to the lowest seventh earth, he would descend. Then he recited: He is the First and the Last and the Manifest and the Hidden, and He is Knowing of all things."
"8815","Arim narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan informed me, from Rabia, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: And I heard it from Rabia and did not deny it. He said: The strong believer is better, or superior, and more beloved to Allah, mighty and majestic, than the weak believer, and in each is good. Strive for what benefits you and do not be incapable, and if a matter overcomes you, say: Allah decreed, and what He willed He did. And beware of if only, for if only opens the work of Satan."
"8816","Arim narrated to us, he said: Mutamir narrated to us, he said: And my father narrated to me, from Baraka, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise his hands in supplication until I could see the whiteness of his armpits. He said: My father, and he is Abu al-Mutamir: I do not think it was except in seeking rain."
"8817","Arim narrated to us, he said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: My father said: Nuaym ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Abi Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, he said: Abu Jahl said: Does Muhammad rub his face in dust among you. He said: So it was said: Yes. So he said: By al-Lat and al-Uzza, an oath by which he swears, if I see him doing that I will surely tread upon his neck, or I will surely rub his face in dust. He said: So he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, intending to tread upon his neck. He said: Nothing suddenly struck them from him except that he was recoiling upon his heels and shielding himself with his hands. He said: They said to him: What is the matter with you. He said: Between me and him is a trench of fire and wings. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he had drawn near to me, the angels would have seized him limb by limb. He said: So it was revealed, I do not know whether in the hadith of Abu Hurayra or something that reached him: No indeed, man transgresses, that he sees himself self-sufficient. Have you seen the one who forbids a servant when he prays. Have you seen if he is upon guidance, or enjoins piety. Have you seen if he denies and turns away, meaning Abu Jahl. Does he not know that Allah sees. No indeed, if he does not desist, We will surely seize by the forelock, a lying sinful forelock. So let him call his assembly, he said: He calls his people, We will call the guards, he said: Meaning the angels. No indeed, do not obey him, and prostrate and draw near."
"8818","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Said ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that Allah, mighty and majestic, says on the Day of Resurrection: Where are those who love one another for My majesty. Today I will shade them in My shade, on a day when there is no shade except My shade."
"8819","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, he said: Ismail, meaning Ibn Zakariyya, narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until the land of the Arabs returns to meadows and rivers, and until a rider travels between Iraq and Mecca fearing nothing except losing the way, and until killing increases much. They said: And what is al-harj, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Killing."
"8820","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, he said: Ismail, meaning Ibn Zakariyya, narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Abi Ubayd, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever glorifies Allah after every prayer thirty-three times, and praises Allah thirty-three times, and magnifies Allah thirty-three times, so those are ninety-nine, then says to complete one hundred: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner for Him, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is capable of all things, his sins will be forgiven even if they are like the foam of the sea."
"8821","Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says in the morning and in the evening: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, one hundred times, no one will come on the Day of Resurrection with better than what he brought, except one who said the like of what he said or added to it."
"8822","Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam al-Nakhai, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abi Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says in the morning and in the evening: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, one hundred times, no one will come on the Day of Resurrection with better than what he brought, except one who said the like of what he said or added to it."
"8823","Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam al-Nakhai, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abi Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lives in the desert becomes harsh, and whoever follows hunting becomes heedless, and whoever comes to the doors of the ruler is tempted, and a servant does not increase in nearness to the ruler except that he increases in distance from Allah."
"8824","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, meaning Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri, narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Abd Allah ibn Mawhab, informed us, he said: My uncle Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mawhab informed me, from Abu Hurayra, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If one of you knew what is against him in walking in front of his brother intercepting him while he is privately conversing with his Lord, standing in that place one hundred years would be more beloved to him than to take a step."
"8825","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Thawr, from al-Husayn, thus he said, from Abi Sad al-Khayr, and he was of the companions of Umar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever applies kohl, let him make it odd, and whoever does so has done well, and whoever does not, there is no harm upon him. And whoever cleanses with stones, let him make it odd, and whoever does so has done well, and whoever does not, there is no harm. And whoever eats, whatever he picks from between his teeth, let him spit it out, and whoever moves it with his tongue, let him swallow it. Whoever does so has done well, and whoever does not, there is no harm. And whoever comes to the place of relieving himself, let him conceal himself, and if he finds nothing except to gather a heap of sand, let him turn his back to it, for Satan plays with the sitting places of the children of Adam. Whoever does so has done well, and whoever does not, there is no harm."
"8826","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Khalaf, meaning Ibn Khalifa, narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Kaysan, from Abi Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, and we heard a thud, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know what this is. We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: This is a stone cast into Hellfire seventy autumns ago, only now it has reached its bottom."
"8827","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Khalaf, meaning Ibn Khalifa, narrated to us, from Abi Malik al-Ashjai, from Abi Hazim, he said: I was behind Abu Hurayra while he was performing ablution, and he was extending the ablution to his armpit, so I said: O Abu Hurayra, what is this ablution. He said: O sons of Farrukh, are you here. If I knew you were here, I would not have performed this ablution. I heard my intimate friend say: The ornament of the believer will reach where the ablution reaches."
"8828","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, narrated to us, he said: al-Ala informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): My father died and left wealth and did not bequeath, so will it expiate for him if I give charity on his behalf. So he said: Yes."
"8829","Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Ismail narrated to us, he said: al-Ala informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do you know who the bankrupt is. They said: The bankrupt among us is one who has no dirham and no goods. He said: The bankrupt of my nation will come on the Day of Resurrection with prayer and fasting and zakat, and will come having reviled this one, and slandered this one, and consumed the wealth of this one, and shed the blood of this one, and struck this one, so this one will be settled from his good deeds, and this one from his good deeds, and if his good deeds are exhausted before he settles what is upon him, some of their sins will be taken and cast upon him, then he will be cast into the Fire."
"8830","Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Ismail narrated to us, he said: al-Ala informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two eyes commit adultery, and the tongue commits adultery, and the two hands commit adultery, and the two feet commit adultery, the private part confirms that or denies it."
"8831","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us: Ismail narrated to us: al-Ala informed us, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a human dies, his deed is cut off from him except from three: except from ongoing charity, or knowledge benefited from, or a righteous child who supplicates for him."
"8832","Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Ismail narrated to us, he said: al-Ala informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The right of a Muslim upon a Muslim is six. It was said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah. He said: When you meet him, greet him with peace, and when he invites you, answer him, and when he seeks your counsel, counsel him, and when he sneezes and praises Allah, bless him, and when he falls ill, visit him, and when he dies, follow him."
"8833","Sulayman narrated to us: Ismail narrated to us: al-Ala informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith is Yemeni, and disbelief is toward the east, and tranquility is among the people of sheep, and pride and showing off are among the loud-voiced ones, and horses, and fur."
"8834","Sulayman narrated to us: Ismail informed us: al-Ala informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rights will surely be rendered to their owners on the Day of Resurrection, until the hornless sheep is retaliated for from the horned sheep."
"8835","Sulayman narrated to us: Ismail informed us: al-Ala informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasten against trials like pieces of the dark night. A man will wake a believer and evening a disbeliever, and evening a believer and wake a disbeliever, selling his religion for goods of this world."
"8836","Sulayman narrated to us: Ismail narrated to us: al-Ala informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasten with deeds six: the rising of the sun from its west, and the Dajjal, and the smoke, and the beast, or the private affair of one of you, or the general affair."
"8837","Sulayman narrated to us: Ismail informed us: al-Ala informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until the sun rises from its west, and when it rises, people will then all believe together, and on that day no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before, or earned good in its faith."
"8838","Sulayman narrated to us: Ismail informed us: al-Ala informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The bell is the pipes of Satan."
"8839","Sulayman narrated to us: Ismail informed us: al-Ala informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that a man said: Fix prices, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Allah alone raises and lowers. I hope to meet Allah, mighty and majestic, with no one having a claim of injustice against me. Another said: Fix prices. So he said: Supplicate Allah, mighty and majestic."
"8840","Sulayman narrated to us: Ismail informed us: al-Ala informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fear the two accursed ones. They said: And what are the two accursed ones, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The one who relieves himself in the path of people or in their shade."
"8841","Sulayman narrated to us: Ismail informed us: al-Ala informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sends blessing upon me once, Allah will send blessing upon him tenfold."
"8842","Sulayman informed me: Ismail informed me, he said: al-Ala informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: He will not enter Paradise whose neighbor is not safe from his harms."
"8843","Sulayman narrated to us: Ismail narrated to us: Amr, meaning Ibn Abi Amr, informed me, from Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Many a fasting one whose share of his fasting is hunger and thirst, and many a standing one whose share of his standing is sleeplessness."
"8844","Sulayman narrated to us: Ismail informed us: Amr informed me, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was sent from the best generations of the children of Adam, generation after generation, until I was sent from the generation in which I was."
"8845","Sulayman narrated to us: Ismail informed us: Amr informed me, from Said, from Abu Hurayra, he said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Who is the happiest of people with your intercession on the Day of Resurrection. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I thought, O Abu Hurayra, that no one would ask me about this hadith before you, because of what I saw of your eagerness for hadith. The happiest of people with my intercession on the Day of Resurrection is one who says: There is no god but Allah, sincerely from before himself."
"8846","Sulayman narrated to us: Ismail informed us: Amr informed me, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon an old man walking between his two sons, leaning upon them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is the matter with this old man. His two sons said: O Messenger of Allah, he had a vow upon him. So he said to him: Ride, O old man, for Allah, mighty and majestic, is in no need of you and your vow."
"8847","Sulayman narrated to us: Ismail informed us: Amr informed me, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A vow does not bring anything near to the son of Adam which Allah had not decreed for him, but a vow coincides with decree, so thereby is extracted from the miser what the miser did not want to give."
"8848","Sulayman narrated to us: Ismail informed us: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Amr, informed me, from Abi Salama, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah called Jibril and sent him to Paradise and said: Look at it and what I have prepared for its people. So he returned to Him and said: By Your might, no one will hear of it except that he will enter it. So it was veiled with hardships, so He said: Return to it and look at it. So he returned to it and said: By Your might, I feared that no one would enter it. Then He sent him to the Fire and said: Go and look at it and what I have prepared for its people in it. So he returned to Him and said: By Your might, no one who hears of it will enter it. So it was veiled with desires, then He said: Return to it and look at it. So he returned to Him and said: By Your might, I feared that no one would remain except that he would enter it."
"8849","Sulayman narrated to us: Ismail informed us: Amr, meaning Ibn Abi Amr, informed me, from Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left the dawn prayer one day and came to the women in the mosque and stood over them and said: O assembly of women, I have not seen any deficient in intellect and religion more removing to the hearts of men of understanding than you. For I have seen you the most of the people of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, so draw near to Allah as much as you can. And among the women was the wife of Abdullah ibn Masud, so she came to Abdullah ibn Masud and informed him of what she heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and took jewelry of hers. So Ibn Masud said: So where are you going with this jewelry. She said: I draw near with it to Allah, mighty and majestic, and His Messenger, perhaps Allah will not make me of the people of the Fire. He said: Woe to you, come, give it in charity to me and my child, for we are a place for it. She said: No, by Allah, until I go with it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So she went to seek permission upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): This is Zaynab seeking permission, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Which of the Zaynabs is she. They said: The wife of Abdullah ibn Masud. He said: Permit her. So she entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I heard a statement from you, so I returned to Ibn Masud and narrated to him, and took jewelry to draw near with it to Allah and to you, hoping Allah will not make me of the people of the Fire. So Ibn Masud said to me: Give it in charity to me and my child, for we are a place for it. So I said: Until I seek permission from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give it in charity to him and his sons, for they are a place for it. Then she said: O Messenger of Allah, have you seen what I heard from you when you stood over us: I have not seen any deficient in intellect ever, nor in religion, more removing to the hearts of men of understanding than you. She said: O Messenger of Allah, so what is the deficiency of our religion and our intellect. He said: As for what I mentioned of the deficiency of your religion, it is menstruation which afflicts you, one of you remains as long as Allah wills her to remain, neither praying nor fasting, so that is of the deficiency of your religion. And as for what I mentioned of the deficiency of your intellect, it is your testimony, the testimony of a woman is but half a testimony."
"8850","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, he said: Said ibn al-Musayyab narrated to me, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah will grasp the earth on the Day of Resurrection and fold the heaven with His right hand, then say: I am the King, where are the kings of the earth."
"8851","Ibrahim narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Said ibn Yazid, from Abi al-Samh, from Ibn Hujayra, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Boiling water will surely be poured upon their heads, so it will pierce the skull until it reaches his interior, then strip out what is in his interior until it comes out from his feet."
"8852","Ibrahim narrated to us: Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Wuhayb: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir informed me, from Sumayy, from Abi Salih, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever dies and did not fight, and did not speak to himself of fighting, dies upon a branch of hypocrisy."
"8853","Ibrahim narrated to us: Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Talha ibn Abi Said: I heard Said al-Maqburi narrating that he heard Abu Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a horse in the path of Allah, out of faith in Allah and belief in His promise, its feed and its drink and its urine and its dung will be good deeds in his scale on the Day of Resurrection."
"8854","Ibrahim narrated to us: Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Ayyub: Yahya ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to me, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: On that day it will relate its news. He said: Do you know what its news is. They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Its news is that it will testify against every servant and maid for what he did upon its back, that it will say: You did upon me such and such, on such and such day. He said: So that is its news."
"8855","Ibrahim narrated to us: Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Isa al-Thaqafi, from the freedman of al-Munbaith, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Learn of your lineages what you join your kinship ties with, for joining kinship is love among family, increase in wealth, delay in his trace."
"8856","Ibrahim narrated to us: From Ibn al-Mubarak, from Mamar, from Hammam, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A good word is charity, and every step he steps toward prayer is charity."
"8857","Ibrahim narrated to us: Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd: Amr ibn Tamim narrated to me, from his father, that he heard Abu Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This month of yours has overshadowed you, by the oath of the Messenger of Allah, no month has passed for the believers better for them than it, nor for the hypocrites a month worse for them than it. Allah, mighty and majestic, writes its reward and its supererogatory deeds before He brings it in, and writes its burden and its misery before He brings it in. That is because the believer prepares in it strength for worship from spending, and the hypocrite prepares following the heedlessness of people and following their faults. So it is spoil for the believer which the wicked takes as spoil."
"8858","Surayj narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Abi al-Muhazzim, he said: I heard Abu Hurayra: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a pilgrimage or lesser pilgrimage, and a swarm of locusts met us, so we began striking them with our whips and our staffs and killing them, then it fell into our hands, so we said: What shall we do while we are in pilgrim sanctity. So we asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: No harm."
"8859","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Malik narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abi Salih, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If people knew what is in the call to prayer and the first row, then found nothing except to draw lots for it, they would draw lots for it. And if they knew what is in hastening early, they would race to it. And if they knew what is in the night prayer and the dawn, they would come to them even crawling."
"8860","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Malik informed us, from Sumayy, from Abi Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner for Him, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is capable of all things, one hundred times, it will be for him equal to freeing ten necks, and one hundred good deeds will be written for him, and one hundred evil deeds will be erased from him, and it will be for him a guard from Satan that day until evening, and no one will come with better than what he brought, except a man who did more than that. And whoever says in a day one hundred times: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, one hundred times, his sins will be removed even if they are like the foam of the sea."
"8861","Ishaq informed us: Malik informed me, from Sumayy, from Abi Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While a man was walking upon a road, thirst became severe upon him, so he found a well and descended into it and drank, then came out, and there was a dog panting, eating moist earth from thirst, so he said: This dog has reached of thirst the like of what reached me. So he descended the well and filled his shoe with water, then held it with his mouth until he climbed with it, and gave drink to the dog. So Allah thanked him and forgave him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and is there for us in beasts a reward. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In every moist liver is a reward."
"8862","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood for prayer, raised his hands extended."
"8863","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Malik informed me, from Nuaym ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon the passes of Medina are angels, the Dajjal will not enter it, nor plague."
"8864","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Malik narrated to us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you see my qibla here. By Allah, neither your humility nor your bowing is hidden from me. I see you from behind my back."
"8865","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Malik informed us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the graves and said: Peace be upon you, abode of believing people, and we, if Allah wills, will join you."
"8866","Ishaq informed us: Malik informed us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was hosted with a guest, and he was a disbeliever, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a sheep and it was milked, so the disbeliever drank its milk, then another, so he drank it, then another, so he drank it, until he drank the milk of seven sheep. Then he woke in the morning and embraced Islam, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a sheep for him, so he drank its milk, then ordered another, but he could not finish it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"8867","Ishaq informed us: Malik informed us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that a man of Aslam said: When I slept this night, a scorpion stung me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had you said in the evening: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created, it would not have harmed you."
"8868","Ishaq narrated to me: Malik informed us, from Thawr ibn Zayd al-Dili, he said: I heard Aba al-Ghayth narrating from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The guardian of an orphan, for him or for another, I and he will be like these two in Paradise, when he fears Allah. And Malik pointed with the forefinger and the middle finger."
"8869","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us: Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, informed us: al-Ala informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever sends blessing upon me once, Allah will send blessing upon him tenfold."
"8870","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abi Salama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches a raka of prayer has caught all of it."
"8871","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abi Salama, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of uncertainty and the sale of pebbles."
"8872","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Khubayb, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yasaf, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between my house and my pulpit is a meadow of the meadows of Paradise, and my pulpit is upon my basin."
"8873","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the slave-girl of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her and not reproach her. If she returns, let him flog her and not reproach her. If she returns, let him flog her and not reproach her. If she returns a fourth time, let him sell her even for a rope of hair or a braid of hair."
"8874","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, sanctified upon my tongue what is between the two lava fields of Medina. Then the sons of so-and-so came, so he said: I do not see you except that you have left the sanctuary. Then he looked and said: Rather you are in it, rather you are in it. He said: My father said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd said: Then the sons of Jariya came, and they are but the sons of Haritha."
"8875","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from his father, he said: And he was staying with Abu Hurayra in Medina. He said: So I saw him praying a prayer neither light nor long. He said: Ismail said: Like the prayer of Qays ibn Abi Hazim. He said: So I said to Abu Hurayra: Was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying thus. He said: And what did you dislike of my prayer. He said: I said: Good, I loved to ask you. He said: So I said: Yes, or shorter."
"8876","Abu Sad al-Saghani Muhammad ibn Muyassar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is but to be followed, so when he magnifies, magnify, and when he recites, listen attentively, and when he says: Nor of those astray, say: Amen, and when he bows, bow, and when he says: Allah hears him who praises Him, say: Our Lord, and to You is praise, and when he prays sitting, pray sitting all together."
"8877","Abu Sad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I intended to command my youths to gather firewood, then command a man to lead the people, then go to men who stay behind from prayer and burn their houses upon them. By Allah, if one of them knew he would have by attending it a fat fleshy bone or two good hoofs, he would attend it. And if they knew what is in it, they would come to it even crawling."
"8878","Abu Sad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glorification is for men, and clapping is for women."
"8879","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from Ibn Dhakwan, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My heirs will not divide a dinar. What I left after the maintenance of my wives and the provision of my worker, meaning the worker of his land, is charity."
"8880","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No child will recompense his father except that he finds him a slave and buys him and frees him."
"8881","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, meaning: Allah said: Pride is My cloak, and greatness is My garment, so whoever disputes Me for one of them, I will admit him into Hell."
"8882","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Dhakwan, from Abu Hurayra, he raised it, he said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, nor does the thief steal when he steals while he is a believer, nor does he drink wine when he drinks while he is a believer, and repentance is presented after."
"8883","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from Ibn Dhakwan, from Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Delaying payment is the injustice of the rich, and whoever is referred upon a solvent one, let him follow."
"8884","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Abi Salama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: A Bedouin came demanding a camel from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek for him the like of the age of his camel. He said: So they sought for him and found nothing except above the age of his camel. He said: So give him above his camel. So the Bedouin said: You have fulfilled to me, may Allah fulfill to you. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are the best of you in repayment."
"8885","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal is blessing."
"8886","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to me: One who heard Abu Hurayra narrated to me, saying: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray in his sandals."
"8887","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Abu Bakr informed us, from Asim, from Abi Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cool with the noon prayer, for its heat is from the exhalation of Hell."
"8888","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Asim, from a man of Banu Amir, he said to Marwan: This is Abu Hurayra at the door. He said: Permit him. He said: O Abu Hurayra, narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man will soon wish he had fallen from the Pleiades and that he had not undertaken, or taken charge, Abu Bakr doubted, anything of the affairs of people. He said: And I heard him say: The destruction of the Arabs is at the hands of youths of Quraysh. He said: Marwan said: Evil, by Allah, are these youths."
"8889","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr informed us, from Asim, from Abi Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade continuous fasting. He said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, you continue fasting. He said: I am not like you, I spend with my Lord, He feeds me and gives me drink."
"8890","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr informed us, from Asim, from Abi Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the mosque and saw them in separate groups, dispersed. He said: So he became angry with a severe anger, we never saw him angry with anger more severe than it. He said: By Allah, I intended to command a man to lead the people, then follow these who stay behind from prayer in their houses and burn them upon them. And perhaps he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque, the night prayer."
"8891","Aswad informed us: Abu Bakr informed us, from Asim, from Abi Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah. So when they say it, they protect from me their blood and their wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."
"8892","Aswad informed us: Abu Bakr informed us, from al-Amash, from Abi Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Two are disbelief: wailing and defaming lineage."
"8893","Aswad narrated to us: Abu Bakr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abi Salama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection as a salt-white ram, and it will be said: O people of Paradise, do you know this. So they will look out fearful, apprehensive. He said: They will say: Yes. He said: Then the people of the Fire will be called: Do you know this. So they will say: Yes. He said: So he will be slaughtered, then it will be said: Eternity in Paradise and eternity in the Fire."
"8894","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Asim, from Abi Salih, from Abu Hurayra, the like of it, except that he added in it: He will be brought upon the Sirat and slaughtered."
"8895","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash informed me: Abu Husayn informed us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity is not lawful for a rich one, nor for one of sound strength."
"8896","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Abi Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The caller to prayer is trusted, and the imam is liable. O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the callers to prayer."
"8897","Qutayba ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Usayd ibn Abi Usayd, from Nafi ibn Abbas, freedman of Aqila bint Talq al-Ghifariya, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves to encircle his beloved with a ring of fire, let him make for him a ring of gold. And whoever loves to necklace his beloved with a necklace of fire, let him necklace him with a necklace of gold. And whoever loves to bracelet his beloved with a bracelet of fire, let him bracelet him with a bracelet of gold. But upon you is silver, so play with it."
"8898","Qutayba narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire the Fire, a caller will call: O people of Paradise, eternity with no death in it, and O people of the Fire, eternity with no death in it."
"8899","Qutayba ibn Said narrated to us, from Layth, from al-Julah Abi Kathir, from al-Mughira ibn Abi Burda, from Abu Hurayra, that people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: We go far in the sea and carry of water only a water-skin and two water-skins, because we do not find game until we go far. So may we perform ablution with sea water. He said: Yes, for its dead is lawful, its water is purifying."
"8900","Qutayba narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Thawr, from Abi al-Ghayth, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first to be called on the Day of Resurrection is Adam, so it will be said: This is your father Adam. So he will say: O Lord, at Your service and blessedness. So our Lord will say to him: Bring out the share of Hell from your offspring. So he will say: O Lord, and how many. So He will say: From every hundred, ninety-nine. So we said: O Messenger of Allah, have you seen, when taken from us from every hundred ninety-nine, what will remain of us. He said: My nation among nations is like a white hair in a black bull."
"8901","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Abu Suhayl ibn Malik from his father from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Ramadan begins, the gates of the Fire are closed, the gates of Paradise are opened, and the devils are chained."
"8902","Qutaybah narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Suhayl from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not make your houses graveyards, and indeed the house in which Surat al-Baqarah is recited, Satan does not enter it."
"8903","Qutaybah narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us from Suhayl from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), meaning he said to some women of the Ansar: There is none among you whose three children die and she seeks reward for them except she will enter Paradise. So a woman among them said: Or two, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Or two."
"8904","And with this chain of transmission that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Over the mountain passes of Madinah are angels; neither plague nor the Dajjal shall enter it."
"8905","My father said: And with this chain of transmission that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you travel in fertile land, give the camels their share of the land, and when you travel in a year of drought, hasten them along while their marrow remains, and when you halt for the night, avoid the roads, for they are the paths of beasts and the shelter of vermin by night."
"8906","Qutaybah narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall be no severance beyond three."
"8907","My father said: And with this chain of transmission that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among people sitting and said: Shall I not inform you of the best of you from the worst of you? He said: So they fell silent. So he said that three times. So a man said: O Prophet of Allah, inform us of our best from our worst. He said: The best of you is he whose good is hoped for and whose evil is safe from, and the worst of you is he whose good is not hoped for and whose evil is not safe from."
"8908","With this chain of transmission that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The disbeliever and his killer shall never meet together in the Fire, ever."
"8909","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us from Yazid ibn al-Had from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A servant speaks a word by which he slips into the Fire farther than what is between the east and the west."
"8910","Qutaybah narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us from Suhayl from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This Fire is one part of a hundred parts of Hell."
"8911","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us from Ibn al-Had from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Have you considered, if there were a river at the door of one of you in which he bathed five times every day, what would you say, would any of his dirt remain? They said: None of his dirt would remain. He said: That is the likeness of the five prayers; Allah wipes out sins by them."
"8912","Qutaybah narrated to us: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibn al-Had narrated to us, and he mentioned the like of it; he did not say: He heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8913","Qutaybah narrated to us: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith is sixty-four doors; the highest and loftiest of them is the saying: There is no god but Allah, and the lowest of them is removing harm from the road."
"8914","Qutaybah narrated to us: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the people: Perfect your prayer, for I see you behind me as I see you in front of me."
"8915","Qutaybah narrated to us: Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us from Uqayl from al-Zuhri from Ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A believer is not stung from one hole twice."
"8916","Qutaybah narrated to us: Layth narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan from Said al-Maqburi and al-Qaqa ibn Hakim from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A dirham preceded two dirhams. They said: And how is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A man had two dirhams and gave one of them in charity, then a man went to his vast wealth and took from it a hundred thousand dirhams and gave them in charity."
"8917","Qutaybah narrated to us: Layth narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall remain over this affair a group upon the truth; the opposition of whoever opposes them shall not harm them until the command of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, comes to them while they are upon that."
"8918","Qutaybah narrated to us: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan from al-Qaqa from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Muslim is he from whose tongue and hand people are safe, and the believer is he whom people trust with their blood and their wealth."
"8919","And with this chain of transmission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Over every soul of the children of Adam is written its share of adultery, which it shall inevitably meet: the eye, its adultery is looking, and the ears, their adultery is listening, and the hand, its adultery is grasping, and the foot, its adultery is walking, and the tongue, its adultery is speech, and the heart desires and wishes, and the private part confirms that or denies it."
"8920","And with this chain of transmission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The hoard of one of them shall on the Day of Resurrection be a bald venomous snake with two black spots, following its owner while he seeks refuge from it, and it shall keep following him until it puts his finger into its mouth."
"8921","And with this chain of transmission that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The heart of the old man is young in love of two things: long life and abundance of wealth."
"8922","Muhammad ibn Idris, meaning al-Shafii, narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban and Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mulamasah and munabadhah."
"8923","Muhammad ibn Idris narrated to us: Malik informed us from Musa ibn Abi Tamim from Said ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dinar for dinar and dirham for dirham, with no excess between them."
"8924","Muhammad ibn Idris narrated to us: Malik informed us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you sell over the sale of another, and let no town-dweller sell for a Bedouin, and do not artificially inflate prices, and do not intercept goods."
"8925","And he said: The delay of the rich in paying is injustice, and when one of you is referred to a solvent person, let him accept the transfer."
"8926","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ibn Luhayah narrated to us from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Isa ibn Talhah from Abu Hurayrah that Khawlah bint Yasar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have only one garment and I menstruate in it, so what shall I do? He said: When you become pure, wash it, then pray in it. She said: What if the blood does not come out? He said: Water suffices you, and its trace shall not harm you."
"8927","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ibn Luhayah narrated to us from Musa ibn Wardan from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer wears out his devils as one of you wears out his camel on a journey."
"8928","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us: Ibn Luhayah narrated to us from Yazid ibn Abi Amr from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The makers of images who make them shall be punished by them on the Day of Resurrection; it shall be said to them: Give life to what you created."
"8929","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us: Ibn Luhayah narrated to us from al-Harith ibn Yazid from Thabit ibn al-Harith from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith is Yemeni, understanding is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni. The people of Yemen have come to you; they are the most tender of hearts and the softest of hearts. And disbelief is toward the east, and pride and arrogance are among the people of horses and camels and the clamorous owners of wool, and tranquility is among the people of sheep."
"8930","Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Luhayah narrated to us from Abu Yunus from Abu Hurayrah who said: I never saw anything more beautiful than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as if the sun coursed in his face, and I never saw anyone quicker in his walk than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as if the earth were folded for him; we would exert ourselves while he was untroubled."
"8931","Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Luhayah narrated to us from Abu al-Aswad from Yahya ibn al-Nadr from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and the Fire is surrounded by desires."
"8932","Qutaybah narrated to us: Ibn Luhayah narrated to us from Darraj from Ibn Hujayrah from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Travel and you will be healthy, and raid and you will gain riches."
"8933","Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The heart of the old man is young in love of two: long life and abundance of wealth."
"8934","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Tahla from Muhsin ibn Ali from Awf ibn al-Harith from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution and perfects his ablution, then sets out and finds the people have already prayed, Allah shall give him the like of the reward of whoever prayed it or attended it, without diminishing anything from their rewards."
"8935","Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us from Muawiyah ibn Salih from Abu Talhah from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever guest alights among a people and the guest wakes deprived, he may take to the measure of his hospitality, with no blame upon him."
"8936","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, he said: Abu Zubayd informed us from al-Amash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two garments and two sales. As for the two garments, that he wraps himself in his garment exposing its side, or squats in a single garment exposing his private part to the sky. And as for the two sales, mulamasah: throw to me and I throw to you, and throwing the stone."
"8937","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Zubayd informed us from al-Amash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: When a funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would ask them: Is there a debt upon him? If they said yes, he said: Did he leave means to pay it? If they said yes, he prayed over him; otherwise he said: Pray over your companion."
"8938","Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Zuhri narrated to us, and he was of al-Qarah, and he is an ally, from Amr ibn Abi Amr from Ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab from Abu Hurayrah that they were carrying bricks for building the mosque, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among them. He said: So I faced the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was laying a brick upon his belly, and I thought it had distressed him. I said: Hand it to me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Take another, O Abu Hurayrah, for there is no life but the life of the Hereafter."
"8939","Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ajlan from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was only sent to perfect noble morals."
"8940","Said ibn Mansur and Qutaybah both said: Yaqub ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Abu Hazim from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is hearing and obeying in your hardship and your ease, your eagerness and your aversion, and in preference over you. And Qutaybah said: Obedience, and he did not say: Hearing."
"8941","Said ibn Mansur narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Isa ibn Numaylah al-Fazari from his father who said: I was with Ibn Umar when he was asked about eating the hedgehog, so he recited this verse: Say: I do not find in what was revealed to me anything forbidden, to the end of the verse. So an old man with him said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: It was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: A filthy one among filthy things. So Ibn Umar said: If the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it, then it is as he said it."
"8942","Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan narrated to me from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prostrates, let him not kneel as the camel kneels; let him place his hands then his knees."
"8943","Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father from Abu Hurayrah who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) congratulated a person, he said: May Allah bless for you and bless upon you and join between you in good."
"8944","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he congratulated a person when he married, said: May Allah bless for you and bless upon you and join between you in good."
"8945","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us from his father from Qatadah from Abu Rafi from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created His creation, He wrote: My mercy has overcome, or: has preceded, My anger; it is with Him upon the Throne."
"8946","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us: Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Mamar informed us from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has a supplication; I intend, if Allah wills, to reserve my supplication on the Day of Resurrection as intercession for my nation."
"8947","Affan narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us: Suhayl narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he would say when he went to his bed: O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the earth and Lord of everything, Splitter of the grain and the seed, Revealer of the Torah, the Gospel, and the Quran, I seek refuge in You from the evil of every possessor of evil whose forelock You hold. You are the First, and there is nothing before You, and You are the Last, and there is nothing after You, and You are the Manifest, and there is nothing above You, and You are the Hidden, and there is nothing beneath You. Settle my debt for me and enrich me from poverty."
"8948","Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us: Suhayl narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: One of you gives a date in charity from good earnings and places it in its right place, and Allah takes it with His right hand, then He keeps raising it as the best of what one of you raises his foal, until it becomes like the mountain or greater than the mountain."
"8949","My father said: And he narrated also, meaning Affan, from Khalid, I think al-Wasiti, with its chain and its meaning, except that he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, accepts it with His right hand."
"8950","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Sad ibn Ibrahim from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: While a man was riding a cow, it turned to him and said to him: I was not created for this; I was only created for plowing. He said: So I believed in it, I and Abu Bakr and Umar. He said: And a wolf seized a sheep and the shepherd followed it, so the wolf said: Who will guard it on the day of the beast of prey, the day when it has no shepherd but me? He said: So I believed in it, I and Abu Bakr and Umar. Abu Salamah said: And they were not that day among the people."
"8951","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Sad ibn Ibrahim, he said: I heard Abu Salamah narrating from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Approach the prayer with tranquility upon you; pray what you catch and make up what preceded you."
"8952","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes from his sleep, let him pour upon his hands from his vessel three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night. So Qays al-Ashjai said: O Abu Hurayrah, what if one of our basins comes? He said: I seek refuge in Allah from your evil, O Qays."
"8953","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Sad ibn Ibrahim, he said: I heard Abu Salamah narrating from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Approach the prayer with tranquility upon you; pray what you catch and make up what preceded you."
"8954","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us from al-Hasan, he said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the call is made for prayer, do not come to it running, but walk with tranquility upon you; what you catch, pray, and what preceded you, make up."
"8955","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of that."
"8956","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Humayd from Bakr from Abu Rafi from Abu Hurayrah who said: I met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was impure, so I walked with him until he sat, then I slipped away and went to the lodging and bathed, then I came while he was sitting. He said: Where were you? I said: You met me while I was impure, so I disliked sitting with you while I was impure, so I went and bathed. He said: Glory be to Allah, the believer never becomes impure."
"8957","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrating from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade the earnings of slave women."
"8958","Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us from al-Amash who said: It was narrated to me from Abu Salih, and I think I heard it, from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The imam is a guarantor and the caller to prayer is entrusted. O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the callers to prayer."
"8959","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: Abu Jafar, meaning al-Razi, narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The grazing animal is exempt, the well is exempt, the mine is exempt, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"8960","Affan narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us: Suhayl narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has roaming angels of merit who seek gatherings of remembrance, and when they find a gathering in which there is remembrance, they sit with them, and some of them enfold others with their wings until they fill what is between them and the heaven of the world. Then when they disperse, they ascend or rise to the heaven. He said: So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, asks them, and He knows best: From where have you come? So they say: We have come to You from servants of Yours on earth who glorify You and magnify You and praise You and declare Your oneness and ask You. He said: And what do they ask Me? They say: They ask You for Your Paradise. He said: And have they seen My Paradise? They say: No, O Lord. He said: So how if they had seen My Paradise? They say: And they seek refuge with You. He said: From what do they seek refuge with Me? They say: From Your Fire, O Lord. He said: And have they seen My Fire? They say: No. They say: And they seek Your forgiveness. He said: So He says: I have forgiven them, and given them what they asked, and sheltered them from what they sought shelter from. He said: So they say: Lord, among them is so-and-so, a sinful servant; he only passed and sat with them. He said: So He says: I have forgiven them; they are the people whose companion shall not be wretched."
"8961","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Humayd al-Tawil from al-Hasan and others from Abu Hurayrah who said, and I know it only from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Isa, peace be upon him, saw a man stealing and said to him: O so-and-so, did you steal? He said: No, by Allah, I did not steal. He said: I believe in Allah and I disbelieve my sight."
"8962","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Agharr Abu Muslim who said: I bear witness upon Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said that they bore witness upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Allah grants respite until a third of the night has gone, then He descends and says: Is there any caller, so he is answered? Is there any seeker of forgiveness, so he is forgiven? And Affan said: Abu Awanah had narrated to us hadiths from Abu Ishaq, then it reached me afterward that he said: I heard them from Israil, and I think this hadith is among them."
"8963","Affan narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Jabbar, a man of the Ansar, informed me, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi narrating that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The womb is a branch from the Most Merciful; it says: O Lord, I have been cut, O Lord, I have been wronged, O Lord, I have been ill-treated, O Lord, O Lord. He said: So He answers it: Are you not pleased that I join whoever joins you and cut whoever cuts you?"
"8964","Affan narrated to us: Abd al-Warith narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you is sitting in the sun and it recedes from him, let him move from his sitting place."
"8965","Affan narrated to us: Wuhayb ibn Khalid al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Suhayl narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no owner of a hoard who does not pay its alms except he shall be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hoard, and plates shall be heated for him in the fire of Hell, and his forehead and his side and his back shall be branded with them, until Allah judges between His servants in a day whose measure is fifty thousand years of what you count, then he shall see his way, either to Paradise or to the Fire. And there is no owner of camels who does not pay their alms except he shall be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his camels in their fullest state, and a wide plain shall be spread for them, and whenever the last of them passes, the first of them shall be returned upon him, until Allah judges between His servants in a day whose measure is fifty thousand years of what you count, then he shall see his way, either to Paradise or to the Fire. And there is no owner of sheep who does not pay their alms except he shall be brought with his sheep on the Day of Resurrection in their fullest state, and a wide plain shall be spread for them, and they shall trample him with their hooves and butt him with their horns, and whenever the last of them passes, the first of them shall be returned upon him, until Allah judges between His servants in a day whose measure is fifty thousand years of what you count, then he shall see his way, either to Paradise or to the Fire. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what of horses? He said: Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection. And horses are three: for a man a reward, for a man a shelter, and upon a man a burden. As for what is for him a reward, the one who takes them and keeps them in the path of Allah; whatever they conceal in their bellies is for him a reward, and if they run from him a hill or two hills, for every step they take is for him a reward, and if a river presents itself to him and he waters them from it, for every drop they conceal in their bellies is for him a reward, until he mentioned the reward in their dung and their urine. And as for what is for him a shelter, a man who takes them for continence and adornment and honor, without forgetting their right upon their backs and their bellies in their hardship and their ease. And as for what is upon him a burden, a man who takes them in insolence and pride and showing off before people and extravagance against them. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what of donkeys? He said: Nothing was sent down to me concerning them except this comprehensive unique verse: So whoever does an atom of good shall see it, and whoever does an atom of evil shall see it."
"8966","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Suhayl from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) something like all of this speech."
"8967","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar al-Ghudani narrated, Affan said: with this hadith."
"8968","Affan narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid, meaning Ibn Ziyad, narrated to us, he said: Umarah ibn al-Qaqa narrated to us: Abu Zurah, whose name is Harim ibn Amr ibn Jarir, narrated to us that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has undertaken for whoever goes out in His path, whom nothing brings out but striving in the path of Allah and belief in Me and affirmation of My messengers, that it is upon Me as guarantor to admit him to Paradise or return him to the dwelling from which he went out, attaining what he attained of reward or spoils."
"8969","He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no wounded one wounded in the path of Allah except he shall come on the Day of Resurrection in the state he was in the day he was wounded, his wound bleeding, the color the color of blood and the scent the scent of musk."
"8970","And with its chain he said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose hand is my soul, were it not that I would burden my nation, I would not stay behind any expedition going out in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic; but I do not find what to carry them on, nor do they find room to follow me, nor would their souls be content to stay behind me."
"8971","He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I would love to raid in the path of Allah and be killed, then raid and be killed, then raid and be killed."
"8972","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Yahya ibn Said informed us from Said ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to a town that consumes towns and expels filth as the bellows expels the dross of iron."
"8973","Affan narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: al-Ala narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he was asked: What is backbiting, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Your mentioning your brother with what he dislikes. He said: What if what I say is in my brother, O Messenger of Allah? He said: If what you say is in your brother, you have backbitten him, and if what you say is not in him, you have slandered him."
"8974","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us from Abu Uthman that Abu Hurayrah was on a journey; when they alighted, they sent to him while he was praying to come eat. So he said to the messengers: I am fasting. Then when the food was set and they were about to finish, he came and began eating. So the people looked at their messenger, who said: Why do you look? He told me he was fasting. So Abu Hurayrah said: He spoke truthfully. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Fasting the month of patience and three days of every month is fasting the lifetime. I have fasted three days of every month, and I am breaking fast by the alleviation of Allah and fasting by the multiplication of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"8975","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Amr from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the saying of Lut: If only I had power over you or could take refuge in a strong support. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He was taking refuge in a strong support, his Lord, Mighty and Majestic. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And no prophet was sent after him except among the influential part of his people."
"8976","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Amr from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: If she is pleased, hers is her pleasure, and if she dislikes, there is no validity over her, meaning the orphan girl."
"8977","Affan narrated to us: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid, the companion of al-Ziyadi, narrated to us from a shaykh of Basrah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, who said: There is no Muslim servant who dies and three households of his nearest neighbors bear witness for him with good except Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: I have accepted the testimony of My servants for what they knew, and I have forgiven him for what I know."
"8978","Affan narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us: Suhayl narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Khaybar: I shall surely hand the banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, through whom Allah shall grant conquest. He said: So Umar said: I never loved command before that day; I stretched for it and looked up hoping he would hand it to me. Then on the morrow he called Ali, peace be upon him, and handed it to him and said: Fight and do not turn until conquest is granted you. So he went a little, then called: O Messenger of Allah, over what shall I fight? He said: Until they bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then if they do that, they have protected from me their blood and their wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"8979","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us: Ayyub informed us from Abu Qilabah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, giving glad tidings to his companions: The month of Ramadan has come to you, a blessed month; Allah has obligated its fasting upon you; in it the gates of Paradise are opened and the gates of Hell are closed and the devils are chained; in it is a night better than a thousand months; whoever is deprived of its good has been deprived."
"8980","Affan narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us with this chain the like of it."
"8981","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Amr from Abu al-Hakam from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prize except in a light mount or a hoof."
"8982","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit informed us from Abu Rafi from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was among the children of Israil a man called Jurayj who worshipped in his hermitage. His mother came to him one day and called him, saying: O Jurayj, O my son, look upon me so I may speak to you; I am your mother, look upon me. He said: O Lord, my prayer or my mother? So he turned to his prayer. Then she returned and called him repeatedly, saying: O Jurayj, O my son, look upon me. He said: O Lord, my prayer or my mother? So he turned to his prayer. So she said: O Allah, do not cause him to die until You show him the prostitute. And there was a shepherdess who grazed sheep for her people, then sheltered in the shade of his hermitage, and she committed adultery and was seized, and she became pregnant, and whoever of them committed adultery was killed. They said: From whom? She said: From Jurayj, the man of the hermitage. So they came with axes and picks and said: O Jurayj, O show-off. Then they said: Come down. So he refused and turned to his prayer, praying. So they began demolishing his hermitage. When he saw that, he came down, and they put a rope around his neck and her neck and began parading them among the people. So he placed his finger upon her belly and said: O boy, who is your father? He said: My father is so-and-so, the shepherd of sheep. So they kissed him and said: If you wish, we shall build your hermitage for you of gold and silver. He said: Return it as it was."
"8983","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Nadr ibn Anas from Bashir ibn Nahik from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man goes bankrupt and his creditor finds his goods with the bankrupt in their very form, he has most right to them."
"8984","Ali ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from Qatadah from Khilas ibn Amr from Abu Rafi, meaning the goldsmith, from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer has two wives, the marrow of whose legs is seen from above their garments."
"8985","Ali narrated to us, he said: Muadh narrated to us: My father narrated to me from Qatadah from al-Nadr ibn Anas from Bashir ibn Nahik from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever peeks into a house of a people without their permission and they gouge out his eye, there is no blood-money for him nor retaliation."
"8986","Ali narrated to us: Muadh narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from Qatadah from Zurarah ibn Awfa from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell."
"8987","Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Safwan narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed me from Ibn Shihab, he said: Said ibn al-Musayyab informed me that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You shall surely leave Madinah upon the best it was, made easy for beasts, meaning predators and birds."
"8988","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ali ibn Zayd, he said: One who heard Abu Hurayrah narrated to me, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A tyrant of the tyrants of Banu Umayyah shall surely ascend this pulpit of mine."
"8989","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Hammad, and Thabit from al-Hasan from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan with faith and seeking reward, forgiven for him is what preceded of his sin and what follows."
"8990","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us from Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah who said: I heard Abul Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: By the One in Whose hand is my soul, there is none among you whose deed admits him to Paradise. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even me, except that Allah envelops me from Him with mercy and bounty. And he placed his hand upon his head."
"8991","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ziyad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone."
"8992","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah does not look at him who drags his waist-wrap out of pride."
"8993","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The grazing animal is exempt, the well is exempt, the mine is exempt, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"8994","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ziyad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever buys a sheep whose milk was retained, he has the choice: if he wishes he returns it with a measure of dates."
"8995","Bahz and Affan both said: Hammam narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan and Ata from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He does not steal while he steals while he is a believer, nor commit adultery while he commits it while he is a believer, nor drink wine while he drinks it while he is a believer, nor embezzle while he embezzles while he is a believer, nor plunder while he plunders while he is a believer. And Ata said: Nor plunder a plunder of repute while he is a believer. Bahz said: So it was said to him. He said: Faith is stripped from him; if he repents, Allah turns to him. And Affan said in his hadith: Qatadah said: And in the hadith of Ata: A plunder of repute while he is a believer."
"8996","Affan narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Charity does not diminish wealth, and Allah does not increase a man by pardon except honor, and none humbles himself for Allah except Allah, Mighty and Majestic, raises him."
"8997","And with this chain and wording from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he was asked: What is backbiting, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Your mentioning your brother with what he dislikes. He said: What if what I say is in my brother, O Messenger of Allah? He said: If what you say is in your brother, you have backbitten him, and if what you say is not in him, you have slandered him."
"8998","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us from Sad ibn Ibrahim that he heard Abu Salamah narrating from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr two cycles then greeted. They said: The prayer was shortened. He said: So he stood and prayed two cycles then greeted, then prostrated two prostrations after he greeted."
"8999","Bahz narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Sad ibn Ibrahim from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Approach the prayer with tranquility upon you; pray what you catch and make up what preceded you."
"9000","Bahz narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Sad ibn Ibrahim narrated to me from al-Agharr from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in other mosques except the Kabah."
"9001","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, he said: I heard Zurarah ibn Awfa narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a woman spends the night abandoning her husband's bed, the angels curse her until she returns."
"9002","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed me, he said: I heard Umarah ibn Umayr from Abu al-Mutawwis from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever breaks the fast one day in Ramadan without a concession Allah granted him, then fasting the whole of time will never compensate for it."
"9003","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Yala ibn Ata informed us from Abu Alqamah, and Abu Awanah al-Ansari said, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah, and whoever obeys the commander has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys the commander has disobeyed me, and the commander is a shield. So when he says Allahu Akbar, say Allahu Akbar, and when he bows, bow, and when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: O Allah our Lord, to You is praise. For if that coincides with the saying of the angels, you will be forgiven. And if he prays sitting, pray sitting."
"9004","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Yala ibn Ata from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman that Abu Hurayrah narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever prays over it and follows it has two qirats. Abdullah ibn Umar said to him: Consider what you narrate, O Abu Hurayrah, for you narrate much from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he took his hand and went with him to Aishah, and she confirmed Abu Hurayrah. Abu Hurayrah said: By Allah, O Abu Abd al-Rahman, haggling in the markets never kept me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Nothing concerned me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except a word he would teach me or a morsel he would feed me."
"9005","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Yazid ibn Khumayr from a freedman of Quraysh from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade selling the spoils of war until they are divided, and selling fruit until it is secured against every blight, and that a man pray until he girds himself."
"9006","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Abu Imran from Abu Hurayrah that a man complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the hardness of his heart, so he said: Wipe the head of the orphan and feed the poor."
"9007","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us from Umar ibn Abi Salamah from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever takes a span of land without right will have it hung around him from seven earths."
"9008","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us from Umar ibn Abi Salamah from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: They are days of eating. Abu Awanah said, meaning the days of al-Tashriq."
"9009","And with this isnad he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is al-tiyarah? He said: No bird, three times. And he said: The best of good omens is the good word."
"9010","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Umar ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you hears the iqamah, let him come with tranquility upon him. What he catches, let him pray, and what he misses, let him complete."
"9011","And with this isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed the briber and the bribed in judgment."
"9012","And with this isnad from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you wishes, let him consider what it is he wishes, for he does not know what will be written for him of his wish."
"9013","And with this isnad from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: This Uhud here is a mountain that loves us and we love it. My father said: In all of them, in these four, he said: Umar ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us."
"9014","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us from Umar ibn Abi Salamah from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Trim the mustaches and leave the beards full."
"9015","And with this isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They will keep asking until it is said: This is Allah who created us, so who created Allah Almighty? He said: Abu Hurayrah said: By Allah, I was sitting one day when a man from the people of Iraq said to me: This is Allah who created us, so who created Allah Almighty? Abu Hurayrah said: So I put my fingers in my ears, then I shouted and said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. Allah, the One, the Eternal: He neither begets nor is born, and there is none like Him."
"9016","And with this isnad that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty is jealous, and part of the jealousy of Allah is that the believer commits what is forbidden to him."
"9017","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Umar ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you cleans himself with stones, let him make it odd."
"9018","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us from Umar ibn Abi Salamah from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the slave runs away, and once he said: When he steals, then sell him even for a nashsh, and the nashsh is half an uqiyah."
"9019","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed the briber and the bribed in judgment."
"9020","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Umar ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three, each of them a duty upon every Muslim: visiting the sick, attending the funeral, and blessing the sneezer when he praises Allah Almighty."
"9021","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us from Sulayman al-Amash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Most of the punishment of the grave is from urine."
"9022","Affan narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi ibn Muslim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He does not thank Allah who does not thank people."
"9023","Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us from Sad ibn Ibrahim from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Quraysh and the Ansar and Aslam and Ghifar and Muzaynah and Juhaynah and Ashja are my allies; they have no ally besides Allah and His Messenger."
"9024","Affan narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, he said: Thumamah ibn Abd Allah ibn Anas informed us, and Affan once said: Thumamah claimed that, from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and from Habib ibn al-Shahid from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, let him dip it, for in one of its wings is disease and in the other is cure. And Affan once said: For one of its wings."
"9025","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us from Abu Rafi from Abu Hurayrah that a black person who used to sweep the mosque died, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed her, so he said: What happened to the person who used to sweep the mosque? It was said to him: She died. He said: Why did you not inform me of her? They said: It was nighttime. He said: Show me her grave. So he came to the grave and prayed over her. Thabit said: At that point, or in another hadith: These graves are full of darkness upon their people, and Allah Almighty illuminates them by my prayer over them."
"9026","Affan narrated to us, Khalifah ibn Ghalib al-Laythi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was with him and asked him, saying: O Prophet of Allah, which deeds are best? He said: Faith in Allah and jihad in the path of Allah. He said: If I cannot do that? He said: Then which necks are greatest in reward? He said: The most expensive in price and the most precious to its owners. He said: If I cannot? He said: Then you help one in need or do for one lacking skill. He said: If I cannot do that? He said: Then restrain yourself from evil, for it is a good charity you give in charity to yourself."
"9027","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Isl ibn Sufyan narrated to us from Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No star ever rises in the morning while a blight stands except it is lifted from them or lightened."
"9028","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us from a man from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a voice and it pleased him, so he said: We have taken our good omen from your mouth."
"9029","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us that Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of Umm Burthun, narrated from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah prescribed Friday for those before us, but they differed, and Allah guided us to it. So people follow us in it: the Jews have tomorrow and the Christians the day after tomorrow."
"9030","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not make your houses graves, for Satan flees from the house in which al-Baqarah is recited."
"9031","And with this isnad from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If you speak on Friday, you have engaged in idle talk and caused cancellation."
"9032","And with this isnad that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes a span of land without right will have it hung around him from seven earths."
"9033","And with this isnad that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant covers a servant in this world except Allah will cover him on the Day of Resurrection."
"9034","And with this isnad from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Woe to the heels from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection. My father said about all of them: Suhayl narrated to us thus; thus my father said it."
"9035","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah and Wuhayb narrated to us, both said: Suhayl narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you stands from his seat then returns to it, he has more right to it."
"9036","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: For one of you to sit upon an ember so it burns his clothes until it reaches him is better than for him to step upon the grave of a Muslim man."
"9037","And with this isnad that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a sheep's shoulder, then rinsed his mouth and washed his hand and prayed."
"9038","And with this isnad that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a lump of dried yogurt and performed ablution from it and prayed."
"9039","And with this isnad that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not hate one another, nor turn your backs on one another, nor desert one another, and be servants of Allah, brothers."
"9040","And with this isnad from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No people gather then disperse from other than the remembrance of Allah except as if they dispersed from the carcass of a donkey, and that sitting will be a regret upon them."
"9041","And with this isnad from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The gates of heaven are opened every Monday and Thursday, and on that day every servant who does not associate anything with Allah is forgiven, except a man between whom and his brother is enmity. So it is said: Delay these two until they reconcile."
"9042","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Ala narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Religion began strange and will return strange as it began, so glad tidings to the strangers."
"9043","And with this isnad from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The world is the prison of the believer and the paradise of the disbeliever."
"9044","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim al-Qass narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no disease except in the black seed is cure for it, except death."
"9045","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Tawus narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The parable of the miser and the giver of charity is the parable of two men wearing two cloaks of iron whose hands are forced to their collarbones. Whenever the giver of charity intends a charity, it expands over him until it covers his traces, and whenever the miser intends a charity, every ring of it contracts upon its fellow and shrinks upon him. He said: So I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), meaning he says: So he strives to widen it, but it does not widen."
"9046","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musab ibn Muhammad ibn Shurahbil narrated to us from Abu Salih al-Samman from Abu Hurayrah, he said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, will we see our Lord Almighty on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Do you see the sun at midday when there is no cloud in the sky? They said: Yes. He said: Do you see the moon on the night of full moon when there is no cloud in the sky? They said: Yes. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you will surely see Allah Almighty, and you will not be harmed in seeing Him, just as you are not harmed in seeing them."
"9047","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us from Sulayman al-Amash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Most of the punishment of the grave is from urine."
"9048","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning His Almighty saying: Ask him what about the women who cut their hands. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I been there, I would have hastened the answer and would not have sought the excuse."
"9049","Aswad ibn Amir and Husayn both said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Abu Husayn, and Yahya ibn Ishaq: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Abu Husayn narrated to us from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity is not lawful for a rich person nor for one of sound strength."
"9050","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Abu Husayn from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Richness is not from abundance of goods, but richness is richness of the soul."
"9051","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us from Mujahid from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Gabriel, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I came last night, and nothing prevented me from entering upon you except that there was a picture or a dog in the house."
"9052","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: Abu Hurayrah informed me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you will be admitted to Paradise by his deed, nor saved from the Fire, except by mercy and favor from Allah. He said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, not even you? He said: Not even I, unless Allah envelops me with mercy from Him. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said with his hand, closing it and opening it."
"9053","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Zayd, my uncle, narrated to us, he said: I was sitting with Salim ibn Abd Allah at the gate of Madinah when a young man of Quraysh passed as if his waist-wrapper hung loose. He said: Lift your waist-wrapper. He kept apologizing, saying it hung loose and it is of linen. When he passed, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: While a man walks in a suit of his, admiring himself, Allah sank the earth with him, and he rumbles in it until the Day of Resurrection."
"9054","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Dhawwad Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us from Layth from Mujahid from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I never came early except I found the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying. He said: So he prayed, then said: Ishkamat dard. I said: No. He said: Stand and pray, for in prayer is healing."
"9055","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us from Abu al-Muhazzim from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Madinah will surely leave Madinah when it is at its best, moist and fruitful. It was said: Who will eat it? He said: Birds and beasts."
"9056","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from a man from Abu Zarah from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the charity of my people, and they are the sternest of people against the Dajjal, meaning Banu Tamim. Abu Hurayrah said: No people among the tribes were more hateful to me than them, but I have loved them since I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say this."
"9057","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Israil narrated to us from al-Amash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Excellent for the slave when he fulfills the right of Allah and the right of his masters. Kab said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth: there is no reckoning upon him nor upon a believing ascetic."
"9058","Aswad narrated to us, Israil narrated to us from al-Amash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I am only a human, so whichever Muslim I cursed or harmed, make it purification and nearness for him."
"9059","Ibn Numayr narrated it to us, he said: al-Amash informed us that he said: purification and mercy."
"9060","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us from Darraj Abu al-Samh from Ibn Hujayrah from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, everything will dispute on the Day of Resurrection, even the two sheep over wherein they butted."
"9061","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us from Abu Yunus from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the Arabs from an approaching evil, trials like patches of dark night. A man wakes a believer and sleeps a disbeliever. People sell their religion for a little worldly gain. The one holding to his religion that day is like one grasping an ember, or he said: thorns. Hasan said in his hadith: the tangles of thorns."
"9062","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us from Abu Yunus from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I take with You a covenant You will not break for me: I am only a human, so whichever servant I flogged or insulted or reviled, make it prayer and nearness for him."
"9063","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us from Abu Yunus, and Hasan said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Abu Yunus narrated to us from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the Arabs from an approaching evil, trials like patches of dark night. A man wakes a believer and sleeps a disbeliever. People sell their religion for a little worldly gain. The one holding to his religion that day is like one grasping an ember, or he said: thorns. Hasan said in his hadith: the tangles of thorns."
"9064","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Abu Yunus narrated to us from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The much-wealthy are the least on the Day of Resurrection, except one who says with wealth thus and thus and thus. Yahya said: And few are they. Hasan said: And he gestured between his eyes and to his right and to his left and behind him."
"9065","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu Yunus narrated to us from Abu Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that Allah Almighty said: I am with My servant's expectation of Me. If he expects good from Me, it is for him, and if he expects evil, it is for him."
"9066","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us from Yazid ibn Amr, he said: I heard Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman say: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty said: Who is more unjust than one who intends to create like My creation? Then let him create an atom or a grain. And Yahya once said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Who is more."
"9067","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan, meaning Ibn Salih, narrated to us from Ibn Abi Layla from Ata from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you sacrifices, let him eat from his sacrifice."
"9068","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us from al-Harith ibn Yazid from Abu Alqamah from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are mines. The best of them in ignorance are the best of them in Islam when they understand the religion."
"9069","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from Muhammad, the seller of garments, from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When: A multitude from the former and a few from the latter was revealed, that was hard upon the Muslims, so: A multitude from the former and a multitude from the latter was revealed. So he said: You are a third of the people of Paradise; rather you are half of the people of Paradise, and you share with them the remaining half."
"9070","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from Umarah ibn al-Qaqa from Abu Zarah from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of the most deserving people of my companionship. So he said: Yes, by Allah, you shall be informed. He said: Who? He said: Your mother. He said: Then who? He said: Then your mother. He said: Then who? He said: Then your father."
"9071","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from Umarah ibn al-Qaqa from Abu Zarah from Abu Hurayrah, raising the hadith, he said: Who is more unjust than one who creates creatures like My creation? Then let them create like My creation an atom or a fly or a grain."
"9072","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from Ibn Umayr, meaning Abd al-Malik, from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said upon the pulpit: The truest verse the Arabs spoke is: Indeed everything besides Allah is false. And Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt almost accepted Islam."
"9073","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from al-Amash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, raising it, he said: You will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not guide you to the head of that, or the essence of that? Spread peace among yourselves. And perhaps Sharik said: Shall I not guide you to something which, if you do it, you will love one another? Spread peace among yourselves."
"9074","And Ibn Numayr narrated it to us from al-Amash with its meaning."
"9075","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from al-Amash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the belly of one of you to fill with pus that oozes is better for him than to fill with poetry."
"9076","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from al-Amash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever is wounded in the path of Allah, and Allah knows best who is wounded in His path, the wound comes with its color the color of blood and its smell the smell of musk."
"9077","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from Suhayl from his father from Abu Hurayrah, raising it: He forbade muhaqalah, which is buying crops while in their ears with wheat, and he forbade muzabanah, which is buying fruits with dates."
"9078","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from Suhayl from his father from Abu Hurayrah, raising it, he said: The angels do not accompany a group in which there is a bell."
"9079","Aswad ibn Amir Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from Layth from Tawus from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: People will be raised, and perhaps Sharik said: People will be gathered, according to their intentions."
"9080","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us in the explanation of Shayban from Qatadah, he said: al-Hasan narrated from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Children of Israel used to bathe naked, and the Prophet of Allah Moses, peace be upon him, had modesty and covering, and he would cover himself when he bathed. So they accused him of a defect. He said: So while the Prophet of Allah Moses, peace be upon him, was bathing one day, he placed his clothes upon a rock, and the rock ran off with his clothes. So the Prophet of Allah followed it, striking it with his staff, saying: My garment, O stone; my garment, O stone, until he ended up at a gathering of the Children of Israel and stood among them. So it stopped, and the Prophet of Allah took his clothes, and they looked, and behold he was the best of people in form and the most just in appearance. So the Children of Israel said: May Allah destroy the liars of the Children of Israel. So that was his vindication with which Allah Almighty vindicated him."
"9081","Husayn narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us from Mansur from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah, he said, and I think he mentioned it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No abandonment above three. So whoever abandons his brother above three then dies enters the Fire."
"9082","Husayn narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid from one who heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not sleep in a state of major impurity until you perform ablution."
"9083","Husayn narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to say: Name yourselves with my name and do not use my kunyah."
"9084","Husayn narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adam met Moses, and he said: Are you Adam whom Allah created with His Hand and settled you in His Paradise and made His angels prostrate to you, then you did what you did? So Adam said to Moses: Are you the one to whom Allah spoke and upon whom He sent down the Torah? He said: Yes. He said: Do you find it written against me before I was created? He said: Yes. He said: So Adam overcame Moses, peace be upon them."
"9085","Husayn narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us from Dawud Abu Yazid from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Most of what admits man to the Fire are the two hollows: the mouth and the private part. And most of what admits man to Paradise is fear of Allah Almighty and good character."
"9086","Yunus narrated to us, he said: al-Mastur, meaning Ibn Abi Abbad, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: A man met Abu Hurayrah while he was circumambulating the House and said: O Abu Hurayrah, did you forbid people from fasting Friday? He said: No, by the Lord of the Kabah, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it."
"9087","Yunus narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn al-Mukhtar al-Ansari, narrated to us from Abd Allah, meaning Ibn Fayruz, he said: Abu Rafi al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: Three things I memorized from my friend Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): the witr before sleep, fasting three days of every month, and the two rakahs of forenoon."
"9088","Husayn narrated to us, he said: Abu Uways narrated to us, Safwan ibn Sulaym, the freedman of Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, narrated to us from Said ibn Salamah ibn al-Azraq al-Makhzumi from al-Mughirah ibn Abi Burdah, one of Banu Abd al-Dar ibn Qusayy, from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that seafaring fishermen came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are people of rafts, and we carry little water. If we drink from it, there is not in it what we perform ablution with, and if we perform ablution, there is not in it what we drink. So shall we perform ablution from seawater? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, its water is purifying and its dead is lawful."
"9089","Ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Malik from al-Mughirah ibn Abi Burdah."
"9090","Husayn narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When you say to your companion while the imam preaches: Be silent, you have engaged in idle talk."
"9091","Husayn narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every newborn is born upon the fitrah. Then his parents make him a Jew and make him a Christian and make him a Magian, like the animal produces the animal: is there in it any mutilated?"
"9092","Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he was asked about the children of the polytheists, so he said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"9093","Husayn narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us from Abu al-Walid from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When you lead people, lighten, for among them are the old and the weak and the young. And he said in another hadith: from Abu al-Walid Amr ibn Khidash."
"9094","Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us from Abu al-Walid and Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The intensity of heat is from the breath of Hell, so cool the prayer."
"9095","al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man had a claim upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of a camel of a certain age. So he came demanding it, and they sought for him but found only a camel older than his. So he said: Give him. So he said: You have fulfilled me; may Allah fulfill for you. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are the best of you in repayment."
"9096","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Abu Rafi from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When he sits between her four parts then exerts, ghusl has become obligatory."
"9097","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us from Qatadah from Zurarah ibn Awfa from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah has overlooked for my nation what their souls whisper, so long as they do not speak of it or act upon it."
"9098","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Salih ibn Nabhan from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not hate one another, nor turn your backs on one another, nor compete, and be servants of Allah, brothers."
"9099","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The truest word the poet spoke is: Indeed everything besides Allah is false. And Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt almost accepted Islam."
"9100","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The poor is not the one whom a morsel or two morsels, or a date or two dates, turn away. But the poor is the one who asks for nothing and whose place is not noticed so he is given."
"9101","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Fasting is Mine and I reward for it; he leaves his food and his drink and his desire for My sake; so fasting is a shield; and for the fasting person there are two joys, a joy when he breaks his fast and a joy when he meets Allah, Mighty and Majestic; and the altered breath in his mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."
"9102","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The best women who rode camels are the women of Quraysh, most affectionate toward a child and most careful with a husband regarding his property."
"9103","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Dhakwan, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: The son of Adam insults Me, and it is not fitting for him to insult Me, and he denies Me, and it is not fitting for him to deny Me; as for his insulting Me, it is his saying that I have a son; and as for his denying Me, it is his saying that He will not return me as He began me."
"9104","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from Musa ibn Uthman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: One should not urinate in water that does not flow and then wash from it."
"9105","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Let none of you say: O failure of time; for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is Time."
"9106","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Labid, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was a prophet among the prophets who drew lines, so whoever coincides with his knowledge, then it is his knowledge."
"9107","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Furafisah, from a man, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is guileless and generous, and the wicked one is deceitful and vile."
"9108","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Each of you remains in prayer as long as he remains in his seat waiting for the prayer, and the angels say: O Allah forgive him, O Allah have mercy on him, so long as he does not break his ablution."
"9109","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not hate one another, and do not envy one another, and do not engage in false bidding, and do not turn away from one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers; let no townsman sell for a desert dweller, and do not meet the caravans for trade; and whenever a man buys a sheep and finds it with milk retained in its udder, let him return it and return with it a saa of dates; and let none of you outbid his brother, and let him not propose over his proposal; and let not a woman ask for the divorce of her sister so as to overturn what is in her vessel, for her provision is upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"9110","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Messiah, Isa son of Maryam, is about to descend as a just judge and a fair leader, and he will kill the pig and break the cross, and the call will be one; so convey to him greeting from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I convey to him and he believes me; then when death came to him he said: Convey to him greeting from me."
"9111","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Maqil, meaning Ibn Ubaydullah, narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity is from surplus wealth, and begin with those you support, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand."
"9112","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The heart of the old man is young in love of two things: long life and much wealth."
"9113","Yunus narrated to us, Aban, meaning al-Attar, narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a woman being married over her paternal aunt or over her maternal aunt."
"9114","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Aban, meaning al-Attar, narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Abu Hurayrah, that Hell asked permission of its Lord, so He allowed it to breathe twice each year; so the severity of heat is from the heat of Hell, and the severity of cold is from its bitter cold."
"9115","And Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the heat is intense, delay the prayer until it cools, for the severity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell."
"9116","Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade singling out Friday for fasting."
"9117","Hawdhah narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Among the signs of the Hour are that shepherds of sheep are seen as heads of people, and that the barefoot, naked, hungry are seen competing in building, and that the slave woman gives birth to her master or her mistress."
"9118","Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Dreams are three: glad tidings from Allah, self-talk, and frightening from Satan; so if one of you sees a dream that pleases him, let him recount it if he wishes; and if he sees something he dislikes, let him not recount it to anyone, and let him stand and pray."
"9119","Hawdhah narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever repents before the sun rises from its setting place, Allah turns to him in forgiveness."
"9120","Hawdhah narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Take my name, but do not take my kunya."
"9121","Hawdhah narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Khilas, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are followers of Quraysh in this matter; their disbelievers are followers of their disbelievers, and their Muslims are followers of their Muslims."
"9122","Hawdhah narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Khilas, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Upon every limb of the sons of Adam there is charity."
"9123","Hawdhah narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Khilas, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: By Allah, for one of you to take a rope and go to this mountain and gather firewood and sell it and become independent of people is better for him than to ask people, whether they give him or withhold from him."
"9124","Hawdhah narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Khilas, he is Ibn Amr al-Hajari as he reckons, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: While a woman among those before you was nursing a son of hers, a proud horseman passed by her with fine attire upon him, so the woman said: O Allah, do not let this son of mine die until I see him like this horseman upon such a horse; he said: So the boy left the breast, then said: O Allah, do not make me like this horseman; he said: Then he returned to the breast nursing; then they passed by an Abyssinian or African corpse being dragged, so she said: I seek refuge for my son with Allah from dying the death of this Abyssinian woman or African woman; so he left the breast and said: O Allah, let me die the death of this Abyssinian woman or African woman; so his mother said: O my son, I asked your Lord to make you like that horseman, and you said: O Allah, do not make me like him; and I asked your Lord not to let you die the death of this Abyssinian woman or African woman, and you asked your Lord to let you die her death; he said: So the boy said: You asked your Lord to make me like a man among the people of the Fire, and the Abyssinian woman or African woman, her people used to insult her and beat her and wrong her, and she would say: Allah suffices me, Allah suffices me."
"9125","Hawdhah narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Khilas and Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and from al-Hasan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you fasts a day and forgets and eats and drinks, let him complete his fast, for Allah has fed him and given him drink."
"9126","Hawdhah narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Khilas and Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not curse time, for Allah is Time."
"9127","Hawdhah narrated to us, Awf ibn Abi Jamilah narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The altered breath of the mouth of the fasting person is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk; he said: Your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, said: My servant has left his desire and his food and his drink seeking My pleasure, and fasting is Mine and I reward for it."
"9128","Hawdhah narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you wakes from his sleep and intends purification, let him not put his hand into the vessel until he washes it, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"9129","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, informed us, he said: Sharik, meaning Ibn Abi Namir, informed me, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The poor man is not the one whom a date or two dates, or a morsel or two morsels, turn away; the poor man is the abstinent one; recite if you wish: They do not ask people importunately."
"9130","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah informed us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was aided with terror, and I was given comprehensive speech, and while I was sleeping I was brought the keys of the treasures of the earth and they were placed in my hand."
"9131","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Abu Wahb, freedman of Abu Hurayrah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best of creation? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah; he said: A man holding the bridle of his horse in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic; whenever there is an alarm he mounts it; shall I not inform you of the one who follows him? They said: Yes; he said: A man among a small flock of sheep, establishing prayer and giving zakat; shall I not inform you of the worst of creation? They said: Yes; he said: The one who is asked by Allah and does not give by Him."
"9132","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: Abu Uways narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me that Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For every prophet there is a supplication, and I intend, if Allah wills, to reserve my supplication for the Day of Resurrection as intercession for my nation."
"9133","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: Abu Uways narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah destroy the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"9134","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: Abu Uways narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-Araj say: Abu Hurayrah informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever asks his neighbor to place a beam in his wall, let him not prevent him; then Abu Hurayrah said: What is wrong with me that I see you turning away from it? By Allah, I shall surely cast it between your shoulders."
"9135","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: Abu Uways narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Fadl and Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, the same as it."
"9136","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, that Said ibn al-Musayyab informed him that Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If you say to your companion: Be quiet, while the imam is preaching, you have engaged in idle talk."
"9137","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: Abu Uways narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri said: Abu Ubayd, freedman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Each of you is answered so long as he is not hasty, saying: I supplicated my Lord and He did not answer me."
"9138","He said: Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, he said: My father Ubayd ibn Umayr narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut in the dawn prayer after bowing, saying: O Allah, save al-Walid ibn al-Walid, and Salamah ibn Hisham, and Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah, and the oppressed among the Muslims, and the Muslims among the people of Makkah; he said: So al-Qasim agreed with him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut after bowing."
"9139","He said: Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The excellence of congregational prayer over the prayer of one of you alone is twenty-five parts."
"9140","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The angels of night and day gather at the dawn prayer and the afternoon prayer; he said: So they gather at the dawn prayer; he said: Then the angels of the night ascend and the angels of the day remain; he said: And they gather at the afternoon prayer; he said: Then the angels of the day ascend and the angels of the night remain; he said: Then their Lord asks them: How did you leave My servants? He said: So they say: We came to them while they were praying, and we left them while they were praying; he said: Sulayman said: And I do not know but that he said in it: So forgive them on the Day of Judgment."
"9141","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Would one of you like, when he returns to his family, to find three large fat pregnant camels? He said: We said: Yes; he said: Then three verses which he recites in prayer are better for him than they are."
"9142","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Khubayb al-Ansari narrated to me, from Hafs ibn Asim ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: My pulpit is upon my basin, and what is between my pulpit and my house is a garden among the gardens of Paradise, and a prayer in this mosque of mine is like a thousand prayers in other mosques except the Sacred Mosque."
"9143","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq and al-Miswar ibn Rifah ibn Abi Malik al-Qurazi, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as the hadith of Khubayb from Hafs, neither adding nor omitting."
"9144","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: I heard Maysur, freedman of Quraysh, in the circle of Said, narrating, meaning Ibn Abi Arubah, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Qurashi, from Abu Hurayrah, that a youth passed by him dragging his lower garment, so he struck him with an iron piece that was with him, then said: Has it not reached you what Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not look at the one who drags his lower garment arrogantly."
"9145","Abu al-Jawwab al-Dabbi, al-Ahwas ibn Jawwab, narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Zurayq narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I speak to myself with speech so that falling from the sky is dearer to me than speaking of it; he said: That is pure faith."
"9146","Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, Ammar ibn Zurayq narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Ikrimah, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever entices a servant against her family is not from us, and whoever corrupts a wife against her husband is not from us."
"9147","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three traits are in the hypocrite, even if he prays and fasts and claims that he is a Muslim: when he speaks he lies, and when he promises he breaks, and when he is trusted he betrays."
"9148","Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, wrote a book with His hand for Himself before He created the heavens and the earth, and placed it beneath His Throne, in it: My mercy precedes My anger."
"9149","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, he said: Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, informed us, he said: al-Ala informed us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever calls to guidance has reward like the rewards of those who follow him, none of that diminishing their rewards at all; and whoever calls to misguidance has sin like the sins of those who follow him, none of that diminishing their sins at all."
"9150","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ismail informed us, he said: al-Ala informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None endures the hardship and severity of Madinah except that I shall be for him an intercessor on the Day of Resurrection, or a witness."
"9151","And with this chain, that the Messenger of Allah said: Yawning is from Satan, so when one of you yawns, let him suppress it as much as he can."
"9152","And with this chain, that the Messenger of Allah said: A disbeliever and his killer never gather in the Fire ever."
"9153","And with this chain, that the Prophet said: If the believer knew what punishment is with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, none would hope for His Paradise; and if the disbeliever knew what mercy is with Allah, none would despair of His mercy."
"9154","And with this chain, that the Prophet said: There is no contagion, and no Safar, and no Hama, and no rain-star."
"9155","And with this chain, that the Prophet said: The false Messiah, al-Dajjal, comes from the east with his aim upon Madinah, until he descends beside Uhud; then the angels turn his face toward Sham, and there he perishes; Abdullah said: Thus my father said in these hadiths."
"9156","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ismail informed us, from Ibn Dinar, meaning Abdullah, from Abu Salih al-Samman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My parable and the parable of the prophets before me is like a man who built a building and made it excellent and beautiful, except for the place of a brick in a corner of its corners; so people walk around it and admire it and say: Would that this brick were placed; he said: So I am that brick, and I am the seal of the prophets."
"9157","Sulayman narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, Utbah ibn Muslim, freedman of Banu Tamim, informed us, from Ubayd ibn Hunayn, freedman of Banu Zurayq, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a fly falls into the drink of one of you, let him immerse all of it, then let him throw it away, for in one of its wings there is cure and in the other there is disease."
"9158","And the Messenger of Allah said: When a dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times."
"9159","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, Sulayman al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When Satan hears the caller calling to prayer, he turns with flatulence so that he does not hear the sound; then when he finishes, he returns and whispers; then when he begins the iqama, he does the same."
"9160","Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: You will find among the worst of people on the Day of Resurrection the one who comes to these with the talk of these, and to these with the talk of these."
"9161","Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Hour will not come until the sun rises from its setting place, and all people believe; then on that day no soul shall benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good in its faith; and the Hour will not come until you fight the Jews, and the Jew flees behind the stone, and the stone says: O servant of Allah, O Muslim, this is a Jew behind me; and the Hour will not come until you fight a people whose sandals are of hair."
"9162","Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Whoever takes as masters a people without permission of his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people; Allah does not accept from him on the Day of Resurrection any ransom or exchange; and Madinah is sacred, so whoever introduces an innovation in it or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people; Allah does not accept from him on the Day of Resurrection any ransom or exchange; and the protection of the Muslims is one, the lowest of them strives by it; so whoever betrays a Muslim, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people; Allah does not accept from him on the Day of Resurrection any ransom or exchange."
"9163","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, guarantees the protection of a man who goes out in the path of Allah, nothing bringing him out but striving in the path of Allah and belief in the words of Allah, until He grants him Paradise, or returns him to his house, or to where he went out from."
"9164","Muawiyah narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, he said: Sulayman al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever is wounded in the path of Allah, and Allah knows best who is wounded in His path, comes on the Day of Resurrection with his wound as it was on the day he was wounded; its color is the color of blood and its scent is the scent of musk."
"9165","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Adam and Musa argued; he said: So Musa said: O Adam, you whom Allah created with His hand and breathed into you of His spirit, you misled people and brought them out of Paradise; he said: So Adam said: You are Musa, you whom Allah chose with His speech, you blame me for a deed which I did, which Allah decreed for me before He created the heavens and the earth; he said: So Adam overcame Musa."
"9166","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dhakwan, called Abu al-Zinad, narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O sons of Abd al-Muttalib, O sons of Hashim, ransom yourselves from Allah, Mighty and Majestic; I avail you nothing against Allah; O Umm al-Zubayr, aunt of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), O Fatimah daughter of Muhammad, ransom yourselves from Allah; I avail you nothing against Allah; ask me of my wealth what you both wish."
"9167","Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I do not like that this Uhud of yours be turned into gold, with anything of it remaining with me after three except something I set aside for a debt; the wealthy are the least on the Day of Resurrection, except one who says thus and thus and thus and thus, and how few they are, to his right and to his left and before him and behind him."
"9168","Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, from Muhammad, meaning Ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Were it not that I would burden my nation, or the believers, I would command them to use the tooth-stick at every prayer."
"9169","Abdah, and he is Ibn Sulayman, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, and he mentioned the same as it with its chain."
"9170","Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man praying with his hands on his waist."
"9171","Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you stands at night, let him open his prayer with two light rakahs."
"9172","Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dhakwan Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever catches a prostration before sunrise has caught the prayer, and whoever catches a prostration before sunset has caught the prayer."
"9173","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Muslim, meaning Ibn Khalid, narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you enters upon his Muslim brother and he feeds him food, let him eat of his food and not ask him about it; and if he gives him drink of his drink, let him drink of his drink and not ask him about it."
"9174","Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when a funeral was brought to him or he passed by it, would ask them: Did he leave a debt? If they said: Yes, he said: Did he leave means to pay it? If they said: Yes, he prayed over him; and if they said: No, he said: Pray over your companion."
"9175","Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two never gather in the Fire ever in a gathering that harms one of them; they said: Who, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A believer killed by a disbeliever, then he remains upright after that."
"9176","And with this chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah guarantees for one who goes out in His path, nothing bringing him out but faith in Me and belief in My messengers, that I admit him to Paradise, or return him to his dwelling from which he went out, attaining what he attained of reward or booty."
"9177","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none of you who is wounded in the path of Allah, and Allah knows best who is wounded in His path, but that he meets Allah, Mighty and Majestic, in the form he was on the day he was wounded; its color is the color of blood and its scent is the scent of musk."
"9178","Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, similar to this hadith."
"9179","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn Ayyash, informed me, he said: Abu Husayn narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Quran was presented to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) every year once, and in the year in which he died it was presented to him twice."
"9180","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash informed me, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is the fasting day of one of you, let him not speak obscenely and let him not act ignorantly; and if ignorance is shown toward him, let him say: I am a fasting man."
"9181","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Delay the prayer until it cools, for its heat is from the fierceness of Hell."
"9182","Abd al-Samad ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Dhakwan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant is wounded in the path of Allah, and Allah knows best who is wounded in His path, but his wound comes on the Day of Resurrection; its color is the color of blood and its scent is the scent of musk."
"9183","Abu al-Ala al-Hasan ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, if he indeed said it: Were it not that I would burden my nation, I would command them to use the tooth-stick with ablution; and Abu Hurayrah said: I used to clean my teeth before I slept, and after I woke, and before I ate, and after I ate, when I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say what he said."
"9184","Abu al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Nuaym al-Mujmir, that he said: I went up with Abu Hurayrah upon the roof of the mosque, and he wore trousers beneath his shirt; so he removed his trousers, then performed ablution and washed his face and his hands, raising the ablution in his upper arms, and his feet, raising in his legs; then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: My nation comes on the Day of Resurrection radiant from the marks of ablution, so whoever of you can extend his radiance, let him do so."
"9185","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Razi, son-in-law of Salamah al-Abrash, narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from his uncle Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not wish to meet the enemy, for you do not know what will be in that."
"9186","Harun narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Abu Sakhr Humayd ibn Ziyad narrated to me that Umar ibn Ishaq, freedman of Zaidah, narrated to him, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: The five prayers, and Friday to Friday, and Ramadan to Ramadan, are expiations for what is between them, so long as major sins are avoided."
"9187","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, he said: Abdullah said: And I heard it myself from Harun, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Abu Sakhr informed me, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is affectionate, and there is no good in one who does not befriend and is not befriended."
"9188","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: It was recited to Malik, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The gates of Paradise are opened on Monday and Thursday, so every servant who does not associate anything with Allah is forgiven, except a man between whom and his brother there is hatred; so it is said: Delay them until they reconcile, twice."
"9189","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: al-Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Zahr narrated to me that Abu Hurayrah said: O people, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has obligated for you, upon the tongue of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), prayer in residence as four, and on travel as two."
"9190","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi Salih, freedman of al-Tawamah, informed me, he said: Abu Hurayrah informed me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will surely bestow favor on the Day of Resurrection upon people who never did any good at all, and bring them out of the Fire after they have burned, and admit them to Paradise by His mercy, after the intercession of whoever intercedes."
"9191","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Talqani narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, he said: Said ibn al-Musayyab narrated to me that Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There enters Paradise from my nation a group, seventy thousand, whose faces shine like the shining of the moon on the night of full moon; so Abu Hurayrah said: So Ukkashah ibn Mihsan al-Asadi stood, lifting a striped garment upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me among them; so he said: O Allah, make him among them; then a man of the Ansar stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me among them; he said: Ukkashah has preceded you."
"9192","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus and Ali ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdullah informed us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Qabisah ibn Dhuayb informed us that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade joining between a woman and her paternal aunt, and between a woman and her maternal aunt."
"9193","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, he said: Ibn Abi Anas informed me that his father narrated to him that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is Ramadan, the gates of mercy are opened, and the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are chained."
"9194","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah informed us, and Attab said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Shubah informed us, from a man of Khatham, that he heard Abu Zurah narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went out on a journey and mounted his camel, said: O Allah, You are the Companion in travel and the Successor among family; he said: And I think he said: And the Bearer upon the back; O Allah, accompany us with good counsel and return us with protection; I seek refuge with You from the hardship of the roughness of travel and the gloom of return."
"9195","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah informed us, he said: al-Ajlah informed us that Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa al-Ashari informed him, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: In Friday there is an hour in which no believing servant asks Allah for anything but Allah answers him."
"9196","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah informed us, Yunus informed me, from al-Zuhri, Abd al-Rahman al-Araj informed me that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday; in it Adam was created, and in it he was admitted to Paradise, and in it he was brought out of it."
"9197","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah informed us, and Attab said: Abdullah narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Abd al-Rahman al-Araj narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever attends the funeral until it is prayed over has a qirat, and whoever attends it until it is buried, and Attab said: until it is finished, has two qirats; it was said: And what are the two qirats, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Like two great mountains."
"9198","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah informed us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me that Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Jews and the Christians do not dye, so oppose them."
"9199","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah informed us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, Abu Idris al-Khawlani informed me that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution, let him sniff water into his nose, and whoever cleans himself with stones, let him do so an odd number of times."
"9200","Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Luhayah ibn Uqbah, and from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Luhayah ibn Uqbah, from Abu al-Ward, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Beware of lagging horses, for if they meet they flee, and if they gain spoils they misappropriate."
"9201","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to observe itikaf during the last ten days of Ramadan and the middle ten days, then when he died he died while observing itikaf for twenty days."
"9202","Nuh ibn Maymun narrated to us, he said: Abdullah, meaning al-Umari, informed us, from Jahm ibn Abi al-Jahm, from Miswar ibn Makhramah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah has placed the truth upon the tongue of Umar and his heart."
"9203","Nuh ibn Maymun narrated to us, he said: Abdullah informed us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between my minbar and my house is a garden from the gardens of Paradise, and my minbar is upon my Hawd."
"9204","Nuh narrated to us: Abdullah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of that, except that he said: My minbar is upon a channel from the channels of Paradise."
"9205","Nuh narrated to us: Abdullah, meaning al-Umari, informed us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: It is imminent that people will return to Madinah until their frontier posts are at al-Silah."
"9206","Nuh ibn Maymun narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from Sufyan, from Tariq ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Zadham, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: My close friend enjoined upon me three things: the witr before sleep, fasting three days of every month, and the two rakahs of Duha."
"9207","Yamar ibn Bishr narrated to us: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, he said: Abu Zurah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What do you command me? He said: Be dutiful to your mother. Then he returned and he said: Be dutiful to your mother. Then he returned a fourth time and he said: Be dutiful to your father."
"9208","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab informed us, he said: My uncle Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no believer pricked by a thorn in this world while expecting reward except that his sins are reduced thereby on the Day of Resurrection."
"9209","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah informed us: al-Zubayr ibn Said informed us, and he mentioned a hadith, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, he said: And Safwan ibn Sulaym also narrated, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Indeed a man speaks a word to make his companions laugh, and he falls because of it further than al-Thurayya."
"9210","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, he said: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: There is no sadaqah in less than five awsuq, nor any sadaqah in less than five awaqi, nor any sadaqah in less than five dhawd."
"9211","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar informed us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade meeting caravans in advance and that a townsman should sell for a Bedouin."
"9212","Yamar ibn Bishr narrated to us: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Said ibn al-Musayyab informed me that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is that given from sufficiency, and begin with those you support."
"9213","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Talqani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, he said: I heard Said ibn al-Musayyab say: Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The righteous owned slave has two rewards. By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Abu Hurayrah, were it not for jihad in the cause of Allah and Hajj and dutifulness to my mother, I would have loved to die while a slave."
"9214","Attab narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, he said: Abu Yunus narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Fasting is a shield and a fortified fortress from the Fire."
"9215","Attab narrated to us: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yazid informed us, he said: Jarir ibn Yazid narrated to me that he heard Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir narrating that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A legal punishment carried out in the land is better for the people of the land than being rained upon for thirty mornings."
"9216","Attab narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Qays informed us, he said: Abu Thifal al-Murri narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: A jadha of sheep is better than a sayyid of goats. Dawud said: Al-sayyid means the large mature one."
"9217","Attab narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal narrated to me that Abdullah ibn Rafi informed him, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade the thrown target, that a beast should be shot at and then eaten; rather it should be slaughtered, then let them shoot if they wish."
"9218","Attab narrated to us: Abdullah informed us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Said ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me that Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: An ant bit a prophet from among the prophets, so he ordered the ant village and it was burned, so Allah Almighty revealed to him: Because an ant bit you, you destroyed a nation from among the nations that glorify Allah."
"9219","Attab narrated to us: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sad informed us, from al-Hasan ibn Thawban, I think from Musa ibn Wardan, he said: Abu Hurayrah said to a man: Come, I will bid you farewell as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bade me farewell, or as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bade farewell: I entrust you to Allah, Who does not waste His deposits."
"9220","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Mujahid and al-Mughirah ibn Hakim, from Abu Hurayrah, they both said: We heard him say: There was no one more knowledgeable of the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than me except what belonged to Abdullah ibn Amr, for he used to write with his hand and retain with his heart, while I retained with my heart and did not write with my hand; and he sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to write from him, and he permitted him."
"9221","Attab narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, he said: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: There is no sadaqah in less than five awsaq, nor any sadaqah in less than five awaqi, nor any sadaqah in less than five dhawd."
"9222","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Balj Yahya ibn Abi Sulaym narrated to us, from Amr ibn Maymun, that he narrated to him, he said: Abu Hurayrah said to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Shall I not teach you a word from the treasure of Paradise? He said: I said: Yes, may my father and mother be ransom for you. He said: Say: There is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"9223","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Ibn Mawhab, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has not bestowed a blessing upon a servant except that He loves to see its trace upon him."
"9224","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best of you? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The best of you are the longest of you in age and the best of you in manners."
"9225","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting the incoming produce, and if a buyer buys, the owner of the goods has the choice when they reach the market."
"9226","Surayj ibn al-Numan al-Lului and Abu Kamil both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, Surayj said in his hadith: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, men will leave Madinah out of aversion to it, while Madinah is better for them if they only knew."
"9227","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: Jabir informed me that Abu Hurayrah informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes from his sleep, let him pour water over his hands three times before putting them into the vessel, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"9228","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he said: Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: On Friday there is an hour that no Muslim servant coincides with except that he is answered."
"9229","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Dhawwad ibn Ulbah narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come early for prayer. He said: So I prayed, then I came and sat with him, and he said: O Abu Hurayrah, has your stomach ached? He said: I said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Pray, for in prayer there is healing."
"9230","Ali ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Warqa narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ibrahim did not tell a lie except for three lies: his saying when he was called to their gods, Indeed I am sick, and his saying, Rather the eldest of them did this, and his saying to Sarah, Indeed she is my sister. He said: And Ibrahim entered a town in which there was a king from among the kings or a tyrant from among the tyrants, and it was said: Ibrahim entered tonight with a woman from among the most beautiful people. He said: So the king or the tyrant sent to him: Who is this with you? He said: My sister. He said: Send her to me. He said: So he sent her to him, and he said to her: Do not belie my words, for I have informed him that you are my sister; there is no believer on earth other than me and other than you. He said: When she entered to him, he rose toward her. He said: So she turned to perform ablution and pray, saying: O Allah, if You know that I believed in You and in Your Messenger and guarded my chastity except for my husband, then do not give the disbeliever power over me. He said: So he was seized until he struck the ground with his foot. Abu al-Zinad said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman said, from Abu Hurayrah, that she said: O Allah, if he dies it will be said: She killed him. He said: So he was released. Then he rose toward her, so she stood performing ablution and praying, saying: O Allah, if You know that I believed in You and in Your Messenger and guarded my chastity except for my husband, then do not give the disbeliever power over me. He said: So he was seized until he struck the ground with his foot. Abu al-Zinad said: Abu Salamah said, from Abu Hurayrah, that she said: O Allah, if he dies it will be said: She killed him. He said: So he was released, and he said the third or fourth time: You have sent to me none but a devil; return her to Ibrahim and give her Hajar. He said: So she returned and said to Ibrahim: Did you know that Allah Almighty repelled the plot of the disbeliever and gave a slave girl as a servant."
"9231","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar, from Said ibn Abi Said, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Allah Almighty that He said: I was sick and the son of Adam did not visit Me, and I was thirsty and the son of Adam did not give Me drink. So I said: Do You fall sick, O Lord? He said: A servant from among My servants on earth falls sick and is not visited; had he been visited, what visited him would have been for Me. And he thirsts on earth and is not given drink; had he been given drink, what gave him drink would have been for Me."
"9232","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu Yunus, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Indeed in Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a swift rider travels for a hundred years, and its leaves indeed cover Paradise."
"9233","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies guarding the frontier is protected from the trial of the grave and is secured from the greatest terror, and he is provided morning and evening with his provision from Paradise, and the reward of one guarding the frontier is written for him until the Day of Resurrection."
"9234","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Sabrah and Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us that they both heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad say: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah Almighty accepts charity and accepts from it only the pure; He accepts it with His right hand, blessed and exalted is He, and nurtures it for His Muslim servant, the morsel, just as one of you raises his foal or his young camel, until he meets it on the Day of Resurrection like Uhud."
"9235","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ayyash, meaning Ismail, narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: A servant entered Paradise because of a branch of thorns on the road of the Muslims, so he removed it from it."
"9236","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate at sleep: O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the mighty Throne, our Lord and Lord of everything, Revealer of the Torah, the Gospel, and the Quran, Splitter of the grain and the seed, there is no god but You; I seek refuge in You from the evil of everything whose forelock You hold; You are the First, there is nothing before You, and You are the Last, there is nothing after You, and You are the Manifest, there is nothing above You, and You are the Hidden, there is nothing below You; settle our debt for us and enrich us from poverty."
"9237","Khalaf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: No servant covers a servant in this world except that Allah will cover him on the Day of Resurrection."
"9238","Khalaf narrated to us, he said: Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah: A crescent then a crescent would pass over the households of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with no fire kindled in any of their houses, neither for bread nor for cooking. So they said: With what did they live, O Abu Hurayrah? He said: With the two black ones: dates and water; and they had neighbors from the Ansar, and may Allah reward them with good, who had milch camels and would send them some milk."
"9239","Khalaf narrated to us, he said: Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Exchange gifts, for a gift removes the rancor of the chest."
"9240","Khalaf narrated to us, he said: Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lives to sixty or seventy years, the excuse in lifespan has been conveyed to him."
"9241","Khalaf narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from al-Tuhawi, from Dhuhayl, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: We were on a journey with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and our provisions ran out and were exhausted, so we came upon camels with tied udders bound with tree bark, and the people rushed to milk them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: These may contain the sustenance of a Muslim household; would you like it if they came upon what is in your provisions and took it? Then he said: If you must do it, then drink but do not carry away."
"9242","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Ibn Saylan, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not leave the two rakahs of Fajr even if the horses trample you."
"9243","Affan narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in what he narrates from his Lord Almighty, He said: Whoever remembers Me in himself, I remember him in Myself, and whoever remembers Me in an assembly of people, I remember him in an assembly greater than them and better."
"9244","Affan and Bahz both said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Sad ibn Ibrahim informed me, he said: I heard Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: It is not fitting for a servant to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta."
"9245","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to us, he said: There was in Madinah a storyteller called Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah. He said: So I heard him say: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed a servant commits a sin and says: O Lord, I committed a sin, so forgive me. So his Lord Almighty says: My servant knew that he has a Lord who forgives sins and seizes for them, so He forgave him. Then he remained as long as Allah willed, then he committed another sin and said: O Lord, I committed a sin, so forgive it for me. So his Lord said: My servant knew that he has a Lord who forgives sins and seizes for them; I have forgiven My servant."
"9246","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zakariyya was a carpenter."
"9247","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Ibn Saylan, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not leave the two rakahs of Fajr even if the horses trample you."
"9248","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Farahij informed me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: We had no food at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except the two black ones: dates and water."
"9249","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Aws ibn Khalid, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of one who hears wisdom and follows the worst of what he hears is like a man who comes to a shepherd and says to him: Give me a sheep from your sheep. So he says: Go and take the best sheep by its ear. So he goes and takes the sheepdog by its ear."
"9250","Affan narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us: al-Numan ibn Rashid narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The worst food is the food of the wedding feast to which the rich are invited and the poor are kept away; and whoever leaves the invitation has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"9251","Affan narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no omen, and the best of it is optimism. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is optimism? He said: The righteous word that one of you hears."
"9252","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A sick one should not be brought to a healthy one."
"9253","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when food from other than his family was brought to him, he would ask about it; if it was said to be a gift, he ate, and if it was said to be charity, he said: Eat, and he did not eat."
"9254","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad informed us that Abu Hurayrah saw a man with stained feet and said: Perfect your ablution, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"9255","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A dumb beast is without liability, and a well is without liability, and a mine is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth; and whoever buys a sheep and finds it with retained milk has the choice: if he wishes he returns it with a sa of dates."
"9256","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad informed us, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Charity dates were brought and he gave an order concerning them, then al-Hasan or al-Husayn was carried on his shoulder and his saliva began to flow over him, then he looked at him and there he was chewing a date, so he moved his cheek and said: Throw it, my son; do you not know that the family of Muhammad do not eat charity."
"9257","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Abi Ammar informed us, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a slave obeys his Lord and his master, he has two rewards."
"9258","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Abi Ammar informed us, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant of one of you brings his food, having borne its heat and labor, then if he does not seat him with him to eat, let him give him a morsel of his food."
"9259","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Adam, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prophets are brothers from different mothers; their mothers are diverse and their religion is one. And I am the most entitled of people to Isa son of Maryam, because there was no prophet between me and him, and he will descend. So when you see him, recognize him: a man of medium stature inclining to redness and whiteness, wearing two yellowish garments, as if his head drips though no wetness touches it. So he will break the cross and kill the pig and abolish the jizyah and call people to Islam, and Allah will destroy in his time all religions except Islam, and Allah will destroy in his time the false Messiah, the Dajjal, and security will fall upon the earth until lions graze with camels and leopards with cattle and wolves with sheep, and children play with snakes without harming them. Then he remains forty years, then he dies, and the Muslims pray over him."
"9260","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad informed us, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Our Lord Almighty wonders at men who are driven to Paradise in chains."
"9261","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated to us, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a grave."
"9262","Affan narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Jabbar informed me, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi narrating that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed kinship is a branch from al-Rahman; it says: O Lord, I was cut; O Lord, I was wronged; O Lord, I was oppressed; O Lord. He said: So He answers it: Are you not pleased that I join whoever joins you and cut whoever cuts you?"
"9263","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us: Sulayman al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: There are no people who gather in a house from the houses of Allah Almighty, reciting and learning the Book of Allah Almighty, studying it among themselves, except that the angels surround them and mercy covers them and Allah mentions them among those with Him. And there is no man who travels a path seeking knowledge thereby except that Allah eases for him thereby a path to Paradise. And whoever is slowed by his deeds, his lineage does not hasten him."
"9264","Affan narrated to us, he said: Salim narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The altered smell of the mouth of the fasting person is better with Allah on the Day of Resurrection than the scent of musk."
"9265","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Muhazzim informed us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during a Hajj or Umrah, and a swarm of locusts faced us, so we began striking them with our whips and sticks, killing them. Then we were confounded about what we had done, being in ihram, so we asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: No harm; it is sea game."
"9266","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from one who heard Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The food of one suffices two, and the food of two suffices four."
"9267","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Ziyad ibn Riyah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasten with deeds before six: the rising of the sun from its west, and the Dajjal, and the smoke, and the beast of the earth, and the private affair of one of you, and the general affair. And Qatadah used to say: When he said the general affair, he meant the affair of the Hour."
"9268","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as Hammad reckoned, he said: Indeed whoever enters Paradise enjoys bliss and does not despair; his clothes do not wear out and his youth does not fade; in Paradise is what no eye has seen and no ear has heard and has not occurred to the heart of a human."
"9269","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Wasi, from Shutayr ibn Nahar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good opinion is part of good worship."
"9270","Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Khuthaym ibn Irak ibn Malik narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: There is no sadaqah on the slave of a man nor on his horse."
"9271","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah informed us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as Hammad reckoned, that a man used to sell wine in a ship, and with him in the ship was a monkey, and he used to dilute the wine with water. He said: So the monkey took the purse, then climbed with it above the deck and opened the purse, and began taking a dinar and throwing it into the ship and a dinar into the sea, until he made it into halves."
"9272","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad informed us that Abu Hurayrah saw a man with stained feet and said: Perfect your ablution, for I heard Abu al-Qasim say: Woe to the heel from the Fire."
"9273","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, he said: A companion of ours narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade fasting the day of Friday except a continuous fast."
"9274","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abdullah ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi or Ibrahim ibn Abdullah al-Qurashi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate after the Zuhr prayer: O Allah, deliver al-Walid ibn al-Walid and Salamah ibn Hisham and Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah and the weak Muslims from the hands of the polytheists, those who can contrive no plan and find no way."
"9275","Affan narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith is Yemeni, and disbelief is toward the east, and tranquility is among the people of sheep, and pride and showing off are among the loud herdsmen. The false Messiah will come from the east with his aim upon Madinah, until when he comes behind Uhud the angels strike his face toward Sham; there he perishes. And he said once: The angels turned his face."
"9276","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not precede Ramadan by fasting a day or two days, except a man whose fasting coincides, then let him fast it."
"9277","He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever stands Ramadan in faith and expecting reward, then what preceded of his sin is forgiven for him."
"9278","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever stands Laylat al-Qadr in faith and expecting reward, then what preceded of his sin is forgiven for him. Affan said: And Aban narrated to us in this chain the like of it."
"9279","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Hakim al-Athram informed us, from Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to a menstruating woman or a woman in her back passage or a soothsayer and believes him, has disavowed what Allah revealed to Muhammad."
"9280","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Hammad said: And I do not know it except that he raised it. Then Hammad said: I think from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a man visited a brother of his in another village, so Allah placed an angel on his path, and when he came to him the angel said: Where do you intend? He said: I visit a brother of mine in this village. He said: Does he have any favor upon you that you maintain? He said: No, except that I loved him for the sake of Allah Almighty. He said: Then I am the messenger of Allah to you: Indeed Allah Almighty has loved you as you loved him."
"9281","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the cemetery and greeted its people. He said: Peace be upon you, abode of believing people; and we, Allah willing, will join you. I wished that we had seen our brothers. They said: Are we not your brothers, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Rather you are my companions, and my brothers are those who have not yet come, and I am their predecessor at the Hawd. They said: And how do you recognize those of your nation who have not yet come, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Have you seen if a man has horses with white foreheads and legs among dark black horses, does he not recognize his horses? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then they will come with white marks from ablution, he says it three times, and I am your predecessor at the Hawd. Indeed men will be driven away from my Hawd as a stray camel is driven away; I will call them: Come, come. Then it will be said: Indeed they altered after you. So I will say: Away, away."
"9282","Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Salamah ibn al-Azraq, that he was sitting with Abdullah ibn Umar one day in the market, and a funeral passed by while weeping over it, so Ibn Umar disapproved of that and rebuked them. So Salamah ibn al-Azraq said to him: Do not say that, O Abu Abd al-Rahman, for I bear witness upon Abu Hurayrah: I heard him, and a woman from the kinswomen of Marwan died and Marwan attended her and ordered the weeping women and they were struck. So Abu Hurayrah said to him: Leave them, O Abu Abd al-Malik, for a funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while weeping over it, and I was with him, and with him was Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah have mercy on him, and Umar rebuked the women weeping with the funeral. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Leave them, O Ibn al-Khattab, for the soul is afflicted and the eye is tearful and the covenant is recent. He said: Did you hear it? He said: Yes. He said: Allah and His Messenger know best."
"9283","Affan narrated to us, he said: Aban al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, he said: Abu Kathir al-Anbari narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Wine is from these two trees: from the date-palm and the grapevine."
"9284","Affan narrated to us, he said: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid, the companion of al-Ziyadi, narrated to us, from a scholar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who dies and three households of his nearest neighbors testify good for him except that Allah, blessed and exalted is He, says: I have accepted the testimony of My servants for what they knew, and I have forgiven him for what I know."
"9285","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar said, and one other than Hammam added to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The most lying of people are the artisans."
"9286","Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us: al-Awzai narrated to us, from Abu Kathir al-Ghubari, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wine is from these two trees: the date-palm and the grapevine."
"9287","Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my wife gave birth to a black boy. So he said: Do you have camels? He said: Yes. He said: What are their colors? He said: Reddish. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps a gray camel came among them? He said: O Messenger of Allah, yes. He said: How do you see that? He said: I think a strain pulled it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And this one, a strain pulled him."
"9288","Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Thabit al-Zuraqi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: We were with Umar ibn al-Khattab on the road to Makkah when a wind stirred, so he said to those around him: About the wind. He said: They did not return anything to him. He said: What he asked about reached me, so I urged my mount until I caught up with him, and I said: O Commander of the Believers, it reached me that you asked about the wind, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The wind is from the mercy of Allah, so do not curse it; ask its good and seek refuge with Him from its evil."
"9289","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: I heard Yazid ibn al-Asamm say: I was in Madinah with Marwan ibn al-Hakam and Abu Hurayrah, and a funeral passed by them, so Abu Hurayrah stood and Marwan did not stand. So Abu Hurayrah said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a funeral passed by him, he stood. So Marwan stood at that."
"9290","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade the fara and the atirah. Muhammad said: And I heard it myself from Mamar."
"9291","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The child belongs to the owner of the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone."
"9292","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For every prophet there is a supplication with which he supplicated for his nation and is answered; and I wish, Allah willing, to delay my supplication as intercession for my nation on the Day of Resurrection."
"9293","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, that he said: Abu Hurayrah used to come upon people while they performed ablution in the washroom, and he would say to them: Perform ablution fully, perform ablution fully, for I heard Abu al-Qasim say: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"9294","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: Marwan used to employ Abu Hurayrah over Madinah. He said: When he saw a man dragging his izar, he would strike with his foot, then say: The commander has come, the commander has come. Then he would say: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not look at one who drags his izar in arrogance."
"9295","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Remove them both together or wear them both together; when you put on, begin with the right, and when you take off, begin with the left."
"9296","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant of one of you comes to him with food, then if he does not seat him with him, let him give him a morsel or two morsels, or a mouthful or two mouthfuls, Shubah doubted, for he bore its treatment and its heat."
"9297","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, that al-Hasan took a date from the charity dates and put it in his mouth. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Kikh, kikh, throw it; do you not know that we, the household, do not eat charity."
"9298","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or Abu al-Qasim said: If the Ansar took a valley or a ravine and the people took a valley or a ravine, I would take the valley of the Ansar; and were it not for the Hijrah, I would be a man from the Ansar. He said: So Abu Hurayrah used to say: May my father and mother be ransom, they sheltered and helped him, and another word."
"9299","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Do not retain milk in camels and sheep; so whoever buys a musarrat has one of two choices: if he wishes he returns it with a sa of dates. He said: And a man should not sell over the sale of his brother, and a woman should not ask for the divorce of her sister to overturn what is in her dish, for her provision is what was written for her. And do not practice najsh, and do not meet the caravans."
"9300","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Whoever performs Hajj to this House and does not utter obscenity nor commit wickedness returns as his mother bore him."
"9301","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrates from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: There is no wudu except from hadath or wind."
"9302","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said Shubah narrated to us from Sayyar from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah, he said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever performs Hajj to this House and does not commit obscene speech and does not commit disobedience returns as his mother bore him."
"9303","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said Shubah narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, he said I heard Sulayman ibn Yasar narrating from Irak ibn Malik from Abu Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: There is no sadaqah upon the slave of a Muslim nor upon his horse."
"9304","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir from Abu al-Shatha al-Muharibi, he said we were sitting with Abu Hurayrah in the mosque, then the muadhdhin called the adhan, then a man in the mosque stood and left, then Abu Hurayrah said: As for this one, he has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"9305","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Abu Husayn, he said I heard Dhakwan Abu Salih narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me, for Satan does not take my form. Shubah said, or he said: does not resemble me. And whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"9306","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Sulayman from Dhakwan from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Every newborn is born upon the fitrah, then his parents make him a Jew and make him a Christian and make him a polytheist."
"9307","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said Shubah narrated to us from Abu Bishr from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The best of you are my generation, then those who follow them. Abu Hurayrah said: I do not know whether he mentioned it twice or three times. Then after them will come people who love fatness, they testify though they are not asked to testify."
"9308","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said I heard Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whatever is below the ankles is in the Fire, meaning the izar."
"9309","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Nadr ibn Anas from Bashir ibn Nuhayk from Abu Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When a man goes bankrupt with the wealth of people, and a man sees his goods intact, he has more right to them than others."
"9310","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, he said al-Zuhri informed us from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah, he said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Five are from the fitrah: circumcision, shaving the pubes, plucking the armpit, trimming the nails, and clipping the mustache."
"9311","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan al-Qurdusi narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: A good deed is ten times its like, and fasting is Mine and I reward for it; he leaves his food and his drink for My sake; fasting is Mine and I reward for it; and the breath of the mouth of the fasting person with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is sweeter than the scent of musk."
"9312","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever among you lives will soon meet Isa ibn Maryam as a guided imam and a just judge; he will break the cross and kill the pig and abolish the jizyah, and war will lay down its burdens."
"9313","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me, for Satan does not assume my likeness."
"9314","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said Hisham narrated to us from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever intends a good deed and does not do it, one good deed is written for him; if he does it, ten times its like up to seven hundred and seven times its like are written for him; and if he does not do it, one good deed is written for him; and whoever intends an evil deed and does not do it, it is not written against him."
"9315","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said Hisham narrated to us from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The mouse is from what was transformed, and the sign of that is that the milk of milch camels is placed for it and it does not approach it, but when the milk of sheep is placed for it, it eats from it. He said, then Kab said to him: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Was the Torah revealed to me?"
"9316","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said Hisham narrated to us from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The injury caused by a beast is without liability, and the well is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"9317","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said Shubah narrated to us from Musa ibn Abi Uthman, he said I heard Abu Uthman, he said I heard Abu Hurayrah saying the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The muadhdhin is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, and every moist and dry thing bears witness for him; and the one who attends the prayer has twenty-five good deeds written for him and what is between them is expiated for him."
"9318","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah, he said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The imam is only to be followed, so when he says the takbir, say the takbir, and when he bows, bow, and when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: Our Lord, to You is praise; and if he prays sitting, pray sitting all together."
"9319","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said Said, meaning Ibn Abi Arubah, narrated to us from Abu Muhammad, I think it is Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Abu Hurayrah, he said: In every prayer there is recitation; whatever the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made audible to us, we make audible to you, and whatever he concealed from us, we conceal from you."
"9320","Affan narrated to us, he said Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, he said al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The two eyes commit adultery, and the tongue commits adultery, and the two hands commit adultery, and the two feet commit adultery, and the private part confirms that or denies it."
"9321","Affan narrated to us, he said Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim narrated to us from al-Ala from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was traveling on the road of Makkah and came upon Jumdan, then he said: This is Jumdan; proceed; the mufarridun have preceded. They said: And who are the mufarridun? He said: Those who remember Allah much. Then he said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. They said: And those who shorten. He said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. They said: And those who shorten. He said: And those who shorten."
"9322","And with this isnad, he said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Rights will surely be rendered to their owners until retaliation is taken for the hornless sheep from the horned sheep."
"9323","And with this isnad, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: A man must not outbid the bargain of his Muslim brother, nor propose over his proposal."
"9324","And with this isnad, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This heat is from the fieriness of Jahannam, so cool the prayer."
"9325","And with this isnad, he said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When Satan hears the adhan, he turns away passing wind so that he does not hear the sound."
"9326","And with this isnad, he said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was favored over the prophets with six. It was said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I was given the concise speech, and I was aided with terror, and spoils were made lawful for me, and the earth was made for me a mosque and a purification, and I was sent to all creation, and the prophets were sealed with me. My example and the example of the prophets, upon them prayer and peace, is like a man who built a palace and completed its building and made its structure excellent except for the place of one brick; people looked at the palace and said: How excellent is the structure of this palace, if only this brick were completed. Behold, I am the brick; behold, I am the brick."
"9327","Affan narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: My minbar is upon a stream of the streams of Paradise, and what is between my minbar and my chamber is a garden of the gardens of Paradise."
"9328","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The servant says: My wealth; yet from his wealth he has only three: what he ate and consumed, or wore and wore out, or gave and stored; what is besides that is gone and he leaves it for people."
"9329","And with this isnad, he said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not make vows, for a vow does not advance anything of the decree; it is only extracted through it from the miser."
"9330","Affan narrated to us, he said Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim al-Qass narrated to us, he said al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The right of a Muslim upon a Muslim is six. They said: And what are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: When you meet him, greet him; and when he invites you, answer him; and when he seeks your advice, advise him; and when he sneezes and praises Allah, say yarhamuk Allah to him; and when he is ill, visit him; and when he dies, accompany him."
"9331","And with this isnad, he said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A disbeliever and his Muslim killer will never gather in the Fire ever."
"9332","And with this isnad, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have relatives I join and they cut me, and I forbear toward them and they act ignorantly toward me, and I do good to them and they do evil to me. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If it is as you say, it is as if you feed them hot ashes, and there will remain with you a supporter from Allah against them as long as you remain upon that."
"9333","Affan narrated to us, he said Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When there came down upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: To Allah belongs what is in the heavens and what is in the earth, and whether you reveal what is in yourselves or conceal it, Allah will call you to account for it, then He forgives whom He wills and punishes whom He wills, and Allah is over all things Capable, that weighed heavily upon the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so they came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then they knelt upon their knees and said: O Messenger of Allah, we were charged with deeds we can bear: prayer, fasting, jihad, and sadaqah, yet this verse has been sent down upon you and we cannot bear it. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you want to say as the people of the two Books before you said: We hear and we disobey? Rather say: We hear and we obey; Your forgiveness, our Lord, and to You is the return. So they said: We hear and we obey; Your forgiveness, our Lord, and to You is the return. When the people affirmed it and their tongues were humbled with it, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down after it: The Messenger believes in what was sent down to him from his Lord, and the believers; each believes in Allah and His angels and His Books and His messengers; we make no distinction between any of His messengers. Affan said: Sallam Abu al-Mundhir recited it: yufarriqu. And they said: We hear and we obey; Your forgiveness, our Lord, and to You is the return. When they did that, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, abrogated it with His saying: Allah does not charge a soul except its capacity; for it is what it earned and against it is what it acquired. So for him became what he earned of good and against him what he acquired of evil. Al-Ala explained this: Our Lord, do not take us to task if we forget or err, He said: Yes; Our Lord, do not lay upon us a burden as You laid upon those before us, He said: Yes; Our Lord, do not burden us with what we have no strength for, He said: Yes; pardon us and forgive us and have mercy upon us; You are our Protector, so aid us against the disbelieving people."
"9334","Affan narrated to us, he said Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to Ubayy ibn Kab while he was praying, and said: O Ubayy. He turned but did not answer him. Then Ubayy prayed and shortened, then he went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And upon you. He said: What prevented you, O Ubayy, when I called you, from answering me? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I was in prayer. He said: Do you not find in what Allah revealed to me: Respond to Allah and to the Messenger when he calls you to what gives you life? He said, he said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, I will not do it again. He said: Would you like me to teach you a surah the like of which was not sent down in the Torah nor in the Zabur nor in the Injil nor in the Furqan? He said: I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I hope you will not leave this door until you know it. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took my hand, speaking to me while I slowed down fearing he would reach before finishing the talk; when we neared the door, I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the surah you promised me? He said: How do you recite in prayer? He said: So I recited to him the Mother of the Quran. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, Allah did not send down in the Torah nor in the Injil nor in the Zabur nor in the Furqan the like of it; it is the seven oft-repeated."
"9335","Affan narrated to us, he said Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said Thabit narrated to us from Abu Rafi that a youth of Quraysh came to Abu Hurayrah strutting in a hulla of his, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: A man of those before you was strutting in a hulla of his, his forelock and his two cloaks having pleased him, when the earth was made to swallow him, and he sinks in it until the Hour comes."
"9336","Affan narrated to us, he said Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said Qatadah narrated to us from al-Nadr ibn Anas from Bashir ibn Nuhayk from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When a man goes bankrupt, the creditor has more right to his goods when he finds them intact."
"9337","Affan narrated to us, he said Hammam narrated to us, he said Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us from Abu Salamah, he said: I saw Abu Hurayrah recite: When the sky splits, then prostrate. I said: Why do I see you prostrating in it? He said: Had I not seen the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prostrating in it, I would not have prostrated."
"9338","Affan narrated to us, he said Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: A false oath sells the goods but wipes out the profit."
"9339","Affan narrated to us, he said Abd al-Wahid, meaning Ibn Ziyad, narrated to us, he said Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, he said my father narrated to me, he said I heard Abu Hurayrah saying, and he used to begin his talk by saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Abu al-Qasim the truthful, the believed: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"9340","Affan narrated to us, he said Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, he said Sulayman al-Amash narrated to us, he said Abu Salih narrated to us, he said I heard Abu Hurayrah saying the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: I am with the opinion of My servant of Me, and I am with him when he remembers Me; if he remembers Me in himself, I remember him in Myself; and if he remembers Me in an assembly, I remember him in an assembly better than it; and whoever draws near to Me a span, I draw near to him a cubit; and whoever draws near to Me a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom; and whoever comes to Me walking, I come to him hastening."
"9341","Affan narrated to us, he said Abu Awanah narrated to us, he said Suhayl narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves a servant, He calls Jibril, peace be upon him, and says: O Jibril, I love so-and-so, so love him. He said: Then Jibril, peace be upon him, loves him. He said: Then he calls among the people of heaven: Allah loves so-and-so. He said: Then the people of heaven love him. Then acceptance is placed for him on earth. And when Allah, Mighty and Majestic, hates a servant, He calls Jibril and says: O Jibril, I hate so-and-so, so hate him. He said: Then Jibril hates him. Then he calls among the people of heaven: Allah hates so-and-so, so hate him. He said: Then the people of heaven hate him. Then hatred is placed for him on earth."
"9342","Affan narrated to us, he said Wuhayb narrated to us, he said Khalid narrated to us from Ikrimah from Abu Hurayrah, he said: No man after the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wore sandals or shoes, or rode mounts, or wore a kor, better than Jafar ibn Abi Talib, meaning in generosity and nobility."
"9343","Affan narrated to us, he said Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Sirin, narrated to us, he said Abu Hurayrah and Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to me; one of them referred it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the other referred it to Umar. One of them said he forbade skins and pitch-coated vessels, and gourds and hantam; and the other said he forbade skins and pitch-coated vessels, and gourds and earthen jars or pottery; Muhammad doubted."
"9344","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you feels a movement in his anus in his prayer and it is unclear to him whether he broke wudu or not, let him not leave until he hears a sound or finds wind."
"9345","Affan narrated to us, he said Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said Ali ibn Zayd and Salih al-Muallim and Humayd and Yunus informed us from al-Hasan from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The five prayers and Friday to Friday are expiations for what is between them, as long as major sins are avoided."
"9346","He said Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah from Abu Rafi from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the trial of life and death and from the evil of the Masih al-Dajjal."
"9347","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from al-Hasan from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Women who seek khul and who tear themselves away are the hypocrites."
"9348","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ata ibn al-Saib from al-Agharr from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in what he relates from his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, He said: Pride is My cloak and greatness is My izar; whoever disputes with Me one of them, I cast him into the Fire."
"9349","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, that he said: I was walking with my father, then my father looked into the house of some people and saw a woman, then he said: If they had gouged my eye, it would be wasted. Then he said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to me that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever looks into the house of people without their permission and they gouge his eye, it is wasted. And Affan once said: an eye."
"9350","He said Affan narrated to us, he said Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said Suhayl ibn Abi Salih informed us from Abd Allah ibn Dinar from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Faith is seventy-odd doors, the best of them is: There is no god but Allah, and the lowest of them is removing a bone from the road, and modesty is a branch of faith."
"9351","Affan narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Qatadah from Zurarah ibn Awfa from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell."
"9352","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, says: O son of Adam, for every good deed are ten good deeds up to seven hundred times up to many multiples; and fasting is Mine and I reward for it; and fasting is a shield from the Fire; and the breath of the mouth of the fasting person is sweeter with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, than the scent of musk; if an ignorant one acts ignorantly against one of you while he is fasting, let him say: I am fasting."
"9353","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: Abu al-Qasim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Had the Ansar taken a valley or a mountain pass, I would have taken the mountain pass of the Ansar or the valley of the Ansar; and were it not for the Hijrah, I would have been a man of the Ansar. Then Abu Hurayrah said: By my father and my mother, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he did no wrong; they sheltered and aided him. He said, and I think he said: and consoled him with wealth."
"9354","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said Alqamah ibn Marthad informed me, he said I heard Abu al-Rabi narrating that he heard Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Four things in my ummah they will not leave: reviling lineages, and wailing, and saying: We were given rain by such-and-such a star. You buy a mangy camel or it becomes mangy, then you place it among a hundred camels and they become mangy; who infected the first?"
"9355","Affan narrated to us, he said Shubah narrated to us, he said Qasim ibn Mihran informed me, he said I heard Abu Rafi narrating from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw sputum in the qiblah. He said: He used to say once: Then he scraped it. He said: Then he said: I stood and scraped it. Then he said: Does one of you, when he is in his prayer, like to have mucus in his face or to be spat in his face? When one of you is in his prayer, let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, but to his left under his foot; if he does not find that, he said: with his garment, like this."
"9356","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Euphrates will soon uncover a mountain of gold, and people will fight over it until nine of every ten are killed and one remains."
"9357","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Sulayman al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, he said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you prays the two rakahs before the dawn prayer, let him lie down on his right side."
"9358","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Hisham, meaning Ibn Urwah, narrated to us from a man from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you eats, let him lick his fingers, for he does not know in which of that is the blessing."
"9359","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said I heard Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The injury of a grazing animal is without liability, and the mine is without liability, and the well is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"9360","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of this, except that he said: buried treasures."
"9361","Affan narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, my father narrated to me from Muawiyah al-Mahri, he said Abu Hurayrah said: O Mahri, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the price of a dog, and the earnings of a prostitute, and the earnings of a cupper, and the earnings of a stallion stud fee."
"9362","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Abbas al-Jurayri narrated to us, he said I heard Abu Uthman al-Nahdi saying: I was a guest of Abu Hurayrah for seven days. He said, and I heard him saying: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, divided dates among his companions, and I received seven dates, one of them a dry one, and nothing was more pleasing to me than it; it strengthened my chewing."
"9363","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit informed us from Abu Rafi from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The servant remains in prayer as long as he is in his prayer place waiting for the prayer; the angels say: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy upon him, until he leaves or breaks wudu. I said: And what is breaking wudu? He said: Passing wind loudly or quietly."
"9364","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said Ali ibn Zayd informed us from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The people of Paradise enter hairless, white, curly-haired, kohled, aged thirty-three, upon the creation of Adam, seventy cubits by seven cubits."
"9365","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ziyad informed us, he said I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard Abu al-Qasim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Fast the crescent upon sighting it and break upon sighting it; if it is obscured for you, count thirty."
"9366","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Adi ibn Thabit from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"9367","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said Umarah ibn al-Qaqa ibn Shubrumah al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir informed us, he said Abu Hurayrah narrated to us, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, which sadaqah is greatest? He said: To give while you are healthy and miserly, fearing poverty and hoping for life; and do not delay until when it reaches the throat you say: For so-and-so is such, and for so-and-so is such, though it already belonged to so-and-so."
"9368","Affan narrated to us, he said Hammad narrated to us, he said Thabit informed us from Abu Rafi from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There was a tree harming the people of the road, so a man cut it and removed it, and entered Paradise."
"9369","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Amr from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The noble, son of the noble, son of the noble, son of the noble is Yusuf ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, peace of Allah be upon them all."
"9370","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Dawud ibn Farahij narrated to us, he said I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: We had no food in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, except the two black ones: dates and water."
"9371","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir informed me, he said I heard Abu al-Shatha al-Muharibi, he said: We were with Abu Hurayrah in a mosque, then a man left after the muadhdhin had called the adhan. He said, then he said: As for this one, he has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"9372","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Asim ibn Bahdalah from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, delayed the last Isha one night until nearly a third of the night had gone or near it. He said: Then he came while among people there was softness and they were in scattered groups. Then he became severely angry. Then he said: Had a man invited people to a marrow bone or two hooves, they would have answered him, yet they lag behind this prayer. I intended to order a man to stay behind over the people of these houses who lag behind this prayer, then burn them upon them with fires."
"9373","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said Abu al-Muhazzim informed us from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered Fatimah or Umm Salamah to drag her train an arm span."
"9374","Affan and Bahz narrated to us, they said Abu Awanah narrated to us from Yala ibn Ata from Abu Alqamah al-Ansari, he said Abu Hurayrah narrated to me from his mouth to my mouth, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah; and whoever obeys the commander has obeyed me. The commander is only a shield. If he prays sitting, pray sitting or seated. When he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise; for when the saying of the people of earth coincides with the saying of the people of heaven, what preceded of his sin is forgiven for him."
"9375","He said: And Caesar perishes and there will be no Caesar after him, and Khosrau perishes and there will be no Khosrau after him."
"9376","And he said: Seek refuge in Allah from five: from the torment of Jahannam, and the torment of the grave, and the trial of life and death, and the trial of the Masih al-Dajjal."
"9377","Affan narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, he said Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us from Abu Hurayrah, he said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Had ten of the rabbis of the Jews believed in me, every Jew upon the face of the earth would have believed in me. Kab said: Twelve; their confirmation is in Surat al-Maidah."
"9378","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said Qays and Habib informed us from Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Abu Hurayrah that he said: In every prayer there is recitation; whatever the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made audible to us, we made audible to you, and whatever he concealed from us, we concealed from you."
"9379","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said Salamah ibn Kuhayl informed me, he said I heard Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman at Mina narrating from Abu Hurayrah that a man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, demanding payment, and spoke harshly to him. He said: His companions were about to attack him, then he said: Leave him, for the owner of a right has a say. He said: Buy a camel for him and give it to him. They said: We find only one better in age than his. He said: Buy it and give it to him, for among the best of you are the best in repayment."
"9380","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit informed us from Abu Rafi from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in what Hammad thinks that he said: Whoever enters Paradise enjoys and does not despair; his clothes do not wear out and his youth does not perish; in Paradise is what no eye has seen and no ear has heard and has not occurred to a human heart."
"9381","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said Yaqub ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Qari, from a tribe called Qarah of the Ansar, narrated to us, and he settled in Alexandria, the land of the gate of Egypt, so he was called al-Iskandarani, from Amr ibn Abi Amr from Said al-Maqburi from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was sent in the best of the generations of the sons of Adam, generation after generation, until I was from the generation I was in."
"9382","Qutaybah narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Amr ibn Abi Amr from Said al-Maqburi from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: My believing servant has no reward with Me, when I take his beloved from the people of the world and then he seeks reward, except Paradise."
"9383","Qutaybah narrated to us, he said Yaqub narrated to us from Abu Hazim from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whomever Allah grants sixty years of age, Allah has excused him regarding age."
"9384","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said Yaqub narrated to us from Suhayl from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Hour will not come until wealth increases and overflows, until a man brings out the zakat of his wealth and finds no one to accept it from him, and until the land of the Arabs returns to meadows and rivers, and until harj increases. They said: And what is harj, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Killing, killing."
"9385","And with this isnad, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever bears arms against us is not of us, and whoever cheats us is not of us."
"9386","And he said: Whoever buys a musarrat sheep has the choice regarding it for three days; if he wishes, he keeps it, and if he wishes, he returns it and returns with it a sa of dates."
"9387","And he said: The Hour will not come until the Muslims fight the Jews, then the Muslims kill them until the Jew hides behind the stone or the tree, then the stone or the tree says: O Muslim, O servant of Allah, this is a Jew behind me, so come and kill him, except the gharqad, for it is of the trees of the Jews."
"9388","And he said: Among the strongest of my ummah in love for me are people who will be after me; one of them would wish to see me with his family and his wealth."
"9389","And he said, peace be upon him: Whoever allies with a people without the permission of his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels; Allah does not accept from him any exchange nor any ransom."
"9390","And he said, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: When the reciter says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, and whoever behind him says: O Allah, our Lord, and to You is praise, and his saying coincides with the saying of the people of heaven: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise, what preceded of his sin is forgiven for him."
"9391","Qutaybah narrated to us, he said Yaqub narrated to us from Suhayl from his father from Abu Hurayrah that he used to say the takbir whenever he lowered and raised, and he narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do that."
"9392","Qutaybah narrated to us, he said Yaqub narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan from Sumayy from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah that he said: People complained to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the opening between the elbows, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered them to seek help with the knees."
"9393","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Abu Thifal al-Murri from Rabah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Hurayrah, he said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The blood of a reddish-brown sheep is dearer to me than the blood of two black ones."
"9394","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us from Thawr ibn Zayd from Abu al-Ghayth from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Dhu al-Suwayqatayn of Abyssinia will destroy the House of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"9395","And he said, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The Hour will not come until a man of Qahtan emerges driving people with his stick."
"9396","Qutaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us from Thawr from Abu al-Ghayth from Abu Hurayrah that he said: We were sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when Surat al-Jumuah came down upon him; when he recited: And others of them who have not yet joined them, he said: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not answer him until he asked him once or twice or three times, and among us was Salman al-Farisi. He said: Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, placed his hand upon Salman and said: Had faith been at the Pleiades, men of these would have attained it."
"9397","Qutaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us from Thawr from Abu al-Ghayth from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever takes the wealth of people intending to repay it, Allah will repay for him; and whoever takes it intending to destroy it, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will destroy him."
"9398","Qutaybah narrated to us, he said al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Qurashi narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, he said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Ibrahim, peace be upon him, was circumcised at eighty years of age with a qadum."
"9399","And he said: The best day the sun rose upon is Friday; in it Adam was created, and in it he was entered into Paradise, and in it he was taken out of it; and the Hour will come only on Friday."
"9400","He said: And Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: When My servant loves meeting Me, I love meeting him; and when he hates meeting Me, I hate meeting him."
"9401","And he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The head of disbelief is toward the east, and pride and arrogance are among the people of horses and camels and the loud-voiced cultivators, the people of wabar, and tranquility is among the people of sheep."
"9402","And he said: You will find among the best of people those most averse to this affair, until he falls into it."
"9403","And when he raised his head from the last rakah he would say: O Allah, save Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah, O Allah, save Salamah ibn Hisham, O Allah, save al-Walid ibn al-Walid, O Allah, save the oppressed among the believers, O Allah, make Your grip severe upon Mudar, O Allah, make them years like the years of Yusuf, peace be upon him."
"9404","And he said: Ghifar, may Allah forgive her, and Aslam, may Allah keep her safe."
"9405","And he said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, if you knew what I know you would weep much and laugh little."
"9406","And he said: Beware of wisal. They said: But you practice wisal, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I am not in this like you; I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink, so take upon yourselves only what you have capacity for."
"9407","And he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider travels a hundred years and does not cross it."
"9408","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa, meaning al-Makhzumi, narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prayer for one who has no ablution, and no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah over it."
"9409","Qutaybah said, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Humayd al-Kharrat, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to this mosque of mine, coming only for some good he learns, he is at the rank of the mujahid in the path of Allah, and whoever comes for other than that is at the rank of a man looking at the goods of another."
"9410","Qutaybah narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Zaidah, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never raised his head to the sky except that he said: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your obedience."
"9411","Qutaybah said, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Ala, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man opens for himself a door of begging except Allah opens for him a door of poverty. For a man to take his rope and go to the mountain and gather firewood upon his back and eat from it is better for him than to ask people, whether they give or withhold."
"9412","Qutaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every beast of prey with fangs."
"9413","Qutaybah narrated to us, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, that Said ibn Yasar Abu al-Hubab informed him, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no believing servant who gives charity from wholesome earnings, and Allah accepts only what is wholesome, and nothing ascends to heaven except what is wholesome, except that He places it in the Hand of the Most Merciful, or in the Palm of the Most Merciful, and He rears it for him as one of you rears his foal or his young camel, until a date becomes like the great mountain."
"9414","Qutaybah said, Ibn Luhayyah narrated to me, from Darraj, from Ibn Hujayrah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: The mosques have pegs; the angels are their companions. If they are absent they miss them, and if they are sick they visit them, and if they are in need they help them."
"9415","And he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The companion of the mosque is upon three traits: a brother gained, or a decisive word, or a mercy awaited."
"9416","Qutaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Thawr, from Abu al-Ghayth, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sweat on the Day of Resurrection will go seventy cubits into the earth, and it will reach the mouths of people or their noses; Thawr doubted which of the two he said."
"9417","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Abu Suhayl ibn Abi Malik, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not love to have Uhud as gold with me, with three nights passing over me while I have anything of it, except something I set aside for settling a debt due upon me."
"9418","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is a guarantor and the muadhdhin is trusted, so may Allah guide the imams and forgive the muadhdhins."
"9419","And with this isnad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fasting person has two joys: a joy when he breaks his fast, and a joy when he meets his Lord, Mighty and Majestic."
"9420","Qutaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon Hira, he and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman and Ali and Talhah and al-Zubayr, and the rock moved, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be still, for there is upon you none but a prophet or a siddiq or a martyr."
"9421","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What a good man is Abu Bakr, what a good man is Umar, what a good man is Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, what a good man is Usayd ibn Hudayr, what a good man is Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, what a good man is Muadh ibn Jabal, what a good man is Muadh ibn Amr ibn al-J [source truncated]."
"9422","Qutaybah narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad, meaning al-Qari, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from al-Muttalib, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dawud the prophet had intense protective jealousy, and when he went out the doors were locked so none entered upon his family until he returned. He said: He went out one day and the house was locked, and his wife came looking toward the house, and there was a man standing in the middle of the house. She said to those in the house: From where did this man enter the house while the house is locked. By Allah, you will be disgraced by Dawud. Then Dawud came and there was the man standing in the middle of the house. Dawud said to him: Who are you. He said: I am the one who does not fear kings and nothing is withheld from me. Dawud said: By Allah, you are the angel of death. Welcome to the command of Allah. Then Dawud fell where his soul was taken until they finished with him and the sun rose upon him. Sulayman said to the birds: Shade Dawud. So the birds shaded him until they darkened the earth over them both. Sulayman said to them: Draw in a wing, a wing. Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) showed us how the birds did, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken and the Masrakhiyyah overcame him on that day."
"9423","Qutaybah ibn Said said, Yaqub, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you gives a date in charity from wholesome earnings except Allah takes it with His Right Hand and rears it for him as one of you rears his foal or his young camel, until it becomes for him like the mountain or greater."
"9424","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man who believes in Allah and the Last Day hates the Ansar. And were it not for the Hijrah I would have been a man of the Ansar. And if the Ansar took a valley or a mountain pass, I would take their valley or their pass. The Ansar are the inner garment and the people are the outer garment."
"9425","And with his isnad, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two kinds of wearing: al-samma, and that a man sit with his garment gathered around him with nothing of it over his private part, and he forbade mulamasah and munabadhah and muhaqalah and muzabanah."
"9426","And that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, descends to the lowest heaven every night when the first third of the night has passed, and He says: I am the King, twice. Who is it that calls upon Me so I may answer him. Who is it that asks Me so I may give him. Who is it that seeks My forgiveness so I may forgive him. And He remains thus until dawn breaks."
"9427","Ali ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath ibn Talq ibn Muawiyah al-Nakhai narrated to us, he said: I heard Talq ibn Muawiyah, he said: I heard Abu Zura narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a boy of hers and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah for him, for I have buried three. He said: You have sought protection with a strong enclosure from the Fire. Hafs said: I heard this hadith sixty years ago when I had not reached ten years, and I heard Hafs mention this speech in the year one hundred and eighty-seven."
"9428","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad said, and I myself heard it from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah, he said: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is only appointed to be followed, so when he says takbir, say takbir, and when he recites, be silent."
"9429","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad said, and I heard it myself from him: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Sad while he was supplicating, and he said: Make it one, make it one."
"9430","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Awf informed us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If knowledge were at al-Thurayya, men of the people of Faris would reach it."
"9431","Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd Allah, meaning Ibn Said ibn Abi Hind, narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Hakim, freedman of the family of al-Zubayr, from Said ibn Marjanah, that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frees a believing neck, Allah frees for every limb of him a limb from the Fire, until He frees for the hand the hand, and for the leg the leg, and for the private part the private part. Ali ibn Husayn said: Did you hear this from Abu Hurayrah. Said said: Yes. Ali ibn Husayn said to a slave boy of his, the finest of his slave boys: Call Mutarri for me. When he stood before him he said: Go, for you are free for the Face of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"9432","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Aslam and Ghifar and something of Juhaynah and Muzaynah are better with Allah on the Day of Resurrection than Tamim and Asad ibn Khuzaymah and Hawazin and Ghatafan."
"9433","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The women of the people of Paradise, the marrow of their shanks is seen from behind the flesh."
"9434","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad said, and I heard it myself from him, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves the meeting with Allah, Allah loves meeting him, and whoever hates the meeting with Allah, Allah hates meeting him."
"9435","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Maruf ibn Suwayd al-Judhami narrated to me, that he heard Ali ibn Rabah say: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no adwa and no tiyarah, and the evil eye is true."
"9436","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Makhramah ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from his father, from Irak ibn Malik, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: There is no charity due on the slave except Sadaqat al-Fitr."
"9437","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not leave camels and sheep unmilked. Whoever buys a musarrat has the better of the two views: if he wishes he keeps it, and if he wishes he returns it with a sa of dates. And a woman should not ask for the divorce of her sister, and do not outbid one another, and none of you should sell over the sale of another, and a townsman should not sell for a Bedouin."
"9438","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed me, Haywah informed me, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Abd Allah, freedman of Shaddad ibn al-Had, that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever hears a man announcing a lost animal in the mosque, let him say: May Allah not return it to you, for the mosques were not built for that."
"9439","Harun narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: I heard Haywah say: Humayd ibn Hani al-Khawlani narrated to me, from Abu Said, freedman of Ghifar, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not sell surplus water, and do not withhold herbage, lest wealth waste away and dependents go hungry."
"9440","Harun narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to me, from Haywah, from Ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: If he said it, the jihad of the old, the weak, and the woman is Hajj and Umrah."
"9441","Harun narrated to us, Ibn Wahb said, Amr ibn al-Harith al-Taymi informed me, that Jafar ibn Rabiah narrated to him, that Abd al-Rahman al-Araj narrated to him, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No ham, no ham."
"9442","Harun said, Abd Allah said, and I myself heard it from Harun, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Sumayy, freedman of Abu Bakr, that he heard Abu Salih Dhakwan narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The closest a servant is to his Lord is while he is prostrating, so increase supplication."
"9443","Harun narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ibn Hurmuz, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of you remains in prayer as long as he sits waiting for the prayer, so long as he does not break his ablution; the angels supplicate for him: O Allah, forgive him, O Allah, have mercy upon him."
"9444","Harun narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, that Abu Yunus, freedman of Abu Hurayrah, narrated to him, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, never sends down a blessing from heaven except that many people become disbelievers thereby in the morning; Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sends down rain, and they say: By such and such a star."
"9445","Hashim ibn al-Qasim said, Abd al-Hamid, meaning Ibn Bahram, narrated to us, he said: Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: While a man and his wife in former times could not afford anything, the man came from his journey and entered upon his wife hungry, struck by severe hunger. He said to his wife: Have you anything. She said: Yes, rejoice, the provision of Allah has come to you. He urged her and said: Woe to you, seek if you have anything. She said: Yes, wait a little, we hope for the mercy of Allah. When his hunger wore long upon him he said: Woe to you, get up and seek if you have bread and bring it to me, for I am spent and exhausted. She said: Yes, now the oven is baking, do not hasten. When he was silent from her for a while and she also waited lest he speak to her, she said to herself: If I got up and looked at my oven. So she got up and found her oven full of the sides of sheep and her two millstones grinding. She went to the millstone and shook it off and took out what was in her oven of the sides of sheep. Abu Hurayrah said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Abu al-Qasim, from the saying of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If she had taken what was in her two millstones and not shaken them, they would have ground until the Day of Resurrection."
"9446","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah and Jafar ibn Abi Wahshiyyah and Abbad ibn Mansur, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to his companions while they were disputing about the tree uprooted from above the earth, having no stability. Some of them said: I think it is the truffle. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The truffle is of manna, and its water is a cure for the eye, and the ajwah is of Paradise, and it is a cure for poison."
"9447","Fazarah ibn Amr said, Fulayh informed us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on a campaign he fought, and the Muslims ran out of provisions and needed food. They sought permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to slaughter the camels, and he permitted them. That reached Umar ibn al-Khattab. He said: He came and said: O Messenger of Allah, their camels carry them and convey them to their enemy; they are slaughtering them. Rather, O Messenger of Allah, call for the remnants of provisions and supplicate to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, for blessing in them. He said: Yes. He said: He called for the remnants of provisions, and the people came with what remained with them, and he gathered it, then he supplicated to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, for blessing in it, and he called for their vessels and filled them, and much remained over. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said at that: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger, and whoever meets Allah, Mighty and Majestic, with them without doubt enters Paradise."
"9448","Affan said, Abu Awanah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from a man of Banu al-Harith ibn Kab, he said: I was sitting with Abu Hurayrah, and a man came to him and asked him and said: O Abu Hurayrah, did you forbid people to fast on Friday. He said: No, by my life, but by the Lord of this sanctuary, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None of you should fast on Friday except in days he fasts therein. Then another came and said: O Abu Hurayrah, did you forbid people to pray in their sandals. He said: No, by my life, but by the Lord of this sanctuary, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying toward this station while wearing his sandals, then he left with them upon him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9449","Muhammad ibn Ubayd said, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you prays and then sits, the angels do not cease to say: O Allah, forgive him, O Allah, have mercy upon him, so long as he does not break his ablution or stand."
"9450","Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi said, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar ibn Hafs ibn Asim narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to his bed, let him take the inside of his lower garment and shake his bed with it, for he does not know what happened upon it after him. Then let him lie upon his right side, then let him say: In Your Name, my Lord, I lay my side, and by You I raise it. If You withhold my soul, have mercy upon it, and if You send it forth, guard it with what You guard Your righteous servants."
"9451","Yahya ibn Said ibn Aban ibn Said ibn al-As narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the servant girl of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her and not revile her. If she returns a second time, let him flog her and not revile her. If she returns a third time, let him flog her and not revile her. If she returns a fourth time, let him flog her and sell her for a rope of hair or a braid of hair."
"9452","Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi said, Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam retreats to Madinah as the snake retreats to its hole."
"9453","Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi said, al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast upon seeing it and break fast upon seeing it, and if the month is obscured for you, complete the number as thirty."
"9454","Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If knowledge were at al-Thurayya, men of the sons of Faris would reach it."
"9455","Makki ibn Ibrahim said, Abd Allah, meaning Ibn Said ibn Abi Hind, narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Hakim, freedman of the family of al-Zubayr, from Said ibn Marjanah, that he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frees a believing neck, Allah frees for every limb of it a limb of him from the Fire, until He frees for the hand the hand, and for the leg the leg, and for the private part the private part. He said: Ali ibn al-Husayn said: Did you hear this from Abu Hurayrah. Said said: Yes. Ali ibn al-Husayn said to a slave boy of his, the finest of his slave boys: Call a singer for me. When he stood before him he said: Go, for you are free for the Face of Allah, the Exalted."
"9456","Abd al-Razzaq said, Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Aslam and Ghifar and something of Juhaynah and Muzaynah are better with Allah on the Day of Resurrection than Tamim and Asad ibn Khuzaymah and Hawazin and Ghatafan."
"9457","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The women of the people of Paradise, the marrow of their shanks is seen from behind the flesh."
"9458","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: While I was praying the noon prayer, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam after two rakahs. A man of Banu Sulaym stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It was neither shortened nor did I forget. He said: O Messenger of Allah, you prayed only two rakahs. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is what Dhu al-Yadayn says true. They said: Yes. He said: He stood and prayed with them two other rakahs. Yahya said: Damdam ibn Jaws narrated to me, that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated two prostrations."
"9459","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, he said: Abu Salamah informed me, that Abu Hurayrah informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever stands Ramadan in faith and seeking reward, forgiven for him is what preceded of his sin, and whoever stands Laylat al-Qadr in faith and seeking reward, forgiven for him is what preceded of his sin."
"9460","Hasan said, Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, Abu Salamah narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would supplicate with these words: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the Fire, and from the punishment of the grave, and from the trial of life and death, and from the evil of the False Messiah, the Dajjal."
"9461","Hasan said, Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to me, that he heard Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not married with her maternal aunt, nor a woman with her paternal aunt."
"9462","Hasan said, Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, from Said ibn Abi Said, that his father informed him, that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman to travel a day or more except with her is one unmarriageable by kinship."
"9463","Ghassan ibn al-Rabi, a Mawsili, narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Death will be brought as a speckled ram and made to stand between Paradise and Hell. It will be said: O people of Paradise. They will crane their necks and look. And it will be said to the people of Hell. They will crane their necks and look, and they will think relief has come. Then it will be slaughtered. Then it will be said: Eternity, no death."
"9464","Abu Muawiyah and Muhammad ibn Ubayd said, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they mentioned it."
"9465","Ghassan ibn al-Rabi said, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should say: my slave and my slave girl, and the slave should not say: my lord and my lady. Let the owner say: my youth and my young woman, and let the slave say: my master and my lady, for they are the owned, and the Lord is Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"9466","Ghassan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If there is good in anything you treat yourselves with, it is in cupping."
"9467","And with his isnad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: The black seed is a cure for every disease except al-sam, and al-sam is death."
"9468","And with his isnad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: When one of you hears the adhan while the vessel is upon his hand, let him not put it down until he finishes from it."
"9469","Muhammad ibn Yazid said, Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah ibn Masud, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: I was commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah. When they say it, they protect from me their blood and their wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic. He said: When the Riddah came, Umar said to Abu Bakr: You fight them though you heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say such and such. He said: Abu Bakr said: By Allah, I will not separate between prayer and zakah, and I will fight whoever separates between them. He said: We fought with him, and we saw that was guidance."
"9470","He said, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about donkeys, is there zakah in them. He said: Nothing came to me about them except this lone verse: Whoever does an atom weight of good sees it, and whoever does an atom weight of evil sees it."
"9471","He said, Abu Muawiyah Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah guarantees for one who goes out in His path to admit him to Paradise, or to return him to his house attaining what he attained of reward or booty."
"9472","Muhammad ibn Ubayd said, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is a guarantor and the muadhdhin is trusted. O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the muadhdhins."
"9473","He said, and thus Aswad narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, as Muhammad said: Guide the imams and forgive the muadhdhins. He said, and thus he said, meaning Ibn Fudayl also, and Zaidah also; Muawiyah narrated it to us, meaning from him."
"9474","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Disputation about the Quran is disbelief."
"9475","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah guarantees for one who goes out in His path to admit him to Paradise, or to return him to his house attaining what he attained of reward or booty."
"9476","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I intended not to stay behind from a detachment going out in the path of Allah, while I have nothing to carry them upon, and I wished I were killed in the path of Allah, then brought to life, then killed, then brought to life, then killed."
"9477","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, inform us of a deed equal to jihad in the path of Allah. He said: You cannot bear it, twice or thrice. He said: They said: Inform us, perhaps we can bear it. He said: The likeness of the mujahid in the path of Allah is like the fasting, standing, devout one with the verses of Allah, not flagging from fasting nor prayer until the mujahid returns to his family."
"9478","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman was punished for a cat she tied; she neither fed it nor let it go to eat of the vermin of the earth."
"9479","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Razin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I saw him striking his forehead with his hand and saying: O people of Iraq, you claim I lie upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); let you have the benefit and upon me the sin. I bear witness I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the strap of one of you breaks, let him not walk in the other until he repairs it, and when the dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him not perform ablution until he washes it seven times."
"9480","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution on Friday and does ablution well, then comes to Friday and draws near and listens silently and hears, forgiven for him is what is between it and the next Friday, plus three days. He said: And whoever touches pebbles has engaged in idle talk."
"9481","Abu Muawiyah and Waki said, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a foreleg were gifted to me I would accept, and if I were invited to a shank I would answer. Waki said in his hadith: If a foreleg were gifted to me."
"9482","Abu Muawiyah said, al-Amash narrated to us, and Ibn Numayr said, al-Amash informed us, the meaning, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The heaviest prayer upon the hypocrites is the night prayer and the dawn prayer, and if they knew what is in them they would come to them even crawling. I intended to command the muadhdhin to call, then command a man to pray with the people, then go with men bearing bundles of firewood to people who stay behind from prayer and burn their houses over them with fire."
"9483","Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Numayr said, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu al-Hakam, freedman of the Laythiyyin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no wager except in a camel hoof or a horse hoof."
"9484","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen the truth, for Satan cannot take my likeness."
"9485","Ismail ibn Ibrahim, and he is Ibn Ulayyah, narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, and Yazid ibn Harun said, Hisham informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever forgets while fasting and eats or drinks, let him complete his fast, for Allah fed him and gave him drink."
"9486","Ismail said, Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The dog, the donkey, and the woman cut off prayer. Hisham said: I know it only from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9487","Ismail said, al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The previously married woman is consulted about herself, and the virgin is asked permission. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how is her permission. He said: That she be silent."
"9488","Ismail ibn Ibrahim said, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Amir al-Uqayli, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shown to me are the first three to enter Paradise and the first three to enter Hell. As for the first three to enter Paradise: the martyr, and an owned slave who perfects worship of his Lord and counsels his master, and a chaste continent one with dependents. And as for the first three to enter Hell: a ruler given power, and one of wealth with property who does not give the right of his property, and a boastful poor man."
"9489","Ismail said, Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog, a qirat of his deed decreases every day, except a dog of tillage or livestock."
"9490","Ismail said, Yunus, meaning Ibn Ubayd, informed us, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Hakim al-Dabbi, that he feared in the time of Ziyad or Ibn Ziyad, and came to Madinah and met Abu Hurayrah. He asked my lineage and I gave it to him. He said: O youth, shall I not narrate to you a hadith, perhaps Allah will benefit you by it. I said: Yes, may Allah have mercy upon you. He said: The first men are reckoned with on the Day of Resurrection for prayer. He said: Our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, says to His angels, and He knows best: Look into the prayer of My servant, did he complete it or diminish it. If it was complete it is written for him complete, and if he diminished anything of it, He says: Look, has My servant voluntary prayers. If he has voluntary prayers, He says: Complete for My servant his obligation from his voluntary. Then deeds are taken upon that. Yunus said: I think he mentioned the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9491","Ismail narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What security has one who raises his head in prayer before the imam that Allah will transform his form into the form of a donkey."
"9492","Ismail narrated to us, from Layth, from al-Hajjaj ibn Ubayd, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Is one of you unable, when he prays, to step forward or step back, or to his right or to his left."
"9493","Ismail narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When Ramadan came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ramadan has come to you, a blessed month; Allah has obligated its fasting upon you; in it the gates of Paradise are opened, and in it the gates of Hell are closed, and in it the devils are chained; in it is a night better than a thousand months; whoever is deprived of its good is deprived."
"9494","Ismail narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, pardons for my nation what their souls speak of, so long as they do not speak of it."
"9495","Ismail said, al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu Musab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he pointed with his hand toward Yemen: Faith is Yamani, faith is Yamani, faith is Yamani; the head of disbelief is the east, and arrogance and pride are among the loud-voiced, the people of wabar."
"9496","Ismail Ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a woman be married over her paternal aunt, and the paternal aunt over the daughter of her brother, and a woman over her maternal aunt, and the maternal aunt over the daughter of her sister; the elder is not married over the younger, nor the younger over the elder."
"9497","Ismail narrated to us, Abu Hayyan narrated to us, from Abu Zura ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was one day out before people, and a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is faith. He said: Faith is to believe in Allah and His angels and His Book and meeting Him and His messengers, and to believe in the Last Resurrection. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is Islam. He said: Islam is to worship Allah, associating nothing with Him, and to establish the prescribed prayer, and to give the obligatory zakah, and to fast Ramadan. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is ihsan. He said: To worship Allah as though you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you. He said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour. He said: The one asked about it knows no more than the asker, but I will tell you of its signs: when the slave woman gives birth to her master, that is of its signs, and when the barefoot, naked, coarse ones are heads of people, that is of its signs, and when the herders of sheep vie in building, that is of its signs, in five none knows but Allah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: Allah, with Him is knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down rain, and knows what is in wombs, and no soul knows what it earns tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it dies; Allah is Knowing, Aware. Then the man turned away, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring the man back to me. They went to bring him back and saw nothing. He said: This is Jibril, peace be upon him, he came to teach people their religion."
"9498","Ismail narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Whoever frees a share of his in a slave, its completion is in his wealth, if he has wealth; if he has no wealth, the slave is made to earn without hardship upon him."
"9499","Ismail narrated to us, Abu Hayyan narrated to us, from Abu Zura ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us one day and mentioned ghulul and magnified it and magnified its matter. Then he said: Let me not find one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a camel upon his neck, bellowing, saying: O Messenger of Allah, help me. I say: I own nothing for you; I conveyed to you. Let me not find one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a sheep upon his neck, bleating, saying: O Messenger of Allah, help me. I say: I own nothing for you; I conveyed to you. Let me not find one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a horse upon his neck, neighing, saying: O Messenger of Allah, help me. I say: I own nothing for you; I conveyed to you. Let me not find one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a soul upon his neck, crying out, saying: O Messenger of Allah, help me. I say: I own nothing for you; I conveyed to you. Let me not find one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with cloths upon his neck, fluttering, saying: O Messenger of Allah, help me. I say: I own nothing for you; I conveyed to you. Let me not find one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with gold and silver upon his neck, saying: O Messenger of Allah, help me. I say: I own nothing for you; I conveyed to you."
"9500","Abu Muawiyah and Yala ibn Ubayd said, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has an answered supplication; every prophet hastened his supplication, and I kept my supplication as intercession for my nation; it reaches, if Allah wills, whoever dies not associating anything with Allah. Yala said: Intercession."
"9501","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of the five prayers is like a flowing, abundant river at the door of one of you; he bathes in it every day five times."
"9502","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Usamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it: So what would that leave of dirt?"
"9503","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Yahya, the freedman of Jadah ibn Hubayrah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disparage food at all; if he desired it he ate it, and if he did not desire it he remained silent."
"9504","Ismail narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib informed us, from al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, he says: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: Pride is My cloak and greatness is My lower garment; whoever disputes with Me over one of them, I shall cast him into Hell."
"9505","Ismail narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever repents before the sun rises from its west, Allah will turn to him in forgiveness."
"9506","Ismail narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Umayr ibn Ishaq, he said: I saw Abu Hurayrah meet al-Hasan and say to him: Uncover your stomach so I may kiss where I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kiss; he said: So he uncovered his stomach and he kissed it."
"9507","Ismail narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The purification of the vessel of one of you, when a dog laps in it, is to wash it seven times, the first of them with dust."
"9508","Ismail narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays in a single garment, let him cross its two ends over his shoulders."
"9509","Ismail narrated to us, from Hisham, and Yazid, meaning Ibn Harun, said: Hisham informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has ninety-nine names, one hundred minus one; whoever enumerates them all will enter Paradise."
"9510","Ismail narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the call for prayer is made, none of you should hurry to it, but let him walk with calmness and dignity; pray what you catch and make up what you missed."
"9511","Ismail narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwai, from Yahya, from a man, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A funeral is not to be followed with fire or with a raised voice."
"9512","Ismail narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: So-and-so slept last night and did not pray anything until morning; so he said: Satan urinated in his ear; Yunus said: al-Hasan said: His urine, by Allah, is heavy."
"9513","Ismail narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no man who takes a word or two or three or four or five from what Allah and His Messenger decreed and puts them in the edge of his cloak and acts upon them and teaches them; I said: I, and I spread out my garment, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept speaking until his speech ended, then I gathered my garment to my chest; so I hope I have not forgotten any hadith I heard from him."
"9514","Ismail narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man must not outbid his brother, nor propose marriage upon the proposal of his brother."
"9515","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Qariz or Qarad, I do not know, Ismail doubted, that Abu Hurayrah ate lumps of dried yogurt and performed ablution, and said: Do you know what I performed ablution from; I ate lumps of dried yogurt and performed ablution from it; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Perform ablution from what fire has touched."
"9516","Ismail narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Abi Zaynab, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The martyr was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: The earth does not dry of his blood until his two wives hasten to him, as though they are two nursing mothers who lost their young in an open land; in the hand, or he said: in the hand of each one of them, is a robe better than the world and what is in it."
"9517","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, he said: Said narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Women are married for four: for their wealth, their beauty, their lineage, and their religion; so win the religious one, may your hands be dusty."
"9518","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: I heard my father narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was traveling on a journey, and a man cursed a she-camel; so he said: Where is the owner of the she-camel; the man said: I am; he said: Put her back, for your supplication against her has been answered."
"9519","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: I heard my father narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave me as I have left you; those before you perished only because of their many questions to their prophets and their differing with them; when I forbid you something, abstain from it, and when I command you with a matter, do of it what you can."
"9520","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: I heard my father narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woman is like a rib; if you insist on straightening it you will break it, and if you leave it you will enjoy it, and crookedness is in it."
"9521","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: I heard my father narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If a man peeks at you in your house and you throw a pebble at him and put out his eye, there is no sin upon you."
"9522","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: I heard my father narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Those who amass much are the lowest, except one who says with wealth: like this and like this and like this and like this, in front of him and to his right and to his left and behind him."
"9523","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: I heard my father narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until knowledge is taken away, ignorance appears, and harj increases; it was said: What is harj; he said: Killing."
"9524","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Every son of Adam decays and dust consumes him, except the tailbone; from it he was created and in it he will be reassembled."
"9525","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Maymun, he said: Abu Uthman al-Nahdi narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to go out and announce that there is no prayer except with the recitation of the Opening of the Book, and what is more."
"9526","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Maqburi, and Hajjaj said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, Saeed ibn Abi Saeed narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves sneezing and dislikes yawning; whoever sneezes and praises Allah, it is a duty upon whoever hears him to say: May Allah have mercy on you; and when one of you yawns, let him suppress it as much as he can, and let him not say: Ah, ah; for when one of you opens his mouth, Satan laughs at him or from him; Hajjaj said in his hadith: As for yawning, it is only from Satan."
"9527","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mihran narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The farther, then the farther from the mosque, the greater in reward."
"9528","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, he said: Ajlan, the freedman of al-Mushmail, narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not exchange insults while you are fasting, and if a person insults you, say: I am fasting."
"9529","Yahya, meaning Ibn Said, narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Kaysan, he said: Abu Hazim narrated to me, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the mosque, he said: O Aishah, hand me the garment; she said: I am not praying; he said: It is not in your hand; so she handed it to him."
"9530","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Kaysan, he said: Abu Hazim narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: We halted for rest with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and did not wake until the sun rose; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let each man take the head of his mount, for this is a place where Satan was present with us; he said: So we did; he said: Then he called for water and performed ablution, then prayed two rakahs before the dawn prayer, then the prayer was established and he prayed the dawn prayer."
"9531","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Kaysan narrated to us, he said: Abu Hazim narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gather, for I shall recite to you one-third of the Quran; he said: Those who gathered gathered, then he came out and recited: Say, He is Allah, One, then he entered; some of us said to others: This is news that came to him from heaven, that is what made him enter; then he came out and said: I told you I would recite to you one-third of the Quran, and it equals one-third of the Quran."
"9532","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Awf, he said: Khilas narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah and al-Hasan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever goes to a soothsayer or a fortune-teller and believes him in what he says has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9533","Yahya narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn Saeed informed us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Bushayr ibn Kab, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you differ or dispute about the road, leave seven cubits."
"9534","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, he said: Abu Hazim narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a man who left two or three dinars, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two brands or three."
"9535","Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every intoxicant is unlawful."
"9536","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, and Yahya ibn Main, they said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Saeed, meaning Ibn Abi Hind, narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Hakim narrated to me, from Saeed ibn Marjanah, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frees a slave, Allah will free, for each limb of his, a limb of him from the Fire."
"9537","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, he said: Musa ibn Abi Uthman narrated to me, he said: Abu Yahya, the freedman of Jadah, narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, that he heard from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: The caller to prayer is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, and everything moist and dry bears witness for him; and the one who attends the prayer has twenty-five good deeds written for him, and what is between them is expiated."
"9538","Yahya, and he is Ibn Said, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hold to this black seed, for in it is healing from every disease except al-sam; it was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is al-sam; he said: Death."
"9539","Yazid ibn Harun and Yala said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, the like of it about the black seed."
"9540","Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found the smell of garlic in the mosque and said: Whoever eats of this foul tree must not approach our mosque."
"9541","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A life grant is an inheritance for its people, or a permitted gift for its people."
"9542","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Ata, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"9543","Yahya narrated to us, from Awf, he said: Khilas narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Before the Hour there will be nearly thirty lying impostors, each of them saying: I am a prophet, I am a prophet."
"9544","Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would burden my community, I would command them to use the tooth-stick at every prayer, or with every prayer."
"9545","Yahya narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi, and he was a scribe for Ali, he said: Marwan used to appoint Abu Hurayrah over Madinah; he appointed him once and he prayed Friday prayer and recited Surah al-Jumuah and When the hypocrites come to you; when he finished I walked beside him and said: Abu Hurayrah, you recited two surahs that Ali, peace be upon him, recited; he said: My beloved Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited them."
"9546","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever follows the funeral of a Muslim out of faith and seeking reward, prays over it and stays until it is buried, returns with two qirats of reward, each qirat like Uhud; and whoever prays over it and returns before it is buried returns with one qirat."
"9547","Yahya narrated to us, from Awf, he said: Khilas narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The likeness of one who takes back his gift is like a dog that, when full, vomits then returns to its vomit."
"9548","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, and Muhammad ibn Jafar said: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, Ghundar said in his hadith, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every prophet has a supplication he made, and I wish to save my supplication, Allah willing, as intercession for my community on the Day of Resurrection; Ibn Jafar said: For his community."
"9549","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: Abu Hurayrah used to pass by us while we performed ablution from the water vessel and say to us: Perform ablution fully; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the heels from the Fire; Hajjaj said: The heel."
"9550","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, Allah willing, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Marwan used to appoint Abu Hurayrah over Madinah, and he would stamp his foot and say: Clear the way, clear, the commander has come, the commander has come; Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not look at one who drags his lower garment out of arrogance."
"9551","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Fast upon seeing it and break fast upon seeing it; if it is obscured to you, complete the number as thirty."
"9552","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Fast upon seeing it and break fast upon seeing it; if it is obscured to you, complete the number as thirty."
"9553","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, and Ibn Jafar said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Trim them both together or wear sandals on them both together; when you wear sandals begin with the right, and when you remove them begin with the left."
"9554","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, and Ibn Jafar said: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the servant of one of you brings his food, let him seat him with him; if he does not seat him with him, let him hand him a morsel or two, for he undertook its preparation and its heat."
"9555","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever buys a sheep whose milk was withheld then returns it returns a sa of dates with it, not brown wheat."
"9556","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, he said: Ata ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to me, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The name of Zaynab was Barrah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named her Zaynab."
"9557","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, he said: Sad ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, and Ibn Jafar said: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said, I remember it, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the dawn prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim, the Revelation, and Has there come."
"9558","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Saeed ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Hakim narrated to us, from Saeed ibn Marjanah, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frees a slave, Allah will free, for each of his limbs, a limb of him from the Fire."
"9559","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, he said: My maternal uncle al-Harith narrated to me, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah has written upon every soul its share of adultery."
"9560","Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Hospitality is three days; what is more is charity."
"9561","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Saeed ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim gives charity from wholesome earnings, and nothing ascends to heaven except what is wholesome, but it is as though he places it in the palm of the Most Merciful, Mighty and Majestic, and He nurtures it as a man nurtures his foal or his young camel, until a date becomes like a great mountain."
"9562","Yahya narrated to us, from Mujalid, he said: Amir narrated to us, from al-Muharrar ibn Abi Hurayrah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will keep asking until they say: Allah was before everything, so what was before Him."
"9563","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, he said: Ibn Abi Num narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to me, he said: Abu al-Qasim, the Prophet of repentance (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to us, he said: Whoever slanders his slave, innocent of what he said to him, the prescribed punishment will stand against him on the Day of Resurrection, unless it is as he said."
"9564","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, he said: Saeed narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Who are the most noble of people; he said: The most God-fearing of them; they said: We are not asking you about this; he said: Then Yusuf, the prophet of Allah, son of the prophet of Allah, son of the prophet of Allah, son of the intimate friend of Allah; they said: We are not asking you about this; he said: Then are you asking me about the stocks of the Arabs; the best of them in ignorance are the best of them in Islam, when they understand."
"9565","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, he said: Saeed ibn Abi Saeed narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of wrongdoing, for wrongdoing is darknesses with Allah on the Day of Resurrection; beware of obscenity, for Allah does not love obscenity or foul speech; and beware of stinginess, for it called those before you and they deemed their sacred things lawful, shed their blood, and severed their ties of kinship."
"9566","Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Saeed ibn Abi Saeed, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant girl of one of you commits adultery, then he mentioned the meaning of the hadith, meaning Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan, from Ubaydullah, he said: [source matn breaks off here]."
"9567","Yahya al-Qattan narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Saeed narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of wrongdoing, and he mentioned the hadith."
"9568","Narrated to us: [source text truncated to this single word; unable to translate further]."
"9569","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, he said: Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to me, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man demanded a camel from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); they said: We find only better than his age; so he said: Give him; so he said: You repaid me fully, may Allah repay you fully; he said: The best of people are the best of them in repayment."
"9570","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Saeed narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: And I heard my father narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: My father said: I said to Yahya: Both from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: Yes; he said: There is no commander over ten but he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection shackled; nothing will free him but justice, or injustice will destroy him."
"9571","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Saeed narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: And I heard my father narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: My father said: I said to Yahya: Both from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: Yes; he said: Two traits of the affairs of ignorance people will never leave: wailing and reviling lineage."
"9572","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, he said: al-Aswad ibn al-Ala ibn Jariyah narrated to me, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: From the time one of you leaves his house to his mosque, one foot writes a good deed and another erases a bad deed."
"9573","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The lightest of the people of the Fire in punishment wears two sandals from which his brain boils."
"9574","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."
"9575","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Khuthaym ibn Irak narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): There is no charity upon a Muslim for his horse or his slave."
"9576","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Usamah narrated to us, from Makhul, from Irak, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"9577","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, he said: Saeed narrated to me, and Hajjaj said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Saeed narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O Muslim women, Yahya said it three times: Let no woman neighbor belittle for her neighbor, even a sheep hoof."
"9578","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: I heard my father, from Abu Hurayrah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the voice of a child in prayer and lightened the prayer."
"9579","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever seizes a handspan of land without right will be collared with it on the Day of Resurrection down to seven earths."
"9580","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, he said: Saeed ibn Abi Saeed narrated to us, from Ishaq, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No people sit in a gathering and do not mention Allah in it but it will be a loss upon them; no man walks a path and does not mention Allah, Mighty and Majestic, but it will be a loss upon him; and no man goes to his bed and does not mention Allah but it will be a loss upon him."
"9581","My father said: Rawh narrated it to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Maqburi, from Ishaq, the freedman of Abdullah ibn al-Harith, and he did not say: When he goes to his bed."
"9582","Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two sales in one sale, and two kinds of wearing: that one of you wrap himself in a single garment covering the whole body, or sit with knees drawn up in a garment with nothing between him and the sky."
"9583","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Awf, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, and al-Hasan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Glorification is for men and clapping is for women."
"9584","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A woman is not to be married upon her paternal aunt or upon her maternal aunt."
"9585","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Saeed narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which women are best; he said: The one who pleases him when he looks at her, obeys him when he commands, and does not oppose him in what he dislikes concerning herself or his wealth."
"9586","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: I heard my father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: We have not made peace with them since we fought them; whoever leaves something out of fear is not of us, meaning snakes."
"9587","Yahya narrated to us, from Abdullah, he said: Saeed narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you goes to his bed, let him shake his bed with the inside of his lower garment, lie on his right, then say: In Your name, my Lord, I lay my side and by You I raise it; O Allah, if You hold my soul have mercy on it, and if You release it guard it with what You guard Your righteous servants."
"9588","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik, and he is al-Harrani, narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Saeed ibn Abi Saeed narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you goes to his bed, then he mentioned the hadith."
"9589","Yahya narrated to us, Ubaydullah informed me, from Saeed, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Were it not that I would burden my community, I would command them to use the tooth-stick with ablution, and I would delay the evening prayer to a third of the night or half the night; when a third of the night or half the night passes, He descends to the lowest heaven, Majestic and Mighty, and says: Is there any asker that I may give him; is there any seeker of forgiveness that I may forgive him; is there any repenter that I may turn to him; is there any supplicant that I may answer him."
"9590","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah informed us, from Saeed al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would burden, then he mentioned its meaning, and he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, descends each night to the lowest heaven, and he said in it: Until dawn rises."
"9591","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim narrated to us, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People follow Quraysh in this matter; their best follow their best, and their worst follow their worst."
"9592","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: I heard my father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Three at whom Allah does not look, meaning at them, on the Day of Resurrection: the lying ruler, the old adulterer, and the conceited worker."
"9593","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day must not harm his neighbor; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day must honor his guest; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day must speak good or remain silent; and Yahya once said: Or keep quiet."
"9594","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: I heard my father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: None of you should urinate in stagnant water, nor bathe in it from major impurity."
"9595","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: I heard my father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When Allah created creation, He wrote with His hand upon Himself: My mercy overcomes My anger."
"9596","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: I heard my father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not combine my name and my kunyah, for I am Abu al-Qasim; Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gives and I distribute."
"9597","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Saeed informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he traveled he used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the hardship of travel, the gloom of return, and an evil sight in family and wealth; O Allah, You are the Companion in travel and the Successor over family; O Allah, fold the earth for us and ease travel for us."
"9598","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Saeed, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Let not the desert folk overcome you over the name of your prayer."
"9599","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, he said: Salih, the freedman of al-Tawamah, narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever washes a dead person must wash himself."
"9600","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Jurayj used to worship in his hermitage; his mother came to him and said: O Jurayj, I am your mother, so speak to me; Abu Hurayrah used to describe as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) described it, placing his hand upon his right eyebrow; she found him praying and he said: O Lord, my mother and my prayer, so he chose his prayer and she returned; then she came to him and found him praying and said: O Jurayj, I am your mother, so speak to me; he said: O Lord, my mother and my prayer, so he chose his prayer; then she came to him and found him praying and said: O Jurayj, I am your mother, so speak to me; he said: O Lord, my mother and my prayer, so he chose his prayer; so she said: O Allah, this is Jurayj, and he is my son, and I spoke to him and he refused to speak to me; O Allah, do not let him die until You show him the prostitutes; had she supplicated against him to be tempted he would have been tempted; a shepherd used to shelter at his monastery; a woman went out and the shepherd lay with her and she bore a boy; it was said: From whom is this; she said: He is from the owner of the monastery; so they came with their axes and spades and came to the monastery and called him and he did not speak to them, so they began demolishing his monastery and he came down to them; they said: Ask this woman; I think he smiled; then he wiped the head of the boy and said: Who is your father; he said: The shepherd of sheep; so they said: O Jurayj, we shall rebuild what we demolished of your monastery with gold and silver; he said: No, but restore it as dust as it was; so they did."
"9601","He said: Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was a man among Banu Isra'il, a merchant, and he would lose one time and gain another; he said: There is no good in this trade; I seek a trade better than this; so he built a hermitage and devoted himself therein, and he was called Jurayj, then he mentioned it similarly."
"9602","He said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you strikes, let him avoid the face, and let him not say: May Allah disgrace your face and the face of whoever resembles your face, for Allah, mighty and majestic, created Adam, peace be upon him, in His image."
"9603","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The previously married woman is not married until she is consulted, and the virgin is not married until she is asked permission. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, and how is her permission? He said: That she remain silent."
"9604","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three supplications, there is no doubt in them: the supplication of the traveler, and the oppressed, and the supplication of the father against his son."
"9605","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, he said: I saw Abu Hurayrah prostrate in: When the sky splits asunder; I said: You prostrate in it? He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated in it."
"9606","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, and Yazid ibn Harun said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, the meaning, he said: Sa'id ibn Sam'an narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurayrah came to us in the mosque of Banu Zurayq, he said: Three things the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do which the people have abandoned: he would raise his hands extended when he entered the prayer, and magnify Allah each time he bowed and rose, and the pause before recitation, asking Allah of His bounty; Yazid said: supplicating and asking Allah of His bounty."
"9607","Yahya narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah has one hundred mercies; He sent down one mercy among mankind and jinn and vermin; by it they show affection, and by it they show mercy, and by it wild beasts show tenderness to their young; and He deferred ninety-nine to the Day of Resurrection, with which He will show mercy to His servants."
"9608","Yahya narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn Kaysan, he said: Abu Hazim narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his uncle: Say: There is no god but Allah, I shall testify for you with it on the Day of Resurrection. He said: Were it not that Quraysh would reproach me, saying: Only fear carried him to that, I would have gladdened your eye with it; so Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: Indeed you do not guide whom you love."
"9609","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Kaysan, he said: Abu Hazim narrated to me, he said: I saw Abu Hurayrah pointing with his finger repeatedly: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Abu Hurayrah, the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his family never ate their fill three consecutive days of wheat bread until he parted the world."
"9610","Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The sick is not to bring to the healthy, and he said: There is no contagion, and no bad omen, and no Hamah; so who infected the first?"
"9611","Yahya narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, he said: Ata narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The best charity is from sufficiency, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support; and Yahya once said: There is no charity except from sufficiency."
"9612","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no ablution except from ritual impurity or wind."
"9613","Yahya narrated to us, from Malik, he said: Sa'id narrated to me, and Hajjaj said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from Sa'id, the meaning, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever has, meaning with him, a wrong in his wealth or honor, let him come to him and seek absolution from him before it is taken, or taken, while he has neither dinar nor dirham; if he has good deeds, it will be taken from his good deeds and given to this one, otherwise it will be taken from the sins of this one and cast upon him."
"9614","Yahya narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Ata, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: Every prayer is recited in; what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made audible to us we made audible to you, and what he concealed from us we concealed from you."
"9615","Yahya narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas, from Abu Hurayrah, Yahya said, and perhaps he mentioned the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The servant does not draw near to Me a span except I draw near to him a cubit, and he does not draw near to Me a cubit except I draw near to him a fathom."
"9616","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The one who stabs himself is only stabbing himself in the Fire, and the one who plunges into it plunges in the Fire, and the one who strangles himself strangles himself in the Fire."
"9617","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, meaning: Allah, mighty and majestic, said: I am the best of partners; whoever does for Me a deed in which he associates other than Me, I am free of it, and it is for the one he associated."
"9618","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There will surely come upon people a time when a man will not care by what he takes wealth, by lawful or by unlawful."
"9619","Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, and Yazid said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"9620","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: I heard my father narrating, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Ibrahim was circumcised when he was eighty years old, circumcised with the adze."
"9621","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Zur'ah ibn Amr ibn Jarir narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought meat, and the foreleg was handed to him, and it pleased him, so he took a bite from it, then he said: I am the master of people on the Day of Resurrection, and do you know why that is? Allah, mighty and majestic, will gather the first and the last on one plain, the caller will make them hear and the sight will reach them, and the sun will draw near, and there will reach people of grief and distress what they cannot bear nor endure, so some people will say to others: Do you not see what you are in, do you not see what has reached you, will you not look for one who will intercede for you with your Lord, mighty and majestic; so some people will say to others: Your father Adam; so they will come to Adam, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and say: O Adam, you are the father of mankind, Allah created you with His hand and breathed into you of His spirit and commanded the angels and they prostrated to you, so intercede for us with your Lord; do you not see what we are in, do you not see what has reached us; so Adam, peace be upon him, will say: My Lord, mighty and majestic, has become angry today with an anger He never became angry with the like of before, and will never become angry with the like of after, and He forbade me from the tree and I disobeyed Him; myself, myself, myself, myself, myself; go to other than me; go to Nuh; so they will come to Nuh, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and say: O Nuh, you are the first of the messengers to the people of the earth, and Allah named you a grateful servant, so intercede for us with your Lord; do you not see what we are in, do you not see what has reached us; so Nuh will say: My Lord has become angry today with an anger He never became angry with the like of before, and will never become angry with the like of after, and I had a supplication against my people; myself, myself, myself, myself; go to other than me; go to Ibrahim; so they will come to Ibrahim and say: O Ibrahim, you are the Prophet of Allah and His close friend from the people of the earth, intercede for us with your Lord; do you not see what we are in, do you not see what has reached us; so Ibrahim will say to them: My Lord has become angry today with an anger He never became angry with the like of before, and will never become angry with the like of after, then he mentioned his lies; myself, myself, myself, myself; go to other than me; go to Musa, peace be upon him; so they will come to Musa and say: O Musa, you are the Messenger of Allah, Allah chose you with His messages and with His speech over people, intercede for us with your Lord; do you not see what we are in, do you not see what has reached us; so Musa will say to them: My Lord has become angry today with an anger He never became angry with the like of before, and will never become angry with the like of after, and I killed a soul I was not commanded to kill; myself, myself, myself, myself; go to other than me; go to Isa; so they will come to Isa and say: O Isa, you are the Messenger of Allah and His word which He cast to Maryam and a spirit from Him, he said: Thus it is, and you spoke to people in the cradle, so intercede for us with your Lord; do you not see what we are in, do you not see what has reached us; so Isa will say to them: My Lord has become angry today with an anger He never became angry with the like of before, and will never become angry with the like of after, and he did not mention for him a sin; go to other than me; go to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so they will come to me and say: O Muhammad, you are the Messenger of Allah and the seal of the prophets, Allah forgave you your sin, what preceded of it and what followed, so intercede for us with your Lord; do you not see what we are in, do you not see what has reached us; so I shall stand and come beneath the Throne and fall prostrate to my Lord, mighty and majestic, then Allah will open upon me and inspire me of His praises and good praise of Him something He never opened upon anyone before me, then it will be said: O Muhammad, raise your head, and ask and you shall be given, intercede and you shall be granted intercession; so I shall say: O Lord, my nation, my nation, O Lord, my nation, my nation, O Lord, my nation, my nation, O Lord; then He will say: O Muhammad, admit of your nation those upon whom there is no reckoning from the right gate of the gates of Paradise, and they are partners of people in what is besides of the gates; then he said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, what is between two leaves of the leaves of Paradise is as between Makkah and Hajar, or as between Makkah and Busra."
"9622","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man reviled Abu Bakr while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to wonder and smile; when he exceeded, he answered back some of his saying, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry and stood; so Abu Bakr followed him and said: O Messenger of Allah, he was reviling me while you were sitting, then when I answered back some of his saying you became angry and stood; he said: There was with you an angel defending you, then when you answered back some of his saying, Satan came, so I would not sit with Satan; then he said: O Abu Bakr, three, all of them true: no servant is wronged with a wrong and overlooks it for Allah, mighty and majestic, except Allah strengthens his victory with it, and no man opens a door of giving seeking thereby kinship except Allah increases him thereby in abundance, and no man opens a door of asking seeking thereby abundance except Allah, mighty and majestic, increases him thereby in poverty."
"9623","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, Wahb ibn Kaysan narrated to me, he said: My father passed by Abu Hurayrah and he said: Where do you intend? He said: A small flock of mine; he said: Yes, wipe its mucus and make its resting place good and pray at the side of its resting place, for it is of the beasts of Paradise, and be familiar with it, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is a land of little rain, meaning al-Madinah."
"9624","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, he said: Salm ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked shikal among horses."
"9625","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: al-Qa'qa' ibn Hakim narrated to me, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on a man who stands at night and prays and wakes his family and she prays, and if she refuses he sprinkles water on her face, and may Allah have mercy on a woman who stands at night and wakes her husband and he prays, and if he refuses she sprinkles water on his face."
"9626","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of pebbles and the sale of uncertainty."
"9627","Yahya narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, he said: Thabit al-Zuraqi narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile the wind, for it comes with mercy and punishment, but ask Allah of its good and seek refuge from its evil."
"9628","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel a day except with a mahram."
"9629","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Sa'id narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three, all of them Allah, mighty and majestic, has a right to aid: the struggler in the way of Allah, mighty and majestic, and the one who marries to keep chaste, and the contracted slave seeking payment."
"9630","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Arubah, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Adam, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The prophets are brothers of co-wives, their religion is one and their mothers different, and I am the most worthy of people of Isa son of Maryam, for there was no prophet between me and him, and he will descend, so when you see him recognize him, for he is a man of medium stature inclining to redness and whiteness, lank-haired, as if his head drips though wetness did not strike it, between two dyed garments, so he will break the cross and kill the pig and abolish the jizya and suspend the faiths until Allah destroys in his time all faiths except Islam, and Allah will destroy in his time the Messiah, the Dajjal, the liar, and security will fall upon the earth until camels graze with lions together, and tigers with cattle, and wolves with sheep, and boys and lads will play with snakes, none harming another, so he will remain as long as Allah wills him to remain, then he will die, and the Muslims will pray over him and bury him."
"9631","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Adam, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The prophets, then he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: until there is destroyed in his time the messiah of misguidance, the one-eyed liar."
"9632","Husayn narrated to us, in the exegesis of Shayban, from Qatadah, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Adam narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then he mentioned the hadith."
"9633","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man entered the mosque and prayed, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted, so he returned the greeting upon him and said: Return and pray, for you did not pray; so he returned and did that three times; he said: So he said: By the One Who sent you with the truth, I do not do better than this, so teach me; he said: When you stand for prayer, magnify Allah, then recite what is easy with you of the Quran, then bow until you are tranquil bowing, then rise until you stand straight, then prostrate until you are tranquil prostrating, then rise until you are tranquil sitting, then do that in all your prayer."
"9634","Yahya narrated to us, from Isma'il, meaning Ibn Abi Khalid, he said: Ziyad narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no Kisra after Kisra, and no Caesar after Caesar, and by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, their treasures will surely be spent in the way of Allah, mighty and majestic."
"9635","Yahya and Yazid narrated to us, from Isma'il, from his father, that Abu Hurayrah used to pray with them in al-Madinah like the prayer of Qays, and Qays did not lengthen; he said: I said: Was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying thus? He said: Yes, or briefer; and Yazid said: and briefer; Waki' narrated it to us, he said: Yes, and briefer."
"9636","Yahya narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from Muhammad, from Abu Salih Dhakwan, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id and Jabir, or two of these three, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sarf."
"9637","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Nu'm narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Gold for gold, and silver for silver, and wariq for wariq, like for like, hand to hand; whoever increases or seeks increase has dealt in usury."
"9638","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah forbade the earnings of slavewomen."
"9639","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: What is between my house and my pulpit is a meadow of the meadows of Paradise, and my pulpit is upon my Basin."
"9640","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The believer feels jealousy, and Allah is more jealous."
"9641","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: al-Ala narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No man pardons except Allah increases him thereby in honor, and charity does not decrease wealth, and no man ever pardons except Allah increases him in honor."
"9642","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: al-Ala narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Shall I not guide you to what Allah, mighty and majestic, raises degrees with and expiates sins with: abundance of steps to the mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer, and completing ablution upon dislikes."
"9643","Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah, and let them go out unfragrant."
"9644","Yahya narrated to us, from Malik, he said: al-Zuhri informed me, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced to us al-Najashi on the day he died, so he went out to the prayer place and his companions lined behind him and he magnified over him four times."
"9645","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Richness is not from abundance of goods, but richness is richness of soul."
"9646","And with its chain: The example of the struggler in the way of Allah, mighty and majestic, is the example of the devout fasting one in his house who does not flag until he returns with what he returns of spoil, or Allah takes him and admits him to Paradise."
"9647","Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa'id, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, exalted, said: I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye saw, and no ear heard, and what never occurred to the heart of a human, so recite if you wish: No soul knows what is hidden for them of comfort of eyes."
"9648","And he said (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): In Paradise is a tree, a rider travels in its shade a hundred years, not cutting it, so recite if you wish: And extended shade."
"9649","The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The place of the whip of one of you in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it, and he recited: Whoever is moved away from the Fire and admitted to Paradise has succeeded, and the life of this world is but the enjoyment of delusion."
"9650","And with its chain, he said: When the imam magnifies, magnify, and when he bows, bow, and when he prostrates, prostrate, and if he prays sitting, pray sitting."
"9651","And with its chain, he said (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): People are minerals, so the best of them in ignorance are the best of them in Islam when they understand."
"9652","And with its chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not precede the month by a day nor two days, except that one of you agrees with a fast he used to fast; fast at its sighting and break at its sighting, then if it is obscured for you, complete thirty days, then break."
"9653","And with its chain, he said: In the fetus is a ghurrah, a slave or slavewoman, so the one against whom judgment was made said: Does one have intellect who neither ate nor drank nor cried nor wailed, so the like of that is void; so he said: This speech is surely the speech of a poet; in it is a ghurrah, a slave or slavewoman."
"9654","And with its chain, he said: The righteous dream, which the Muslim sees or is seen for him, is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"9655","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: I heard my father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My eye sleeps and my heart does not sleep."
"9656","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: I heard my father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, which women are best? He said: The one who pleases him when he looks, and obeys him when he commands, and does not oppose him in what he dislikes in herself and his wealth."
"9657","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Sa'id narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Let not the people of the desert overcome you over the name of your prayer."
"9658","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: I heard my father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The least of the people of the Fire in punishment is a man for whom two sandals are made, his brain boils from them."
"9659","And with its chain, he said: I fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah, then when they say: There is no god but Allah, they protect from me their blood and wealth except by its right."
"9660","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Sumayy narrated to me, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he sneezed placed his garment or his hand upon his forehead and lowered, or softened, his voice."
"9661","Yahya narrated to us, from Malik, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced to us al-Najashi the day he died, so he went out to the prayer place and his companions lined behind him, and he magnified over him four times."
"9662","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Sa'id narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you comes to a gathering, let him greet, then if it appears to him to sit, let him sit, then if he stands while the people are sitting, let him greet, for the first is not more entitled than the last."
"9663","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, he said: Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Seven, Allah will shade them in His shade on a day there is no shade except His shade: the just ruler, and a youth who grew in the worship of Allah, and a man whose heart is attached to the mosques, and two men who loved each other in Allah, mighty and majestic, gathered upon it and parted upon it, and a man who gave charity with a charity he concealed, his left not knowing what his right spends, and a man who remembered Allah alone and his eyes overflowed, and a man whom a woman of rank and beauty called to herself, he said: I fear Allah, mighty and majestic."
"9664","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Sa'id narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O Allah, I enjoin the right of the two weak: the orphan and the woman."
"9665","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar; he said: And shighar is that a man says: Marry me your daughter and I shall marry you my daughter, or marry me your sister and I shall marry you my sister; he said: And he forbade the sale of uncertainty and pebbles."
"9666","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Thawr, meaning Ibn Yazid, narrated to us, from Makhul, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The evil eye is true, and Satan attends with it, and the envy of the son of Adam."
"9667","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man was forgiven who removed a branch of thorns from the path of people."
"9668","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih, freedman of the Sa'dis, narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Men will call forth their clans, saying: Prosperity, prosperity, while al-Madinah is better for them had they known; and by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, none endures its hardship and severity except I shall be for him a witness or intercessor on the Day of Resurrection; and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it surely expels its people as the bellows expels the dross of iron; and by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, none leaves it disliking it except Allah, mighty and majestic, replaces it with better than him."
"9669","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, and Waki' said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Hazim al-Ashja'i, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man calls his wife to his bed and she refuses him and he spends the night while angry, the angels curse her until morning; Waki' said: Upon her, angry."
"9670","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Hayyan narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Bilal, tell me of the most hopeful deed you did in Islam with benefit with you, for I heard tonight the movement of your sandals before me in Paradise; so Bilal said: I did no deed in Islam more hopeful with me in benefit except that I never purified a complete purification in an hour of night or day except I prayed with that purification what Allah decreed for me to pray."
"9671","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj, meaning Ibn Dinar, informed us, from Ja'far ibn Iyas, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mas'ud, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us with Hasan and Husayn, this upon his shoulder and this upon his shoulder, kissing this once and kissing this once until he reached us, so a man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, you love them; so he said: Whoever loves them has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me."
"9672","Ibn Numayr and Abu Usamah said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sayhan and Jayhan and the Nile and the Euphrates, and all are of the rivers of Paradise; Abu Usamah said: All are of the rivers of Paradise."
"9673","He said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash informed me, from Abu Yahya, freedman of Ja'dah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, such a woman is mentioned for abundance of her prayer and fasting and charity, except that she harms her neighbors with her tongue; he said: She is in the Fire; he said: O Messenger of Allah, such a woman is mentioned for littleness of her fasting and charity and prayer, and she gives charity of pieces of dried yogurt and does not harm her neighbors with her tongue; he said: She is in Paradise."
"9674","Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir informed me, from Isma'il ibn Ubaydullah, from Abu Salih al-Ash'ari, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he visited a sick man, and with him was Abu Hurayrah, of a fever that was with him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Rejoice, indeed Allah, mighty and majestic, says: My fire, I impose it upon My believing servant in the world, to be his portion of the Fire in the Hereafter."
"9675","Asbat narrated to us, he said: Mutarrif narrated to us, from Abu al-Jahm, from Abu Zayd, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so a woman came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, a necklace of gold? He said: A necklace of fire; she said: O Messenger of Allah, two bracelets of gold? He said: Two bracelets of fire; she said: Two earrings of gold? He said: Two earrings of fire; he said: And upon her was a bracelet of gold, so she threw it, then she said: O Messenger of Allah, if one of us does not adorn herself for her husband she is disliked with him; he said: So he said: What prevents one of you to make two earrings of silver then yellow them with saffron."
"9676","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Amr, narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down the Quran upon seven letters: Knowing, Wise, Forgiving, Merciful."
"9677","Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The soul of the believer is suspended as long as debt is upon him."
"9678","Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated to us, from Sharik, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two kinds of my nation of the people of the Fire I have not seen after: women clothed naked, deviating, enticing, upon their heads like the humps of camels, they shall not enter Paradise nor find its scent, and men with whips like the tails of cattle, beating people with them."
"9679","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glorification is for men, and clapping is for women."
"9680","And with its chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us not to precede the imam with bowing and prostration, and when he magnifies, magnify, and when he prostrates, prostrate, and when he says: Not of those who earned anger nor of those astray, say: Amen, then when it agrees with the speech of the angels, those in the mosque are forgiven, and when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: Our Lord, to You is praise."
"9681","Ya'la and Muhammad, sons of Ubayd, narrated to us, they said: al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from a shaykh of the Ansar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lives in the desert is harsh, and whoever follows hunting is heedless, and whoever comes to the doors of the ruler is tempted, and no servant increases in nearness to the ruler except he increases in distance from Allah, mighty and majestic."
"9682","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Dawud al-Awdi narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning His saying: It may be that your Lord will raise you to a praised station, he said: It is the station in which I shall intercede for my nation."
"9683","Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Usamah, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How many a fasting one has nothing of his fasting except hunger, and how many a standing one has nothing of his standing except wakefulness."
"9684","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn Kaysan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a grave and said: Bring me two palm stalks, so he placed one of them at its head and the other at its feet; so it was said: O Prophet of Allah, does that benefit him? He said: It shall not cease that some of the punishment of the grave is lightened from him as long as moisture is in them."
"9685","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Yazid, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his uncle: Say: There is no god but Allah, I shall testify for you with it with Allah on the Day of Resurrection; he said: Were it not that Quraysh would reproach me I would have gladdened your eye with it; he said: So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: Indeed you do not guide whom you love, but Allah guides whom He wills, and He is most knowing of the guided."
"9686","Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Tanafisi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited the grave of his mother and wept, and those around him wept, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I sought permission of my Lord to seek forgiveness for her and I was not permitted, and I sought His permission to visit her grave and He permitted me, so visit graves, for they remind of death."
"9687","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with madness, and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to heal me; he said: If you wish I shall supplicate Allah to heal you, and if you wish be patient and there is no reckoning upon you; she said: Rather I shall be patient and there is no reckoning upon me."
"9688","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two are in people disbelief: wailing over the dead, and reviling lineage."
"9689","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: al-A'mash said: I do not see but that he raised it, he said: Woe to the Arabs from an affair that has drawn near; successful is whoever withholds his hand; and Abu Mu'awiyah agreed with him, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9690","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of these five prayers is but the example of a flowing river at the door of one of you, he bathes from it every day five times, so what does it leave of his dirt."
"9691","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Abi Yazid, from Husayn ibn al-Lajlaj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Miserliness and faith do not gather in the belly of a Muslim man, nor do dust in the way of Allah and the smoke of Hell gather in the belly of a Muslim man."
"9692","Muhammad ibn Ubayd and Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, we find in ourselves what distresses us to speak of it, and for us is what the sun rose upon; he said: Did you find that? They said: Yes; he said: That is clear faith."
"9693","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us, from Abu Malik ibn Tha'labah ibn Abi Malik al-Qurazi, from Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: What do you count the martyr? They said: The one who fights in the way of Allah until he is killed; he said: The martyr in my nation then is surely few: the slain in the way of Allah is a martyr, and the plague-struck in the way of Allah is a martyr, and the drowned in the way of Allah is a martyr, and the one falling from his mount in the way of Allah is a martyr, and the pleurisy-afflicted in the way of Allah is a martyr; Muhammad said: The majnub is the one with side pain."
"9694","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Dawud narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The most of what admits people to the Fire are the two hollows; they said: O Messenger of Allah, and what are the two hollows? He said: The private part and the mouth; he said: Do you know the most of what admits to Paradise? Fear of Allah and good character."
"9695","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Dawud narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you shall stand to prayer while with him is harm, meaning urine and stool."
"9696","Talid ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Hajjaf narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at Ali and al-Hasan and al-Husayn and Fatimah and said: I am war to whoever wars you, and peace to whoever makes peace with you."
"9697","Ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: I heard Suhayl ibn Abi Salih mentioning, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you pray after Friday, pray four, then if something hastens you, pray two rakahs, and two rakahs when you return; Ibn Idris said: And I do not know whether this is of the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or not."
"9698","Marwan al-Fazari narrated to us, he said: Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Ja'far, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best faith with Allah, mighty and majestic, is faith in which there is no doubt, and fighting in which there is no misappropriation, and an accepted pilgrimage; he said: So Abu Hurayrah said: An accepted pilgrimage expiates the sins of that year; Marwan said: There is no doubt in it, from al-Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, or from Hisham."
"9699","Marwan al-Fazari narrated to us, he said: Subayh Abu al-Malih informed us, he said: I heard Abu Salih narrating, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not ask Him, He is angry with him."
"9700","Ammar ibn Muhammad, and he is the son of the sister of Sufyan al-Thawri, narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Mercy is not removed except from a wretched one."
"9701","Narrated to us Ammar ibn Muhammad, from Ata, meaning Ibn al-Saib, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Pride is My cloak and Greatness is My lower garment, so whoever disputes Me over anything of them I shall cast him into Hell."
"9702","Narrated to us Ammar ibn Muhammad, from al-Salt ibn Quwayd, from Abu Hurayra, who said: I heard my beloved friend Abu al-Qasim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The Hour will not come until a horned one does not butt a hornless one."
"9703","Narrated to us Abdah ibn Sulayman, who said: Narrated to us Muhammad, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I have been given comprehensive speech, and the earth has been made for me a mosque and a means of purification."
"9704","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Sufyan, from Habib, from Ibn al-Mutawwis, from al-Mutawwis, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever breaks the fast on a day of Ramadan without an excuse, fasting for a lifetime will not make up for it."
"9705","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Abu al-Umayis Utba, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yaqub, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When it is the middle of Shaban, refrain from fasting until Ramadan comes."
"9706","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Isa ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Zura, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The cat is a beast of prey."
"9707","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another. Then he said: Shall I not point you to something which, if you do it, you will love one another. Spread peace among you."
"9708","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Sufyan, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Modesty is a branch of faith."
"9709","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to lead us in prayer, reciting aloud and silently. So we recited aloud in what he recited aloud, and silently in what he kept silent, and I heard him say: There is no prayer except with recitation."
"9710","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Ibn Abi Dhib, from his uncle al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Muslims prostrated at al-Najm, except for two men of Quraysh who intended thereby to seek fame."
"9711","Narrated to us Waki and Yala and Muhammad, the two sons of Ubayd, who said: Informed us al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the son of Adam recites the prostration, Satan withdraws weeping, saying: O woe to him. He was commanded to prostrate and he prostrated, so for him is Paradise, and I was commanded to prostrate and I disobeyed, so for me is the Fire."
"9712","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every deed of the son of Adam is multiplied, the good deed ten times its like up to seven hundred times up to what Allah wills. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: Except fasting, for it is Mine and I reward for it. He leaves his food and his desire for My sake. For the fasting person are two joys, a joy at his breaking the fast and a joy at meeting his Lord, and the changed breath of the mouth of the fasting person is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk. Fasting is a shield. Fasting is a shield."
"9713","Narrated to us Waki, from al-Amash, from Abu Razin and Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, who said, and al-Amash raised it as a Prophetic report: When the strap of the sandal of one of you breaks, let him not walk in a single sandal."
"9714","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us al-Nahhas ibn Qahm al-Subahi, from Shaddad Abu Ammar, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever guards the optional forenoon prayer, his sins will be forgiven even if they are like the foam of the sea."
"9715","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Khalil ibn Murra, from Muawiya ibn Qurra, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever does not pray witr is not of us."
"9716","Narrated to us Waki, narrated to us Jafar ibn Burqan, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Richness is not from abundance of goods. Rather richness is richness of the soul."
"9717","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Abu Malih al-Madani, he heard it from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever does not call upon Allah, Allah becomes angry with him."
"9718","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Sufyan, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The heart of the old man remains young in love of two things, in gathering wealth and in long life."
"9719","Narrated to us Waki, from Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If a fly falls into the food or drink of one of you, let him dip it, when he takes it out, for in one of its wings is a disease and in the other is a cure, and it presents the disease first."
"9720","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us al-Nahhas, from a shaykh in Makkah, from Abu Hurayra, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Flee from the leper as you flee from the lion."
"9721","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Usama ibn Zayd, from Baja ibn Abdullah al-Juhani, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will come upon the people a time when the best of the people in it will be at the level of a man who has taken hold of the bridle of his horse in the path of Allah, whenever he hears a cry of alarm he mounts its back, then seeks death at its likely places, and a man in a mountain pass among these mountain passes who establishes prayer and gives zakat and leaves the people except for good."
"9722","Narrated to us Waki, narrated to us Usama ibn Zayd, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, who said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, intending a journey, and said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: I advise you to be conscious of Allah and to say Allah is Most Great upon every high place. Then when he went away he said: O Allah, fold up the earth for him and make the journey easy for him."
"9723","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Sadan al-Juhani, from Sad Abu Mujahid al-Tai, from Abu Mudilla, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The just ruler, his supplication is not rejected."
"9724","Narrated to us Waki and Abu Nuaym, and he is al-Fadl ibn Dukayn, who both said: Narrated to us Sufyan, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If you meet the Jews on the road, force them to its narrowest part, and do not greet them first. Abu Nuaym said: The polytheists on the road."
"9725","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Sufyan, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Ubayd, the freedman of Abu Ruhm, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Any woman who perfumes herself then goes out to the mosque so that her scent may be found, no prayer will be accepted from her until she washes herself as she washes from major impurity."
"9726","Narrated to us Waki, narrated to us Shuba, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayra, and Abd al-Rahman reported from Shuba, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, who said: I heard Abu Hurayra, the meaning being that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw al-Hasan ibn Ali take a date from the dates of charity and chew it in his mouth, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Kikh, kikh, for charity is not lawful for us."
"9727","Narrated to us Waki, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let none of you say to his slave: My slave, but let him say: My youth. And let the slave not say to his master: My lord, but let him say: My master."
"9728","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Ibn Abi Dhib, from Salih, the freedman of al-Tawama, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever prays over a funeral in the mosque, there is nothing for him."
"9729","Narrated to us Waki, narrated to us Hisham ibn Urwa, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was at a funeral, and Umar saw a woman and shouted at her, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Leave her, O Umar, for the eye is tearful and the soul is afflicted and the covenant with the deceased is recent."
"9730","Narrated to us Waki, narrated to us Sufyan, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: For one of you to sit upon a live coal until his clothes burn is better for him than to sit upon a grave."
"9731","Narrated to us Waki, narrated to us Sufyan, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from al-Harith ibn Makhlad, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Cursed is he who approaches his wife in her anus."
"9732","Narrated to us Waki and Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zinad, from Musa ibn Abi Uthman, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A woman shall not fast a single day while her husband is present except with his permission. Waki said: Except Ramadan."
"9733","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Dawud al-Zaafiri, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, regarding: Perhaps your Lord will raise you to a praised station. He said: Intercession."
"9734","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Sufyan, from Ziyad ibn Ismail, from Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Jafar, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The polytheists of Quraysh came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, disputing with him about the decree, and there was revealed: The Day they are dragged in the Fire upon their faces, taste the touch of Saqar. Indeed We created everything with a decree."
"9735","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Sharik, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say upon the pulpit: The most poetic word the Arabs have spoken is the saying of Labid ibn Rabia: Indeed everything except Allah is false."
"9736","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to me Sharik, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a dog or a bell."
"9737","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to me Uthman ibn Waqid, meaning al-Umari, from Kidam ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abu Kibash, who said: I brought young sheep to Medina and they became unsalable for me, so I met Abu Hurayra and asked him, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Excellent is the sacrifice, the young sheep from sheep. So the people seized upon them."
"9738","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Malik ibn Anas, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Travel is a portion of torment, preventing one of you from his sleep and his food. So when one of you has fulfilled his need from his journey, let him hasten back to his family."
"9739","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Ibn Abi Dhib, from Said ibn Abi Said, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A woman shall not travel a full day's journey except with a mahram."
"9740","Narrated to us Waki, from Sufyan, from al-Suddi, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, who said, Sufyan raising it as a Prophetic report, he said: The dead one hears the thud of their sandals when they turn away retreating."
"9741","Narrated to us Waki, narrated to us Sadan al-Juhani, from Abu Mujahid, from Abu Mudilla, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Three whose supplication is not rejected: the just ruler, and the fasting person until he breaks his fast, and the supplication of the oppressed. Allah raises it above the clouds on the Day of Resurrection, and opens for it the doors of heaven, and the Lord, Mighty and Majestic, says: By My Might, I shall surely aid you even after a while."
"9742","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Sadan al-Juhani, from Abu Mujahid al-Tai, from Abu Mudilla, from Abu Hurayra, who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, inform us about Paradise, of what is its building. He said: A brick of gold and a brick of silver, its mortar is strong-scented musk, its pebbles are ruby and pearl, and its soil is wars and saffron. Whoever enters it will abide forever and not die, and will enjoy bliss and not despair. Their youth will not wear out, nor will their garments be torn."
"9743","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Sufyan, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A child does not repay his father except by finding him enslaved, then buying him and setting him free."
"9744","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Yunus, meaning Ibn Abi Ishaq, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Jibril kept advising me about the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."
"9745","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Hammad ibn Salama, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The needy one is not the one who goes around to you, whom a morsel or two morsels turn away, but the needy one is the abstinent one."
"9746","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Sufyan, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Faith is seventy-odd doors, the lowest of them is removing harm from the road, and the highest of them is the saying: There is no god but Allah."
"9747","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Jafar ibn Burqan, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Faith is seventy-odd doors, the lowest of them is removing harm from the road, and the highest of them is the saying: There is no god but Allah."
"9748","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Jafar ibn Burqan, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: I am with the thought of My servant about Me, and I am with him when he calls upon Me."
"9749","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Ikrima ibn Ammar, from Abu Kathir al-Hanafi, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade mixing raisins and dates, and unripe dates and ripe dates, and said: Each one of them should be steeped separately."
"9750","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Aban ibn Sama, from Zubayba, the daughter of al-Numan, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade vessels except a vessel whose mouth is tied shut."
"9751","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Fudayl ibn Ghazwan al-Dabbi, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Three, when they emerge, no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before, or earned good in its faith: the rising of the sun from its west, and the smoke, and the beast of the earth."
"9752","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us al-Amash, from Umara ibn al-Qaqa, from Abu Zura, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, make the provision of the family of Muhammad a sustenance."
"9753","Narrated to us Waki, from Jarir ibn Ayyub, from Abu Zura, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever loves to recite the Quran fresh, as he said, as it was revealed, let him recite it upon the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd."
"9754","Narrated to us Waki, from Sufyan, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He is more entitled to his seat when he returns to it."
"9755","Narrated to us Waki, narrated to us Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade foul medicine, meaning poison."
"9756","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Sufyan, and Abd al-Rahman reported from Sufyan, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Ziyad ibn Thuwayb, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to me while I was complaining of illness. Abd al-Rahman said in his narration: visiting me. And he said: Shall I not teach you, Abd al-Rahman said: Shall I not perform ruqya for you with a ruqya with which Jibril, peace be upon him, performed ruqya for me. I said: Yes, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. He said: In the name of Allah I perform ruqya for you, and Allah heals you from every disease that harms you, and from the evil of the blowers in knots, and from the evil of an envier when he envies. And Abd al-Rahman said: From every disease in you."
"9757","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Sufyan, from Asim ibn Kulayb al-Jarmi, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray Duha at all except once."
"9758","Narrated to us Waki, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Jahhaf, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, I love them both, so love them both."
"9759","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Hawshab ibn Aqil, who said: Narrated to me Mahdi al-Abdi, from Ikrima, who said: He said: I entered upon Abu Hurayra in his house and asked him about fasting on the day of Arafa at Arafat, and Abu Hurayra said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade fasting on the day of Arafa at Arafat."
"9760","Narrated to us Waki, from Harun al-Thaqafi, who said: I heard Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: In every prayer there is recitation. So what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made us hear, we made you hear, and what he did not make us hear, we did not make you hear."
"9761","Narrated to us Waki, from Harun al-Thaqafi, who said: I heard Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: In every prayer there is recitation. So what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made us hear, we made you hear, and what he did not make us hear, we did not make you hear."
"9762","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be servants of Allah as brothers. Do not show enmity and do not hate one another. Be correct and draw near, and receive glad tidings."
"9763","Narrated to us Waki, from Sufyan, from Salih, meaning the freedman of al-Tawama, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No people gather in a sitting then disperse without remembering Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and sending blessings upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, except that their sitting will be a cause of regret for them on the Day of Resurrection."
"9764","Narrated to us Waki, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Salih, the freedman of al-Tawama, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he performed Hajj with his wives, said: It is only this Hajj, then remain upon the backs of mats."
"9765","Narrated to us Waki, from Muhammad ibn Sharik, who said: Narrated to us Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Excellent are thirty camels: its noble one is ridden, its utensils are lent, its rich-milking one is granted, and it is brought on its watering day to its enclosures."
"9766","Narrated to us Waki, from Sufyan, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from a shaykh who heard Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will come upon the people a time when a man will be given a choice between incapacity and immorality, so let him choose incapacity over immorality."
"9767","Narrated to us Waki, from Sufyan, from Umara ibn al-Qaqa, from Abu Zura, from Abu Hurayra, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, which charity is best. He said: That you give charity while you are miserly, or healthy, hoping for life and fearing poverty, and do not delay until when it reaches the throat you say: For so-and-so such, and for so-and-so such, and it already belonged to so-and-so."
"9768","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Mansur ibn Dinar, from Ikrima al-Makhzumi, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let none of you prevent his neighbor from placing his beams upon his wall."
"9769","Narrated to us Waki, from Aflah, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Salman al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Medina: whoever endures its hardship and adversity, I shall be for him an intercessor or a witness on the Day of Resurrection."
"9770","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Ali ibn al-Mubarak, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Maymuna, from Abu Hurayra: A woman came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, whose husband had divorced her, and she wanted to take her child. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Cast lots for him. And the man said: Who will come between me and my son. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to the son: Choose whichever of them you wish. So he chose his mother, and she went away with him."
"9771","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Israil reported from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, who said: I testify regarding Abu Hurayra and Abu Said that they both testified for me regarding the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said, and I testify regarding them both: No people sit remembering Allah except that the angels surround them, and tranquility descends upon them, and mercy covers them, and Allah mentions them among those with Him."
"9772","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to me Abdullah ibn Said, meaning Ibn Abi Hind, from Ismail ibn Abi Hakim, from Said ibn Marjana, that he narrated to Ali ibn Husayn, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever frees a slave, for him by the freeing of every limb of him will be a limb from the Fire, until he mentioned the private part. He said: So Ali ibn Husayn called a slave boy of his and set him free."
"9773","Narrated to us Waki, from Sufyan, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When a man stands from his sitting place then returns, he is more entitled to it."
"9774","Narrated to us Waki, from Sufyan, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadra, from al-Tufawi, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A man shall not touch a man in a single garment, nor a woman a woman, except the child and the mother."
"9775","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Dhakwan, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The heart of the old man remains young in love of two things: gathering wealth and long life."
"9776","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to me Malik ibn Anas, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Abu Sufyan, the freedman of Abu Ahmad, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with them and forgot, and when he gave the greeting of peace he prostrated two prostrations, then gave the greeting of peace."
"9777","Narrated to us Waki, narrated to us al-Amash, who said: Informed us Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, who said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: So-and-so prays at night, then when morning comes he steals. He said: What he says will soon forbid him from that."
"9778","Narrated to us Waki, narrated to us Hammad ibn Salama, from Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayra, who said: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, carrying al-Hasan ibn Ali upon his shoulder, with his saliva flowing upon him."
"9779","Narrated to us Waki, narrated to us Hammad, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Leave me as I have left you, for those before you were destroyed only by their questioning and their differing with their prophets. So when I command you with a matter, follow it as much as you are able, and when I forbid you from a matter, avoid it."
"9780","Narrated to us Waki, from Sufyan, from Umara ibn al-Qaqa, from Abu Zura, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had a pause in the prayer."
"9781","Narrated to us Waki, from Sufyan, from Umara ibn al-Qaqa, from Abu Zura, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had a pause in the prayer."
"9782","Narrated to us Waki, narrated to us Kamil Abu al-Ala, who said: I heard Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Seek refuge with Allah from the head of the seventieth year and the rule of boys. Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Kamil Abu al-Ala, who said: I heard Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, wonders at people who are led to Paradise in chains."
"9783","Narrated to us Waki, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: When al-Tufayl and his companions came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Daws has disobeyed. He said: O Allah, guide Daws and bring them."
"9784","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mawhab, from his uncle Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Wahb, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no Muslim who turns his face to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, in a request, except that He gives it to him, either hastening it for him, or storing it for him."
"9785","Narrated to us Waki, who said: Narrated to us Usama ibn Zayd, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, the freedman of al-Aswad ibn Sufyan, from Ibn Thawban, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to prayer, and when he said the takbir he left and gestured to them, meaning: As you are. Then he went out and performed ghusl, then came with his head dripping, and prayed with them. Then when he had prayed he said: I was in a state of major impurity and forgot to wash."
"9786","Narrated to us Yazid ibn Harun, who said: Informed us Ibn Abi Dhib, and Rawh said: Narrated to us Ibn Abi Dhib, from Salih, the freedman of al-Tawama, who said: I heard Abu Hurayra describe the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: He was broad in the forearms, long in the eyelashes of the eyes, wide between the shoulders, turning all together when he turned, and withdrawing all together when he withdrew. Rawh said in his narration: May my father and mother be sacrificed for him, he was not obscene, nor using obscene language, nor shouting in the markets."
"9787","Narrated to us Yazid ibn Harun, who said: Informed us Ibn Abi Dhib, and Hashim ibn al-Qasim reported from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said regarding the Mother of the Quran: It is the Mother of the Quran, and it is the Seven Oft-Repeated, and it is the Magnificent Quran."
"9788","Narrated to us Yazid ibn Harun and Hashim, who both said: Informed us Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, who said, Hashim said in his narration: from his father, that he heard Abu Hurayra say: Were it not for two matters I would have loved to be a slave, and that is because I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Allah has not created a slave who fulfills the right of Allah and the right of his master except that Allah gives him his reward twice. Yazid said: The slave cannot dispose of anything in his wealth."
"9789","Narrated to us Ismail ibn Umar, who said: Narrated to us Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Praise be to Allah is the Mother of the Quran, and the Mother of the Book, and the Seven Oft-Repeated."
"9790","Narrated to us Yazid ibn Harun, who said: Informed us Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: You will covet leadership, and it will become regret and remorse on the Day of Resurrection. So evil is the nursing and good is the weaning."
"9791","Narrated to us Yazid, who said: Informed us Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayra, who said: Adam and Musa disputed, peace and blessings of Allah be upon them both, and Adam overcame Musa. And Musa said: You are Adam who made mankind wretched and brought them out of Paradise. And Adam said: You are Musa whom Allah chose with His messages and with His speech, and upon whom He sent down the Torah. Do you not find in it that Allah had decreed it upon me before He created me. He said: Yes. Amr ibn Said and Ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari said: So Adam overcame Musa. Muhammad said: The beginning of the narration suffices me: So Adam overcame Musa, peace be upon them both."
"9792","Narrated to us Yazid, who said: Informed us Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O sons of Abd al-Muttalib, buy yourselves from Allah. O Safiyya, aunt of the Messenger of Allah, and O Fatima, daughter of the Messenger of Allah, buy yourselves from Allah. I avail you nothing against Allah. Ask me of my wealth what you wish."
"9793","Narrated to us Yazid, who said: Informed us Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, there will come upon one of you a day when seeing me, then seeing me, will be dearer to him than having the like of his family and his wealth."
"9794","Narrated to us Yazid, who said: Informed us Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A woman will not be straight for you upon one character. She is only like the rib: if you straighten it you break it, and if you leave it you enjoy her, and in her is crookedness."
"9795","Narrated to us Yazid, who said: Informed us Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in Zuhr prayer, and in the rear rows was a man who prayed badly. Then when he gave the greeting of peace, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called to him: O so-and-so, will you not be conscious of Allah. Do you not see how you pray. You think that anything of what you do is hidden from me. By Allah, I see from behind me as I see from in front of me."
"9796","Narrated to us Yazid, who said: Informed us Muhammad, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of women who rode camels are the righteous women of Quraysh, the kindest to a child in his smallness, and the most caring for a husband in what he possesses."
"9797","Narrated to us Yazid, who said: Informed us Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The needy one is not he whom a date turns away, but the needy one is he who does not ask the people, and is not noticed so that he is given to."
"9798","Narrated to us Yazid, who said: Informed us Muhammad, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, and Muhammad reported from one who heard Abu Salih al-Samman narrate from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If one of you fights, let him avoid the face."
"9799","Narrated to us Yazid, who said: Informed us Muhammad ibn Amr, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: For every people of a deed there is a gate of the gates of Paradise by which they are called with that deed, and for the people of fasting there is a gate by which they are called, called al-Rayyan. And Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, is there anyone who will be called from all those gates. He said: Yes, and I hope that you are among them, O Abu Bakr."
"9800","Narrated to us Yazid, who said: Informed us Muhammad, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A prophet among the prophets alighted under a tree, and an ant bit him, so he ordered his baggage and it was taken out from under it, then he ordered it and it was burned with fire. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed to him: Why not a single ant."
"9801","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn al-Mughira ibn Mu'ayqib, from Amr ibn Sulayman ibn Abd — Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Its isnad was not accurately preserved; rather he is Sulayman ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Utwar, and he is the companion of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, Abu al-Haytham — from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, and from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayra — both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I take with You a covenant which You will never break for me, for I am only a human being, so whichever of the believers I harm, or revile, or curse, or flog, make it for him a purification and a prayer and a nearness by which You draw him near to You on the Day of Resurrection."
"9802","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salama, he said: I saw Abu Hurayra prostrate in ""When the sky is rent asunder,"" so I said: You prostrated in a sura in which prostration is not performed? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrate in it."
"9803","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the reciter says ""not of those who earned anger nor of those astray,"" and those behind him say Amin, and that coincides with the saying of the people of heaven, Amin, he is forgiven what preceded of his sin."
"9804","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has never listened to anything as He listens to a prophet chanting the Qur'an aloud."
"9805","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and heard the recitation of a man, so he said: Who is this? It was said: Abdullah ibn Qays. So he said: This one has been given of the melodious voices of the family of Dawud."
"9806","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I seek Allah's forgiveness, Mighty and Majestic, and repent to Him every day a hundred times."
"9807","And with his isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Madina — whoever commits an innovation therein, or shelters an innovator, or takes as an ally other than his master, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; Allah will not accept from him any sarf nor any adl."
"9808","And with his isnad he said: Ma'iz ibn Malik al-Aslami came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed adultery. So he turned away from him. Then he came from his right side and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed adultery. So he turned away from him. Then he came to him from his left side and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed adultery. He said that to him four times. So he said: Take him away and stone him. He said: So they took him away, and when the stones touched him he turned and fled with force, so a man met him with a camel's jawbone in his hand and struck him with it. His flight when the stones touched him was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Why did you not leave him?"
"9809","And with his isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The religion will remain manifest as long as the people hasten the breaking of the fast; indeed the Jews and the Christians delay it."
"9810","And with his isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tribulation will not cease to afflict the believing man or the believing woman in his body and his wealth and his child until he meets Allah, Mighty and Majestic, with no sin upon him."
"9811","And with his isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This minbar of mine is upon a channel of the channels of Paradise."
"9812","And with his isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ghifar and Aslam and Muzayna and whoever is of Juhayna are better than the two treacherous allied tribes, Asad and Ghatafan and Hawazin and Tamim, for they are the people of horses and of fur."
"9813","And with his isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves wealth, it is for his family, and whoever leaves dependents, they come to me."
"9814","And with his isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lowest of the people of Paradise in station is one who wishes upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and it is said: That is yours, and the like of it with it, except that he is prompted, so it is said to him: Such-and-such and such-and-such, and it is said: That is yours, and the like of it with it. Then Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So it is said: That is yours, and ten times its like."
"9815","And with his isnad he said: The Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Fire and Paradise argued. The Fire said: The tyrants and the arrogant will enter me. And Paradise said: The weak and the poor will enter me. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said to the Fire: You are My punishment; I take vengeance with you upon whom I will. And He said to Paradise: You are My mercy; I show mercy with you to whom I will."
"9816","And with his isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I would not love to have Uhud as gold with a third night passing over me while I have any of it with me and I find one who would accept it from me, except that I reserve it for a debt that is upon me."
"9817","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until thirty liars come out, men, all of them lying upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9818","And with his isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will surely follow the ways of those before you, arm's length by arm's length, cubit's length by cubit's length, span by span, until if they entered the hole of a lizard you would enter it with them. They said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews and the Christians? He said: Then who?"
"9819","The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was at a well drawing water, Abu Bakr came and drew a bucket or two buckets, and in them was weakness, and Allah forgive him. Then Umar, may Allah have mercy on him, came and drew until it turned in his hand into a large bucket, and the people watered the camels at the resting place, and I never saw a strong genius working like his working."
"9820","And with this isnad he said: A Jew in the market of Madina said: By the One Who chose Musa above mankind. So a man of the Ansar slapped him and said: You say this while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is among us? So the Jew came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And the Trumpet will be blown, and whoever is in the heavens and whoever is on the earth will fall down except whom Allah wills, then it will be blown in it another time, and behold they will be standing, looking. He said: So I will be the first to raise his head, and behold Musa holding to a leg of the legs of the Throne, and I will not know whether he raised his head before me or he was of those whom Allah exempted. And whoever says that I am better than Yunus ibn Matta has lied."
"9821","And with his isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: When the servant loves meeting Me, I love meeting him, and when the servant hates meeting Me, I hate meeting him. He said: So it was said to Abu Hurayra: There is none of us but hates death and is frightened by it. Abu Hurayra said: When that time comes, it is unveiled to him."
"9822","And with the isnad the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The poor of the believers will enter Paradise before the rich by half a day, five hundred years."
"9823","And with the isnad the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, meaning: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: And who is more unjust than one who creates like My creation? Then let them create a gnat, or let them create an atom."
"9824","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If you find nothing but sheepfolds and camel resting places, then pray in the sheepfolds and do not pray in the camel resting places."
"9825","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Layth informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, he said: While we were in the mosque, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: Set out to the Jews. So we went out with him until we came to the House of Study, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and called them: O company of Jews, accept Islam and you will be safe. They said: You have conveyed, O Abu al-Qasim. He said: That is what I intend. Then he said it a third time and said: Know that the earth belongs to Allah and His Messenger, and I intend to expel you from this land, so whoever of you finds anything for his property, let him sell it, otherwise know that the earth belongs to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and His Messenger."
"9826","And with his isnad, from Abu Hurayra, he said: When Khaybar was conquered, a sheep containing poison was given to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gather for me whoever is here of the Jews. So they were gathered for him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: I am asking you about something, so will you be truthful to me about it? They said: Yes, O Abu al-Qasim. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Who is your father? They said: Our father is so-and-so. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have lied; your father is so-and-so. They said: You spoke the truth and were right. He said to them: Will you be truthful to me about something I ask you about? They said: Yes, O Abu al-Qasim, and if we lie to you, you will know our lie as you knew it about our father. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who are the people of the Fire? They said: We will be in it a little while, then you will succeed us in it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: We will never succeed you in it. Then he said to them: Will you be truthful to me about something I ask you about? They said: Yes, O Abu al-Qasim. So he said: Did you put poison in this sheep? They said: Yes. He said: What carried you to do that? They said: We intended, if you were a liar, to be rid of you, and if you were a prophet, it would not harm you."
"9827","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prophet among the prophets but has been given of the signs the like of which mankind believed upon, and what I was given was only a revelation which Allah revealed to me, so I hope to be the most followed of them on the Day of Resurrection."
"9828","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to me, from his brother Abbad ibn Abi Sa'id, that he heard Abu Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from four: from knowledge that does not benefit, and from a heart that does not humble itself, and from a soul that is never satisfied, and from a supplication that is not heard."
"9829","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth said, he said: Bukayr ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Nu'aym Abu Abdullah al-Mujmir, that he said: I prayed with Abu Hurayra above this mosque, and he recited ""When the sky is rent asunder"" and prostrated in it, and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrate in it."
"9830","Hajjaj and Yunus narrated to us, both said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Bukayr narrated to me, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The deed of none of you will save him. A man said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, except that Allah envelops me with His mercy. But be upright."
"9831","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: In Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider travels a hundred years."
"9832","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to me that he heard Abu Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent horsemen toward Najd, and they brought a man of Banu Hanifa, Thumama ibn Uthal, the chief of the people of Yamama, and they tied him to a pillar of the pillars of the mosque. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to him and said to him: What do you have, O Thumama? He said: I have good, O Muhammad: if you kill, you kill one with blood upon him, and if you bestow favor, you bestow it upon a grateful one, and if you want wealth, ask and you will be given of it what you wish. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left him until the next day, when he said to him: What do you have, O Thumama? He said: What I said to you: if you bestow favor, you bestow it upon a grateful one, and if you kill, you kill one with blood upon him, and if you want wealth, ask and you will be given of it what you wish. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left him until the day after the next day, and said: What do you have, O Thumama? He said: I have what I said to you: if you bestow favor, you bestow it upon a grateful one, and if you kill, you kill one with blood upon him, and if you want wealth, ask and you will be given of it what you wish. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Release Thumama. So they took him to palm trees near the mosque, and he washed himself, then entered the mosque and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. O Muhammad, by Allah, there was no face on the earth more hateful to me than your face, and your face has become the most beloved of all faces to me. By Allah, there was no religion more hateful to me than your religion, and your religion has become the most beloved of religions to me. By Allah, there was no land more hateful to me than your land, and your land has become the most beloved of lands to me. Your horsemen took me, and I intend Umra, so what do you think? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him glad tidings and ordered him to perform Umra. When he came to Makka, one said to him: You have apostatized? He said: No, but I have accepted Islam with Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No, by Allah, not a grain of wheat will come to you from Yamama until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permits it."
"9833","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, he said: Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, that he was asked about a man joining between a woman and the maternal aunt of her father, and a woman and the maternal aunt of her mother, or between a woman and the paternal aunt of her father, or a woman and the paternal aunt of her mother. He said: Qabisa ibn Dhu'ayb said: I heard Abu Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade joining between a woman and her maternal aunt, and between a woman and her paternal aunt. So we consider the maternal aunt of her mother and the paternal aunt of her mother to be of that station, and if it is through suckling, it is of that station as well."
"9834","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, that he said: Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf informed me that he heard Abu Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, do not come to it running, but come to it walking, with tranquility upon you; what you catch, pray, and what you miss, complete."
"9835","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Hurayra, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever says to a child: Come, take this, then does not give him, it is a lie."
"9836","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, he said: I am the most like you in prayer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said ""Allah hears him who praises Him,"" he said: O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise. Both said: And he used to say takbir when he bowed, and when he stood from prostration, and when he raised his head from the two prostrations."
"9837","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, both said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A time will surely come upon the people when a man will not care by what he takes wealth, whether lawful or unlawful."
"9838","Hajjaj and Yazid narrated to us, both said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever does not leave false speech and acting upon it and ignorance, Allah has no need that he leave his food and his drink."
"9839","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from his father, that he heard Abu Hurayra say: Were it not for two matters, I would love to be an owned slave, and that is because the owned slave cannot dispose of his wealth in anything, and that is because I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah has not created a servant who fulfills the right of Allah and the right of his master but Allah pays him his reward twice."
"9840","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: No Muslim man habituates himself to the mosques for prayer and remembrance but Allah rejoices with him, meaning when he comes out of his house, as the family of an absent one rejoice at their absent one when he comes to them."
"9841","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to me, from Abu Ubayda, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, that he heard Abu Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he mentioned the like of it."
"9842","Hajjaj narrated to us, and Yazid narrated to us, both said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from Salih the freed slave of al-Taw'ama, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No people sit in a gathering in which they do not remember Allah therein and do not send blessings upon their Prophet but it will be a loss upon them."
"9843","Hajjaj narrated to us, from Layth, he said: Bukayr ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us in an expedition and said: If you find so-and-so and so-and-so, two men of Quraysh, burn them with fire. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when we intended to depart: I had ordered you to burn so-and-so and so-and-so with fire, yet none punishes with fire but Allah, so if you find them, kill them."
"9844","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to me, he said: Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman and Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, that he said: A man of the Muslims came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the mosque and called him: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed adultery. So he turned away from him. Then he moved to face him and said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed adultery. So he turned away from him, until he repeated that to him four times. When he testified against himself four times, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and said: Are you mad? He said: No. He said: Have you been married? He said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take him away and stone him. Ibn Shihab said: One who heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say informed me: I was among those who stoned him. So we stoned him at the place of prayer, and when the stones hurt him he fled, and we caught him at al-Harra and stoned him."
"9845","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he judged for one who committed adultery and was not married that he be exiled a year with the hadd upon him."
"9846","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Uqayl narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that Abu Hurayra used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."
"9847","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be brought a deceased man with a debt upon him, and he would ask: Has he left anything to settle it? If they said: Yes, he left payment, he would pray over him; otherwise he would say to the Muslims: Pray over your companion. When Allah granted him conquests, he stood and said: I am closer to the believers than their own selves, so whoever of the believers dies and leaves a debt, its payment is upon me, and whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs."
"9848","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba, from Abu Hurayra, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is no omen, and the best of it is the good omen. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the good omen? He said: A good word which one of you hears."
"9849","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: May Allah fight the Jews and the Christians; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"9850","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, that he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith informed me that he heard Abu Hurayra say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for prayer, he would say takbir when he stood, then say takbir when he bowed, then say ""Allah hears him who praises Him"" when he raised his spine from the bow, then say while standing ""Our Lord, to You belongs praise,"" then say takbir when he went down prostrating, then say takbir when he raised his head, then say takbir when he went down prostrating, then say takbir when he raised his head, then do that in the whole prayer until he finished it, and say takbir when he stood from the two rak'as after sitting."
"9851","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'qub narrated to me, from Ibn Darra the freed slave of Uthman, he said: While we were at al-Baqi' with Abu Hurayra, we heard him say: I am the most knowledgeable of people about the intercession of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Resurrection. He said: So the people crowded upon him and said: Tell us, may Allah have mercy on you. He said: He says: O Allah, forgive every Muslim servant who meets You believing in me, not associating anything with You."
"9852","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said — or Abu al-Qasim said, upon him be prayer and peace: Fast at its sighting and break the fast at its sighting, and if it is obscured to you, count thirty."
"9853","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he mentioned it."
"9854","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayra narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — or he said: Abu al-Qasim said, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever drags his lower garment out of arrogance, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will not look at him."
"9855","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to me, from Budayl, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to seek refuge in Allah from the torment of the grave, and from the torment of Hell, and from the trial of the Masih al-Dajjal."
"9856","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: People of my companions will surely be driven away from the Hawd as the strange one of the camels is driven away."
"9857","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Juhada narrate, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade the earnings of slavewomen."
"9858","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayra, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — or he said: Abu al-Qasim said, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The wound of the stray beast is without liability, and the well is without liability, and the mine is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth. Shu'ba said: I heard no one say ""al-raka'iz"" except him."
"9859","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, and Abu al-Nadr, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ayyash, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he prostrated in ""When the sky is rent asunder."""
"9860","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Ash'ath ibn Sulaym, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The congregational prayer exceeds the prayer alone by twenty-seven degrees, or twenty-five degrees."
"9861","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Ibrahim ibn Jarir, from Abu Zur'a, from Abu Hurayra, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the lavatory, he called for water and cleaned himself, then wiped his hand on the ground, then performed ablution."
"9862","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from Salih the freed slave of al-Taw'ama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever washes a dead person, let him wash himself, and whoever carries him, let him perform ablution."
"9863","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Salm ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Nakha'i, from Abu Zur'a, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever names himself with my name, let him not use my kunya, and whoever uses my kunya, let him not name himself with my name."
"9864","Aswad narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, and he mentioned the like of it."
"9865","Hajjaj and Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, both said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from Salih the freed slave of al-Taw'ama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays over a funeral in the mosque, there is nothing for him."
"9866","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Irak, from Abu Hurayra, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Among the worst of people is the double-faced one who comes to these with a face and to these with a face."
"9867","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that Abu Hurayra said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I was sent with concise speech, and I was aided with terror, and while I was sleeping I was brought the keys of the treasuries of the earth and they were placed in my hands."
"9868","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Ubayd the freed slave of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, that he heard Abu Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That one of you bundles a bundle of firewood and carries it on his back and sells it is better for him than asking a man who either gives him or withholds from him."
"9869","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When one of you wakes from his sleep, let him not dip his hand in his vessel until he washes it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"9870","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj narrated to us, both said: Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Dahhak narrate, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: In Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider travels seventy or a hundred years; it is the tree of eternity. Hajjaj said: Or a hundred years, the tree of eternity. I said to Shu'ba: Is it the tree of eternity? He said: There is no ""it"" in it."
"9871","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shu'ba informed us, and Affan said: Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrate, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The womb is a shoot from the Most Merciful; it says: O Lord, I have been cut; O Lord, I have been wronged; O Lord, I am treated badly; O Lord, O Lord. So its Lord, Mighty and Majestic, answers it and says: Are you not pleased that I join whoever joins you and cut whoever cuts you?"
"9872","Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Jabbar, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, he said: I heard Abu Hurayra say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that."
"9873","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shu'ba informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Abu al-Rabi', from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Four things in my nation are of the affair of ignorance which they will never leave: reviling lineages, and wailing, and ""we were rained by such-and-such star,"" and contagion: a man buys a mangy camel and puts it among a hundred camels and they become mangy — then who infected the first?"
"9874","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Warqa, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When the prayer is established, there is no prayer but the prescribed one."
"9875","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Bahz narrated to us, both said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit — Bahz said in his hadith, he said: Adi ibn Thabit informed me — he said: I heard Abu Hazim al-Ma'na narrate, from Abu Hurayra, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was a disbeliever and used to eat much food, then he accepted Islam and used to eat little food. That was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, and the Muslim eats in one intestine."
"9876","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Bahz narrated to us, both said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit — Bahz said in his hadith, he said: Adi ibn Thabit narrated to us — he said: I heard Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs, and whoever leaves a burden, its charge is upon me. Bahz said: And whoever leaves a burden, it is to us."
"9877","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj narrated to us, both said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdala, from Dhakwan, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that they said: O Messenger of Allah, one of us speaks to himself of a thing which he would hate to utter though he had all that is on the earth for it. He said: That is pure faith."
"9878","Mu'awiya narrated to us, he said: Za'ida narrated to us, from Asim, with his isnad, he said: Of the affair of the Lord, Mighty and Majestic."
"9879","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: Alqama ibn Marthad narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu al-Rabi' — and he used to sit with Abu Burda — narrate, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four things in my nation. And he mentioned the hadith like the hadith of Muhammad ibn Ja'far."
"9880","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Marwan al-Asghar, he said: I heard Abu Rafi', he said: I saw Abu Hurayra prostrate in ""When the sky is rent asunder."" He said: So I asked him, and he said: My beloved prostrated in it, and I will not cease to prostrate until I meet him."
"9881","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: A man had a right upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was harsh to him, so the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were about to attack him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: The owner of the right has speech. And he said to them: Buy for him a camel of his age and give it to him. They said: We find nothing but a camel better than his. He said: Buy for him and give him. He said: The best of you — or: your best — is the best of you in repayment."
"9882","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Hazim, narrating from Abu Hurayra — Shu'ba said: He raised it once, then did not raise it afterwards — that he said: There is no estrangement beyond three days, or above three days; so whoever estranges beyond three days, or above three days, and dies, enters the Fire."
"9883","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The wound of the stray beast is without liability, and the well is without liability, and the mine is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"9884","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ziyad say: I heard Abu Hurayra say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Seventy thousand of my nation will enter Paradise without reckoning. He said: So Ukkasha said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me of them. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make him of them. He said: Then another man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me of them. He said: So he said: Ukkasha has beaten you to it."
"9885","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj narrated to us, both said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said — Hajjaj said: Or he said: Abu al-Qasim said: Does not one of you fear — or: Does one of you not fear — that Allah will make his head the head of a donkey, or his form the form of a donkey, when he raises his head before the imam while the imam is prostrate?"
"9886","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not fast until you see the crescent, and do not break the fast until you see the crescent. And he said: Fast at its sighting and break the fast at its sighting, and if it is hidden from you, count thirty. Shu'ba said: And most of my knowledge is that he said: Do not fast until you see the crescent, and do not break the fast until you see the crescent."
"9887","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj narrated to us, both said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — Hajjaj said in his hadith, he said: I heard Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said — or Abu al-Qasim said — that he said: While a man was walking, wearing a suit, combing his forelock, admiring himself, he was swallowed up, and he keeps sinking in the earth until the Day of Resurrection. And Hajjaj said: When Allah caused him to sink."
"9888","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave me as I left you, for the people of the Book before you — or: those before you — were destroyed only by their much differing upon their prophets and their much asking. So look at what I ordered you with and follow it as much as you can, and what I forbade you, leave it."
"9889","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrating it from your Lord, Mighty and Majestic: Every deed is expiation, and fasting is Mine, and I reward for it; and the breath of the mouth of the fasting one is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."
"9890","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah wonders at peoples who are brought in chains until they enter Paradise."
"9891","And with the isnad that he said: The poor one is not he whom a morsel or two morsels, and a mouthful or two mouthfuls, or a date or two dates, repel — Shu'ba doubted about the mouthful and the date — but the poor one is he who has no sufficiency to suffice him, and does not ask people importunately, or is shy to ask people importunately."
"9892","And with his isnad he said: A woman entered the Fire for a cat which she tied and did not let it eat of the vermin of the earth."
"9893","And with the isnad: In Friday there is an hour which no Muslim servant meets asking Allah, Mighty and Majestic, therein for good but He gives it to him."
"9894","And with the isnad that he said: I would not love to have the like of Uhud as gold — Shu'ba said: Or he said: I would not love to have Uhud as gold — leaving at the day I die a dinar, unless I reserve it for a debt."
"9895","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Nakha'i, he said: I heard Abu Zur'a narrate, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Name yourselves with my name, and do not use my kunya."
"9896","He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to dislike shikal — or ashkal — in horses. Abdullah said: My father said: Shu'ba errs in this wording, Abdullah ibn Yazid; rather he is Salm ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Nakha'i."
"9897","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Ala narrate, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Faith is Yemeni, and disbelief is from the direction of the East, and tranquility is among the people of sheep, and ostentation and pride are among the loud-voiced farmers, the people of fur and the people of horses. And the Masih will come from the direction of the East, and his aim is Madina, until when he comes behind Uhud, the angels will meet him and strike his face toward Sham; there he will perish, there he will perish."
"9898","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Ala narrate, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The sun neither rises on a day nor sets on one better or greater than Friday. And there is no beast but fears Friday except these two weighty ones, of the jinn and mankind. And upon every gate are two angels writing the first then the first, like a man who offered a camel, and like a man who offered a cow, and like a man who offered a sheep, and like a man who offered a bird, and like a man who offered an egg. When the imam sits, the scrolls are folded."
"9899","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrate, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The Hour will not come until thirty impostors appear, all claiming that he is the messenger of Allah, and wealth flows and increases, and trials appear, and harj increases. It was said: What is harj? He said: Killing, killing — three times."
"9900","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Ala narrate, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Every prayer in which the Mother of the Book is not recited, it is deficient, it is deficient, it is deficient, incomplete."
"9901","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard al-'Ala' narrating from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man shall not outbid his brother, nor shall he propose marriage over his proposal."
"9902","And with his chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When one of you supplicates, let him not say: O Allah, if You will; rather let him make his desire great, for Allah, mighty and majestic is He, nothing He gives is too great for Him."
"9903","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard al-'Ala' narrating from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know what backbiting is? He said: They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Your mentioning your brother with what is not in him. He said: What do you think, if what I say about my brother is in him? He said: If what you say is in him, then you have backbitten him, and if what you say is not in him, then you have slandered him."
"9904","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from a man of Banu al-Harith, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: It is not I who forbid you to fast on Friday, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not fast on Friday unless you fast before it. And it is not I who pray in sandals, but I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in sandals."
"9905","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from Ziyad al-Harithi, he said: I heard a man asking Abu Hurayrah, and he mentioned its meaning."
"9906","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, he said: I heard Salim al-Barrad Abu 'Abdullah, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever follows a funeral and prays over it - or he said: Whoever prays over it, Shu'bah doubted - will have a qirat; and if he witnesses its burial, he will have two qirats; the qirat is like Uhud."
"9907","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The truest verse the poets have spoken is: Verily, everything besides Allah is false."
"9908","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi 'Uthman, he said: I heard Abu Yahya, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The caller to prayer is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, and everything moist and dry bears witness for him; and the one who attends the prayer will have twenty-five good deeds recorded for him, and what is between them will be expiated for him."
"9909","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, he said: I heard al-Agharr, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Perform ablution from what fire has cooked."
"9910","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Bahz both said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit - Bahz said in his hadith, he said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed me - he said: I heard 'Umarah ibn 'Umayr, from Abu al-Mutawwis, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah - and Muhammad ibn Ja'far said: from Ibn al-Mutawwis, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever breaks the fast one day in Ramadan without an excuse permitted by Allah, fasting a lifetime will not make up for it."
"9911","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, he said: A freedman of Quraysh informed me that he heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade selling war booty until it is divided - then he said after Yazid ibn Khumayr, and he knows what it is, Yazid said it the last time - and selling fruit until it is safe from every blight, and that a man should not pray unless he is girded."
"9912","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Farahij, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, kept enjoining me regarding the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."
"9913","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Farahij, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: We had no food at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except the two black things: dates and water."
"9914","And with his chain, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said - meaning Allah; Allah, mighty and majestic is He, says: Fasting is Mine, and I shall reward for it; and the changed breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."
"9915","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Jallas, he said: I heard 'Uthman ibn Shammas, he said: Marwan used to pass through al-Madinah, he said: and he would pass by Abu Hurayrah while he was narrating, and he said: Some of your hadith, O Abu Hurayrah. He said: Then he went on. He said: Then he returned and said: O Abu Hurayrah, how did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicating over the funeral? He said: He said: You created it - or he said: You created it, Shu'bah is the one who doubted - and You guided it to Islam, and You took its soul; You know its secret and its open state; we have come as intercessors, so forgive it."
"9916","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn Abi Maymunah, he said: I heard Abu Rafi' narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that Zaynab's name was Barrah, and it was said she praised herself, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named her Zaynab."
"9917","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn Abi Maymunah, from Abu Rafi', he said: I saw Abu Hurayrah prostrating during When the Sky Splits Open, and I said: Do you prostrate in it? He said: Yes; I saw my close friend prostrating in it, and I shall continue to prostrate in it until I meet him. Shu'bah said: I said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes."
"9918","Muhammad said: Shu'bah narrated to us, and Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah informed us, from 'Abbas, meaning al-Jurayri, he said: I heard Abu 'Uthman narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: My close friend enjoined upon me three things: the witr before sleep, the two rak'ahs of Duha, and fasting three days of every month."
"9919","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Shimir al-Duba'i, he said: I heard Abu 'Uthman al-Nahdi narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: My close friend enjoined upon me three things: the witr before sleep, the two rak'ahs of Duha, and fasting three days of every month."
"9920","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Abu al-Nadr both said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever catches a rak'ah of the dawn prayer before sunrise has caught the prayer, and whoever catches two rak'ahs of 'Asr before the sun sets has caught the prayer."
"9921","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said regarding the People of the Book: Do not initiate greetings with them, and if you meet them on a road, force them to its narrowest part."
"9922","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The example of the one striving in the path of Allah is like the example of the one standing in prayer without ceasing, and like the example of the one fasting without breaking fast, until the one striving in the path of Allah, mighty and majestic is He, returns."
"9923","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi: Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, that they both informed him, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the reciter says amin, then say amin, for whoever's amin coincides with the amin of the angels, his past sins will be forgiven."
"9924","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Sumayy, freedman of Abu Bakr, from Abu Salih al-Samman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the imam says: Not of those who earned anger, nor of those who went astray, then say amin, for whoever's saying coincides with the saying of the angels, his past sins will be forgiven."
"9925","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Sumayy, freedman of Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salih al-Samman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the imam says: Allah hears him who praises Him, then say: O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise, for whoever's saying coincides with the saying of the angels, his past sins will be forgiven."
"9926","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you says amin, the angels in heaven say amin, and if one of them coincides with the other, his past sins will be forgiven."
"9927","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Abu Sufyan - in the hadith of 'Abd al-Rahman, freedman of Ibn Abi Ahmad - that he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the 'Asr prayer and gave salutations after two rak'ahs, so Dhu al-Yadayn stood and said: Has the prayer been shortened, O Messenger of Allah, or did you forget? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Neither of that happened. He said: It did happen, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to the people and said: Is Dhu al-Yadayn truthful? They said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) completed what remained of his prayer, then prostrated two prostrations while seated."
"9928","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, he said: and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Sumayy, freedman of Abu Bakr, from Abu Salih al-Samman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever bathes on Friday - in the hadith of 'Abd al-Rahman: the bath of janabah - then goes early, it is as if he offered a camel; and whoever goes in the second hour, it is as if he offered a cow; and whoever goes in the third hour, it is as if he offered a horned ram - Ishaq said: horned - and whoever goes in the fourth hour, it is as if he offered a chicken; and whoever goes in the fifth hour, it is as if he offered an egg; and when the imam comes out, the angels come forward to listen to the remembrance."
"9929","Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Sayyar narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not trade by pebbles, nor practise najsh, nor trade by touching; and whoever among you buys a muhaffalah and dislikes it, let him return it, and let him return with it a sa' of food."
"9930","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Were it not that I would impose hardship upon my ummah, I would have commanded them to use the siwak with every ablution."
"9931","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, he said: and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a dog drinks from the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times."
"9932","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to me, from al-'Ala' ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'qub, from his father - in the hadith of 'Abd al-Rahman and Ishaq ibn 'Abdullah - that they both heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the call for prayer is announced, do not come to it running, but come to it with tranquillity upon you; what you catch, pray, and what you miss, complete; for one of you is in prayer as long as he is intending prayer."
"9933","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the call for prayer is made, Satan turns back with farting until he does not hear the adhan; and when the call is finished, he comes forward, until when the iqamah is announced, Satan turns back with farting until he does not hear the adhan; until when the iqamah is finished, he comes forward whispering between a man and himself, saying: Remember such-and-such, remember such-and-such, for what he did not remember, until a man remains not knowing how much he prayed."
"9934","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from al-'Ala' ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'qub, that he heard Abu al-Sa'ib, freedman of Hisham ibn Zuhrah, saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays a prayer in which he does not recite the Mother of the Qur'an, it is deficient, it is deficient, it is deficient, incomplete. So I said: O Abu Hurayrah, sometimes I am behind the imam. He said: So he squeezed my forearm and said: Recite it, O Persian, to yourself, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah, mighty and majestic is He, said: I have divided prayer between Me and My servant into two halves; half of it is Mine, and half of it is My servant's, and My servant shall have what he asks. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite. The servant says: Praise belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds. Allah, mighty and majestic is He, says: My servant has praised Me. The servant says: The Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. Allah, mighty and majestic is He, says: My servant has extolled Me. The servant says: Master of the Day of Judgment. Allah, mighty and majestic is He, says: My servant has glorified Me. The servant says: You alone we worship, and You alone we ask for help. Allah, mighty and majestic is He, says: This verse is between Me and My servant, and My servant shall have what he asks. The servant says: Guide us along the straight path, the path of those upon whom You have bestowed favor, not of those who earned anger, nor of those who went astray. These are for My servant, and My servant shall have what he asks."
"9935","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah informed us, from 'Abdullah ibn Yazid - Hajjaj said: of al-Nakha' - he said: I heard Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take my name, but do not take my kunya. And he used to dislike shikal in horses. Hajjaj said: meaning one of its legs black or white."
"9936","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah said: I heard Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, after he had grown old, saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whatever is below the ankles of the lower garment is in the Fire."
"9937","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi 'Uthman, he said: I heard Abu Yahya narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The caller to prayer is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, and everything moist and dry bears witness for him; and the one who attends the prayer will have twenty-five recorded for him, and what is between them will be expiated for him."
"9938","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashja'i, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no deception in prayer nor in greeting."
"9939","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Asim ibn 'Ubaydullah, from 'Ubayd, freedman of Abu Rahm, he said: I went out with Abu Hurayrah from the mosque, and he saw a woman with a gust of perfume from her trail, and he said: O female servant of the Almighty, did you come from the mosque? She said: Yes. He said: And did you perfume yourself for it? She said: Yes. He said: Go back, for I heard Abu al-Qasim saying: Allah does not accept the prayer of a woman who perfumes herself for the mosque - or for this mosque - until she bathes her bath from janabah."
"9940","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from 'Ata' ibn Mina', from Abu Hurayrah, he said: We prostrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during When the Sky Splits Open and Read in the Name of Your Lord."
"9941","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Mansur wrote to me that he heard Abu 'Uthman narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the truthful, the believed, the owner of this chamber, saying: Mercy is not removed except from a wretched one."
"9942","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An accepted hajj has no reward except Paradise, and two umrahs expiate the sins between them."
"9943","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The imam is a guarantor, and the caller to prayer is trusted. O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the callers to prayer."
"9944","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When it is a fasting day of one of you, let him not utter obscenity nor act ignorantly; and if someone acts ignorantly toward him, let him say: I am a fasting man."
"9945","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi' ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He who does not thank people does not thank Allah."
"9946","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu 'Uthman, freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, while we were in the mosque of the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu al-Qasim, the owner of this chamber, said: Mercy is not removed except from a wretched one."
"9947","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to me, from Sa'id, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The changed breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk. Bahz said: on the Day of Resurrection."
"9948","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Salim narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and Bahz said: Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to me, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: Fasting is a shield; and when one of you is fasting a day, let him not utter obscenity nor act ignorantly; and if someone insults him - or if a man insults him - let him say: I am fasting. Bahz said: If a man insults him or fights him, let him say: I am fasting. And likewise 'Affan said: or fights him."
"9949","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Umrah expiates what is between it and the next umrah, and an accepted hajj has no reward except Paradise."
"9950","'Affan narrated to us, he said: Salim narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting is a shield."
"9951","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Dahhak, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider travels a hundred years without crossing it: the tree of eternity."
"9952","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you shall propose over the proposal of his brother."
"9953","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman shall not be combined with her paternal aunt, nor a woman with her maternal aunt."
"9954","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed me, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer after 'Asr until the sun sets, and prayer after dawn until the sun rises."
"9955","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from 'Ata' ibn Yasar and from Busr ibn Sa'id and from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches a rak'ah of 'Asr before the sun sets has caught 'Asr, and whoever catches a rak'ah of dawn before the sun rises has caught it."
"9956","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from 'Abdullah ibn Yazid, freedman of al-Aswad ibn Sufyan, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman and Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the heat is intense, cool the prayer, for the fierceness of heat is from the exhalation of Hell. And he mentioned that the Fire complained to its Lord, so He permitted it two breaths each year: a breath in winter and a breath in summer."
"9957","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the heat is intense, delay the prayer, for the fierceness of heat is from the exhalation of Hell."
"9958","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever enters Paradise is blessed and never wretched; his clothes never wear out, and his youth never ends. In Paradise is what no eye has seen, nor ear has heard, nor has crossed the heart of man."
"9959","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man visited a brother of his in another village, so Allah stationed an angel on his path, and he said to him: Where are you going? He said: I am visiting a brother of mine for the sake of Allah in such-and-such village. He said: Does he have some favor over you that you tend? He said: No, but I loved him for the sake of Allah, mighty and majestic is He. He said: Then I am the messenger of Allah to you, that Allah has loved you as you loved him in Him."
"9960","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-'Ala' ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, and from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man outbidding his brother or proposing over his proposal."
"9961","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever buys a musarrah sheep, let him milk it; and if he is not pleased with it, let him return it, and let him return with it a sa' of dates."
"9962","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from 'Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If his neighbor asks him to plant a piece of wood in his wall, let him not prevent him."
"9963","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id narrated to us, and Bahz said: Humam narrated to us both, from Qatadah, from Abu Ayyub, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you fights, let him avoid the face. Ibn Mahdi said: For Allah, mighty and majestic is He, created Adam in His image."
"9964","'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Zuhayr, from al-'Ala', from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not vow, for a vow does not repel anything of the decree; it is only extracted by it from the miser."
"9965","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to me, from al-'Ala', from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: None of you shall say: my male slave and my female slave; all of you are slaves of Allah, and all your women are female slaves of Allah; rather let him say: my boy and my girl, and my young man and my young woman."
"9966","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No people sit in a sitting place without remembering Allah, mighty and majestic is He, and sending blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except it will be regret upon them on the Day of Resurrection, even if they enter Paradise for the reward."
"9967","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me, for Satan does not take my likeness."
"9968","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent."
"9969","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you shall say: O Allah, forgive me if You will; O Allah, have mercy on me if You will; rather let him be resolute in asking, for there is no compeller for Him."
"9970","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cleans himself with stones, let him use an odd number."
"9971","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent."
"9972","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade withholding surplus water to withhold pasture thereby."
"9973","And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We, the company of prophets, are not inherited; what I leave after the wages of my workers and the maintenance of my wives is charity."
"9974","And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Delay by the rich is injustice; and whoever is referred to a solvent one, let him transfer."
"9975","And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the closest of people to 'Isa; the prophets are brothers, children of 'allat, and there is no prophet between me and 'Isa, peace be upon him."
"9976","'Umar ibn Sa'd, and he is Abu Dawud al-Hafari, narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from 'Abd al-Rahman, meaning al-A'raj, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the closest of people to 'Isa; the prophets are sons of 'allat, and there is no prophet between me and 'Isa."
"9977","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah laughs at two men, one of whom kills the other, both entering Paradise: this one fights in the path of Allah and is martyred. He said: Then Allah turns to his killer, so he embraces Islam, then fights in the path of Allah until he is martyred."
"9978","And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not call grapes karm, for karm is only the Muslim man."
"9979","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Delay is the injustice of the rich; and whoever is referred to a solvent one, let him follow."
"9980","And with his chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: None of you shall say: O Allah, forgive me if You will, for Allah, mighty and majestic is He, has no compeller; rather let him be resolute in asking."
"9981","And with the chain: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man praying in a single garment with nothing of it upon his shoulder."
"9982","And with the chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): My heirs shall not divide a dinar; what I leave after the maintenance of my wives and the wages of my workers is charity."
"9983","And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two sales: touching and throwing, and wearing samma', and that a man sit wrapped in a single garment with nothing between him and the ground."
"9984","Mu'ammal narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am closer to every believer than himself; whoever leaves a debt or dependents, it is upon me; and whoever leaves wealth, it is for the heir."
"9985","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from 'Ammar, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the servant of one of you comes with his food, having borne its heat and labor, let him seat him to eat with him, or hand him a morsel."
"9986","Isma'il ibn 'Umar and Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham both said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It was said to him: Spend, and it will be spent upon you. Mu'awiyah said in his hadith, he said: Our Lord, mighty and majestic is He, says: Spend, and I shall spend upon you."
"9987","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman shall not fast while her husband is present except with his permission."
"9988","'Abdullah ibn al-Walid and Mu'ammal both said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to me, from Musa ibn Abi 'Uthman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man driving a sacrificial camel, and he said: Ride it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, it is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it."
"9989","He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade urinating in stagnant water that does not flow, then bathing from it. Mu'ammal said: stagnant, then bathing from it."
"9990","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from 'Ammar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Adam met Musa, and he said: Are you Adam, whom Allah created with His hand, and made His angels prostrate to you, and settled you in Paradise, then you did? He said: Are you Musa, whom Allah spoke to, and chose with His message, and sent down the Torah upon you; then am I older, or the remembrance? He said: No, rather the remembrance. So Adam prevailed over Musa; so Adam prevailed over Musa, peace be upon them both."
"9991","'Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from 'Ammar ibn Abi 'Ammar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and Humayd, from al-Hasan, from a man - Hammad said: I think him Jundub ibn 'Abdullah al-Bajali - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Adam met Musa, and he mentioned its meaning."
"9992","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Za'idah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, then the newborn? He said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"9993","'Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from 'Ammar ibn Abi 'Ammar, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When a slave obeys his Lord and obeys his master, he will have two rewards."
"9994","'Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad and 'Ammar ibn Abi 'Ammar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Men will surely leave al-Madinah desiring other than it, while al-Madinah is better for them, if only they knew."
"9995","Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Ammar ibn Abi 'Ammar and Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"9996","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Abu al-Zinad - and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman shall not be combined with her paternal aunt, nor a woman with her maternal aunt."
"9997","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, he said: and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes from his sleep, let him wash his hand before putting it into his vessel, for one of you does not know where his hand spent the night."
"9998","Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the worst of people is the double-faced one, who comes to these with one face and to these with another face."
"9999","Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting is a shield; and when one of you is fasting, let him not utter obscenity nor act ignorantly; and if a man insults him or fights him, let him say: I am fasting."
"10000","And with his chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the changed breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah, mighty and majestic is He, than the scent of musk. He says: He only abandons his desire and his food and his drink for My sake; so fasting is Mine, and I shall reward for it, from every good deed ten like it up to seven hundredfold, except fasting, for it is Mine, and I shall reward for it."
"10001","Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the one who strives in the cause of Allah is like that of the constantly fasting person who stands in prayer, who does not slacken in fasting and prayer until he returns."
"10002","Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the most false of speech. Do not spy, do not eavesdrop, do not compete against one another, do not envy one another, do not hate one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and be, O servants of Allah, brothers."
"10003","Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed me, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Delaying payment by a rich person is injustice, and if one of you is referred to a solvent person, let him accept the transfer."
"10004","Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you puts on sandals, let him begin with the right foot, and when he removes them, let him begin with the left, and let the right be the first to be shod and the last to be unshod."
"10005","And with its chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not meet the caravans on the way, and let none of you sell over the sale of another, and do not engage in false bidding, and a townsman must not sell for a Bedouin, and do not leave camels and sheep unmilked to deceive buyers. Whoever buys such an animal after that has the better of two choices after milking it: if he is pleased with it, he keeps it, and if he dislikes it, he returns it along with a sa of dates."
"10006","Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you hear a man saying, The people are ruined, he is the most ruined of them."
"10007","And with its chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The gates of heaven are opened on Monday and Thursday, and every servant who associates nothing with Allah is forgiven, except a man between whom and his brother there is enmity, whereupon it is said: Delay these two until they make peace."
"10008","And with its chain, that Sad ibn Ubadah said: O Messenger of Allah, if I find a man with my wife, should I give him respite until I bring four witnesses? He said: Yes."
"10009","He said: I recited to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Khubayb - and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Khubayb, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah or from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between my house and my minbar is a garden from the gardens of Paradise, and my minbar is over my Basin."
"10010","Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Abdullah ibn Salman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except al-Masjid al-Haram."
"10011","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr informed us, from Abu Hasin, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be upright and aim for what is right, and know that none of you will be saved by his deeds. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, unless Allah envelops me with His mercy."
"10012","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr and Israil informed us, both from Abu Hasin, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Command me with something. He said: Do not become angry. He said: Then he went on, or went away, then returned and said: Command me with something. He said: Do not become angry. He said: He repeated it several times, each time he returned, he would say: Do not become angry."
"10013","Waki narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna ibn Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Bushayr ibn Kab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make the road seven cubits wide."
"10014","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan and Misar, from Ibrahim ibn Amir ibn Masud al-Jumahi - Sufyan said: from Amir ibn Sad, and Misar said: I think, from Amir ibn Sad - from Abu Hurayrah, he said: They passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a funeral and praised it with good, so he said: It has become due. Then they passed by him with another funeral and praised it with evil, so he said: It has become due. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what has become due? He said: Some of you are witnesses over others."
"10015","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah finished creation, He wrote upon His Throne: My mercy precedes My anger."
"10016","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salih, the freedman of al-Tawamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers in other mosques, except al-Masjid al-Haram."
"10017","Waki narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does one of you love, when he returns to his family, to find three large fat pregnant camels? Three verses that one of you recites in his prayer are better for him than three large fat pregnant camels. Indeed the heaviest prayers for the hypocrites are the Isha and Fajr prayers, and if they knew what is in them, they would come to them even if crawling."
"10018","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty said: I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and what has never occurred to a human heart, as a stored reward, apart from what you have already been informed of."
"10019","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same, except that he said: Apart from what you have already been informed of."
"10020","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, he said: I saw Abu Hurayrah prostrate in Idha al-Sama unshaqqat, so I said: Did I not see you prostrate in it? He said: Had I not seen the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrate in it, I would not have prostrated."
"10021","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Marwan al-Asfar and Ata ibn Abi Maymunah, that they heard Abu Rafi saying: I saw Abu Hurayrah prostrate in Idha al-Sama unshaqqat. He said: I said: You prostrate in it? He said: I saw my dearest friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrate in it, so I will keep prostrating in it until I meet him."
"10022","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard Abu al-Qasim saying: The child belongs to the husband, and the adulterer gets the stone."
"10023","And with its chain, he said: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The best of you are the best of you in character, when they gain understanding."
"10024","And with its chain, he said: I heard Abu al-Qasim saying: Allah Almighty does not look at the one who drags his garment out of pride."
"10025","And with its chain, he said: Perform ablution well, for I heard Abu al-Qasim saying: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"10026","And with its chain, I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah Almighty said: Every deed is expiation except fasting; fasting is Mine and I reward for it."
"10027","And with its chain, he said: I heard Abu al-Qasim saying: The changed smell of the fasting person's mouth is more pleasant to Allah than the scent of musk."
"10028","And with its chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought dates from the charity dates, and he gave an instruction concerning it, then he carried al-Hasan or al-Husayn on his shoulder, and his saliva was flowing. He looked at him and saw him chewing a date from the charity dates. He said: Throw it away; did you not know that the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do not eat charity."
"10029","And with its chain, he said: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Leave me with what I have left you, for those before you were destroyed only by their questioning and their disagreeing with their prophets. When I command you with something, do it as much as you can, and when I forbid you something, avoid it."
"10030","And he said, meaning Abd al-Rahman: Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard Abu al-Qasim saying: If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much, but be upright, aim for what is right, and receive glad tidings."
"10031","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Abu Kamil narrated to us, they said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, I will drive men away from my Basin as stray camels are driven away."
"10032","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard Abu al-Qasim saying: It would not please me to have Uhud in gold with three nights passing while a dinar of it remains with me, except something I set aside for a debt."
"10033","And with its chain, I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The fire of the sons of Adam which they kindle is one part of seventy parts of the fire of Hell. A man said: It would have been sufficient. He said: It has been favored over it by sixty-nine parts, heat upon heat."
"10034","And with its chain, he said: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: While a man was walking, admiring his hair and his two cloaks, the earth swallowed him, and he keeps sinking in it until the Hour comes."
"10035","And with its chain, I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A woman entered the Fire because of a cat she tied up, neither feeding it nor watering it, nor letting it eat from the vermin of the earth."
"10036","And with its chain, I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Injury caused by a dumb animal is without liability, a mine accident is without liability, a well accident is without liability, and one-fifth is due on buried treasure."
"10037","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Bahz, in wording, narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam - Bahz said in his hadith: al-Hakam informed me - from Muhammad ibn Ali, that a man said to Abu Hurayrah: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, recites on Friday Surah al-Jumuah and Idha jaaka al-munafiqun. Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite both of them."
"10038","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, he said: I heard Abu Alqamah saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah, and whoever obeys the commander has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys the commander has disobeyed me. The Imam is but a shield. If he prays sitting, then pray sitting, and when he says, Allah hears whoever praises Him, then say, O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise. When the speech of the people on earth coincides with the speech of the people of heaven, his past sins are forgiven."
"10039","He said: Caesar will perish and there will be no Caesar after him, and Khosrau will perish and there will be no Khosrau after him."
"10040","He said: And he used to seek refuge from five: the punishment of the grave, the punishment of Hell, the trial of life, the trial of death, and the trial of al-Masih al-Dajjal."
"10041","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah informed us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, as far as I know - Shubah doubted - from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Quraysh, the Ansar, Aslam, Ghifar, Juhaynah, Muzaynah and Ashja are my allies; they have no protector besides Allah and His Messenger."
"10042","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Bahz, in wording, narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah - Bahz said: he heard Abu Salamah - from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr as two rakahs then gave the salutation. It was said to him: The prayer has been shortened. So he prayed two more rakahs, then gave the salutation, then prostrated two prostrations."
"10043","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah informed us, from Sad, he said: I heard Abu Salamah narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Aslam, Ghifar, Muzaynah, and those of Juhaynah - Hajjaj said: and those of Muzaynah - are better than Banu Tamim, Banu Amir, and the two allies, Asad and Ghatafan."
"10044","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, he said: I heard Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: No servant should say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta."
"10045","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Sad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Salamah, and he asked al-Agharr about this hadith, so al-Agharr narrated that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in other mosques, except the Kabah."
"10046","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Zurarah - Hajjaj said in his hadith: I heard Zurarah ibn Awfa - from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a woman spends the night abandoning her husband's bed, the angels curse her until she returns."
"10047","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Hilal al-Muzani, or al-Mazini, narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: This black seed is a medicine - Shubah said, or he said: a cure - for everything except al-sam. Qatadah said: Al-sam is death."
"10048","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: I heard Shubah narrating from Qatadah, from Hilal ibn Yazid, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): This black seed is a cure for every disease except al-sam. Shubah said: I said to Qatadah: What is al-sam? He said: Death."
"10049","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas - Hajjaj said in his hadith: I heard al-Nadr ibn Anas - from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When a man becomes bankrupt and a man finds his goods intact with him, he has the most right to them."
"10050","Husayn narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed me, he said: I heard Hilal ibn Yazid, of Banu Mazin ibn Shayban, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): This black seed is a cure for everything, except al-sam. And Qatadah said: Al-sam is death."
"10051","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umra is permissible."
"10052","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said concerning a slave owned by two men, when one of them frees his share: He guarantees compensation."
"10053","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, from Qatadah, he said: I heard al-Nadr ibn Anas narrating from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade gold rings."
"10054","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard a man, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had large palms."
"10055","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, he said: I heard a man ask Abu Hurayrah, he said: Was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) large in the palms and feet? I have not seen anyone like him after him."
"10056","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Sulayman ibn Yasar narrating from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No charity is due on a Muslim's servant nor on his horse."
"10057","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Hasin, he said: I heard Dhakwan Abu Salih narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has truly seen me, for Satan cannot take my form - or Shubah said: cannot resemble me - and whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"10058","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Ubayd, the freedman of Abu Ruhm, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Shall I not guide you - Hajjaj said: Shall I not guide you - to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise: There is no power except through Allah."
"10059","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If knowledge were at the Pleiades, men from the sons of Persia would attain it."
"10060","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever buys a sheep and finds it with its milk retained, he has the choice; let him return it if he wishes, along with a sa of dates."
"10061","And with its chain, I heard Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The best women who rode camels are the most affectionate to a child and the most careful of a husband regarding his property, meaning the women of Quraysh."
"10062","And with its chain, I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Fast upon seeing it and break your fast upon seeing it, and if it is obscured from you, then count thirty."
"10063","And with its chain, I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: None of you will be admitted to Paradise by his deeds. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, unless Allah envelops me with mercy from Him. Bahz said: And favor, and he placed his hand on his head."
"10064","And with its chain, I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not turn your backs on one another, do not hate one another, and be, O servants of Allah, brothers."
"10065","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If the Ansar took a valley or a mountain pass, I would take the valley of the Ansar or their mountain pass, and were it not for the Hijrah, I would be a man of the Ansar. Abu Hurayrah said: He did no wrong, may my father and mother be his ransom; they sheltered him and helped him - or: they comforted him and helped him."
"10066","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, and Abu Dawud said: Shubah informed us, in wording, except that he said: he heard Abu al-Qasim, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Aslam, may Allah grant it peace, and Ghifar, may Allah forgive it."
"10067","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Hammad, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: In Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels a hundred years without crossing it."
"10068","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The best of you in Islam are the best of you in character, when they gain understanding."
"10069","And with its chain, I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The needy person is not the one who goes around, turned away with one or two dates, and one or two morsels, but the needy person is the one who finds no sufficiency to make him rich and does not beg people importunately."
"10070","And with its chain, he said: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: In Friday there is an hour which no Muslim man coincides with, asking Allah for good therein, but He gives it to him."
"10071","And with its chain, I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Does one of you not fear, when he raises his head while the Imam is prostrating, that Allah will turn his head into the head of a donkey."
"10072","And with its chain, he said: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking refuge with Allah from the trial of life and death, from the punishment of the grave, and from the evil of al-Masih al-Dajjal."
"10073","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Ibn Qariz, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from what fire has touched."
"10074","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he raised his head from the last rakah of the last Isha prayer, would supplicate and say: O Allah, save al-Walid ibn al-Walid; O Allah, save Salamah ibn Hisham; O Allah, save Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah; O Allah, save the oppressed among the believers; O Allah, tighten Your grip on Mudar; O Allah, make them years like the years of Yusuf, peace be upon him."
"10075","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, he said: Abu Hurayrah used to say: I will show you the prayer closest to the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Hurayrah used to supplicate in the last rakah of the Zuhr prayer, the last Isha prayer, and the Fajr prayer, after saying, Allah hears whoever praises Him, supplicating for the believers and cursing the disbelievers."
"10076","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The truest word spoken by a poet is the word of Labid: Indeed everything besides Allah is false. And Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt almost accepted Islam."
"10077","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No charity is due on a believer for his servant nor for his horse."
"10078","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibrahim ibn Amir, from Amir ibn Sad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told of a man who died, and they spoke good of him and praised him with good, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has become due. And another man was mentioned to him, and they spoke evil of him and praised him with evil, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has become due. He said: You are witnesses, some of you over others."
"10079","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah."
"10080","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Salim narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is among the most false of speech. Do not spy, do not eavesdrop, do not hate one another, do not envy one another, do not compete against one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and be, O servants of Allah, brothers."
"10081","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever prays over a funeral, a qirat is recorded for him, and if he follows it until its burial is completed, he gets two qirats, the smaller of them - or one of them - like Uhud. That reached Ibn Umar and he deemed it great, so he sent to Aishah, and she said: Abu Hurayrah spoke the truth. Ibn Umar said: We have neglected many qirats."
"10082","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sufyan, he said: Habib narrated to me, from Umarah, from Ibn al-Mutawwis - then I met Ibn al-Mutawwis and he narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever breaks the fast on a day in Ramadan without an excuse which Allah Almighty has permitted, fasting eternity will not make up for it, even if he fasts it."
"10083","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib, he said: Ibn al-Mutawwis narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever breaks the fast on a day in Ramadan without illness or excuse, fasting eternity, all of it, will not make up for it, even if he fasts it. Sufyan said: Habib said: Umarah narrated to me, from Abu al-Mutawwis, then I met Abu al-Mutawwis and he narrated to me. Abu Nuaym narrated to us, and Abu al-Mutawwis said."
"10084","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Habib, from Ibn al-Mutawwis, from his father, and he mentioned it."
"10085","Yahya narrated to us, from al-Ashath, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When he sits between her four limbs and exerts himself, ghusl has become obligatory."
"10086","Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the children of the polytheists, so he said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"10087","Yahya narrated to us, from Humayd, he said: Bakr ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met me on a road of Madinah, so I slipped away and went and washed myself, then came. He said: Where were you? He said: You met me while I was junub, so I disliked sitting with you without purification. He said: The Muslim never becomes impure."
"10088","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Said narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urged charity, so a man said: I have a dinar. He said: Spend it on yourself. He said: I have another dinar. He said: Spend it on your wife. He said: I have another dinar. He said: Spend it on your child. He said: I have another dinar. He said: Spend it on your servant. He said: I have another dinar. He said: You know best."
"10089","Waki narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah or from Abu Said - al-Amash doubted - he said: It will be said to the companion of the Quran on the Day of Resurrection: Read and ascend, for your station is at the last verse you recite."
"10090","Waki narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Mansur and Ismail narrated to us - he said: Abbad informed us, in wording - from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah - and Ismail said: from Abu Hurayrah - saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty accepts charities and takes them with His right hand, and nurtures them for one of you as one of you raises his foal, or his young horse, or his young camel, until a morsel becomes like Uhud. And Waki said in his hadith: And the confirmation of that in the Book of Allah: And He is who accepts repentance from His servants and takes the charities, and Allah destroys riba and nurtures charities."
"10091","Waki narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever obeys the Imam has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys the Imam has disobeyed Allah Almighty."
"10092","Waki and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas - Bahz said in his hadith: Qatadah narrated to us - from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has two wives and inclines with one of them against the other will come on the Day of Resurrection with one of his sides fallen."
"10093","Waki narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih and Abu Razin, from Abu Hurayrah, in raised form - thus al-Amash said - he said: When one of you wakes from his sleep, let him not dip his hand into the vessel until he washes it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"10094","Waki narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, that he saw people performing ablution from the water vessel, so he said: Perform ablution thoroughly, for I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"10095","Waki narrated to us, from Shubah, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No ablution except from a sound or a smell."
"10096","Waki narrated to us, Dawud al-Awdi narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should stand for prayer while troubled by stool or urine."
"10097","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Abu al-Shatha, he said: A man left the mosque after the call for Asr was made in it, so Abu Hurayrah said: As for this one, he has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10098","Waki narrated to us, Abu Mawdud narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hadrad al-Aslami, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you spits in my mosque - or: the mosque - let him dig and bury deep, or let him spit in his garment until he takes it out."
"10099","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from his father, he said: I saw Abu Hurayrah pray a prayer in which he shortened, so I said to him: Was the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) like this? He said: Yes, and brief."
"10100","Waki narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Imam is a guarantor and the muezzin is entrusted. O Allah, guide the Imams and forgive the muezzins."
"10101","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be light in the prayer, for among them are the weak, the elderly, and the one with a need."
"10102","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The heaviest prayer upon the hypocrites is the Isha prayer and the Fajr prayer, and if they knew what is in them they would come to them even if crawling."
"10103","Waki' narrated to us: Ja'far ibn Burqan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I have intended to order my young men to gather bundles of firewood, then order the prayer to be established, then burn down upon people who do not attend the prayer."
"10104","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, and Abd al-Rahman said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to recite in the Fajr on Friday Alif Lam Mim Tanzil and Hal Ata ala al-Insan."
"10105","Waki' and Abd al-Rahman said: Sufyan narrated to us, to the same meaning, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you come to the prayer, come to it with dignity and tranquility, so what you catch, pray it, and what you miss, complete it."
"10106","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Does not the one who raises his head before the imam fear that his head be turned into the head of a donkey."
"10107","Waki' narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, from a freedman of Quraysh, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating to Mu'awiyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade a man to pray until he girds his waist-wrapper tightly."
"10108","He said: And I heard him narrating to him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling the spoils of war until they are divided. Shu'bah said: Once he said: And it is known what remains, what it is."
"10109","He said: And he forbade selling fruits until they are secured against every blight."
"10110","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The most complete of the believers in faith is the best of them in character, and the best of you are the best of you to their wives."
"10111","Yahya narrated to us: Ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever frees his share in a slave, upon him is to complete his full freedom from his wealth, and if he has no wealth, the slave shall work to pay it without undue hardship upon him."
"10112","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, he said: Salih, the freedman of al-Taw'amah, narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever washes a dead person, let him take a bath."
"10113","Yahya and Ibn Ja'far said: Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me, for Satan does not take my likeness."
"10114","Yahya narrated to us, from Zakariyya, he said: Amir narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A riding animal may be ridden in return for its maintenance when it is pledged, and the milk of a milch animal may be drunk when it is pledged, and upon the one who drinks and rides is its maintenance."
"10115","Yahya narrated to us, from Imran Abu Bakr, he said: Al-Hasan narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: My close friend, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, enjoined upon me three things: the Witr before sleeping, fasting three days of every month, and bathing on Friday."
"10116","Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Qariz, from Abu Hurayrah, if Allah wills, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque."
"10117","Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, he said: Salman al-Agharr narrated to us, he heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"10118","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, and al-Hasan, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Glorifying Allah is for men, and clapping is for women."
"10119","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: Yahya narrated to me, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Whoever keeps a dog, a qirat decreases from his deeds every day, except a dog for tillage or livestock."
"10120","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Mubarak, he said: Yahya narrated to me, he said: Damdam narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered killing the two black ones in the prayer: the snake and the scorpion."
"10121","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, forgiven for him is what preceded of his sin, and whoever stands the Night of Decree out of faith and seeking reward, forgiven for him is what preceded of his sin."
"10122","Abd al-Samad and Abu Amir narrated to us, they said: Hisham narrated to us, and they mentioned the like of it, except that they said: Whoever stands Ramadan out of faith."
"10123","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muzahim ibn Zufar, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as far as I know - Yahya doubted - he said: A dinar you spent in the path of Allah Almighty, and a dinar for the needy, and a dinar for a neck, and a dinar for your family; the greatest of them in reward is the dinar which you spend on your family."
"10124","Yahya narrated to us, from Malik, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: There is no Muslim whose three children die before reaching puberty but the Fire touches him except to fulfil the oath."
"10125","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Malik, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The excellence of congregational prayer over the prayer of a man alone is twenty-five parts. Yahya said: If Allah wills."
"10126","Yahya narrated to us, from Isma'il, meaning Ibn Abi Khalid, he said: Ziyad, meaning the freedman of Banu Makhzum, narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: We are the last, the foremost on the Day of Resurrection, and the first group of my community to enter Paradise, the form of each man of them is upon the form of the moon on the night of full moon, then those who follow them like the most intense light of a star in the sky, then they are ranks after that."
"10127","Yahya narrated to us: Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ziyad, freedman of Banu Makhzum, narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: There is none of you who enters Paradise by his deed. It was said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Not even I, unless Allah envelops me with mercy from Him and bounty."
"10128","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"10129","Yahya narrated to us, from Isma'il, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When the servant of one of you comes to him with his food, let him seat him with him, and if he does not seat him, let him give him some of it."
"10130","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa'id, he said: Dhakwan Abu Salih narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Were it not that I would cause hardship upon my community, I would not have stayed behind from an expedition going out, but they do not find mounts, nor do I find what to carry them on, and it is hard upon them to stay behind from me, and I would love to fight in the path of Allah and be killed, then be brought to life, then be killed, then be brought to life, then be killed, then be brought to life."
"10131","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, he said: Ajlan, freedman of al-Mushma'ill, narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about riding the sacrificial camel, and he said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, woe to you."
"10132","Yahya narrated to us, from Malik, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When a man says to his companion on Friday while the imam is preaching: Be quiet, he has engaged in idle talk."
"10133","Yahya narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, he said: Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever catches a prostration of the Fajr prayer before the sun rises has caught it, and whoever catches a prostration of the Asr prayer before the sun sets has caught it."
"10134","Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Narrate from the Children of Israel, and there is no blame."
"10135","Yahya narrated to us, from Yahya, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever finds his property intact with a man who has gone bankrupt, he has the most right to it."
"10136","He said: Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When it is a day one of you is fasting, let him not speak obscenely nor act ignorantly, and if ignorance is shown against him, let him say: I am a fasting man."
"10137","He said: Asbat narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: And Al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, regarding His saying Almighty: And the recitation of dawn, indeed the recitation of dawn is witnessed. He said: The angels of the night and the angels of the day witness it."
"10138","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Abu al-Qasim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The people of Yemen have come to you, they are the softest of hearts; faith is Yemeni, understanding is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni."
"10139","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Al-Muthanna reported to us, he said: Qatadah, from Bushayr ibn Ka'b, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When you dispute or differ about the road, leave seven cubits."
"10140","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Arubah, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Zurarah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Allah has overlooked for my community what their selves speak of, so long as they do not act upon it or speak of it."
"10141","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, and Hajjaj said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b reported to us, to the same meaning, he said: Sa'id narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mihran, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When I die, do not pitch a tent over me, nor follow me with fire, and hasten me to my Lord, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When the servant, or the righteous man, is placed upon his bier, he says: Take me forward, take me forward, and when the evil man is placed, he says: Woe to you, where are you going with me."
"10142","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Nafi' ibn Abi Nafi', he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no prize race except in a light-footed camel, or a blade, or a hoof. My father said: ..."
"10143","And Waki' and Yazid narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Nafi' ibn Abi Nafi', freedman of Abu Ahmad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"10144","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: A woman is not married over her paternal aunt, nor over her maternal aunt."
"10145","Yahya narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, he said: Abu Kathir narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Wine is from these two trees: the date-palm and the grapevine."
"10146","Yahya and Abd al-Rahman, to the same meaning, from Sufyan, Yahya said: Sulayman narrated to me, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never criticized food at all; when he desired it he ate it, and when he did not desire it he left it."
"10147","Yahya narrated to me, from Yazid, meaning Ibn Kaysan, he said: Abu Hazim narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and if he follows it until it is placed in the grave, he has two qirats. He said: I said: O Abu Hurayrah, what is the qirat. He said: Like Uhud."
"10148","Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Disputing about the Quran is disbelief."
"10149","Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad, meaning Ibn Amr, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah, and let them go out unattired."
"10150","And with his chain he said: For the fasting person are two joys: a joy when he breaks his fast, and a joy when he meets his Lord, and the breath of the mouth of the fasting person is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."
"10151","And with this chain of his he said, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The orphan girl is consulted about herself, so if she is silent, that is her permission, and if she refuses, there is no binding upon her."
"10152","And with his chain he said, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The wound of a dumb animal is void, and the well is void, and the mine is void, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"10153","Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he forbade two sales in one sale, and two ways of wearing: that one of you wraps himself in al-samma' in a single garment, and sits with his knees drawn up in a single garment with nothing between him and the sky."
"10154","And with his chain the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the imam says the takbir, say the takbir, and when he bows, bow, and when he prostrates, prostrate, and when he prays sitting, pray sitting."
"10155","Yahya narrated to us, from Isma'il, meaning Ibn Abi Khalid, he said: Qays ibn Abi Hazim narrated to me, he said: We came to Abu Hurayrah to greet him, he said: We said: Narrate to us. He said: I accompanied the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for three years; I was never in years more intelligent than I was in them, nor more loving to retain what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, says in them, and I saw him saying with his hand: Soon, before the Hour, you will fight a people whose sandals are hair, and you will fight a people small of eyes, red of faces, as if they are hammered shields, and by Allah, for one of you to go early and gather firewood upon his back and sell it and be independent by it and give charity from it is better for him than to come to a man and ask him, whether he gives him or withholds from him, and that is because the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support, and the breath of the mouth of the fasting person is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."
"10156","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, and Ibn Ja'far said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone."
"10157","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, and Isma'il said: Ali ibn al-Mubarak informed me, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Damdam ibn Jaws al-Hiffani, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered us to kill the two black ones in the prayer: the scorpion and the snake."
"10158","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Aflah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The prayer of a man in congregation exceeds the prayer of the solitary by twenty-five degrees."
"10159","Waki' and Abu Nu'aym said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The soul of the believer is suspended while there is debt upon him."
"10160","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - without therein from his father - the like of it."
"10161","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salih, freedman of al-Taw'amah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: I have been ordered to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah, and when they say: There is no god but Allah, they protect from me their blood and their wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah Almighty."
"10162","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salih, freedman of al-Taw'amah, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I have been ordered to fight people, and he mentioned the like of it."
"10163","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salm ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Nakha'i, from Abu Zur'ah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to dislike shikal among horses."
"10164","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The angels do not accompany a party in which there is a bell or a dog."
"10165","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b reported to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You will be eager for leadership, and it will become regret and remorse. Hajjaj said: On the Day of Resurrection. What a good nursing mother it is, and what an evil weaning mother."
"10166","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not call grapes al-karm, for al-karm is only the Muslim man."
"10167","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Isma'il al-Makhzumi, from Muhammad ibn Abbad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The idolaters of Quraysh came disputing with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the decree, so this verse was revealed: The Day they are dragged in the Fire upon their faces: Taste the touch of Saqar. Indeed, everything We created with a decree."
"10168","Waki' narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, meaning al-Laythi, from al-Maqburi, he heard it from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wanting to travel, and said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: I advise you with fear of Allah and saying the takbir upon every elevation. So when he went away, he said: O Allah, fold the earth for him and ease the journey for him."
"10169","Waki' narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Khalid, from Ziyad, freedman of Banu Makhzum, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no Kisra after Kisra, and no Caesar after Caesar, and by Him in Whose Hand my soul is, their treasures will be spent in the path of Allah."
"10170","Waki' narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hakim al-Athram, from Abu Tamimah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever comes to a menstruating woman, or a woman in her back passage, or a soothsayer and believes him in what he says, has disbelieved in what Allah revealed to Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"10171","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abi al-Zinad, from Musa ibn Abi Uthman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A woman does not fast a single day while her husband is present except with his permission, except Ramadan."
"10172","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the sale of munabadhah and mulamasah."
"10173","Waki' narrated to us: Ali ibn Salih narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of you are the best of you in repayment."
"10174","Waki' narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said in his talbiyah: I respond to You, God of truth."
"10175","Waki' narrated to us: Al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best charity is what is from surplus wealth, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support."
"10176","Waki' narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw al-Hasan ibn Ali take a date from the dates of charity and chew it in his mouth, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Kikh, kikh, three times; charity is not lawful for us."
"10177","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Muzahim ibn Zufar, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A dinar you spent in the path of Allah, and a dinar you spent for a neck, and a dinar you gave as charity, and a dinar you spent on your family; the best of them is the dinar which you spent on your family."
"10178","Waki' narrated to us: Al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, and Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every deed of the son of Adam is multiplied, the good deed ten times its like, up to seven hundred fold, up to what Allah wills; Allah Almighty says: Except fasting, for it is Mine and I reward for it; he leaves his food and his drink for My sake, and for the fasting person are two joys: a joy when he breaks his fast, and a joy at the meeting with his Lord, and the breath of the mouth of the fasting person is sweeter to Allah Almighty than the scent of musk; fasting is a shield; fasting is a shield."
"10179","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, and he mentioned its meaning."
"10180","Waki' narrated to us: Al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Him in Whose Hand my soul is, you will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another; shall I not guide you to a thing which, if you do it, you will love one another: Spread peace among you."
"10181","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Abu Mulayh al-Madani narrated to us, a shaykh from the people of Madinah, he heard it from Abu Salih, and once he said: I heard Abu Salih narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever does not call upon Allah, Allah is angry upon him."
"10182","Waki' narrated to us: Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Abu Sa'd al-Himsi, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: A supplication I memorized from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I do not leave it: O Allah, make me magnify gratitude to You, and follow Your counsel, and increase remembrance of You, and keep Your bequest."
"10183","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Muhammad ibn Abi A'ishah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you testifies, let him seek refuge in Allah from four, saying: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the torment of Hell, and the torment of the grave, and the evil of the trial of the False Messiah, and from the trial of life and death."
"10184","Waki' narrated to us: Al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"10185","Waki' narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."
"10186","Waki' narrated to us: Sa'dan al-Juhani narrated to us, from Sa'd Abu Mujahid al-Ta'i, from Abu Mudillah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The fasting person, his supplication is not rejected."
"10187","Waki' narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not precede the month of Ramadan by fasting a day or two days, except a man who used to fast a fast, let him fast it."
"10188","Waki' narrated to us: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Take the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal is blessing."
"10189","Waki' narrated to us: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Makhul, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no charity upon the Muslim man in his slave, nor his servant, nor his horse."
"10190","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan and Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no charity upon the Muslim in his horse nor his slave."
"10191","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih and Abi Razin, from Abu Hurayrah, he raising it: When the strap of the sandal of one of you breaks, let him not walk in the single sandal."
"10192","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you puts on sandals, let him begin with the right, and when he removes them, let him begin with the left; let him wear them both together or remove them both together."
"10193","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Al-Umari narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade wearing al-samma' and that a man sits with his knees drawn up in a single garment exposing his private part to the sky."
"10194","Waki' narrated to us: Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Name yourselves with my name, and do not take my kunyah."
"10195","Waki' narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: So I saw him riding it, with a sandal on its neck."
"10196","Waki' narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Gabriel came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I came to you last night, and nothing prevented me from entering upon you except a dog that was in the house, and a figure of an image on a curtain that was upon the door. He said: So they looked, and there was a puppy of al-Hasan or al-Husayn under a couch of theirs. He said: So he ordered the dog to be taken out, and the head of the image to be cut so that it becomes like a tree, and the curtain to be made into two cushions."
"10197","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade foul medicine, meaning poison."
"10198","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sips poison and kills himself with it, he will sip it in the Fire of Hell, abiding therein forever, and whoever kills himself with an iron, his iron will be in his hand stabbing himself in his belly in the Fire of Hell, abiding therein forever, and whoever throws himself from a mountain and kills himself, he will fall in the Fire of Hell, abiding therein forever."
"10199","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abi Ja'far, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Three supplications are answered, no doubt in them: the supplication of the oppressed, and the supplication of the parent, and the supplication of the traveler."
"10200","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: For the belly of one of you to fill with pus until it overcomes him is better for him than to fill with poetry."
"10201","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Rahman from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prayer in which the Opening of the Book is not recited is abortive, it is abortive, it is abortive, incomplete."
"10202","Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan from Asim ibn Kulayb from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray Duha except once."
"10203","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Dawud al-Za'afiri narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Praiseworthy Station is intercession."
"10204","Waki' narrated to us from Hammad from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed this fire of yours is one part of seventy parts of the Fire of Hell. A man said: It is surely enough, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then it was favored over it by sixty-nine parts, heat upon heat."
"10205","Waki' and Abd al-Rahman narrated from Sufyan from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim from Umar ibn Abi Salamah from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Disputation about the Qur'an is disbelief."
"10206","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from al-Aswad ibn al-Ala' ibn Jariyah from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: From the time one of you leaves his house for my mosque, one foot records a good deed and one foot erases a bad deed."
"10207","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah, narrated to us from Ibn Shihab from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz from Ibrahim ibn Qariz, he said: I saw Abu Hurayrah performing ablution above the mosque, so I said: Why are you performing ablution? He said: From bowls of dried yogurt I ate; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Perform ablution from what fire has touched."
"10208","Waki' narrated to us from Ali ibn Mubarak from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Amir al-Uqayli from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed I know the first three to enter Paradise: the martyr, and a slave who fulfilled the right of Allah and the right of his masters, and a poor chaste one who is modest; and indeed I know the first three to enter Hell: an overbearing ruler, and a wealthy man of property who does not pay its due, and a poor boastful one."
"10209","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from al-Harith ibn Makhlad from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cursed is he who approaches a woman in her anus."
"10210","Waki' narrated to us from Hammad ibn Salamah, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad said from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drags his lower garment out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"10211","He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman tied up a tomcat, or a she-cat, and did not feed it, nor let it eat from the vermin of the earth, so she entered Hell."
"10212","Waki' narrated to us from Zam'ah, meaning Ibn Salih al-Makki, from al-Zuhri from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with his Companions over al-Najashi and made four takbirs."
"10213","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Zam'ah narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sends forth three from his loins will not enter Hell except to fulfill the oath."
"10214","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Bishr from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The best of you are my generation, then those who follow them. Abu Hurayrah said: And I do not know whether he mentioned twice or thrice. Then there will succeed after them people who love fatness and testify though they are not asked to testify."
"10215","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: If I were invited to a shank or to a foreleg I would accept, and if a foreleg were gifted to me I would accept it."
"10216","He said: And I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) find fault with food at all; if he desired it he ate it, otherwise he left it."
"10217","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman from Dhakwan from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Clapping is for women and glorification is for men."
"10218","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Rawh, the meaning, both said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman from Dhakwan from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: There is no envy except in two: a man whom Allah gave the Qur'an and he recites it in the hours of the night and the hours of the day, so a man hears him and says: Would that I were given like what this one was given, so I would act in it like what this one acts in it; and a man whom Allah gave wealth and he spends it in truth, so a man says: Would that I were given like what this one was given, so I would act in it like what this one acts in it."
"10219","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us from al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no envy except in two, then he mentioned the same alike."
"10220","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman from Dhakwan from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, nor does the thief steal while he is a believer, nor does he drink wine when he drinks it while he is a believer, and repentance is offered thereafter."
"10221","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman from Dhakwan from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: If there were made for one of them, or for one of you, two good hocks, or a bone of a fat sheep, they would all come to them; and if they knew what is in them, meaning the evening prayer and the morning prayer, they would come to them even crawling; and I have intended to command a man to lead the people in prayer, then go to people who stay behind from it, or from the prayer, and burn down upon them."
"10222","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman from Dhakwan from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every good deed the son of Adam does is ten good deeds up to seven hundred good deeds; Allah Almighty says: Except fasting, it is Mine and I reward for it; he leaves food for My sake, and drink for My sake, and his desire for My sake, so it is Mine and I reward for it; and fasting is a shield; and for the fasting one are two joys: a joy when he breaks his fast and a joy when he meets his Lord; and the changed breath of the mouth of the fasting one, when it changes from food, is more pleasant to Allah than the scent of musk."
"10223","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Sulayman narrating from Dhakwan from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Do not break ties, nor hate one another, nor envy one another, nor turn your backs on one another, and be brothers as Allah commanded you."
"10224","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman, and Abu Ahmad said: Sufyan narrated to us from al-A'mash from Dhakwan from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: That the belly of one of you be filled with pus until it consumes him is better for him than to be filled with poetry."
"10225","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman from Dhakwan from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: When the strap of one of you breaks, let him not walk in one sandal; and when the dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times."
"10226","Shu'bah said: Sulayman said: And Abu Razin narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating it in this mosque, wearing two cloaks, so I said to Shu'bah: Like his hadith? So Shu'bah said: I did not hear him say the like of it about the dog lapping in the vessel."
"10227","And with its chain that he said, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The people of Yemen have come; they are the most tender in hearts and the softest in hearts; understanding is Yemeni, and faith is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni; and pride and arrogance are in the owners of camels, and calmness and dignity are in the owners of sheep."
"10228","And with its chain from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The best charity is what leaves sufficiency, that you give charity out of sufficiency; and begin with those you support; and the upper hand is better than the lower hand."
"10229","And with its chain from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah Almighty said: My servant is according to his opinion of Me, and I am with him when he supplicates Me; if he remembers Me in himself I remember him in Myself, and if he remembers Me in a gathering I remember him in a gathering better than them and more pleasant; and if he draws near to Me a handspan I draw near to him a cubit, and if he draws near a cubit I draw near an armspan, and if he comes to Me walking I come to him hastening."
"10230","Waki' narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man calls his wife to his bed and she refuses, and he spends the night angry with her, the angels curse her until morning."
"10231","Waki' narrated to us from al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three Allah will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor look at them, nor purify them, and for them is a painful punishment: a man who withheld surplus water he had from the traveler, and a man who swore upon merchandise after the afternoon prayer, meaning falsely, and a man who pledged allegiance to a ruler: if he gives him he fulfills for him, and if he does not give him he does not fulfill for him."
"10232","Waki' narrated to us from al-A'mash from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three Allah will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor look at them, nor purify them, and for them is a painful punishment: an old adulterer, and a lying king, and a poor arrogant one."
"10233","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Abi al-Zinad from al-A'raj from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of munabadhah and mulamasah."
"10234","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Juhadah al-Azdi from Abu Hazim al-Ashja'i from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the earnings of slave women."
"10235","Waki' narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most poetic word the Arabs said is the word of Labid: Indeed everything except Allah is false."
"10236","Waki' narrated to us from Ja'far ibn Burqan from Yazid ibn al-Asamm from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Trials appear, and killing increases, and knowledge is lifted. When Umar heard Abu Hurayrah say: Knowledge is lifted, Umar said: Indeed it is not stripped from the chests of the scholars, but the scholars pass away."
"10237","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ziyad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The best of you in Islam are the best of you in character when they understand."
"10238","Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan from Abi al-Zinad from al-A'raj from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man driving a sacrificial camel, he said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, woe to you."
"10239","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ziyad from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed in Friday there is an hour no man coincides with, supplicating good in it, except Allah answers him."
"10240","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Salih, freedman of al-Taw'amah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let no townsman sell for a Bedouin."
"10241","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Kathir al-Ghubari from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you sells a sheep or a milch camel, let him not leave milk gathered in its udder."
"10242","Waki' narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us from Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa' from Abu Zur'ah from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make the provision of the family of Muhammad sustenance."
"10243","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Hisham and Mis'ar narrated to us from Qatadah from Zurarah ibn Awfa from Abu Hurayrah; Hisham said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and Mis'ar reported it as a saying of Abu Hurayrah, he said: Indeed Allah Almighty overlooked for my community what their souls speak of, so long as they do not act upon it or speak."
"10244","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ziyad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever buys a sheep with milk gathered in its udder is given the choice; if he wishes he returns it, and with it a measure of dates."
"10245","Waki' narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ziyad from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you in Islam are the best of you in character when they understand."
"10246","Waki' narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no newborn born except upon the creed, and he once said: Every newborn is born upon the natural disposition; then his parents make him Jewish, and make him Christian, and make him associate partners. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what about one who died before that? He said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"10247","Waki' narrated to us from al-A'mash, he said: I think Abu Hazim mentioned it from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never found fault with food at all; if he desired it he ate it, otherwise he left it."
"10248","Waki' narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a foreleg were gifted to me I would accept it, and if I were invited to a shank I would accept."
"10249","Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan from Salih, freedman of al-Taw'amah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No people sit in a sitting in which they do not remember Allah, nor send blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except it will be a cause of regret upon them on the Day of Resurrection."
"10250","Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan, and Abd al-Rahman said: Sufyan narrated to us, the meaning, and Abu Nu'aym said: Sufyan narrated to us from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-A'raj from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Quraysh, and the Ansar, and Ashja', and Ghifar, and Aslam, and Muzaynah, and Juhaynah are the allies of Allah and His Messenger; they have no ally besides Him. Abu Nu'aym said: Allies; they have no ally besides Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10251","Waki' narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to me from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Look to those below you, and do not look to those above you, for it is more fitting that you not despise the blessing of Allah upon you."
"10252","Waki' narrated to us from Hammad from Thabit from Abi Rafi' from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man left his village to visit a brother of his in another village, so Allah appointed an angel for him, who sat on his path and said to him: Where do you intend? He said: I intend a brother of mine to visit him for Allah in this village. He said to him: Does he have any favor upon you that you tend? He said: No, but I loved him for Allah Almighty. He said: Then I am the messenger of your Lord to you, that He has loved you for your loving him therein."
"10253","Waki' narrated to us from Hammad from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"10254","And with its chain that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge from the trial of the Dajjal and from the trial of life and death."
"10255","And with its chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The beast is without liability, and the well is without liability, and the mine is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"10256","Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us from Hilal ibn Ali from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the most false speech; and do not spy, nor compete, nor turn your backs on one another, nor hate one another, and be servants of Allah, brothers."
"10257","And with this chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you cleans with stones let him use an odd number; and when the dog laps in the vessel of one of you let him wash it seven times; and let him not withhold surplus water to withhold thereby herbage; and part of the right of camels is that they be milked at the water on the day of their watering."
"10258","And with this chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah Almighty says: I am according to the opinion of My servant of Me, and I am with him when he remembers Me; if he remembers Me in himself I remember him in Myself, and if he remembers Me in a gathering I remember him in a gathering better than the gathering of those in which he remembers Me; and if the servant draws near to Me a handspan I draw near to him a cubit, and if he draws near to Me a cubit I draw near to him an armspan, and when he comes to Me walking I come to him hastening; for Him are favor and bounty."
"10259","And with this chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will continue to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah; and when they say: There is no god but Allah, they have protected from me their properties and themselves except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah Almighty."
"10260","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us from Hilal ibn Ali from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave me with what I leave you; those before you were destroyed only by their many questions and their differing with their prophets; but what I forbid you, refrain from it, and what I command you, do of it what you can."
"10261","And with this chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you will be saved by his deed. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, except that Allah envelops me with favor and mercy from Him; but draw near, and be upright, and receive glad tidings."
"10262","And with this chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, I do not give you nor withhold from you; I am only a distributor, I place it where I am commanded."
"10263","And with this chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the closest of people to Isa ibn Maryam in this world and the Hereafter; the prophets are brothers from co-wives, their mothers are different and their religion is one."
"10264","And with this chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed in Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels a hundred years; recite if you wish: And extended shade."
"10265","And with this chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The space of a bow, or a whip, in Paradise is better than what the sun rises and sets upon."
"10266","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us from al-Harith ibn Fudayl al-Ansari from Ziyad ibn Sa'd from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Isa ibn Maryam will descend as a just leader and an equitable judge; he will break the cross, and kill the pig, and restore peace, and take swords as sickles; and the venom of every venomous creature will go away; and the sky will send down its provision, and the earth will bring forth its blessing, until the boy plays with the snake and it does not harm him, and the wolf shepherds the sheep and does not harm them, and the lion shepherds the cattle and does not harm them."
"10267","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Husayn al-Aslami from Abd Allah ibn Subayhah from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is the loaned milch animal; it goes out with reward and returns with reward; the loan of a camel is like freeing a red slave, and the loan of a sheep is like freeing a black slave."
"10268","Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me: Surayj narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us from Salamah ibn Safwan ibn Salamah al-Zuraqi from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Satan, when he hears the call, turns away with loud farting; then when the caller falls silent he comes forward until he intervenes between a man and his heart to make him forget his prayer; so when one of you doubts in his prayer, let him give greeting, then prostrate two prostrations while sitting."
"10269","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us from Suhayl, meaning Ibn Abi Salih, from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you stands from his sitting place then returns, he is more entitled to it."
"10270","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us from Amr ibn al-Ala' al-Thaqafi from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Madinah and Makkah are surrounded by angels; upon every pass thereof is an angel; neither the Dajjal nor the plague enters them."
"10271","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us from Ayyub ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'sa'ah al-Ansari from Ya'qub ibn Abi Ya'qub from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man does not stand for a man from his sitting place, but make room, Allah will make room for you; and when the servant of one of you prepares food and bears its heat and hardship, let him invite him to eat with him; and if he does not invite him, let him hand him some of it; and whoever sells a sheep with milk gathered in its udder, the buyer has the choice for three days: if he wishes he returns it and returns with it a measure of dates."
"10272","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us from Suhayl, meaning Ibn Abi Salih, from Abi Ubayd from Ata' ibn Yazid from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever glorifies Allah thirty-three times, and magnifies Allah thirty-three times, and praises Allah thirty-three times, and says: There is no god but Allah alone, He has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Capable, after the prayer, his sin is forgiven even if it were more than the foam of the sea."
"10273","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah, meaning Ibn Umar, narrated to us from Sa'id al-Maqburi from Abu Hurayrah that Thumamah ibn Uthal al-Hanafi embraced Islam, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that he be taken to the garden of Abu Talhah to wash; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your companion's Islam has become good."
"10274","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us from Sa'id from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will surely know one of you when a hadith from me reaches him while he reclines on his couch, and he says: Recite a Qur'an to me about it; whatever good reaches you from me, whether I said it or did not say it, I say it; and whatever evil reaches you, I do not say evil."
"10275","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Khazraj ibn Uthman al-Sa'di narrated to us, he said: Abu Ayyub, freedman of Uthman ibn Affan, narrated to us from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The space of a whip of one of you in Paradise is better than the world and the like of it with it; and the space of a bow of one of you in Paradise is better than the world and the like of it with it; and a headcover of a woman of Paradise is better than the world and the like of it with it. He said: I said: O Abu Hurayrah, what is the headcover? He said: The veil."
"10276","Yunus narrated to us, he said: al-Khazraj narrated to us from Abu Ayyub from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I entered the mosque with him on Friday, and he saw a boy and said to him: O boy, go play. He said: I only came to the mosque. He said: O boy, go play. He said: I only came to the mosque. He said: Then will you sit until the leader comes out? He said: Yes. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed the angels come on Friday and sit at the doors of the mosque, recording the first, and the second, and the third, and the people according to their stations, until the leader comes out; and when the leader comes out, the records are folded."
"10277","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Khazraj, meaning Ibn Uthman al-Sa'di, narrated to me from Abu Ayyub, meaning the freedman of Uthman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed the deeds of the sons of Adam are presented every Thursday, the night of Friday, and the deed of one who breaks kinship is not accepted."
"10278","Yunus narrated to us: al-Khazraj narrated to us from Abu Ayyub from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Abu al-Qasim, my beloved, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me with three I will not leave: washing on Friday, fasting three days of every month, and witr before sleep."
"10279","Waki' and Abd al-Rahman said: Sufyan narrated to us from Mansur from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs pilgrimage to the House and does not utter obscenity nor commit wickedness returns as his mother bore him. Abd al-Rahman said: He leaves his sins as on the day his mother bore him, or as he came out of his mother's belly."
"10280","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Salih, freedman of al-Taw'amah, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better, or superior, to a thousand prayers in other mosques except the Sacred Mosque."
"10281","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan, and Abu Nu'aym said: Sufyan narrated to us from Salih, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a townsman to buy for a Bedouin. And Abu Nu'aym said: Let no townsman sell for a Bedouin."
"10282","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Salih from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No people sit in a sitting in which they do not remember their Lord therein, nor send blessings upon their Prophet therein, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except it will be a cause of regret upon them on the Day of Resurrection: if He wills He seizes them for it, and if He wills He pardons them."
"10283","Mu'ammal narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Salih ibn Nabhan, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No people gather, then he mentioned it."
"10284","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim from Umar ibn Abi Salamah from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muhaqalah and muzabanah; and muhaqalah is wheat for wheat."
"10285","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us from al-Ala' from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If the believer knew what punishment is with Allah Almighty, no one would hope for Paradise; and if the disbeliever knew what mercy is with Allah, no one would despair of Paradise; Allah created a hundred mercies, and placed one among His creation by which they show mercy to one another, and with Allah are ninety-nine mercies."
"10286","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us from al-Ala' from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Let none of you say: My male slave and my female slave; all of you are slaves of Allah, and all your women are slave women of Allah; but let him say: My boy, and my girl, and my youth, and my young woman."
"10287","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Zuhayr from al-Ala' from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no disease except in the black seed is healing from it, except death."
"10288","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Zuhayr from al-Ala' from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Faith is Yemeni, and disbelief is toward the East; and calmness is in the people of sheep; and pride and showing off are in the loud-voiced owners of horses and the owners of camels."
"10289","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Zuhayr from al-Ala' from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I have kin I join and they break me, and I do good to them and they do evil to me, and they act ignorantly toward me and I forbear them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If it is as you say, it is as if you feed them hot ashes, and there will remain with you a supporter from Allah Almighty so long as you remain upon that."
"10290","And with its chain from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed the five prayers, and Friday to Friday, are expiations for what is between them, so long as major sins are not committed."
"10291","And with its chain, he said: Indeed a man acts for a long time with the deeds of the people of Paradise, then Allah seals for him with the deeds of the people of Hell, so He makes him of the people of Hell; and indeed a man acts for a long time with the deeds of the people of Hell, then Allah seals his deed for him with the deeds of the people of Paradise, so He makes him of the people of Paradise, and admits him to Paradise."
"10292","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Zuhayr, and Abu Amir: Zuhayr narrated to us from al-Ala' from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever sends blessings upon me once, Allah sends blessings upon him ten times."
"10293","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Zuhayr, and Abu Amir said: Zuhayr narrated to us from al-Ala' from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The world is the prison of the believer and the paradise of the disbeliever."
"10294","And with its chain from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: While a man walked on a road he found a branch of thorns, so he said: I will surely lift this, perhaps Allah Almighty will forgive me for it; so he lifted it, and Allah forgave him for it and admitted him to Paradise."
"10295","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad al-Khurasani, and Abu Amir said: Zuhayr narrated to us from al-Ala' from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Make the rows straight in prayer; the best rows of men in prayer are the first of them and the worst of them are the last of them; and the best rows of women in prayer are the last of them and the worst of them are the first of them."
"10296","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us from Musa ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The changed breath of the mouth of the fasting one is more pleasant to Allah than the scent of musk."
"10297","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Simak, he said: Abd Allah ibn Zalim narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard my beloved Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed the corruption of my community is at the hands of foolish youngsters from Quraysh."
"10298","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Abi Tamim narrated to me from Sa'id ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dinar for dinar and dirham for dirham, no excess between them. Abd al-Rahman said: And I read it to Malik, meaning this hadith."
"10299","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Hammad from Thabit from Abi Rafi' from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Zakariya, upon him prayer and peace, was a carpenter. Abd al-Rahman said: Sometimes he raised it, and sometimes he did not raise it."
"10300","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us from Ammar, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you in the pre-Islamic age are the best of you in Islam when they understand."
"10301","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are mines in good and evil; the best of you in the Jahiliyyah are the best of you in Islam when they gain understanding."
"10302","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Abi Ammar informed us, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: People are mines in good and evil; the best of them in the Jahiliyyah are the best of them in Islam when they gain understanding."
"10303","Muammal narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Abi Ammar narrated to us that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the slave obeys his Lord and his master, he has two rewards."
"10304","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Aflah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hazm, from Salman al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is like a thousand prayers in other mosques except al-Masjid al-Haram, and congregational prayer equals twenty-five times the prayer of the individual."
"10305","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you say to your companion while the Imam is delivering the sermon, Be silent, you have engaged in idle talk."
"10306","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of that."
"10307","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned Friday, he said: In it is an hour no Muslim slave coincides with while standing praying asking Allah for something but He gives it to him. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured with his hand. Ishaq said: indicating its brevity."
"10308","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said: I went out to al-Tur and met Kab al-Ahbar, and I sat with him, and he narrated to me from the Torah, and I narrated to him from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And among what I narrated to him was that I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday; in it Adam was created, and in it he was sent down, and in it his repentance was accepted, and in it he died, and in it the Hour will be established. And there is no creature but that it is apprehensive on Friday from the morning until the sun rises out of fear of the Hour, except jinn and men. And in it is an hour no Muslim slave meets while praying asking Allah for something but He gives it to him. Kab said: That is once in every year. So I said: Rather it is in every Friday. So Kab read the Torah and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke the truth. Abu Hurayrah said: Then I met Abd Allah ibn Salam and I narrated to him my sitting with Kab and what I had narrated to him about Friday. And I said to him: Kab said that is one day in every year. Abd Allah ibn Salam said: Kab lied. Then Kab read the Torah and said: Rather it is in every Friday. Abd Allah ibn Salam said: Kab spoke the truth."
"10309","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Ibn Shihab, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever stands Ramadan in faith and seeking reward, what preceded of his sin is forgiven for him."
"10310","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Congregational prayer is better than the prayer of one of you alone by twenty-five parts."
"10311","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you leads the people in prayer, let him lighten, for among them are the weak, the sick, and the elderly; and when one of you prays for himself, let him lengthen as he wishes."
"10312","Abd Allah narrated to us, he narrated to me, he said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels invoke blessings upon one of you as long as he remains in his place of prayer, saying: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him."
"10313","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of you remains in prayer as long as the prayer detains him; nothing prevents him from returning to his family except the prayer."
"10314","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Angels succeed one another among you by night, and in the hadith of Abd al-Rahman: and angels by day, and they gather at the Asr prayer and the Fajr prayer. Then those who spent the night among you ascend, and He asks them, and He knows best about them: How did you leave My servants? So they say: We left them while they were praying, and we came to them while they were praying."
"10315","Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, he said: And I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say: O Allah, forgive me if You will; O Allah, have mercy on me if You will. Let him be resolute in asking. Both said together: There is none to compel Him."
"10316","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, he said: And Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every Prophet has a supplication with which he supplicates, and I intend to withhold my supplication as intercession for my Ummah in the Hereafter. Ishaq said: I intended to withhold my supplication as intercession."
"10317","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Ubayd, freedman of Banu Azhar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of you is answered as long as he does not hasten, saying: I supplicated and I was not answered."
"10318","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Abd Allah al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Our Lord, mighty and majestic is He, descends every night to the lowest heaven when the last third of the night remains, and says: Who calls upon Me that I may answer him; who asks Me that I may give him; who seeks My forgiveness that I may forgive him."
"10319","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, freedman of al-Aswad ibn Sufyan, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Abu Hurayrah recited to them: When the heaven is split asunder, and prostrated in it. And when he finished, he informed them that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated in it."
"10320","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man driving a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, woe to you, on the second or the third. Ishaq said: Ride it, woe to you. He said: Ride it, woe to you."
"10321","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let no townsman sell for a Bedouin, and do not engage in false bidding, and let no man outbid his brother, and let none propose marriage over the proposal of his brother, and let not a woman ask for the divorce of her sister to overturn what is in her vessel, but let her marry, for hers is only what Allah has decreed for her."
"10322","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared sacred what is between its two lava tracts, meaning Madinah. He said: If I found the gazelles resting I would not frighten them."
"10323","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ukaymah al-Jundaui, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed a prayer and recited aloud in it. And when he finished, he said: Did any of you recite with me just now? A man among the people said: I did. He said: I say, why is the Quran being contended with me."
"10324","Ismail narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yaqub informed me that Abu al-Saib informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays a prayer in which he does not recite the Mother of the Quran, it is deficient, it is deficient, it is deficient, incomplete. So I said: O Abu Hurayrah, I am sometimes behind the Imam. He said: So he squeezed my arm and said: O Persian, recite it to yourself."
"10325","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Ayyub informed us, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking from the mouth of the waterskin. Ayyub said: I was informed that a man drank from the mouth of a waterskin and a snake came out."
"10326","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Said al-Jurayri informed us, from Mudarib ibn Hazn, he said: I said, meaning to Abu Hurayrah: Did you hear from your close friend anything you can narrate to me? He said: Yes, I heard him say (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): No contagion, no hamah, and the best of omens is the good omen, and the evil eye is real."
"10327","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever finds his goods intact has more right to them than the creditors."
"10328","Ismail and Ibn Jafar narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata; Ibn Jafar said in his hadith: Ata narrated to me that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: In every prayer there is recitation; so what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made audible to us, we made audible to you, and what he concealed from us, we concealed from you."
"10329","Ismail and Yazid narrated to us, they said: Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not meet the caravans; and whoever meets any of them, its owner has the choice when he reaches the market."
"10330","Ismail narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Khalid ibn Ghallaq al-Ayshi, he said: I stayed with Abu Hurayrah, he said: And a son of mine died, and I grieved over him. So I said: Did you hear from your close friend anything with which we may comfort ourselves about our dead? He said: Yes, I heard him say: Their little ones are the small dwellers of Paradise."
"10331","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Umayr ibn Ishaq, he said: I saw Abu Hurayrah meet al-Hasan ibn Ali, and he said: Uncover for me your belly where I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kiss. He said: So he uncovered his belly for him, and he kissed it."
"10332","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Yemen have come; they are the most tender-hearted; faith is Yemeni, understanding is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni."
"10333","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Yemen have come, and he mentioned the like of it."
"10334","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yaqub, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two who revile each other, whatever they say is upon the initiator, unless the wronged one transgresses."
"10335","Ismail narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Musab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: He said, meaning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): None of you will be saved by his deed. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, unless my Lord envelops me with mercy and bounty from Him."
"10336","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu al-Salil, from Abu Hassan, he said: Two sons of mine died, so I said to Abu Hurayrah: Did you hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a hadith you can narrate to us to comfort us about our dead? He said: Yes. Their little ones are the small dwellers of Paradise; one of them meets his father, or he said: his parents, and takes hold of the edge of his garment or his hand, just as I take hold of the edge of this garment of yours, and he does not part from him until Allah admits him and his father into Paradise."
"10337","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Ayyub informed us, from Nafi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasten with your funerals; for if it was good, you hasten it to it, and if it was evil, you cast it off your necks, or he said: off your backs."
"10338","Ismail narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Ziyad ibn Riyah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Whoever leaves obedience and parts the community and dies, his death is one of Jahiliyyah. And whoever rebels against my Ummah striking its righteous and its wicked, not sparing its believer nor fulfilling the covenant of its covenant-holder, he is not of my Ummah. And whoever is killed under a blind banner calling to tribal partisanship, or angering for partisanship, or fighting for partisanship, his killing is one of Jahiliyyah."
"10339","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, he said: I heard Ziyad ibn Rabah, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: Whoever parts the community and opposes obedience, and he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: nor fulfills the covenant of its covenant-holder."
"10340","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The truffle is from manna, and its water is a cure for the eye; and the ajwah date is from Paradise, and it is a cure from poison."
"10341","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Affan narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Dhakwan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O Allah, I am only a man; so whichever Muslim I flogged, Ibn Jafar said: or insulted or cursed, make it for him purification and reward and nearness by which You bring him near to You on the Day of Resurrection."
"10342","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Dhakwan, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills himself with an iron weapon, his iron weapon will be in his hand stabbing his belly with it in the Fire of Hell, abiding therein forever; and whoever throws himself from a mountain and kills himself, he will be in the Fire of Hell throwing himself therein, abiding therein forever."
"10343","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri informed us, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five are from the fitrah: circumcision, shaving the pubic area, plucking the armpit, trimming the nails, and shortening the mustache."
"10344","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Rawh narrated to us, they said: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Khilas, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays a rakah of the Fajr prayer before the sun rises, then it rises, let him pray another rakah to it."
"10345","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, and Abd al-Wahhab, from Said, with the meaning, from Qatadah, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, walk to it with tranquility and dignity upon you; so what you catch, pray, and what you miss, complete."
"10346","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: And he was asked about a vessel in which a dog licks. He said: Said narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: It is washed seven times, the first of them with dust."
"10347","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: My close friend Abu al-Qasim enjoined upon me three I will not leave in travel nor in residence: fasting three days of every month, sleeping upon witr, and the two rakahs of Duha. He said: Then al-Hasan became confused and assigned the two rakahs of Duha to the washing on Friday."
"10348","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Rawh narrated to us, they said: Shubah or Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: In Friday there is an hour no Muslim slave meets while praying asking Allah therein for good but He gives it to him."
"10349","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves a treasure, it will be likened for him on the Day of Resurrection as a bald serpent following him, having two spots. He keeps seeking him, saying: Woe to you, what are you? He says: I am your treasure which you left after you. He said: So he puts his hand into its mouth and it bites it, then it follows him with the rest of his body."
"10350","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The umra grant is permissible for its people, or an inheritance for its people."
"10351","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Hisham al-Qurdusi narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Let none of you propose marriage over the proposal of his brother, nor outbid his brother, nor shall a woman be married over her paternal aunt nor over her maternal aunt, nor shall she ask for the divorce of her sister to overturn her dish, but let her marry, for hers is only what Allah has decreed for her."
"10352","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Khilas, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, that two men disputed over an animal, neither of them having proof, so the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to cast lots for the oath whether they liked or disliked."
"10353","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, that Abu Rafi narrated from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats or drinks in his fast forgetfully, let him complete his fast, for Allah, mighty and majestic is He, fed him and gave him drink."
"10354","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you is invited, let him respond; and if he is fasting, let him invoke blessings, meaning supplication."
"10355","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Umar al-Ghudani, he said: I was sitting with Abu Hurayrah, he said: Then a man from Banu Amir ibn Sasaah passed, and it was said to him: This is the Amirite with the most wealth. So Abu Hurayrah said: Bring him back to me. So they brought him back to him. So he said: I have been informed that you are a man of much wealth. So the Amirite said: Yes, by Allah, I have a hundred red camels and a hundred dark camels, until he counted kinds of camels, varieties of slaves, and tethered horses. So Abu Hurayrah said: Beware of the hooves of camels and the cloven hooves of sheep, repeating that to him until the color of the Amirite began to change. So he said: What is that, O Abu Hurayrah? So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever has camels and does not give their due in their hardship and their ease. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what are their ease and hardship? He said: In their hardship and their ease. For they will come on the Day of Resurrection in their fullest, largest, fattest, and most vigorous state, then a level plain will be spread for them, and they will trample him therein with their hooves. When the last of them passes him, the first of them is brought back upon him, on a day whose measure is fifty thousand years, until judgment is passed among the people, and he sees his path. And if he has cattle and does not give their due in their hardship and their ease, they will come on the Day of Resurrection in their fullest, largest, fattest, and most vigorous state, then a level plain will be spread for them, and every cloven-hoofed one will trample him with its hoof, and every horned one will gore him with its horn. When the last of them passes him, the first is brought back upon him, on a day whose measure is fifty thousand years, until judgment is passed among the people, until he sees his path. And if he has sheep and does not give their due in their hardship and their ease, they will come on the Day of Resurrection in their fullest, largest, fattest, and most vigorous state, then a level plain will be spread for them, and every cloven-hoofed one will trample him with its hoof, and every horned one will gore him with its horn, meaning there is among them no hornless nor broken-horned one. When the last of them passes him, the first is brought back upon him, on a day whose measure is fifty thousand years, until judgment is passed among the people, and he sees his path. So the Amirite said: And what is the due of camels, O Abu Hurayrah? He said: That you give the noble one, lend the rich-milked one, lend the back for riding, give milk to drink, and lend the stallion for breeding."
"10356","He said: And Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu Umar al-Ghudani, from Abu Hurayrah, and he mentioned its meaning."
"10357","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Khilas, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of a hadith he mentioned from al-Hasan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Abu Umar."
"10358","Sulayman ibn Dawud, and he is Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi, narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Locusts of gold were sent upon Ayyub, and he began to gather them. So He said: Did I not enrich you, O Ayyub? So he said: O Lord, who is ever sated of Your mercy, or he said: of Your bounty."
"10359","Abd Allah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The ajwah date is from Paradise, and it is a cure from poison; and the truffle is from manna, and its water is a cure for the eye."
"10360","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab informed us, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a mouse that fell into ghee and died. So he said: If it was solid, take it and what is around it, and eat what remains; and if it was liquid, do not eat it."
"10361","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No fara and no atirah. Ibn Shihab said: The fara was what the people of the Jahiliyyah used to slaughter of the first offspring they had, and the atirah is the sacrifice of Rajab."
"10362","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir informed us, from Damdam, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered killing the two black ones in prayer. I said to Yahya: What is meant by the two black ones? He said: The snake and the scorpion."
"10363","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed us, from Abd al-Malik, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is offered something without asking for it, let him accept it, for it is provision which Allah has driven to him."
"10364","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah was asked about a man who prayed a rakah of the Fajr prayer, then the sun rose; Affan said: then the horn of the sun rose. So he said: Khilas narrated to me, from Abu Rafi, that Abu Hurayrah narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He completes his prayer."
"10365","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Aws ibn Khalid, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels on Friday come to the doors of the mosque writing the people according to their ranks: So-and-so came at such an hour. Hammad said: I think he said: five times. So-and-so came while the Imam was delivering the sermon, and so-and-so came and caught the prayer but did not catch Friday, or did not catch the sermon."
"10366","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Aws ibn Khalid, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Beast will emerge with the staff of Musa and the seal of Sulayman. So it will brighten the face of the believer with the staff, and seal the nose of the disbeliever with the seal, until the people at the table gather, saying: This, O believer; and this, O disbeliever."
"10367","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman, freedman of Umm Burthun, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic is He, prescribed Friday upon those before us, and they differed about it, and Allah guided us to it. So the people follow us: the Jews tomorrow, and the Christians the day after tomorrow."
"10368","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic is He, has pardoned for my Ummah everything their selves speak of, unless they utter it or act upon it."
"10369","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Wasi narrated to us, from Shutayr ibn Nahar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good opinion is part of good worship."
"10370","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, and Yazid said: Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: If you find nothing but sheepfolds and camel resting places, pray in the sheepfolds and do not pray in the camel resting places."
"10371","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Let no townsman sell for a Bedouin."
"10372","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not revile time, for Allah is time."
"10373","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Let none of you say: my male slave and my female slave; let him say: my boy, my girl."
"10374","Muhammad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, or Abu al-Qasim said: When one of you eats or drinks forgetfully while fasting, let him complete his fast, for Allah fed him and gave him drink."
"10375","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two garments and two sales: that a man sit on his haunches in a single garment with nothing of it over his private part, and that he wrap in a garment raising its ends over his shoulder. And as for the two sales, they are touching and casting."
"10376","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, mighty and majestic is He, is Witr and loves the witr."
"10377","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Name yourselves with my name and do not take my kunyah."
"10378","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, and Yazid said: Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the delegation of Abd al-Qays, when they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he forbade them green jars, hollowed stumps, varnished vessels, and the cut waterskin. And it was said: Make nabidh in your waterskin and tie it and drink it sweet and good. So a man said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me in the like of this. He said: Then you will make it like this. Yazid said: And Hisham opened his hand a little and said: Then you will make it like this, and he opened his hand somewhat higher than that."
"10379","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the falsest speech. And do not spy, nor eavesdrop, nor envy one another, nor compete, nor hate one another, nor turn away from one another. And be servants of Allah, brothers."
"10380","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to me, he said: I know this only from what my father narrated to us, and I read it to him, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say, and I know it only from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Before the Hour there will be harj. It was said: And what is harj? He said: Killing."
"10381","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when food was brought to him, would ask about it; if it was charity, he would not eat, and if it was a gift, he would eat."
"10382","Bahz narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He does not thank Allah who does not thank the people."
"10383","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated to us, Affan said in his hadith, he said: Ishaq ibn Abd Allah informed us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, mighty and majestic is He, says, Affan said: on the Day of Resurrection: O son of Adam, I carried you on horses and camels, married you to women, and made you rule and lead, so where is thanks for that."
"10384","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, narrating from his Lord: My servant committed a sin and said: O Lord, forgive my sin. So blessed and exalted is He said: My servant committed a sin and knew that he has a Lord who forgives sin and seizes for sin, three times. He said: So He says: Do what you will, I have forgiven you."
"10385","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to us, he said: There was in Madinah a storyteller called Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, he said: So I heard him say: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A servant incurred a sin, and he mentioned its meaning."
"10386","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Khilas, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of one who takes back his gift is like the dog: it ate until it was sated, then vomited, then returned to its vomit and ate it."
"10387","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of the hadith of Khilas about the gift."
"10388","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Khilas, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While a young man was walking in a cloak strutting in it, letting his izar trail, the earth swallowed him, and he is rumbling in it until the Day of Resurrection."
"10389","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Rawh narrated to us, they said: Awf narrated to us, from Khilas, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The anger of Allah, mighty and majestic is He, is severe upon a man killed by His Prophet, and Rawh said: killed by the Messenger of Allah, and the anger of Allah is severe upon a man named king of kings; there is no king but Allah, mighty and majestic is He."
"10390","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Rawh narrated to us, they said: Awf narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, Rawh said: and Khilas, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade urinating in stagnant water and then performing ablution from it."
"10391","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, he said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed that the child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer the stone."
"10392","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Khilas, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of that."
"10393","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, he said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tasbih is for men and clapping is for women in prayer."
"10394","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of that."
"10395","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Khilas, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of that."
"10396","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, and Ishaq, meaning Ibn Yusuf al-Azraq, he said: Awf informed us, with the meaning, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever follows the funeral of a Muslim seeking reward, and stays with it until it is prayed over and its burial is finished, he returns with two qirats of reward, each qirat like Uhud. And whoever prays over it and returns before it is buried, he returns with one qirat. Ishaq said: with faith and seeking reward, and he said: If he returns before it is placed in the grave, he returns with one qirat."
"10397","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, he said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is fasting and forgets and eats and drinks, let him complete his fast, for Allah, mighty and majestic is He, fed him and gave him drink."
"10398","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of that."
"10399","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, he said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The mine is exempt, the animal is exempt, the well is exempt, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"10400","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of that."
"10401","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, saying: Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, who said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until you fight a people who wear hair footwear, and until you fight a people with broad faces, flat noses, small eyes, as though their faces are hammered shields."
"10402","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, saying: Awf narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of that."
"10403","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Umayr ibn Ishaq, who said: I was with al-Hasan ibn Ali, and Abu Hurayrah met us and said: Show me where I may kiss you where I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kiss. He said: So he lifted his shirt. He said: So he kissed his navel."
"10404","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, saying: Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Maymunah, from Abu Hurayrah, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, when I see you my soul is content and my eye is delighted, so inform me about everything. He said: Everything was created from water. He said: So inform me of a deed that if I do it I will enter Paradise. He said: Spread peace, speak good words, uphold kinship ties, and stand at night while people are asleep; you will enter Paradise in peace."
"10405","Ishaq, and he is al-Azraq, narrated to us, saying: Sharik informed us, from Harun ibn Sad, who said: I heard Abu Hazim al-Ashjai saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was approached while we were with him, and it was said to him: So-and-so has died and left two dinars, or two dirhams. So he said: Two branding irons."
"10406","Hajjaj narrated to us, saying: Layth narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Abi Said narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim woman to travel a journey of a night except with a man who is a mahram to her."
"10407","Hajjaj narrated to us, saying: Layth narrated to us, saying: Said al-Maqburi narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Muslim women, let not a neighbor woman belittle for her neighbor, even a sheep trotter."
"10408","Hajjaj narrated to us, saying: Layth narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Abi Said narrated to me, from Salim, freedman of the Nasriyyin, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Allah, Muhammad is only a human who becomes angry as humans become angry, and I have taken with You a covenant that You will never break with me; so whichever believer I have hurt, or insulted, or flogged, make it for him an expiation and a nearness by which You bring him near to You on the Day of Resurrection."
"10409","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Said narrated to us, and Hashim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Said narrated to me, from Ata ibn Mina, freedman of Ibn Abi Dhubab, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of Maryam will surely descend as a just judge, and he will surely break the cross, and surely kill the pig, and surely abolish the jizyah, and surely leave the young camels so no effort is made upon them, and hatred and enmity and envy will surely depart, and they will surely be called to wealth and no one will accept it."
"10410","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Said narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that he heard him saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When the slavegirl of one of you commits adultery and her adultery becomes clear, let him flog her the hadd and not rebuke her; then if she commits adultery, let him flog her the hadd and not rebuke her; then if she commits adultery and her adultery becomes clear, let him sell her even for a rope of hair."
"10411","Hajjaj narrated to us, and Hashim narrated to us, both saying: Layth narrated to us, saying: Said narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: There is no god but Allah alone; He strengthened His troops, aided His servant, and defeated the Confederates alone, so there is nothing after Him. Hashim said: He made mighty."
"10412","Hajjaj narrated to us, saying: Layth narrated to us, saying: Said narrated to me, from Ata ibn Mina, freedman of Ibn Abi Dhubab, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has pledged for one who goes out in His cause, whom nothing brings out except faith in Me and jihad in My cause, that I am guarantor for him until I admit him to Paradise through his faith, whatever it was, either by killing or by death, or I return him to the dwelling from which he set out, having attained whatever he attained of reward or spoils."
"10413","Jarir narrated to us, from Umarah ibn al-Qaqa, from Abu Zurah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he said takbir in prayer, would pause briefly. So I said to him: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, what do you say in your silence between the takbir and the recitation? He said: I say: O Allah, distance me from my sins as You distanced between the east and the west; O Allah, purify me of my sins as the white garment is purified of filth; O Allah, wash me of my sins with snow and water and hail."
"10414","Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs hajj to the House and does not utter obscenity nor commit wickedness returns as his mother bore him."
"10415","Hushaym narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Rashid, from Said ibn Abi Khayrah, who said: Al-Hasan narrated to us for about forty or fifty years, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A time will come upon people in which they consume riba. He said: It was said to him: All the people? He said: Whoever of them does not consume it, its dust will reach him."
"10416","Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Awf informed us, from a man who narrated to him, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The protected area of a well is forty cubits around it, all of it for the resting places of camels and sheep, and the wayfarer is the first to drink, and surplus water is not to be withheld so that herbage is thereby withheld."
"10417","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, saying: Ayyub narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The worst food is the food of the wedding feast; the rich are fed it and the poor are denied it, and whoever does not answer has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"10418","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from a man, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No people gather then disperse without remembering Allah, as though they dispersed from the carcass of a donkey."
"10419","Hajjaj narrated to us, saying: Shayban narrated to us, saying: Mansur narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Disputation about the Quran is disbelief."
"10420","Hajjaj narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj said: Musa ibn Uqbah informed me, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever sits in a gathering in which his idle talk is much, then says before he stands: Glory be to You, our Lord, and with Your praise; there is no god but You; I seek Your forgiveness then I repent to You, except Allah forgives for him what was in that gathering of his."
"10421","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dumb animal is without liability, and the well is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"10422","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, saying: Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed, when people differ about their roads, that it is seven cubits."
"10423","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, saying: Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about prayer in a single garment, so he said: Do all of you find two garments?"
"10424","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever repents before the sun rises from its west, Allah turns to him."
"10425","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Umarah ibn Zadham narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is asked about knowledge he knows and conceals it will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire."
"10426","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, saying: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Yahya, freedman of Jadah ibn Hubayrah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disparage food at all; if he desired it he ate it, and if he did not desire it he remained silent."
"10427","Hajjaj narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj said: Ziyad ibn Sad informed me that Salih, freedman of al-Tawamah, informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If people sit in a gathering then stand without remembering Allah in it, it will be a regret upon them in it on the Day of Resurrection."
"10428","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted says: I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, nor ear has heard, nor has occurred to a human heart, as a store, besides what I have shown you. Then he recited: No soul knows what is hidden for them of delight of eyes."
"10429","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not fast Friday except with a day before it or a day after it."
"10430","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-Amash, and Yala said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be moderate and aim aright, for none of you will be saved by his deeds. We said: O Messenger of Allah, nor you? He said: Nor I, except that Allah envelops me with mercy and bounty from Him."
"10431","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: al-Amash informed us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"10432","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: al-Amash informed us, and Yala said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You find the worst of people, and Yala said: You find among the worst of people with Allah on the Day of Resurrection the two-faced. Ibn Numayr said: The one who comes to these with the talk of these and to these with the talk of these."
"10433","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: al-Amash informed us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is the fasting day of one of you, let him not utter obscenity nor act ignorantly; and if one acts ignorantly toward him, let him say: I am a fasting person."
"10434","And with his chain: Leave me with what I have left you, for those before you perished only through their questions and their differing with their prophets; so when I command you with a thing, take from it what you can, and when I forbid you from a thing, desist."
"10435","And with his chain: The dream of a Muslim, or seen for him, is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood. And with this chain he said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, you will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another; if you wish I will guide you to a matter that if you do it you will love one another. They said: Yes. He said: Spread peace among you."
"10436","And with this chain the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was a tree branch on the road harming people, so a man removed it and was admitted to Paradise."
"10437","And with this chain he forbade continuous fasting. They said: You fast continuously. He said: I am not like you; I remain with my Lord, He feeds me and gives me drink. Take upon yourselves of deeds what you can bear."
"10438","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Amash informed us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two things among people are disbelief in them: reviling lineage and wailing over the dead."
"10439","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Amash informed us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am only a human, so whichever Muslim I have insulted, or cursed, or flogged, make it for him purification and mercy."
"10440","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, and Yala said: al-Amash informed us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say: my slave; for all of you are slaves, but let him say: my youth. And let him not say: my lord, for your Lord is Allah, but let him say: my master."
"10441","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That one of you take a rope and go to the mountain and gather firewood from it, then sell it, then eat and give charity, is better for him than asking people for anything."
"10442","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Dhakwan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile time, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: I am time; the days and nights are Mine; I renew them and wear them out, and I bring kings after kings."
"10443","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar. And shighar is that a man says to a man: Marry me your daughter and I will marry you my daughter, or marry me your sister and I will marry you my sister. He said: And he forbade sale of gharar and sale of pebbles."
"10444","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed faith retreats to Madinah as the snake retreats to its hole."
"10445","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, and Muhammad ibn Ubayd said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two prayers and two garments and two sales: he forbade prayer after Fajr until the sun rises, and prayer after Asr until the sun sets, and wrapping in a single garment, and sitting on buttocks wrapped in a single garment with ones private part exposed to the sky. Ibn Numayr said in his hadith: And from munabadhah and mulamasah."
"10446","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Salih, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would burden my ummah, or people, I would have loved not to stay behind from an expedition going out in the cause of Allah, but I do not find what to carry them on, and they do not find what to bear themselves on, so they go out. And I wished to fight in the cause of Allah and be killed, then be brought to life, then be killed, then be brought to life, then be killed."
"10447","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from his father, who said: Abu Hurayrah used to pray in Madinah similar to the prayer of Qays ibn Abi Hazim. So I said to him: O Abu Hurayrah, was this how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray? He said: What have you objected to in my prayer? I said: Nothing, by Allah, except good; I only wanted to ask you. He said: Yes, and briefer."
"10448","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Abu Kathir narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Wine is from these two trees: the date-palm and the grapevine."
"10449","Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Abdillah al-Bakri informed us, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Travel is a portion of torment, for a man is distracted in it from his fasting and his prayer and his worship; so when one of you fulfills his need from his journey, let him hasten back to his family."
"10450","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he mentioned a hadith, then he said: Would one of you love, when he returns to his family, to find therein three large fat pregnant camels? Three verses that one of you recites in his prayer are better for him than three large fat pregnant camels."
"10451","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, al-Nahhas ibn Qahm narrated to me, from Shaddad Abu Ammar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guards the forenoon supererogatory prayer, his sins are forgiven even if they are like the foam of the sea."
"10452","Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhimari narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed women were created from a rib; they do not remain straight on one disposition; if you straighten her you break her, and if you leave her you enjoy her, and in her is crookedness."
"10453","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Rushdin narrated to us, Amr, meaning Ibn al-Harith, narrated to me, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, that Nuaym al-Mujmir narrated to him that he prayed behind Abu Hurayrah, and he recited the Mother of the Quran, and when he said: Not of those who earned anger nor of those astray, he said: Amin, then said takbir for lowering the head. Then he said when he finished: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, I am indeed the most like you in prayer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10454","Mutamir narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid and Shahr, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: My close friend enjoined upon me three: not to sleep except upon witr, to fast three days of every month, and not to leave the two rakahs of Duha."
"10455","Abdullah said: I found these two hadith in my fathers book in his handwriting: Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Ansari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not precede the month, meaning Ramadan, by a day or two, except that it coincides with a fast one of you used to fast. Fast upon seeing it and break fast upon seeing it; and if it is obscured for you, count thirty then break fast."
"10456","Muhammad ibn Abdillah narrated to us, al-Ashath narrated to me, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A nation of nations was lost, and Allah knows best whether it is the mouse or not; do you not see that when camels milk is placed for it, it does not taste it."
"10457","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to me, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon the son of Adam are three knots with silk when he sleeps the night; so if he awakes in the night and remembers Allah, Mighty and Majestic, a knot is loosened; and if he performs ablution a knot is loosened; and if he stands and resolves then prays, all the knots are loosened. And if he sleeps without remembering Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and without performing ablution and without praying until morning, he wakes with all the knots upon him."
"10458","Ismail narrated to us, from Yunus, and he did not raise it."
"10459","Hashim narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, who said: While Abu Hurayrah was narrating to his companions, a man came toward Abu Hurayrah while he was in the gathering, and he came wearing a suit of his, swaying in it, until he stood before Abu Hurayrah and said: O Abu Hurayrah, do you have any ruling about this suit of mine? He raised his head to him and said: The truthful, believed, my close friend Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me, saying: While a man of those before you was strutting between two cloaks, Allah became angry with him and commanded the earth, so it swallowed him. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, he is surely sinking into it until the Day of Resurrection. Go, O man, to the Day of Resurrection."
"10460","Hashim narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I do not know it except from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Let no woman touch another woman, nor a man touch another man."
"10461","Ismail narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: When one of you sleeps, three knots with silk are tied upon his head; so if he stands and remembers Allah, Mighty and Majestic, one is released, and if he goes on and performs ablution the second is released, and if he goes on and prays the third is released. And if he wakes without standing anything of the night and without praying, he wakes with it upon him, meaning the silk."
"10462","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go barefoot in both together or wear sandals in both together; when you put on, begin with the right, and when you take off, begin with the left."
"10463","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying, and he used to pass by us while people were performing ablution from the ablution vessel: Perform ablution fully, for Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"10464","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Indeed in Friday there is an hour that no Muslim servant coincides with while praying, asking Allah for good therein, but He gives it to him. And Abu Hurayrah said: He indicated its brevity with his hand."
"10465","Hajjaj said: Shubah said: And Ibn Awn narrated to me, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of that."
"10466","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever is below the ankles of the lower garment is in the Fire. Shubah said: And Said had grown old."
"10467","Hajjaj and Muhammad ibn Jafar said: Shubah informed us, from Mansur, who said: Shubah said: He wrote it to me, and I read it to him, from Abu Uthman, freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, from Abu Hurayrah, and he did not raise it, who said: There is no Muslim servant who prays in a day twelve rakahs voluntarily except a house is built for him in Paradise."
"10468","al-Hakam narrated to us, Abdullah said: And I heard it myself from al-Hakam ibn Musa: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is overcome by vomiting has no make-up upon him, and whoever deliberately vomits, let him make up."
"10469","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): May he pray in a single garment? So he said: Do all of you find two garments?"
"10470","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: In Friday there is an hour that no Muslim servant coincides with while praying, asking Allah therein for good, but He gives it to him. And he said with his hand, and he clenched the three fingers of his right. We said: He regards it as brief, he regards it as brief."
"10471","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever intends a good deed and does not do it, a good deed is written for him; and if he does it, ten good deeds are written for him. And whoever intends an evil deed and does not do it, it is not written against him; and if he does it, one evil deed is written against him."
"10472","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed concerning the fetus with a ghurrah, a slave or slavegirl. So the one against whom judgment was passed said: Is one to be compensated for who neither drank nor ate nor cried out then raised his voice? Such as that goes in vain. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed this speaks with the speech of a poet. Yes, in it is a ghurrah, a slave or slavegirl."
"10473","Yazid narrated to us, saying: And Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever follows it until its burial is completed has two qirats, one of them, or the smaller of them, like Uhud. Abu Salamah said: So I mentioned it to Ibn Umar, and he deemed it great, so he sent to Aishah, and she said: Abu Hurayrah spoke the truth. So Ibn Umar said: We have missed many qirats."
"10474","Yazid narrated to us, saying: And Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: I am al-Rahman and it is al-rahim; I derived for it from My name; whoever joins it I join him, and whoever cuts it I cut him, so I sever him."
"10475","Yazid narrated to us, saying: And Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are mines; the best of them in Jahiliyyah are the best of them in Islam when they understand."
"10476","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: They passed with a funeral before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and praised it with good among virtues of good, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is due. Then they passed before him with another funeral and praised it with evil among virtues of evil, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is due. You are witnesses of Allah upon the earth."
"10477","Yazid narrated to us, saying: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Change this gray hair and do not resemble the Jews nor the Christians."
"10478","Hajjaj narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yaqub narrated to us, from Ibn Darrah, freedman of Uthman, who said: While we were at al-Baqi with Abu Hurayrah, we heard him saying: I am the most knowledgeable of people about the intercession of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Resurrection. He said: So people crowded upon him and said: Tell, may Allah have mercy on you. He said: He says: O Allah, forgive every Muslim servant who meets You believing in me and not associating with You."
"10479","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hilal al-Madani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The early comer seeking Friday is like one offering a sacrifice: one offering a camel, and one offering a cow, and one offering a sheep, and one offering a chicken, and one offering an egg."
"10480","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hilal informed us, saying: My father narrated to us, Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere except the Sacred Mosque."
"10481","Ammar ibn Muhammad, and he is the son of Sufyans sister, narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abu Iyad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the likeness of knowledge that does not benefit is like the likeness of a treasure not spent in the cause of Allah."
"10482","Amr ibn Mujammi Abu al-Mundhir al-Kindi narrated to us, Ibrahim al-Hajari narrated to us, from Abu Iyad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every bone of the son of Adam decays except the tailbone, and in it creation is composed on the Day of Resurrection."
"10483","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from al-Hajari, from Abu Iyad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything of man decays except the tailbone, and in it creation is composed on the Day of Resurrection."
"10484","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Khalid and Hisham informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile time, for Allah is time."
"10485","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, al-Nahhas ibn Qahm informed us, from Abu Ammar Shaddad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guards the forenoon supererogatory prayer, his sins are forgiven even if they are like the foam of the sea."
"10486","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Khalid and Hisham informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has ninety-nine names; whoever enumerates them all enters Paradise."
"10487","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Khalid and Hisham informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Name yourselves with my name and do not take my kunyah."
"10488","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: My close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me three: not to sleep except upon witr, fasting three days of every month, and the two rakahs of Duha."
"10489","Ali narrated to us, from al-Hadhdha, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dumb animal is without liability, and the mine is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"10490","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): May one of us pray in a garment? He said: Do all of you find two garments?"
"10491","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays Friday, let him pray after it four rakahs."
"10492","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, al-Hajjaj informed us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever conceals knowledge he knows will come on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire."
"10493","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Nuaym, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Prophet of repentance (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whichever man slanders his slave while he is innocent of what he said, the hadd is established against him on the Day of Resurrection, except that he be as he said."
"10494","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade the price of a dog, and the dowry of a prostitute, and the stud fee of a stallion."
"10495","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: He forbade the price of a dog, and the earnings of a cupper, and the dowry of a prostitute. He said: I said to Ata: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said? He said: Then who?"
"10496","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood in prayer, would raise his hands extended."
"10497","Muhammad ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Said ibn Siman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: People have abandoned three things the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to practice: he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood for prayer, would raise his hands extended, then pause before recitation briefly asking Allah of His bounty, and he would say takbir whenever he lowered and raised."
"10498","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Maqburi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mihran, who said: When death came to Abu Hurayrah, he said: Do not follow me with a censer, and hasten with me, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed the believer, when placed upon his bier, says: Hasten with me; and when the disbeliever is placed upon his bier, he says: Woe to it, where are you taking me."
"10499","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Let none of you say: O Allah, forgive me if You will; O Allah, have mercy on me if You will; let him be firm in asking, he said: For He has none to compel Him. Abdullah said: Thus it was in my fathers book, blank."
"10500","And surplus water is not to be withheld so that surplus herbage is thereby withheld."
"10501","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from Musa ibn Abi Uthman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: A woman is not to fast when her husband is present except with his permission."
"10502","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Hazm narrated to us: He said: I heard Muhammad ibn Wasi from some of his companions, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever relieves his Muslim brother of a distress among the distresses of this world, Allah will relieve him of a distress among the distresses of the Hereafter; and whoever conceals (the faults of) his brother, Allah will conceal him in this world and the Hereafter; and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is in the aid of the servant so long as the servant is in the aid of his brother."
"10503","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, and from al-Zuhri and others: They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes up, let him not put his hand into the washing water until he has washed it, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"10504","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is more joyful at the repentance of His servant than one of you at (finding) his stray animal in a desert land, having upon it his food and his drink."
"10505","He said: And Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: When My servant comes to Me a handspan, I come to him an arm's length; and when he comes to Me an arm's length, I come to him a fathom; and when he comes to Me walking, I come to him hastening."
"10506","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, informed us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yaqub, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays and sits in his place of prayer, the angels do not cease to say: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him, so long as he does not stand up or break his ablution."
"10507","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Right Hand of Allah is full; expenditure does not diminish it, bountiful night and day. And He said: Have you considered what He has spent since He created the heaven and the earth? For it has not diminished what is in His Right Hand. He said: And His Throne is upon the water, and in His other Hand is the Balance; He lowers and He raises."
"10508","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, and from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman entered the Fire on account of a cat, or a she-cat, which she tied up: she neither fed it, nor let it go to eat from the vermin of the earth, until it died in its confinement from emaciation."
"10509","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Kisra perishes, there will be no Kisra after him; and when Qaysar perishes, there will be no Qaysar after him."
"10510","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: May a man pray in a single garment? He said: Do all of you have two garments?"
"10511","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The excellence of the congregational prayer over the prayer of the solitary individual is twenty-five degrees."
"10512","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fasting person has two joys: a joy at his breaking of the fast, and a joy on the Day of Resurrection; and the altered smell of the mouth of the fasting person is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."
"10513","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Delay the prayer from the heat, for the intensity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell."
"10514","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Saddles are not to be girded except to the Sacred Mosque, and my mosque, and al-Masjid al-Aqsa."
"10515","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah loves him; and whoever hates the Ansar, Allah hates him."
"10516","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for the Hijrah, I would have been a man of the Ansar; and if people took a valley or a mountain pass, and the Ansar took a valley or a mountain pass, I would take the valley of the Ansar and their mountain pass."
"10517","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade making nabidh in al-muzaffat, and al-muqayyar, and al-naqir, and al-dubba, and al-hantam; and he said: Every intoxicant is unlawful."
"10518","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity is only from a surplus of sufficiency; and the upper hand is better than the lower hand; and begin with those you support."
"10519","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is part of faith, and faith is in Paradise; and foul speech is part of harshness, and harshness is in the Fire."
"10520","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says about me what I have not said, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"10521","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The heart of the old man remains young in love of two things: love of life and love of wealth."
"10522","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The injury caused by a stray animal is without liability, and the mine is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"10523","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not go out to meet the riders for trade; and let no town-dweller sell for a Bedouin; and do not hate one another, and do not envy one another, and do not practice najsh; and be, O servants of Allah, brothers."
"10524","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been aided by terror; and I have been given the comprehensive words; and the earth has been made for me a mosque and a purification; and while I was sleeping, I was brought the keys of the treasuries of the earth and they were placed in my hand."
"10525","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah; and when they say it, they protect from me their blood and their wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."
"10526","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That he used to lead them in prayer, uttering the takbir each time he rose; and when he finished, he said: I am the one among you most resembling in prayer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10527","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels do not cease to invoke blessings upon one of you so long as he remains in the place of prayer in which he prayed, so long as he does not stand up or break his ablution; they say: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him."
"10528","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah bowed in the prayer, then raised his head and said: O Allah, deliver Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah; O Allah, deliver Salamah ibn Hisham; O Allah, deliver al-Walid ibn al-Walid; O Allah, deliver the oppressed among the believers; O Allah, lay Your hardship heavily upon Mudar; O Allah, make them years like the years of Yusuf. Allah is Greatest; then he fell prostrate."
"10529","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is an imam, let him lighten, for behind him stand the weak, and the old, and the one with a need; and when he prays by himself, let him lengthen as he wishes."
"10530","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, I would love to fight in the path of Allah and be killed, then be brought to life, then be killed, then be brought to life, then be killed, then be brought to life, then be killed; and were it not that I would impose hardship upon the believers, I would not have stayed behind any detachment going out or raiding in the path of Allah; but I do not find means to carry them, nor do they find means to follow me, nor are their souls content to stay behind me, or to sit back after me."
"10531","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first group of my ummah to enter Paradise will be in the form of the moon on the night of the full moon; then those who follow them in the form of the most beautiful brilliant star in the sky. Then Ukashah ibn Mihsan stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, invoke Allah that He make me of them. He said: O Allah, make him of them. Then another man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, invoke Allah that He make me of them. He said: Ukkashah has preceded you in it."
"10532","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best women who have ridden camels are the women of Quraysh: the most tender toward an orphan in his childhood, and the most careful toward a husband regarding his means."
"10533","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: Al-Tufayl ibn Amr al-Dawsi came with his companions and said: O Messenger of Allah, Daws has disobeyed and refused, so invoke Allah against them. Abu Hurayrah said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands, and I said: Daws is ruined. Then he said: O Allah, guide Daws and bring them."
"10534","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There have come to you the people of Yemen; they are weakest of hearts and softest of hearts. Faith is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni."
"10535","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."
"10536","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Narrate from the Children of Israel, and there is no harm. He said: And while a man was driving a cow and it became exhausted, so he rode it, and it turned to him — then he mentioned the hadith."
"10537","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are the last, the foremost on the Day of Resurrection, except that they were given the Book before us and we were given it after them; and this is their day which was enjoined upon them and over which they differed, so Allah guided us to it; so the people follow us in it: today is ours, and tomorrow is for the Jews, and the day after tomorrow is for the Christians."
"10538","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those before you were destroyed only by the frequency of their questioning and their differing with their prophets. Do not ask me about anything but that I inform you of it. Then Abdullah ibn Hudhafah said: Who is my father, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Your father is Hudhafah ibn Qays. So he returned to his mother, and she said: Woe to you, what drove you to what you did? For we were people of jahiliyyah and people of ugly deeds. So he said to her: I did love to know who my father was, whoever he might be among the people."
"10539","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has ninety-nine names — one hundred less one; whoever enumerates them all enters Paradise."
"10540","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: A Bedouin entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting, and said: O Allah, forgive me and Muhammad, and do not forgive anyone along with us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed and said: You have constricted what is vast. Then he turned away until, when he was in a corner of the mosque, he spread his legs to urinate. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood toward him and said: This house was only built for the remembrance of Allah and prayer, and one does not urinate in it. Then he called for a bucket of water and poured it over it. He said: The Bedouin said, after he had understood: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood toward me — may my father and mother be ransom for him — and he neither cursed, nor rebuked, nor struck."
"10541","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you will be saved by his deed. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, unless Allah envelops me with mercy from Him; but draw near and be upright."
"10542","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two sales in one sale, and two (kinds of) garments: that one of you wrap himself in a garment with nothing between his private part and the sky; and al-samma, the wrapping of the Jews. And Muhammad described for us: he put it from one of his sides, then raised it."
"10543","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays over a funeral, for him is a qirat; and whoever follows it until its burial is completed, for him are two qirats, one of them — or: the smaller of them — like Uhud."
"10544","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and stands it in prayer with faith and seeking reward, forgiven for him is what preceded of his sin; and whoever stands Laylat al-Qadr with faith and seeking reward, forgiven for him is what preceded of his sin."
"10545","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Fire complained to its Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and said: Parts of me have consumed others. So He permitted it two breaths: so the most intense heat you feel is from its heat, and the most intense cold you feel is its zamharir."
"10546","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: Disputation about the Quran is disbelief."
"10547","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: Every deed of the son of Adam is for him — the good deed by ten like it up to seven hundredfold — except fasting: it is Mine, and I reward for it."
"10548","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"10549","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from what fire has touched, even from a bowl of cottage cheese."
"10550","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the call for the prayer is proclaimed, Satan turns away passing wind; and when the muadhdhin falls silent, he comes between one of you and himself until he makes him forget his prayer, so he does not know how much he has prayed; so whoever finds anything of that, let him prostrate two prostrations."
"10551","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, descends every night to the lowest heaven at the middle of the last night, or at the last third of the night, and says: Who is it that calls upon Me, that I may answer him? Who is it that asks Me, that I may give him? Who is it that seeks My forgiveness, that I may forgive him? Until dawn breaks, or until the reciter finishes the morning prayer."
"10552","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday: in it Adam was created, and in it he was admitted to Paradise, and in it he was sent down from it; and in it the Hour will come; and in it is an hour which no believing man who is praying meets — and he closed his fingers, making it small — asking Allah, Mighty and Majestic, for good, but He gives it to him."
"10553","Yazid narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: Does not one of you fear, when he raises his head while the imam is prostrating, that Allah will make his head the head of a donkey, or his form the form of a donkey?"
"10554","Yazid narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When he gets drunk, flog him; then if he gets drunk, flog him; then if he gets drunk, flog him; then if he returns a fourth time, strike his neck."
"10555","Yazid narrated to us: Ismail informed us, from Ziyad al-Makhzumi, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are the last, the foremost on the Day of Resurrection. The first group of my ummah to enter Paradise: seventy thousand, with no reckoning upon them; each man of them in the form of the moon on the night of the full moon; then those who follow them in the form of the brightest star in the sky; then after that, stations."
"10556","Yazid narrated to us: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: Whoever fashions an image will be punished on the Day of Resurrection until he breathes the spirit into it, and he will never breathe into it; and whoever listens to the speech of a people who dislike their speech being listened to, molten lead will be poured into his ear; and whoever dreams a false dream, a grain of barley will be handed to him, and he will be punished until he ties between its two ends, and he will never tie it."
"10557","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In this black grain is healing from every disease except al-sam. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and what is al-sam? He said: Death."
"10558","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, there will come upon one of you a day in which he does not see me; then that he should see me will be more beloved to him than that he should have the like of his family and wealth."
"10559","Yazid narrated to us: Salim ibn Hayyan informed us: Said narrated to us: He said: I heard Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting is a shield; so when one of you is fasting on a day, let him not utter obscenity and let him not act ignorantly; and if a man reviles him or fights him, let him say: I am fasting."
"10560","Yazid narrated to us: Salim ibn Hayyan informed us: He said: I heard my father: He said: I heard Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the most lying of speech."
"10561","Yazid narrated to us: Shubah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He relates it from his Lord, Mighty and Majestic: He said: For every deed is an expiation, and fasting is Mine, and I reward for it; and the altered smell of the mouth of the fasting person is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."
"10562","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yaqub, freedman of al-Huraqah — my father said, and he is Abu al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman — he said: Abu Hurayrah said: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lower garment of the believer is from the middle of the shanks; and below that, to above the ankles; and what is below that is in the Fire."
"10563","Yazid narrated to us: Sufyan informed us: He said: I heard al-Hasan narrating from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever institutes a practice of misguidance and is followed in it, upon him will be the like of their burdens, without diminishing anything from their burdens; and whoever institutes a practice of guidance and is followed in it, for him will be the like of their rewards, without diminishing anything from their rewards."
"10564","Yazid narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Husayn informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: Whoever enters a horse between two horses while not secure that it will outrun, there is no harm in it; and whoever enters a horse between two horses while secure that it will outrun, it is gambling."
"10565","Yazid narrated to us: Ibn Awn informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: The angels curse one of you when he points with a piece of iron, even if he be his full brother through his father and mother."
"10566","Yazid narrated to us: al-Awwam informed us: Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: My close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me three things, and I shall not abandon them in travel or residence: that I not sleep except upon witr; and that I fast three days of every month; and that I not leave the two rakahs of al-Duha, for it is the prayer of the oft-returning."
"10567","Yazid and Abu Abd al-Rahman said — Yazid said: al-Masudi informed us — from Muhammad, freedman of the family of Talhah, from Isa ibn Talhah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: No one who wept from fear of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will enter the Fire until milk returns to the udder; and dust in the path of Allah and the smoke of Hell will never gather in the two nostrils of a man, ever. And Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri said: In the two nostrils of a Muslim, ever."
"10568","Yazid narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Salih, freedman of al-Tawamah, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays over a funeral in the mosque, there is nothing for him."
"10569","Yazid narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not abandon false speech and acting upon it, and ignorance, Allah has no need that he abandon his food and his drink."
"10570","Yazid narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come upon the people a time when a man will not care whether he takes wealth by lawful or by unlawful means."
"10571","Yazid and Abu Amir both said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Ajlan, freedman of al-Mushmaill — and Abu Amir said: freedman of Hakim — and Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri said: freedman of Hamas — from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do not insult while you are fasting; and if one reviles you, say: I am fasting; and if you are standing, sit down. By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the altered smell of the mouth of the fasting person is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."
"10572","Yazid narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Ajlan, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, I see what is behind me as I see what is before me; so straighten your rows, and perfect your bowing and your prostration."
"10573","Yazid narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Ajlan, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about riding the sacrificial camel, and said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, woe to you."
"10574","Yazid narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Ajlan — and Ismail ibn Umar said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, with the same meaning — from Ajlan, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the slave who prepares your food and handles it: Call him; and if he refuses, feed him in his hand; and when you strike them, do not strike them on their faces."
"10575","Yazid narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Abd Allah al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: When it is Friday, the angels stand at the doors of the mosque and record the first, then the first; so the likeness of the one who comes early to Friday is like the one who offers a camel, then like the one who offers a cow, then like the one who offers a ram, then like the one who offers a chicken, then like the one who offers an egg. Then when the imam comes out and sits upon the minbar, they fold their scrolls and sit listening to the remembrance."
"10576","Yazid narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Abu al-Walid, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: The poor man is not the one who goes around you that you feed him a morsel, a morsel; the poor man is only the abstinent one who does not ask people importunately."
"10577","Yazid narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Abu al-Walid, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: I would not love that Uhud were gold for me, that a third night pass by me with a dinar of it with me, except something I set aside for a creditor."
"10578","Yazid narrated to us: al-Masudi informed us, from Imran ibn Umayr: He said: I complained to Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah about people who withheld water from me, and he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say — al-Masudi said: and I know it only as raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: The surplus of water is not to be withheld after need has been met, nor the surplus of pasture."
"10579","Yazid narrated to us: al-Masudi informed us, from Ashath ibn Sulaym, from his father: That Abu Hurayrah saw a man who had left the mosque after the call to prayer had been made in it, and said: As for this, he has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10580","Yazid narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: Whoever has with him a wrong against his brother, of his honor or his wealth, let him seek release from him today, before it is taken when there will be neither dinar nor dirham; and if he has a righteous deed, taken from him will be according to his wrong; and if he has none, taken from the sins of his companion and cast upon him."
"10581","He said: And he said in Baghdad, before there comes a day on which there is neither dinar nor dirham."
"10582","And Rawh narrated it to us with its isnad and meaning, and he said: Before it is taken from him when there will be neither dinar nor dirham."
"10583","Yazid narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Muslim women — three times — let no neighbor woman belittle for her neighbor, even a sheep's trotter. And it is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and His Messenger and the Last Day to travel a day's journey except with a mahram."
"10584","Yazid narrated to us: al-Awwam informed us: Abdullah ibn al-Saib narrated to me, from a man of the Ansar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: Prayer to the prayer before it is an expiation; and Friday to the Friday before it is an expiation; and the month to the month before it is an expiation, except for three things. He said: So we knew that it was a new matter: except for associating partners with Allah, and breaking the pledge, and abandoning the Sunnah. He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, this associating with Allah we have known; so what are breaking the pledge and abandoning the Sunnah? He said: As for breaking the pledge, it is that you give a man your allegiance, then you fight him with your sword; and as for abandoning the Sunnah, it is leaving the community."
"10585","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Yasar informed us, from Ishaq ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise is what no eye has seen, and no ear has heard, and has not occurred to the heart of a human."
"10586","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: I sought a loan from My servant and he did not lend to Me; and My servant reviled Me, and he does not know — he says: O woe of time, O woe of time — and I am Time."
"10587","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The head of disbelief is toward the east; and pride and arrogance are among the people of horses and camels, among the loud-voiced people of wool; and tranquility is among the people of sheep."
"10588","Yazid narrated to us: Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: Sulayman ibn Dawud (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall go around tonight to a hundred women, and each woman of them shall bear a boy who strikes with the sword in the path of Allah; and he did not make exception. He said: So he went around that night to a hundred women, and none of them bore except one woman, who bore half a human. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he said: If Allah wills, each woman of them would have borne a boy who strikes with the sword in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"10589","Yazid narrated to us: Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah: He said: Whoever repents before the sun rises from its west, Allah turns to him."
"10590","Yazid narrated to us: Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: No contagion, and no omen; and I love the good omen."
"10591","Yazid narrated to us: Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That a profligate woman saw a dog on a hot day circling a well, its tongue hanging out from thirst, so she removed her shoe, and she was forgiven."
"10592","Yazid narrated to us: Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That a woman entered the Fire on account of a cat which she tied up: she neither let it eat from the vermin of the earth, nor fed it, nor gave it to drink, until it died."
"10593","Yazid narrated to us: Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: When one of you is invited, let him respond; and if he is fasting, let him invoke blessings; and if he is not fasting, let him eat."
"10594","Yazid narrated to us: Hisham informed us — and Muhammad ibn Jafar said: Hisham narrated to us — from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: Whoever buys a musarrah, he has the choice for three days; and if he returns it, he returns with it a sa of dates, not wheat."
"10595","Yazid narrated to us: Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: The animal, its injury is without liability; and the mine, its injury is without liability; and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"10596","Yazid narrated to us: Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: Paradise and the Fire disputed. So Paradise said: O Lord, what is with it that the weak of the people and their fallen enter it? And the Fire said: O Lord, what is with it that the tyrants and the arrogant enter it? He said to Paradise: You are My mercy; I afflict through you whom I will. And He said to the Fire: You are My punishment; I afflict through you whom I will. And for each one of you two is its fill. He said: As for Paradise, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, wrongs none of His creation, and there shall be created for it of His creation what He wills. And as for the Fire, they are cast into it, and it says: Is there more? And they are cast into it, and it says: Is there more? Until our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, places in it His Foot; thereupon it fills, and parts of it draw together, and it says: Enough, enough."
"10597","Yazid narrated to us: Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: When one of you wakes from his sleep, let him not dip his hand into his water for purification until he has poured upon it and washed it, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"10598","Yazid narrated to us: Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: When time draws near, the dream of the Muslim hardly lies; and the truest of them in dream are the truest of them in speech. And the dream of the Muslim is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood. He said: And he said: Dreams are three: so the righteous dream is glad tidings from Allah, Mighty and Majestic; and the dream is grief from Satan; and the dream is from what a man speaks to himself about. So when one of you sees what he dislikes, let him not narrate it to anyone, and let him stand and pray. He said: And I love the fetter in sleep, and I hate the shackle: the fetter is firmness in religion."
"10599","Yazid narrated to us: Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: Glorification is for men, and clapping is for women, in the prayer."
"10600","Yazid narrated to us: Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: Delay the prayer in the heat, for the intensity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell, or from the exhalation of the gates of Hell."
"10601","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: We were with him, and they either boasted or reminded one another, and the men said there are more men in Paradise than women, so Abu Hurayrah said: Did not Abu al-Qasim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The first group of my nation to enter Paradise, their faces are like the moon on the night of the full moon, and the second group is like the brightest brilliant star in the sky, for each man among them are two wives from the houris, the marrow of their shins is seen from behind the garments, and by Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, there is no unmarried person in it."
"10602","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: Rats are from what was transformed, and I will inform you of the sign of that: when the milk of milch camels is placed before them they do not touch any of it, and when the milk of sheep is placed they eat from it, he said: So Kab said to him: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say it, he said: So Abu Hurayrah said: Then the Torah was revealed to me."
"10603","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When the dog laps in a vessel, it is washed seven times, the first of them with dust."
"10604","Yazid narrated to us, Said informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Whoever goes bankrupt with the wealth of a people, and a man sees his goods intact, he has more right to it than others."
"10605","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, al-Hajjaj informed us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Whoever conceals knowledge that he knows will come on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire."
"10606","Yazid narrated to us, al-Bara ibn Yazid informed us, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Shall I not inform you of the people of Paradise, they said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, he said: The weak and oppressed, he said: Shall I not inform you of the people of the Fire, they said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, he said: Every harsh arrogant cruel person, they are those who do not feel pain in their heads."
"10607","Yazid narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah informed us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The soul of the son of Adam remains suspended by his debt until it is settled on his behalf."
"10608","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A man went out to visit a brother of his in another village, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, stationed an angel on his path, and when he passed by him he said: Where do you intend, he said: I intend so-and-so, he said: For kinship, he said: No, he said: Then for a favor he has with you that you tend, he said: No, he said: Then why do you come to him, he said: I love him for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, he said: Then I am the messenger of Allah to you, that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves you for your loving him therein."
"10609","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: And I do not know it except that he raised it, and he mentioned its meaning."
"10610","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Hassan al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, the like of it."
"10611","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let none of you say: my male slave, my female slave, but let him say: my young man and my young woman."
"10612","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, and he mentioned the like of it."
"10613","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A man shall not propose over the proposal of his brother, nor outbid over the transaction of his brother, and a woman shall not be married over her paternal aunt nor over her maternal aunt, and she shall not ask for the divorce of her sister to overturn what is in her dish, but let her marry, for she shall have only what Allah has decreed for her."
"10614","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Aws ibn Khalid, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The likeness of one who hears wisdom then does not convey from its owner except the worst of what he heard is like a man who came to a shepherd of sheep and said: Give me a sheep from your sheep in portions, so he said: Choose, and he took hold of the ear of the sheepdog."
"10615","Yazid narrated to us, al-Rabi ibn Muslim al-Qurashi informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: He addressed us, and once he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed us and said: O people, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has made Hajj obligatory upon you, so perform Hajj, so a man said: Every year, O Messenger of Allah, and he remained silent until he said it three times, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Had I said yes it would have become obligatory and you would not have been able, then he said: Leave me as I have left you, for those before you perished only by their much questioning and differing over their prophets, so when I command you with a matter, do from it what you can, and when I forbid you from a thing, leave it."
"10616","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever goes to the mosque in the morning and evening, Allah prepares for him hospitality in Paradise each time he goes morning and evening."
"10617","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri informed us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, borrowed a camel from a man, then he came demanding his camel, so he said: Seek a camel for him and give it to him, and they found none except one older than his, so they said: O Messenger of Allah, we found none except one older than his camel, so he said: Give him, for the best of you are the best in repayment."
"10618","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, raises a degree for the righteous servant in Paradise, and he says: My Lord, how is this for me, so He says: By your child seeking forgiveness for you."
"10619","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Pray in the sheepfolds, and do not pray in the camel resting places."
"10620","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Salih ibn Ibrahim, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Do not call grapes nobility, for nobility is the righteous Muslim man."
"10621","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with the like of it."
"10622","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, and Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: None of you will be admitted to Paradise by his deed, it was said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah, he said: Not even me, except that Allah covers me with mercy from Him and bounty, and he placed his hand upon his head."
"10623","Yazid narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah informed us, Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, he heard his father, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: When Allah loves a servant He says: O Jibril, I love so-and-so, so love him, so Jibril calls out in the heavens: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves so-and-so, so love him, then his love is cast upon the people of the earth, so he is loved, and when He hates a servant He says: O Jibril, I hate so-and-so, so hate him, so Jibril calls out in the heavens: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, hates so-and-so, so hate him, then hatred for him is placed for the people of the earth, so he is hated."
"10624","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Qatadah, from Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of Umm Burthun, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, prescribed Friday upon those before us, so they differed about it, and Allah guided us to it, so people follow us in it: today is ours, tomorrow is for the Jews, and the day after tomorrow is for the Christians."
"10625","Yazid narrated to us, Juhayr ibn Yazid al-Abdi informed us, from Khidash ibn Ayyash, he said: I was in a circle at Kufah, and there was a man narrating, he said: We were sitting with Abu Hurayrah, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever testifies against a Muslim with a testimony he does not deserve, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"10626","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Ata, the freedman of Umm Safiyyah, and Yaqub said Subayyah, and it is the correct form, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Were it not that I would burden my nation, I would have commanded them with the toothstick at every prayer, and I would have delayed the last night prayer to the first third of the night, for when the first third of the night passes, He descends to the lowest heaven until the break of dawn, a caller says: Is there no supplicant who will be answered, is there no asker to be given, is there no sinner seeking forgiveness so he is forgiven."
"10627","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sulayman, meaning al-Taymi, from Anas, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, meaning the Lord, Mighty and Majestic: When the servant draws near to Me a span, I draw near to him a cubit, and when he draws near to Me a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom, and when he draws near to Me a fathom, I come to him hastening."
"10628","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu al-Salil, from Abu Hassan, he said: Two sons of mine died, so I said to Abu Hurayrah: Have you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a hadith you narrate to us to comfort us for our dead, he said: Yes: Their young ones are the small dwellers of Paradise, one of them meets his father, or his parents, and takes hold of the edge of his garment or his hand, as I take hold of the border of this garment of yours, and does not leave him until He admits him and his father into Paradise."
"10629","Ishaq narrated to us, Awf informed us, from Anas ibn Sirin, he said: Awf said: And I know it only from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A sinful woman was forgiven who passed by a dog at the head of a well panting, thirst had almost killed it, so she removed her shoe and tied it with her veil, and drew water for it, so she was forgiven for that."
"10630","Ishaq narrated to us, Awf informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There are no two Muslims who lose three children who have not reached puberty, except Allah admits them and their children into Paradise by His mercy and grace, and he said: It is said to them: Enter Paradise, he said: And they say: Until our parents come, three times, and they say the like of that, then it is said to them: Enter Paradise, you and your parents."
"10631","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade two prayers, two garments, and two sales: He forbade prayer after Fajr until the sun rises, and prayer after Asr until the sun sets, and wrapping in a single garment and sitting with knees drawn up in a single garment exposing the private parts to the sky."
"10632","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, and Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ziyad informed me that Thabit, the freedman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd, informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The rider greets the walker, the walker greets the sitter, and the few greet the many."
"10633","Rawh narrated to us, Hubayb narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The rider greets the walker, and the walker greets the sitter, and he said at Baghdad: And the few greet the many, and the young greet the old, and Rawh said at Baghdad: And the few greet the many."
"10634","Rawh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Hold to the black seed, for it is a cure from everything except death, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Death."
"10635","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abd al-Karim ibn Malik informed me that Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah informed him, from his uncle, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade being given his kunya."
"10636","Rawh narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The right of hospitality is three days, and what befalls after that is charity."
"10637","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When one of you hears the call and the vessel is in his hand, let him not put it down until he fulfills his need from it."
"10638","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it, and he added in it: And the caller to prayer used to call when dawn broke."
"10639","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The fasting person has two joys: joy at his breaking fast, and joy when he meets his Lord, Mighty and Majestic."
"10640","Rawh narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, Abu Rafi narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Gog and Magog dig the dam every day until when they almost see the rays of the sun, the one over them says: Return, you will dig it tomorrow, so they return to it as it was at its hardest, until when their term reaches and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, wills to send them to the people, they dig until when they almost see the rays of the sun, the one over them says: Return, you will dig it tomorrow, if Allah wills, and he makes exception, so they return to it as it was when they left it, and they dig it and emerge upon the people, and they dry up the waters, and people fortify against them in their fortresses, and they shoot their arrows to the sky, and they return with the likeness of blood upon them, and they say: We have conquered the people of the earth and overpowered the people of the sky, so Allah sends upon them worms in their necks and kills them with them, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the beasts of the earth will fatten in gratitude from their flesh and blood."
"10641","Hasan narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Gog and Magog, and he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: When their term reaches and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, wills to send them upon the people."
"10642","Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade fasting two days: the day of breaking fast and the day of sacrifice."
"10643","Rawh narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abi Hasin, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When it is the fasting day of one of you, let him not speak obscenely nor act ignorantly nor harm anyone, and if one acts ignorantly toward him or harms him, let him say: I am fasting."
"10644","Rawh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, marvels at two men, one of them kills the other, then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, admits them both into Paradise, it was said: How can that be, he said: One of them is a disbeliever and kills the other, then he embraces Islam and fights in the path of Allah and is killed."
"10645","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ziyad informed us, from Ibn Shihab, that Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah, and whoever obeys my commander has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys my commander has disobeyed me."
"10646","Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Hammam, from Qatadah, and Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, with the same meaning, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Locusts of gold rained upon Ayyub, and Abd al-Samad said: Moths, so he began to pick them up, so He said: O Ayyub, have I not enriched you, he said: My Lord, who can be satiated from Your mercy, or he said: from Your bounty, Abd al-Samad said: He said: Yes, but I have no independence from Your bounty."
"10647","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to his companions while they were mentioning truffles, they said: Do you see them as the smallpox of the earth, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Truffles are from manna, and their water is a cure for the eye, and Ajwah dates are from Paradise, and they are a cure from poison."
"10648","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Hasten with deeds before six: the rising of the sun from its west, the Dajjal, the smoke, the beast of the earth, the private affair of one of you, and the general affair."
"10649","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Asid, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You will follow the ways of those before you, span by span and cubit by cubit, until if they entered the hole of a lizard you would enter it."
"10650","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said one day while narrating, and with him was a man from the desert folk: A man from the people of Paradise asked permission of his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, for cultivation, so his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, said to him: Are you not in what you wish, he said: Yes, but I love to cultivate, he said: So he sowed, and its growth, ripening, and harvest outpaced the glance, and it became like mountains, he said: So his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, says to him: Take, O son of Adam, for nothing satisfies you, he said: So the Bedouin said: By Allah, you will find him only a Qurashi or an Ansari, for they are cultivators, and as for us, we are not cultivators, he said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, laughed."
"10651","Rawh narrated to us, Said narrated to us, and Abd al-Wahhab, from Said, from Qatadah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Adam, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, prescribed Friday upon those before us, so people differed about it, and Allah guided us to it, so people follow us in it: today is ours, tomorrow is for the Jews, and the day after tomorrow is for the Christians, Saturday is for the Jews and Sunday is for the Christians."
"10652","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of Umm Burthun, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah said: And he mentioned the like of it, but he did not mention: Today is ours."
"10653","Rawh narrated to us, Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best day the sun rose upon is Friday, in it Adam was created, in it he was admitted to Paradise, and in it he was expelled from it."
"10654","Rawh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman and Abi Abdullah al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Upon every door of the mosque on Friday are angels writing the coming of men, and when the imam sits, the scrolls are folded, so the early comer is like one offering a camel, and the one after him like one offering a cow, and the one after him like one offering a sheep, and the one after him like one offering a chicken, and the one after him like one offering an egg."
"10655","Rawh narrated to us, Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: On the night I was taken, I was brought two cups, a cup of milk and a cup of wine, so I looked at them and took the milk, so Jibril said: Praise be to Allah Who guided you to the natural disposition, had you taken the wine your nation would have strayed."
"10656","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ibn Shihab informed us, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, that he narrated to him, from Abu Hurayrah, and he did not raise it, he said: May Allah fight the Jews, Allah forbade them fats, so they sold them and ate their price."
"10657","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr informed us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not practice false bidding, do not turn away from one another, do not compete, do not envy, do not hate one another, and let no man outbid over the transaction of his brother, and let no town dweller sell for a Bedouin, leave people, Allah provides some of them from others, and let no woman stipulate the divorce of her sister."
"10658","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Allah, you will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another, he said: If you wish, I will guide you to what, if you do it, you will love one another: Spread greeting among you."
"10659","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash informed us, from al-Amash, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever asks you by Allah, give him, and whoever invites you, answer him, and had a shank been gifted to me I would have accepted, and had I been invited to a shank I would have answered."
"10660","Aswad informed us, Abu Bakr informed us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every person of the Fire sees his seat in Paradise and says: Had Allah guided me, so it is a regret upon them, he said: And every person of Paradise sees his seat in the Fire and says: Were it not that Allah guided me, he said: So it is gratitude for him."
"10661","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is wounded with a wound in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will come on the Day of Resurrection as he was, his color the color of blood and his scent the scent of musk."
"10662","His father said: And he narrated to us from Sharik also, meaning Aswad."
"10663","Aswad narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The poor enter Paradise before the rich by half a day, and it is five hundred years."
"10664","Aswad narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Dawud, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Sad came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and when he saw him, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: In the face of Sad there is news, he said: Kisra was killed, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, says: May Allah curse Kisra, the first people to perish are the Arabs, then the people of Persia."
"10665","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection as a ram, and it will be said: O people of Paradise, do you know this, so they will look out fearfully, he said: And they will say: Yes, he said: Then the people of the Fire will be called: Do you know this, and they will say: Yes, so it will be slaughtered, then it will be said: Eternity in Paradise and eternity in the Fire."
"10666","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr informed us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, the like of it, except that he added in it: It will be brought upon the bridge and slaughtered."
"10667","Ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr informed us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man entered upon his family, and when he saw their need he went out to the wilderness, and when his wife saw that she stood to the millstone and set it, and to the oven and heated it, then she said: O Allah, provide for us, so she looked and the bowl was full, he said: And she went to the oven and found it full, he said: So the husband returned, he said: Have you obtained anything after me, his wife said: Yes, from our Lord, he stood to the millstone, and that was mentioned to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: Had he not lifted it, it would have kept turning until the Day of Resurrection."
"10668","I witnessed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was saying: By Allah, for one of you to come with a bundle, then carry it and sell it and keep chaste by it, is better for him than coming to a man and asking him."
"10669","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Kamil and Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, Kamil narrated to us, Abu al-Ala, Aswad said: He informed us with the same meaning, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: We used to pray night prayer with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and when he prostrated, al-Hasan and al-Husayn jumped upon his back, and when he raised his head he took them with his hand from behind gently and placed them on the ground, and when he returned they returned, until when he finished his prayer he seated them upon his thighs, he said: So I stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I return them, then lightning flashed, so he said to them: Join your mother, he said: And its light remained until they entered."
"10670","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, with his chain, from Abu Salih, Abu Hurayrah narrated to us, he said: Until they entered to their mother."
"10671","Rawh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Hanzalah ibn Ali al-Aslami, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Isa son of Maryam will enter ihram at Fajj al-Rawha for Hajj or Umrah, or he will combine them both."
"10672","Rawh narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah and Husayn ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not precede Ramadan by fasting a day or two, except a man who used to fast regularly, so he continues it with it."
"10673","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Uthman, that Abu Hurayrah was on a journey, and when they alighted they sent to him while he was praying, so he said: I am fasting, and when they placed the food and were about to finish, he came and they said: Come and eat, so he ate, and the people looked at the messenger, so he said: What are you looking at, he said: By Allah, he said: I am fasting, so Abu Hurayrah said: He spoke truth, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Fasting the month of patience and three days of every month is the fasting of the whole year, and I have fasted three days from the beginning of the month, so I break fast by the alleviation of Allah and fast by the multiplication of Allah."
"10674","Rawh narrated to us, Salih narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent Abdullah ibn Hudhafah to announce in Mina: Do not fast these days, for they are days of eating, drinking, and remembrance of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"10675","Rawh narrated to us, Awf and Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you eats or drinks forgetfully while fasting, let him complete his fast, for Allah has fed him and given him drink."
"10676","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The caller to prayer is entrusted, and the imam is guarantor, O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the callers to prayer."
"10677","Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade fermenting in gourds and pitch-coated vessels."
"10678","Rawh narrated to us, and Abu al-Nadr, they said: al-Masudi narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Abi al-Rabi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was among his supplications: O Allah, forgive me what I advanced and delayed, what I concealed and declared, my extravagance, and what You know better than me, You are the Advancer and the Delayer, there is no god but You."
"10679","Rawh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Abi Ubayd, the freedman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let none of you wish for death, either an evildoer who may seek forgiveness, or a doer of good who may increase."
"10680","Rawh narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Jafar, they said: Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, he said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has one hundred mercies, and He divided one mercy among the people of the earth, and it sufficed them until their terms, and He stored ninety-nine mercies for His allies, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will take back that mercy which He divided among the people of the earth to the ninety-nine, and complete them as one hundred mercies for His allies on the Day of Resurrection."
"10681","Muhammad said in his hadith: And Muhammad ibn Sirin and Khilas both narrated to me this hadith, both from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of that."
"10682","Rawh narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Khilas ibn Amr, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"10683","Rawh narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"10684","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to kiss al-Hasan ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, so al-Aqra ibn Habis said: I have ten children, I have never kissed any of them, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."
"10685","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, and Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Jurayj, Musa ibn Uqbah informed me, from Nafi, that Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When Allah loves a servant, He calls Jibril: Allah has loved so-and-so, so love him, so Jibril loves him, then Jibril calls out among the people of heaven: Allah has loved so-and-so, so love him, so the people of heaven love him, then acceptance is placed for him among the people of the earth."
"10686","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Dawud ibn Farahij, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Jibril kept advising me about the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."
"10687","Rawh narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Wasi, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever relieves a worldly distress for his Muslim brother, Allah will relieve for him a distress of the Hereafter, and whoever conceals for his Muslim brother, Allah will conceal him in this world and the Hereafter, and Allah aids the servant as long as the servant aids his brother."
"10688","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: None of you will be saved by his deed, they said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah, he said: Not even me, except that Allah covers me with mercy from Him, so be upright, draw near, go in the morning and evening, and part of the night journey, and moderation, moderation, you will reach."
"10689","Rawh narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Khilas and Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said concerning this verse: O you who believe, do not be like those who harmed Musa, so Allah cleared him from what they said, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Musa was a shy concealing man, hardly showing anything of his skin from modesty, he said: Those who harmed him from the Children of Israil harmed him, they said: He does not conceal himself with this concealment except from a defect in his skin, either leprosy, or a scrotal hernia, and Rawh once said: hernia, or an ailment, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, willed to clear him from what they said, and Musa was alone one day and placed his garment upon a stone, then bathed, and when he finished he came to his garment to take it, and the stone fled with his garment, so Musa took his staff and sought the stone, and began saying: My garment, O stone, my garment, O stone, until he reached an assembly of the Children of Israil, and they saw him naked, the best-formed of men, and He cleared him from what they said about him, and the stone stood, so he took his garment and began striking the stone with his staff, he said: By Allah, there are marks in the stone from his striking, three or four or five."
"10690","Rawh narrated to us, Umar ibn Dharr narrated to us, from Mujahid, that Abu Hurayrah used to say: By Allah, I used to press my liver upon the ground from hunger, and I used to tie a stone upon my belly from hunger, and I sat one day upon their path from which they emerge, so Abu Bakr, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, passed, and I asked him about a verse from the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, I asked him only that he would make me follow him, but he did not do so, then Umar, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, passed, and I asked him about a verse from the Book of Allah, I asked him only that he would make me follow him, but he did not do so, then Abu al-Qasim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed, and he recognized what was in my face and in myself, so he said: Abu Hurayrah, so I said to him: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, so he said: Follow, and I asked permission and he permitted me, and I found milk in a cup, so he said: Where is this milk for you from, so they said: So-and-so, or the family of so-and-so, gifted it to us, he said: Abu Hurayrah, I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, he said: Go to the people of the bench and invite them to me, he said: And the people of the bench are the guests of Islam, they sheltered neither with family nor wealth, when a gift came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he took from it and sent to them from it, he said: And that grieved me, and I had hoped to obtain a drink of milk to strengthen myself for the rest of my day and night, so I said: I am the messenger, and when the people come I am the one who gives them, so I said: What will remain for me from this milk, and there was no escape from obeying Allah and obeying His Messenger, so I went and invited them, and they came and asked permission and he permitted them, and they took their seats in the house, then he said: Abu Hirr, take and give them, so I took the cup and began giving them, and a man would take the cup and drink until satisfied, then return the cup, so I would give another, and he would drink until satisfied, then return the cup, until I reached the last of them, and I handed it to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he took the cup and placed it in his hand, and there remained in it some excess, then he raised his head and looked at me and smiled, so he said: Abu Hirr, I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, he said: There remain I and you, so I said: You spoke truth, O Messenger of Allah, he said: Sit and drink, he said: So I sat and drank, then he said to me: Drink, so I drank, and he kept saying to me: Drink, so I drank, until I said: No, by Him Who sent you with the truth, I find no path for it in me, he said: Hand me the cup, so I returned the cup to him, and he drank from the excess."
"10691","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: No people sit in a gathering then disperse from other than remembrance, except they disperse from the like of the carcass of a donkey, and that gathering will be a regret upon them on the Day of Resurrection."
"10692","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, he said: I heard Amr ibn Asim ibn Sufyan ibn Abdullah, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The most fitting supplication is for a man to say: O Allah, You are my Lord and I am Your servant, I wronged myself and confessed my sin, O Lord, forgive my sin, You are my Lord, none forgives sin but You."
"10693","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Husayn al-Makki narrated to us, from Amr ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, the like of it."
"10694","Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Sumayy, the freedman of Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salih al-Samman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever says: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, in a day one hundred times, his sins are removed, even if they are like the foam of the sea."
"10695","Rawh narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: I am as My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him where he remembers Me."
"10696","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has ninety-nine names, one hundred minus one, whoever enumerates them enters Paradise."
"10697","Rawh narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with the like of it."
"10698","Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, and Uthman ibn Umar said: Malik informed us, from Ibn Shihab, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man broke fast in Ramadan, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded him to expiate by freeing a slave, or fasting two months, or feeding sixty poor, he said: I cannot find, so there was brought to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a basket of dates, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Take this and give it in charity, he said: O Messenger of Allah, I find none needier than me, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, laughed until his eyeteeth appeared, he said: Take it."
"10699","Rawh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, that a Bedouin came beating his face and tearing his hair and saying: I see myself only ruined, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: What ruined you, he said: I had intercourse with my wife in Ramadan, he said: Can you free a slave, he said: No, he said: Can you fast two consecutive months, he said: No, he said: Can you feed sixty poor, he said: No, and he mentioned need, he said: So there was brought to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a basket, and it is the miktal, in it fifteen measures, I think, of dates, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Where is the man, he said: Feed this, he said: O Messenger of Allah, there is none between its two lava tracts needier than us, my household, he said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, laughed until his eyeteeth appeared, he said: Feed your family."
"10700","Rawh narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Let no man outbid over the transaction of his brother, nor propose over the proposal of his brother, and let no woman be married over her paternal aunt nor over her maternal aunt, and let no woman ask for the divorce of her sister to overturn her dish, for she shall have only what Allah has decreed for her."
"10701","Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not to be taken in marriage together with her paternal aunt, nor a woman together with her maternal aunt."
"10702","Rawh narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A good deed is rewarded with ten the like of it, and fasting is for Me and I shall reward for it, and the breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."
"10703","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ata informed me, from Abu Salih al-Zayyat, that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting, for it is for Me and I shall reward for it. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah on the Day of Resurrection than the scent of musk. Fasting is a shield, and for the fasting person are two joys which he rejoices in: when he breaks his fast he rejoices, and when he meets his Lord, mighty and majestic, he rejoices in his fast."
"10704","Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk. He leaves his food and his drink and his desire for My sake, so fasting is for Me and I shall reward for it. Every good deed is rewarded with ten the like of it up to seven hundredfold, except fasting, for it is for Me and I shall reward for it."
"10705","Rawh narrated to us, Salih informed us, Ibn Shihab informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade continuous fasting without breaking it. A man from the Muslims said: You practice continuous fasting. He said: You are not like me; I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink. When they refused to stop continuous fasting, he fasted continuously with them for a day, then a day, then the crescent was seen, and he said: If it had been delayed I would have added more for you, as one disciplining you."
"10706","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yawning is from Satan, so whichever of you yawns, let him suppress it as much as he can."
"10707","Rawh narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would impose hardship upon my nation, I would have commanded them to use the tooth-stick with ablution."
"10708","Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you hear a man say, The people are ruined, he is the most ruined of them."
"10709","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, who said: I heard Ata ibn Yasar say, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When the prayer is commenced, there is no prayer except the prescribed one."
"10710","Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While a man was walking on a road, thirst became severe upon him, so he found a well and went down into it and drank, then came out, and there was a dog panting, eating the dust from thirst. The man said: This dog has been afflicted with thirst like that which afflicted me. So he went down the well and filled his shoe, then held it with his mouth until he climbed up and gave the dog to drink. So Allah, mighty and majestic, thanked him and forgave him. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, is there reward for us in animals? He said: In every living creature with a moist liver there is reward."
"10711","Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the worst of people is the two-faced one who comes to these with one face and to these with another face."
"10712","Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the most false of speech. Do not spy, do not eavesdrop, do not compete with one another, do not envy one another, do not hate one another, do not turn away from one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers."
"10713","Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The strong is not the one who overcomes in wrestling, but the strong is the one who controls himself at anger."
"10714","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, who said: I heard al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yaqub, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Two persons trading insults, what they say is upon the one who began, until the wronged one transgresses."
"10715","Rawh narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, mighty and majestic, said: I am in the expectation of My servant, and I am with him when he remembers Me."
"10716","Al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave me as I have left you, for those before you perished only by their questioning and their differing with their prophets."
"10717","Al-Dahhak narrated to us, Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that a sheep was cooked, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give me the foreleg. So he handed it to him. Then he said: Give me the foreleg. So he handed it to him. Then he said: Give me the foreleg. He said: O Messenger of Allah, a sheep has only two forelegs. He said: Had you sought it, you would have found it."
"10718","Al-Dahhak narrated to us, Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah loves sneezing and dislikes yawning. When one of you yawns and says, Hah, that is Satan laughing from inside him."
"10719","Al-Dahhak narrated to us, Hajjaj al-Sawwaf narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Jafar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three supplications are answered, with no doubt in them: the supplication of a father against his child, the supplication of the oppressed, and the supplication of the traveler."
"10720","Al-Dahhak narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Abu Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wine is in these two trees: the date-palm and the grapevine."
"10721","Al-Dahhak narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah informed us, Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Kathir, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wine is in these two trees: the date-palm and the grapevine."
"10722","Al-Dahhak narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Yazid ibn Farrukh al-Damri al-Madani, who said: I heard Abu Salamah say: I bear witness that I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant nor slave-girl swears at this minbar a sinful oath, even for a moist tooth-stick, except that the Fire becomes due for him."
"10723","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, Qabisah ibn Dhuayb informed me, that Abu Hurayrah informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade combining a woman with her paternal aunt and a woman with her maternal aunt."
"10724","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Muawiyah ibn Mughith or Muattib, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, what did your Lord, mighty and majestic, return to you concerning intercession? He said: I thought you would be the first to ask me about it from what I have seen of your keenness for knowledge. My intercession is for whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah sincerely, with his heart confirming his tongue and his tongue confirming his heart."
"10725","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Thabit al-Zuraqi, that Abu Hurayrah said: The wind seized the people on the road to Mecca and became severe upon them, so Umar said to those around him: What is the wind? They returned nothing to him. It reached me what he asked about, so I urged my mount until I caught up with him, and I said: O Commander of the Believers, I was told that you asked about the wind. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The wind is from the mercy of Allah, mighty and majestic; it comes with mercy and it comes with punishment. So do not curse it, and ask Allah for its good and seek refuge with Him from its evil."
"10726","Sakan ibn Nafi narrated to us, Salih narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Said ibn al-Musayyab informed me that Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah fought against the Jews and the Christians; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"10727","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah curse the Jews and the Christians; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"10728","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Malik informed us, from al-Zuhri, Qabisah ibn Dhuayb informed me, that Abu Hurayrah informed him that the Messenger of Allah forbade combining a woman with her paternal aunt and a woman with her maternal aunt."
"10729","Uthman informed us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution, let him blow his nose, and whoever cleans himself with stones, let him do so an odd number of times."
"10730","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The prayer was commenced and the rows were straightened standing, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us. When he stood at his place of prayer, he remembered that he was in a state of major impurity, so he said to us: Remain in your places. Then he returned and bathed, then came out to us with his head dripping, and he pronounced the opening takbir and we prayed with him."
"10731","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you say to your companion while the imam is delivering the sermon on Friday, Be quiet, you have engaged in idle talk."
"10732","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the children of the polytheists, and he said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"10733","Uthman informed us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Said al-Maqburi, who said: Abu Hurayrah said: The people say Abu Hurayrah narrates much. I met a man and said: With which chapter did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite last night in the night prayer? He said: I do not know. I said: Did you not attend it? He said: Yes. I said: But I know; he recited such-and-such a chapter."
"10734","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Said al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun has not risen nor set upon a day better than Friday. Allah guided us to it and led the people astray from it, so people follow us in it: it is ours, and for the Jews is Saturday and for the Christians is Sunday. In it there is an hour which no believer meets while praying, asking Allah, mighty and majestic, for something, except that He gives it to him."
"10735","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Said ibn Siman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until trials appear, lying increases, markets draw near, time contracts, and killing increases. It was said: What is killing? He said: Killing."
"10736","Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: When, And warn your nearest kin, was revealed, the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and said: O sons of Kab ibn Luayy, O sons of Hashim, save yourselves from the Fire. O sons of Abd Manaf, save yourselves from the Fire. O Fatimah daughter of Muhammad, save yourself from the Fire, for I own nothing for you from Allah except kinship which I shall keep moist with its due."
"10737","Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Khalid, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Take my name but do not use my agnomen."
"10738","Sulayman ibn Dawud, meaning al-Tayalisi, narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Sayyar, from al-Shabi, from Alqamah, who said: We were with Aishah when Abu Hurayrah entered. She said: Are you the one who narrates that a woman was punished for a cat of hers which she tied up and did not feed nor give drink? He said: I heard it from him, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abdullah said: This is how my father said it. She said: Do you know what the woman was? The woman, along with what she did, was a disbeliever, and the believer is too noble to Allah, mighty and majestic, for Him to punish him for a cat. When you narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), look at how you narrate."
"10739","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abu Husayn, who heard Dhakwan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"10740","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu Awanah informed us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When he drinks wine, flog him; if he returns, flog him. Then he said concerning the fourth time: Kill him."
"10741","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Said informed us, from al-Jurayri, who said: I heard Abu Nadrah narrating from Shutayr ibn Nahar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The poor of my nation will enter Paradise before their rich by half a day. He said: And he recited, And a day with your Lord is as a thousand years of what you count."
"10742","Sulayman ibn Dawud and Abd al-Samad said: Shubah and Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Abu Hurayrah, raising it. Abd al-Samad said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a woman spends the night abandoning the bed of her husband, the angels curse her until morning, or until she returns."
"10743","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, al-Muthanna informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu Ayyub, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you fights, let him avoid the face, for Allah, mighty and majestic, created Adam upon his image."
"10744","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ziyad al-Tahhan, who heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is none among you whom his deed will save. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, except that Allah envelops me with mercy from Him."
"10745","Sulayman ibn Dawud, and he is Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi, narrated to us, Imran, meaning al-Qattan, narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Maymunah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the Night of Decree: It is the night of the twenty-seventh or the twenty-ninth. The angels on that night upon the earth are more numerous than the number of pebbles."
"10746","Sulayman narrated to us, Harb and Aban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, Abu Salamah narrated to me that Abu Hurayrah informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, feels protective jealousy, and the believer feels protective jealousy, and the jealousy of Allah is that the believer commits what He has forbidden him."
"10747","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis, who said: I heard Kumayl ibn Ziyad narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise? I said: Yes. He said: There is no power nor strength except with Allah. He said: I think he said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says: My servant has submitted and surrendered."
"10748","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah informed us, from Yazid ibn Sharik, that al-Dahhak ibn Qays sent with him to Marwan some clothing. Marwan said: See whom you find at the door. Abu Hurayrah said: So he was given permission and said: O Abu Hurayrah, narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I heard him say: Peoples who were put in charge of this affair will wish that they had fallen from the Pleiades and that they had never taken charge of anything. He said: Add more for us, O Abu Hurayrah. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The destruction of this nation will occur at the hands of foolish young men from Quraysh."
"10749","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abu Balj, who said: I heard Amr ibn Maymun narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wishes to taste the flavor of faith, let him love a servant, loving him only for Allah, mighty and majestic."
"10750","Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Ajlan informed us, from al-Qaqa, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man supplicating like this with his two fingers, pointing, and said: Make it one, make it one."
"10751","Safwan informed us, Ibn Ajlan informed us, from al-Qaqa, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no wounded person wounded in the path of Allah, and Allah knows best who is wounded in His path, except that he will come on the Day of Resurrection with the wound as it was on the day he was wounded; the color is the color of blood and the smell is the smell of musk."
"10752","Safwan narrated to us, Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Concerning snakes, we have not made peace with them since we fought them. Whoever leaves anything out of fear of them is not of us."
"10753","Safwan narrated to us, Ibn Ajlan said: informed us, from al-Qaqa, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Congregational prayer exceeds solitary prayer by twenty-five degrees."
"10754","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Hisham and Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When he sits between her four parts, Shubah said: Then exerts himself, and Hisham said: Then strives hard, ritual bathing has become obligatory."
"10755","Shuayb ibn Harb Abu Salih narrated to us, who said: I heard Malik ibn Anas, and he mentioned Sufyan al-Thawri, and said: He parted from me on the condition that he would not drink date-wine."
"10756","Yahya narrated to us, who said: I heard Ibrahim ibn Sad say: I testify concerning Sufyan that I asked him, or he was asked, about date-wine, and he said: Eat dates and drink water; it will become date-wine in your belly."
"10757","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, meaning from al-Hasan, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When he sits between her four parts, then strives hard, ritual bathing has become obligatory. Abd al-Samad said: Then exerts himself."
"10758","Said ibn Amir narrated to us, from Hisham, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays in a single garment, let him cross its two ends over his shoulder."
"10759","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he urged giving for him. A man said: I have such-and-such. He said: No man remained in the gathering except that he gave charity, little or much. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever initiates a good practice and it is followed, he will have his reward in full, along with the rewards of those who follow it, without anything decreasing from their rewards. And whoever initiates an evil practice and it is followed, upon him will be his burden in full, along with the burdens of those who follow it, without anything decreasing from their burdens."
"10760","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two sales: touching and tossing."
"10761","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays one cycle of the morning prayer, then the sun rises, let him add another to it."
"10762","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar, narrated to us, who said: I heard my father mentioning from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man saw a dog eating dust from thirst. The man took his shoe and began to scoop water for it with it until he quenched it. So Allah, mighty and majestic, thanked him and admitted him to Paradise."
"10763","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man passed by a branch of thorns and moved it away from the road. So Allah thanked him and admitted him to Paradise."
"10764","Abd al-Samad and Abu Amir said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to, when he said, Allah hears whoever praises Him, in the last cycle of the latter night prayer, supplicate in standing and say: O Allah, save al-Walid ibn al-Walid. O Allah, save Salamah ibn Hisham. O Allah, save Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah. O Allah, save the oppressed among the believers. O Allah, harden Your grip upon Mudar. O Allah, make them years like the years of Yusuf. My father said: And Abd al-Wahhab said: Like the years of Yusuf. And he said in all of them: Save, save. And Abu Amir said: All of them: O Allah, save, save."
"10765","Abd al-Samad and Abu Amir said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not precede Ramadan by a day nor by two days, unless it is a man who used to fast a fast, then let him fast it."
"10766","Abd al-Samad and Abu Amir said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Jafar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: When a third of the night remains, Allah, mighty and majestic, descends to the lowest heaven and says: Who is it that calls upon Me, that I may answer him? Who is it that seeks My forgiveness, that I may forgive him? Who is it that seeks provision from Me, that I may provide for him? Who is it that seeks relief from harm, that I may relieve it? Until dawn breaks. Abu Amir said: From Abu Jafar, that he heard Abu Hurayrah."
"10767","Abd al-Samad and Abu Amir said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Jafar, from Abu Hurayrah. Abu Amir said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best faith with Allah, mighty and majestic, is faith in which there is no doubt, a military campaign in which there is no misappropriation of spoils, and an accepted pilgrimage."
"10768","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, and Abd al-Wahhab informed us, Hisham informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir. Abd al-Wahhab said: From Abu Muzahim, who heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever follows a funeral and prays over it, he has one qirat, and whoever waits until its burial is completed, he has two qirats. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the two qirats? He said: One of them is like Uhud."
"10769","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, and Abd al-Wahhab informed us, meaning Hisham, from Abbad ibn Abi Ali, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, raising it. Abd al-Wahhab said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Woe to the ministers. Peoples on the Day of Resurrection will wish that their forelocks had been suspended from the Pleiades, dangling between heaven and earth, and that they had never held an office."
"10770","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Sulayman, meaning Ibn al-Mughirah, narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Uthman, who said: It reached me from Abu Hurayrah that he said: Allah, mighty and majestic, gives His believing servant for one good deed a million good deeds. He said: It was decreed that I set out as a pilgrim or as a performer of minor pilgrimage, and I met him and said: It reached me from you a report that you say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, mighty and majestic, gives His believing servant for a good deed a million good deeds. Abu Hurayrah said: No; rather I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, mighty and majestic, gives him two million good deeds. Then he recited, He multiplies it and gives from Himself a great reward. Then he said: When He says a great reward, who can estimate its measure?"
"10771","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever covers his Muslim brother, Allah will cover him on the Day of Resurrection."
"10772","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one killed in the path of Allah is a martyr, the one who dies of plague is a martyr, the one who dies of abdominal illness is a martyr, and whoever dies in the path of Allah is a martyr."
"10773","Abd al-Samad and Affan said: Hammad narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us. Affan said in his report: Suhayl informed me, my father narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say when he entered the morning: O Allah, by You we enter the morning and by You we enter the evening, and by You we live and by You we die, and to You is the return."
"10774","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed me, one who heard Abu Hurayrah informed me, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A tyrant from the tyrants of the Umayyads will surely have a nosebleed upon my pulpit, with his nosebleed flowing. He said: Then one who saw Amr ibn Said ibn al-As having a nosebleed upon the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until his nosebleed flowed narrated to me."
"10775","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Said ibn Ubayd al-Hunai narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Abu Hurayrah narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) camped between Dajnan and Usfan. The polytheists said: These people have a prayer which is dearer to them than their fathers and their sons, and it is the afternoon prayer. So combine your affair and assault them in a single assault. Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and commanded him to divide his companions into two halves: he would pray with some of them while the other party stands behind them, taking their precautions and their weapons; then the others would come and pray with him, while these take their precautions and their weapons, so that there would be for them one cycle each with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two cycles."
"10776","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Hassan, meaning al-Anbari, narrated to me, from al-Qalus, that Shihab ibn Mudlij settled in the desert. His son insulted a man, saying: O son of the one who turned Bedouin after the migration. Shihab came to Medina and met Abu Hurayrah and heard him say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people are two men: a man who campaigns in the path of Allah until he descends in a place that distresses the enemy, and a man in a desert region who establishes the five prayers, pays the dues on his wealth, and worships his Lord until certainty comes to him. So he knelt upon his knees and said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), O Abu Hurayrah, saying it to him? He said: Yes. So he returned to his desert and stayed there."
"10777","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, Abu al-Zira narrated to us, from Abu Umayn, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I set out with Abd Allah ibn Umar and Samurah ibn Jundub, and we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said to us: Go to the mosque of piety. So we headed toward it, and we met him with his hands upon the shoulders of Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah Almighty be pleased with them both. We sprang up before him, and he said: Who are these, O Abu Bakr? He said: Abd Allah ibn Umar, Abu Hurayrah, and Samurah."
"10778","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, and Abd al-Wahhab informed us, Hisham informed us, who said: Yahya informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, the punishment of the Fire, the trials of life and death, and the trial of the False Messiah. Abd al-Wahhab said: And the evil of the False Messiah."
"10779","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When the call is made for prayer, Satan retreats with a breaking of wind so that he does not hear the call to prayer. When the call is completed, he returns. When the second call is made, he retreats. When the second call is completed, he returns, whispering between a man and his heart, or he said: his self, saying: Remember such-and-such, remember such-and-such, for what he did not remember, until a man remains not knowing how many he prayed. When one of you does not know whether he prayed three or four, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting."
"10780","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Nafi narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck the parable of the miser and the charitable one like the parable of two men wearing two cloaks of iron whose hands have been forced to their breasts and their collar-bones. The charitable one, whenever he gives charity, it expands from him until it covers his fingertips and erases his trace. And the miser, whenever he intends charity, each ring contracts and clings to its place. Abu Hurayrah said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gesturing with his fingers in his cloak: you would see him widening it, but it would not widen."
"10781","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Jafar, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three supplications are answered, with no doubt in them: the supplication of the oppressed, the supplication of the traveler, and the supplication of a father against his child."
"10782","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Hasten to deeds before trials like pieces of the dark night. A man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, and a believer in the evening and a disbeliever in the morning, selling his religion for a small portion of the world."
"10783","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Every son of Adam is stabbed by Satan with his finger in his side when he is born, except Isa son of Maryam; he went to stab, and he stabbed the veil."
"10784","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not wish to meet the enemy, but when you meet them, be patient."
"10785","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr and Surayj, in meaning, said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of the believer is like the tender stalk of a crop; from wherever the wind comes, it bends it, and when it calms, it stands straight. Likewise the parable of the believer is tossed about by affliction. And the parable of the disbeliever is like the pine, hard and straight, which Allah breaks when He wills."
"10786","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sasah, from Yaqub ibn Abi Yaqub, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man is not to make a man stand from his seat and then sit in it; rather make room, and Allah will make room for you."
"10787","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The leader is only a shield; fighting is done from behind him and protection is sought through him. If he commands piety and justice, he has reward for that, and if he commands other than that, upon him is sin for it."
"10788","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Nuaym ibn Abd Allah, that he climbed up to Abu Hurayrah upon the back of the mosque and found him performing ablution, raising the water to his upper arms. Then he turned to me and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: My nation on the Day of Resurrection will be bright-faced and bright-limbed from the trace of ablution. Whoever can extend his brightness, let him do so. I do not know whether this is from the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or from the saying of Abu Hurayrah."
"10789","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr and Surayj said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Abd Allah, meaning Ibn Mamar, and he is Abu Tuwalah, from Said ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not tell you of the best of people? A man holding the bridle of his horse in the path of Allah. Shall I not tell you of the best of people in rank after him? A man secluded with sheep or a small flock of sheep who establishes prayer, pays alms, and worships Allah, associating nothing with Him."
"10790","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr and Surayj said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mamar, Abu Tuwalah, from Said ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says: Where are those who love one another for My majesty? Today I shall shade them in My shade, on a day when there is no shade except My shade."
"10791","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Men must surely abandon their boasting of peoples who are only coal from the coal of Hell, or they will surely be more insignificant to Allah than the dung beetle which pushes filth with its nose. He said: Allah, mighty and majestic, has removed from you the pride of ignorance and its boasting of fathers: a God-fearing believer and a wicked wretch. People are the sons of Adam, and Adam is from dust."
"10792","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah Almighty said: I am in the expectation of My servant, and I am with him where he remembers Me. By Allah, Allah is more joyful at the repentance of His servant than one of you finding his lost camel in the desert. Whoever draws near to Me a hand-span, I draw near to him a cubit; whoever draws near to Me a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom; and when he comes walking, I come hastening."
"10793","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, Amr ibn Tamim narrated to me, my father informed me, that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your month has shaded you, by the oath of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No month has ever passed for the Muslims better for them than it, and no month has ever passed for the hypocrites worse for them than it, by the oath of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Allah records its reward and its voluntary acts, and records its burden and its wretchedness, before He brings it in. That is because the believer prepares in it strength from spending for worship, and the hypocrite prepares in it seeking the heedlessness of the believers and their faults. So it is spoil for the believer, exploited by the wicked."
"10794","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, and he is Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri, narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Tamim, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your month has shaded you, then he mentioned it."
"10795","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Zayd, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The best charity is that given from surplus wealth, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support. He said: Abu Hurayrah was asked: Who are those you support? He said: Your wife says: Feed me, or spend upon me, Abu Amir doubted, or divorce me. And your servant says: Feed me and employ me. And your daughter says: To whom do you leave me?"
"10796","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Ibn Abi Dhubab, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a ravine in which was a small spring of sweet water. Its pleasantness pleased him, and he said: If I stayed in this ravine and secluded myself from people. But I will not do it until I seek the permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Do not do it, for the standing of one of you in the path of Allah is better than praying sixty years alone. Do you not love that Allah forgive you and admit you to Paradise? Campaign in the path of Allah. Whoever fights in the path of Allah for the time between two milkings of a camel, Paradise becomes due for him."
"10797","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Khilas, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, that he mentioned two men who claimed an animal and had no proof, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them to draw lots for the oath."
"10798","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Hanzalah informed us, who said: I heard Salim say: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Knowledge will be taken away, trials will appear, and killing will increase. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is killing? He said with his hand like this, meaning killing."
"10799","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none among you, meaning, whom his deed will admit to Paradise, nor save him from the Fire. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, except that Allah envelops me with mercy and favor from Him, twice or thrice."
"10800","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, who said: I heard al-Numan ibn Rashid narrating from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no omen, and the best of it is the good omen. It was said: What is the good omen? He said: The righteous word which one of you hears."
"10801","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Yunus ibn Yazid al-Ayli narrating from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: You find people to be mines, so the best of them in the Jahiliyyah are the best of them in Islam when they understand, and you find among the best of people in this matter the one most averse to it before entering into it, and you find among the worst of people the two-faced one who comes to these with a face and to those with a face."
"10802","Wahb narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Yunus narrating from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Time will draw near, wealth will overflow, tribulations will appear, and harj will increase. They said: What is harj, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Killing, killing."
"10803","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be lenient in the prayer, for behind you are the weak, the elderly, and the one with a need."
"10804","He said: and Ibrahim al-Taymi narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, from Abdallah, with the like of that."
"10805","He said: and Ibrahim ibn Abdallah narrated to us the like of that."
"10806","He said: and Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of that."
"10807","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Hisham, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If any man goes bankrupt, and a man finds his own property with him, and he had not collected anything from his property, then it belongs to him."
"10808","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Kumayl ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out among the palm trees of Madinah and said: O Abu Hurayrah, or O Abu Hirr, the much-hoarders are ruined; indeed the much-hoarders are the fewest on the Day of Resurrection, except one who says with wealth thus and thus, and how few they are. O Abu Hurayrah, shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise: There is no power nor strength except with Allah, and there is no refuge from Allah except to Him. O Abu Hurayrah, do you know what is the right of Allah upon the servants and what is the right of the servants upon Allah? He said: I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The right of Allah upon the servants is that they worship Him and not associate anything with Him, and the right of the servants upon Allah is that He not punish whoever among them does that."
"10809","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salih ibn Nabhan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not a townsman sell for a Bedouin, and do not turn your backs on one another, and do not engage in najsh, and be servants of Allah as brothers."
"10810","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When you meet the polytheists on the road, do not initiate the greeting with them, and force them to its narrowest part."
"10811","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha, from Abi al-Ahwas, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Prayer in congregation exceeds the prayer of the solitary by twenty-five prayers."
"10812","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Amir ibn Yasaf narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn Badr al-Hanafi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not look at the prayer of a man who does not straighten his spine between his bowing and his prostration."
"10813","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abdah, meaning Ibn Sulayman, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Salman, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, causes people to spend the night in blessing, then they wake in the morning and most of them are disbelievers, saying: We were rained by such-and-such a star. He said: So I narrated this hadith to Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, and he said: And we have heard that from Abu Hurayrah."
"10814","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Waqid ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Asim, meaning Ibn Muhammad, from Sa'id ibn Marjanah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any Muslim man who frees a Muslim man, Allah will rescue him from the Fire, every limb of him for a limb of him."
"10815","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque for the last Isha prayer, and they were in scattered separate groups, so he became angry with an anger the like of which I never saw him angered with, more severe than it, then he said: If a man called the people to a meaty bone or two trotters they would come to it for that, while they stay behind from the prayer. I have intended to command a man to lead the people in prayer, then follow the people of these houses whose people stay behind from this prayer and burn it upon them with fires."
"10816","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Qutbah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Madinah is a sanctuary, so whoever commits an offense in it or shelters an offender, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people; Allah will not accept from him on the Day of Resurrection any just recompense nor ransom."
"10817","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ziyad al-Harithi, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, a man said to him: Are you the one who forbids people from fasting the day of Friday? He said: So he said: Yes, by the Lord of this Ka'bah, yes, by the Lord of this Ka'bah, three times, I heard Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: None of you fasts the day of Friday alone except with days along with it. And I saw Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying with his sandals on him and leaving with them on him."
"10818","Abdallah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Ikrimah narrated to us, Abu Kathir narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah saying: Wine is from these two trees, the date-palm and the grapevine."
"10819","And the Messenger of Allah said: Do not make nabidh of dates and raisins together, and do not make nabidh of unripe dates and dates together, and make nabidh of each one of them separately."
"10820","Abdallah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Lahi'ah Abu Abdallah, from a man he named, Salamah ibn Qaysar narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts a day seeking the Face of Allah, the Exalted, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will distance him from Hell like the distance of a crow that flew while a chick until it died old."
"10821","Abdallah ibn Yazid narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Abi al-Rabi', from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four are from the matter of the Jahiliyyah that people will never leave: wailing, impugning lineages, and the stars, a man saying: We were watered by such-and-such a naw, and contagion: a camel becomes mangy and a hundred become mangy, so who infected the first?"
"10822","Mu'ammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has one hundred mercies, so He made one mercy among them in the world by which you show mercy to one another, and with Him are ninety-nine mercies, so when the Day of Resurrection comes He will join this mercy to the ninety-nine mercies, then return with them upon His creation."
"10823","Abdallah ibn Yazid narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, Alqamah ibn Marthad narrated to us, from Abi al-Rabi', from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: O Allah, forgive me what I have advanced and what I have delayed, and what I have concealed and what I have declared, and my excess, and what You know better of than I; You are the Advancer and You are the Delayer, there is no god but You."
"10824","Abdallah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Abu Aqil Zuhrah ibn Ma'bad narrated to me, from his father Ma'bad ibn Abdallah ibn Hisham, that Abu Hurayrah says: My close friend advised me with three I will not leave until I die: he advised me with the two rak'ahs of Duha, and with fasting three days of every month, and not to sleep except upon witr."
"10825","Abdallah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah al-Qurashi narrated to me that Irak ibn Malik informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not turn away from your fathers, for whoever turns away from his father, it is disbelief."
"10826","Abdallah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Abu Sakhr informed me that Sa'd ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: He heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever enters this mosque of ours learning good or teaching it is like the mujahid in the path of Allah, and whoever enters it for other than that is like one looking at what does not belong to him."
"10827","Abdallah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Abu Sakhr narrated to us that Yazid ibn Abdallah ibn Qusayt informed him, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no one who sends salam upon me except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, returns my soul to me so that I return the salam upon him."
"10828","Abdallah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am closer to the believer than his own self; whoever leaves a debt or helpless dependents, then to me, and there is no loss upon him, so let supplication be made for him, and I am his guardian; and whoever leaves wealth, then it is for the agnate kin, whoever he be."
"10829","Abdallah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, Ibn Ajlan narrated to me, from al-Qa'qa' ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most complete of the believers in faith are the best of them in character."
"10830","Abdallah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, Ibn Ajlan narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The best of charity is what is from surplus of wealth, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support. So it was said: Whom do I support, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Your wife is among those you support, saying: Feed me or separate from me; and your slave-girl saying: Feed me and employ me; and your child saying: To whom do you leave me?"
"10831","Muhammad ibn Ubayd and Abu Ubaydah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abi Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: And who does more wrong than one who creates like My creation, so let them create a gnat, and let them create an atom. Abu Ubaydah said: yakhluq."
"10832","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abi Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah loves him, and whoever hates the Ansar, Allah hates him."
"10833","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abi Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Marwan used to leave him in charge of the prayer when he performed Hajj or Umrah, so he would pray with the people, and would say the takbir after the bowing and after the prostration, then when he finished he said: I am the most like you in prayer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10834","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Yazid ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Abi Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I was commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah, so when they say: There is no god but Allah, their reckoning is upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Thus I found it in the original of that."
"10835","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you stands from his seat then returns, he has most right to it."
"10836","Abd al-Samad and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Souls are grouped troops, so those of them that knew one another agree, and those of them that were unfamiliar with one another differ."
"10837","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No people sit in a gathering then disperse from it without remembrance of Allah except they disperse from the like of the carcass of a donkey, and that gathering will be a regret upon them on the Day of Resurrection."
"10838","Abd al-Samad narrated to me, Hammad, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever looks into the house of a people without their permission and his eye is gouged out, it is forfeited."
"10839","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abi Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will follow the ways of those before you, span by span, cubit by cubit, and fathom by fathom, until if one of them entered the hole of a lizard you would enter it. They said: O Messenger of Allah, from the Jews and Christians? He said: Who then?"
"10840","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abi Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Before the Hour there are thirty liars."
"10841","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abi Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two eyes commit adultery, and the two hands commit adultery, and the two feet commit adultery, and the private part confirms that or denies it."
"10842","Bakr ibn Isa Abu Bishr al-Rasibi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Awanah, Umar ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the night I was taken, my feet ascended, and in a copy: I placed my feet, where the feet of the prophets are placed from Bayt al-Maqdis, and Isa son of Maryam was shown to me, and the nearest of people to him in resemblance was Urwah ibn Mas'ud, and Musa was shown to me, and he was a spare man among men as if from the men of Shanua, and Ibrahim was shown to me, and the nearest of people in resemblance to your companion."
"10843","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Harb narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Bab ibn Umayr al-Hanafi narrated to me, a man from the people of Madinah narrated to me that his father narrated to him that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The funeral is not followed by a voice nor fire, and one does not walk in front of it."
"10844","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For one of you to sit upon an ember until his clothes burn and it reaches him is better for him than to step upon a grave."
"10845","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abi Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The servant remains in prayer while he waits for the prayer; the angels say: O Allah, forgive him, O Allah, have mercy on him, while he does not leave or break his ablution. So it was said to him: What is breaking the ablution? He said: Passing wind quietly or loudly."
"10846","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abi Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Disputation about the Qur'an is disbelief."
"10847","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abi Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The female servants of Allah are not to be prevented from the mosques of Allah, and let them go out unattractive."
"10848","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Amr, narrated to us, from Abi Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a funeral and they praised it with good among the traits of good, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has become due; you are the witnesses of Allah on the earth. Then he was passed by with a funeral and they praised it with evil among the traits of evil, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are the witnesses of Allah on the earth."
"10849","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Khubayb, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My pulpit is upon my Basin, and what is between my pulpit and my house is a meadow from the meadows of Paradise, and a prayer in my mosque is like a thousand prayers in other than it among the mosques except the Sacred Mosque."
"10850","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the strap of the sandal of one of you breaks, let him not walk in one sandal until he repairs it."
"10851","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Dawud al-Awdi narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Perhaps your Lord will raise you to a praised station. He said: It is the station in which I intercede for my ummah."
"10852","Rawh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Ubaydallah ibn Abdallah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah, so when they say it they protect from me their blood and their wealth, and their reckoning is upon Allah. He said: When Abu Bakr arose and those who apostatized apostatized, Abu Bakr wanted to fight them. Umar said: How do you fight these people while they pray? So Abu Bakr said: By Allah, I will fight a people who apostatized from zakah; by Allah, if they withheld from me a young goat of what Allah and His Messenger obligated, I would fight them. Umar said: When I saw that Allah had opened the breast of Abu Bakr to fighting them, I knew it was the truth."
"10853","Rawh narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin and Khilas, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should urinate in standing water then perform ablution from it."
"10854","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Umar ibn Ata ibn Abi al-Khuwar informed me that while he was sitting with Nafi' ibn Jubayr, Abu Abdallah, the in-law of Zayd ibn Ziyad al-Juhani, passed by them, so Nafi' called him and said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer with the imam is better than twenty-five prayers one prays alone."
"10855","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abi Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command standing in Ramadan without commanding with firm resolve in it, and he used to say: Whoever stands Ramadan in faith and seeking reward, what preceded of his sin is forgiven."
"10856","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Abi al-Zinad, from Abi al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not combined with her paternal aunt, nor a woman with her maternal aunt."
"10857","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Abdallah ibn Yazid, from Abi Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating in When the heaven is rent asunder."
"10858","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two sales, and two wearings, and two prayers, and fasting two days, and mulamasah and munabadhah, and wrapping in one garment, and sitting on the buttocks in a single garment uncovering his private part, and prayer after Asr until the sun sets, and prayer after Fajr until the sun rises, and fasting the day of Fitr."
"10859","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Malik informed us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the call is made for the prayer, do not come to it while you hasten, and come to it with tranquility upon you; what you catch, pray, and what you miss, complete, for one of you is in prayer while he heads to the prayer."
"10860","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Husayn, meaning al-Mu'allim, narrated to us, from Yahya, Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr narrated to me that he heard al-Muttalib ibn Abdallah ibn Hantab al-Makhzumi saying: Ibn Abbas said: Should I perform ablution from food I find lawful in the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, because the Fire touched it? He said: So Abu Hurayrah gathered pebbles before him and said: I testify by the number of these pebbles that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from what the Fire touched."
"10861","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man should not outbid the bargaining of his brother, nor propose over the proposal of his brother."
"10862","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, al-Ala and Suhayl narrated to us, from their father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man should not propose over the proposal of his brother, nor bid over the sum of his brother."
"10863","Rawh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab and Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tasbih is for men and clapping is for women."
"10864","Rawh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab and Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced the Negus to his companions, then said: Seek forgiveness for him. Then he went out with his companions to the prayer place, stood, and prayed with them as one prays over funerals."
"10865","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Wuhayb informed me, Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was opened from the barrier of Gog and Magog the like of that, and he circled ninety and joined it."
"10866","Ali ibn Hafs narrated to us, Warqa informed us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, it would not please me that Uhud, that one of yours, be gold with me, three days pass over it while with me of it is a dinar, except something I keep for a debt upon me."
"10867","Ali ibn Hafs narrated to us, Warqa informed us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hoard of one of you will be on the Day of Resurrection a bald serpent; its owner flees from it while it seeks him until it feeds him its fingers."
"10868","Ali ibn Hafs narrated to us, Warqa narrated to us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The woman will not stay straight for you upon one disposition; she is only like the rib: if you straighten it you break it, and if you leave it you enjoy it, while crookedness is in it."
"10869","Ali informed us, Warqa informed us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not rise until you fight the Jews, until the Jew hides behind the stone, and the stone says: O Muslim, this is a Jew hiding behind me, come and kill him."
"10870","Ali informed us, Warqa informed us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not rise until people compete with one another in buildings."
"10871","Ali informed us, Warqa informed us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not rise until the sun rises from its west; when it rises and the people see it they will all believe, and that is when no soul's faith will benefit it, to the end of the verse."
"10872","Ali informed us, Warqa informed us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not rise until you fight a people whose sandals are hair."
"10873","Ali informed us, Warqa informed us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not rise until you fight the Turks, small-eyed, red-faced, flat-nosed, as if their faces are hammered shields."
"10874","Ali informed us, Warqa informed us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not rise until wealth overflows among you, and until a man is concerned with his wealth as to who will accept it from him when he gives it in charity, and the one to whom it is offered says: I have no need of it."
"10875","Ali informed us, Warqa informed us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not rise until knowledge is taken, and time draws near, and earthquakes increase, and tribulations appear, and harj increases. He said: What is harj, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Killing, killing."
"10876","Ali informed us, Warqa informed us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not rise until two great factions fight, with a great slaughter between them, while their claim is one."
"10877","Ali informed us, Warqa informed us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not rise until impostor liars arise, near thirty, each of them claiming that he is the Messenger of Allah."
"10878","Ali informed us, Warqa informed us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not rise until a man passes by the grave of a man and says: Would that I were in his place, not from love of meeting Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"10879","Ali informed us, Warqa informed us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should say: O Allah, forgive me if You will, O Allah, have mercy on me if You will; let him be firm in asking, for there is none who compels Him."
"10880","Ali informed us, Warqa informed us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would burden my ummah, I would have commanded them with the siwak at every prayer."
"10881","Ali informed us, Warqa informed us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While a man struts in his two cloaks, self-conceited, Allah sinks him into the earth, and he rattles in its belly until the Day of Resurrection."
"10882","Abdallah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Dhakwan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant is wounded in the path of Allah, and Allah knows who is wounded in His path, whose wound comes on the Day of Resurrection with its color the color of blood and its scent the scent of musk."
"10883","Abdallah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Abi al-Rabi' al-Madani, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four people will not leave of the matter of the Jahiliyyah: wailing, taunting in lineages, their saying: We were watered by such a naw, and contagion: a camel becomes mangy and a hundred camels become mangy, so who made the first mangy?"
"10884","Abdallah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salim, he said: I heard Abu Hazim saying: I was a witness on the day al-Hasan died, and he mentioned the story, then Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah saying: Whoever loves them has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me."
"10885","Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frees his share in a slave, he is freed from his wealth if he has wealth."
"10886","Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the prescribed one."
"10887","Abdallah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Abdallah ibn Hubayrah narrated to me, from Abi Tamim al-Jayshani, he said: Abdallah ibn Hurmuz, a freedman from the people of Madinah, wrote to me mentioning from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever follows a funeral, and carries from its upper side, and throws earth in its grave, and sits until he is permitted to leave, returns with two qirats of reward, each qirat like Uhud."
"10888","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Satan hears the caller calling to the prayer, he goes out with farting so that he does not hear the voice; when he finishes he returns and whispers; when he begins the iqamah he does the like of that."
"10889","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The heaviest of prayer upon the hypocrites is the last Isha prayer and the Fajr prayer; if they knew what is in them they would come to them even crawling; if one of you knew that if he found a fat sheep bone or two good trotters you would all come to it. I have intended to command the prayer to be established, then command a man to pray with the people, then take bundles of firewood and come to those who stayed behind from the prayer and burn their houses upon them."
"10890","And Abu Mu'awiyah and Ibn Numayr narrated it to us, and this is more complete."
"10891","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Khalifah, meaning Ibn Ghalib, narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are best? He said: Faith in Allah and jihad in the path of Allah. He said: If I cannot do that? He said: Restrain yourself from evil, for it is a charity you give upon yourself."
"10892","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Hammad ibn Abbad al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Muhazzim informed us narrating from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that the Heaven chapters be recited in Isha."
"10893","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Harb narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Bab ibn Umayr al-Hanafi informed us, a man from the people of Madinah narrated to me that his father narrated to him, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The funeral is not followed with a voice, nor is one to walk in front of it with fire."
"10894","Abdallah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from al-Dahhak, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslim servant remains in prayer while he sits in his prayer place, and nothing detains him except waiting for the prayer, and the angels say: O Allah, forgive him, O Allah, have mercy on him, while he does not break his ablution."
"10895","Abdallah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, al-Dahhak narrated to me, from Bukayr ibn Abdallah ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said: I never prayed behind anyone more like in prayer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than so-and-so, a man he named. Al-Dahhak said: So Bukayr ibn Abdallah narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that he said: I prayed behind that man and saw him lengthening the first two rak'ahs of Zuhr and lightening the last two, and lightening Asr, and reciting in Maghrib the short Mufassal, and reciting in Isha By the sun and its brightness and what resembles it, then reciting in Fajr the long Mufassal."
"10896","Abdallah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Mina, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning outing in the path of Allah or an evening outing is better than the world and what is in it."
"10897","Abdallah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The altered breath of the mouth of the fasting one is sweeter to Allah on the Day of Resurrection than the scent of musk."
"10898","Muhammad ibn Yusuf, meaning al-Firyabi, in Makkah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Qurrah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Zuhri, from Abi Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shortening the greeting is sunnah."
"10899","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Malik, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man should not combine a woman and her paternal aunt, nor her and her maternal aunt."
"10900","Hammad, meaning Ibn Khalid, narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Dawud, meaning Ibn al-Husayn, from Abi Sufyan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness after the salam."
"10901","Haddathana Hammad from Malik and Ibn Abi Dhi'b from al-Zuhri from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: When you say to your companion while the imam is delivering the khutbah on Friday, Be quiet, you have engaged in idle talk."
"10902","Haddathana Hammad ibn Khalid from Abu Mawdud from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hadrad from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever spits in the mosque, let him dig a hole and bury it away, otherwise let him spit in his garment."
"10903","Haddathana Hammad ibn Khalid, haddathana Mu'awiyah from Abu Bishr the mu'adhdhin of Damascus from Amir ibn Ludayn al-Ash'ari he said: I asked Abu Hurayrah about fasting on Friday, so he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Friday is a day of Eid, so do not make your day of Eid a day of fasting unless you fast before it or after it."
"10904","Haddathana Hammad al-Khayyat, haddathana Hisham ibn Sa'd from Nu'aym ibn Abd Allah al-Mujmir from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the market of Banu Qaynuqa' leaning on my hand, then he walked about in it, then he returned and sat with his knees drawn up in the mosque and said: Where is Luka'? Call Luka' for me. Then al-Hasan, peace be upon him, came and hastened until he leapt into his lap, and he put his mouth into his mouth, then he said: O Allah, indeed I love him, so love him and love whoever loves him, three times. Abu Hurayrah said: I never saw al-Hasan except my eye overflowed, or my eye teared, or I wept; al-Khayyat doubted."
"10905","Haddathana Hammad ibn Khalid, haddathana Mu'awiyah ibn Salih from Abu Maryam from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade urinating in stagnant water and then performing wudu from it."
"10906","Haddathana Hammad, he said, and haddathana Abu al-Nadr from Ibn Abi Dhi'b from Ibn Shihab from Abu Salamah and Ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you hear the iqamah, then walk and do not hurry, and calmness is upon you; what you catch, pray, and what you miss, make up. And Abu al-Nadr said in his narration: so complete it; come with calmness upon you."
"10907","Haddathana Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf from Sa'id from Qatadah from Abu Rafi' from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: When one of you is invited and comes with the messenger, that is permission for him."
"10908","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, haddathana Jarir ibn Hazim he said: I heard al-Hasan narrating from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: A man may utter a word, not thinking it will reach where it reached, by which he plunges into the Fire seventy autumns."
"10909","He said: I recited to Abd al-Rahman: Malik from Sumayy the mawla of Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Salih al-Samman from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While a man was walking on a road, he found a branch of thorns on the road, so he removed it, so Allah Almighty thanked him and forgave him."
"10910","And with the same isnad he said: The martyrs are five: the one who dies of plague, the one who dies of abdominal disease, the drowned, the one crushed under rubble, and the martyr in the path of Allah."
"10911","And with the same isnad he said: If people knew what is for them in the call to prayer and the first row, then found no way except to draw lots for it, they would draw lots; and if they knew what is in going early to prayer, they would race to it; and if they knew what is in al-Atamah and al-Subh, they would come to them even crawling."
"10912","He said: I recited to Abd al-Rahman: Malik from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman from Hafs ibn Asim from Abu Hurayrah or from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between my house and my minbar is a garden from the gardens of Paradise, and my minbar is upon my Hawd."
"10913","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, haddathana Jarir ibn Hazim he said: I heard al-Hasan narrating from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: A man may utter a word, not thinking it will reach where it reached, by which he plunges into the Fire seventy autumns."
"10914","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk, haddathana al-Dahhak ibn Uthman from al-Maqburi from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: The believing servant, as long as he remains in his place of prayer and nothing detains him except waiting for the prayer, the angels are with him, saying: O Allah, have mercy on him, O Allah, forgive him, as long as he does not break his wudu."
"10915","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Isma'il, haddathana al-Dahhak from al-Hakam ibn Mina' from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning going in the path of Allah or an evening going is better than the world and what is in it, or the world and what is upon it."
"10916","Haddathana Umayyah ibn Khalid, haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah, and Abu Umar al-Darir, the meaning being one; he said: Haddathana Hammad from Muhammad ibn Amr from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Lut said, If only I had strength against you or could take refuge in a strong support. He said: He used to take refuge in a strong support, but he meant his clan; Allah Almighty did not send any prophet after him except He sent him among the chiefs of his people. Abu Umar said: Allah Almighty did not send any prophet after him except among the protection of his people."
"10917","Haddathana Umayyah ibn Khalid and Yunus, they said: Haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Yunus said: he raised the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Angel of Death used to come to people openly. He came to Musa and he slapped him and gouged his eye. He came to his Lord Almighty and said: O Lord, Your servant Musa gouged my eye, and were it not for his honor upon You I would have treated him harshly; and Yunus said: I would have caused him hardship. He said to him: Go to My servant and say to him: Let him place his hand on the skin or hide of a bull, and for every hair his hand covers he has a year. He came to him and he said to him: What is after this? He said: Death. He said: Then now. Then he breathed upon him a breath and seized his soul. Yunus said: Allah Almighty restored his eye, and he thereafter used to come to people secretly."
"10918","Haddathana Mu'ammal, haddathana Hammad, haddathana Ammar ibn Abi Ammar he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Angel of Death, peace be upon him, then he mentioned the same account."
"10919","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, akhbarana Ma'mar from al-Zuhri regarding His saying Almighty, Every nation will be called to its record, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi from Abu Hurayrah he said: People said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you suffer harm in seeing the sun with no clouds beneath it? They said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you suffer harm in seeing the moon on the night of full moon with no clouds beneath it? They said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You will see your Lord Almighty on the Day of Resurrection likewise. Allah gathers the people and says: Whoever used to worship something, let him follow it. So whoever used to worship the moon follows the moon, and whoever used to worship the sun follows the sun, and whoever used to worship the false gods follows the false gods, and this Ummah remains with its hypocrites among it. Then Allah Almighty comes to them in other than the form they know and says: I am your Lord. They say: We seek refuge in Allah; this is our place until our Lord Almighty comes to us, and when our Lord comes to us we shall know Him. He said: Then Allah Almighty comes to them in the form they know and says: I am your Lord. They say: You are our Lord, and they follow Him. He said: And a bridge is struck over Hell. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall be the first to cross, and the supplication of the messengers that day is: O Allah, grant safety, grant safety. Upon it are hooks like the thorns of al-Sa'dan. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: They are like the thorns of al-Sa'dan, except none knows the measure of their greatness except Allah Almighty. They snatch people by their deeds; among them is one ruined by his deed, and among them one cut up and then saved, until when Allah Almighty finishes judging between the servants and wills to bring out of the Fire whomever He wills to have mercy on among those who used to testify that there is no god but Allah, He commands the angels to bring them out, and they recognize them by the mark of the traces of prostration, and Allah Almighty forbade the Fire to eat the trace of prostration from the son of Adam. So they bring them out of the Fire burnt up, and water called the water of life is poured upon them, and they sprout as the seed sprouts in the silt of the flood. And a man remains turning his face toward the Fire, saying: O Lord, its wind has poisoned me and its flame has burned me, so turn my face away from the Fire. He keeps supplicating Allah Almighty until He says: Perhaps if I give you that, you will ask Me for other than it. He says: By Your might, I shall not ask You for other than it. So He turns his face away from the Fire. Then after that he says: O Lord, bring me near to the gate of Paradise. He says: Did you not claim you would not ask Me for other than it? Woe to you, O son of Adam, how treacherous you are. He keeps supplicating until He says: Perhaps if I give you that, you will ask Me for other than it. He says: No, by Your might, I shall not ask You for other than it, and he gives Allah Almighty covenants and pledges that he will not ask Him for other than it. So He brings him near to the gate of Paradise. When he draws near to it, Paradise opens before him, and when he sees what is in it of delight and joy, he falls silent as long as Allah wills him to be silent, then he says: O Lord, admit me into Paradise. He says: Did you not claim you would not ask Me for other than it, or He says: Did you not give your covenant and pledges that you would not ask Me for other than it? He says: O Lord, do not make me the most wretched of Your creation. He keeps supplicating Allah Almighty until He laughs. When He laughs at him, He permits him to enter it. When he enters, it is said to him: Wish for such-and-such. So he wishes. Then it is said: Wish for such-and-such. So he wishes, until his wishes are exhausted. Then it is said: This is yours and the like of it with it. Abu Sa'id was sitting with Abu Hurayrah, not altering anything of his speech, until he reached his saying, This is yours and the like of it with it. Abu Sa'id said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This is yours and ten like it with it. Abu Hurayrah said: I memorized, and the like of it with it. Abu Hurayrah said: That man is the last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise."
"10920","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Hisham from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: The right of hospitality is three days; what is received after that is charity."
"10921","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This minbar of mine is upon a rivulet from the rivulets of Paradise, and what is between my chamber and my minbar is a garden from the gardens of Paradise."
"10922","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Zuhayr, haddathana Zayd ibn Aslam from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Allah Almighty said: I am according to My servant's opinion of Me, and I am with him when he remembers Me. Allah is more joyful at the repentance of His servant than one of you who finds his lost animal in the desert. Abu Abd Allah said: I think he said his lost animal. And whoever draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him an arm's length; and whoever draws near to Me an arm's length, I draw near to him a fathom; and when he comes to Me walking, I come to him hastening."
"10923","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Malik from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'mar from Abu al-Hubab from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty says on the Day of Resurrection: Where are those who loved one another for My glory? Today I shade them in My shade, a day when there is no shade except My shade."
"10924","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah from Thabit from Abu Rafi' from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two eyes commit zina, the two hands commit zina, the two feet commit zina, and the private part confirms that or denies it."
"10925","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah from Ali ibn Zayd from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar he said: Abu Hurayrah said: I never witnessed any spoils with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except he allotted to me, except Khaybar, for it was for the people of al-Hudaybiyah exclusively; Abu Hurayrah and Abu Musa came between al-Hudaybiyah and Khaybar."
"10926","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah from Ali ibn Zayd from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adam's height was sixty cubits in seven cubits width."
"10927","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Sa'id and Abd al-Wahhab from Sa'id from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Children of Israel used to bathe naked, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had modesty and shyness in him, so he used to cover himself when he bathed, so they criticized him and disparaged him. He said: While the Prophet of Allah was bathing one day when he placed his clothes on a rock, the rock ran off, so the Prophet of Allah followed it striking with the stick: My garment, O stone; my garment, O stone, until it ended with him at an assembly of the Children of Israel and stopped among them. So the Prophet of Allah took his clothes, and they looked at the best of people in creation and the most just in form, so the assembly said: May Allah fight the slanderers of the Children of Israel. That was his exoneration with which Allah exonerated him."
"10928","Haddathana Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik al-Tayalisi, haddathana Abu Awanah from Abd al-Malik from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Hurayrah he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best prayer after the obligatory is the night prayer, and the best fasting after Ramadan is the month of Allah which you call al-Muharram."
"10929","Haddathana Uthman ibn Umar, haddathana Yunus, haddathana Ibn Shihab from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah he said: Two women from Hudhayl fought, and one of them threw a stone at the other and killed her and what was in her womb. They disputed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged that the blood-money of her fetus is a ghurrah, a slave or a slave-girl, and judged the blood-money of the woman upon her killer. Hamal ibn Nabighah al-Hudhali said: How should I pay for one who neither drank nor ate nor spoke nor cried out? The like of that is wasted. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is only from the brothers of the soothsayers, because of his rhymed speech which he rhymed."
"10930","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Salih, haddathana Ibn Shihab from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abd Allah ibn Hudhafah to circulate in Mina: Do not fast these days, for they are days of eating and drinking and remembrance of Allah Almighty."
"10931","Haddathana Abu Ahmad, haddathana Jabir ibn al-Hurr al-Nakha'i from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis from Kumayl ibn Ziyad from Abu Hurayrah he said: I went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a garden, and he said: O Abu Hurayrah, the majority are ruined except one who says thus and thus, and few are they. I walked with him, then he said: Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise? There is no power nor strength except in Allah. He said: Then he said: O Abu Hurayrah, do you know what is Allah's right upon the servants? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: His right is that they worship Him, not associating anything with Him. Then he said: Do you know what is the servants' right upon Allah? Their right upon Allah, when they do that, is that He not punish them. I said: Shall I not inform them? He said: Leave them, let them work."
"10932","Haddathana Uthman ibn Umar, akhbarana Malik from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman that Ibn Hunayn informed him from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man reciting Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad until he finished it, so he said: It has become due. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what has become due? He said: Paradise. Abu Hurayrah said: I wanted to come to him and congratulate him, but I preferred lunch with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I feared lunch with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would escape me. Then I returned to the man and found him gone."
"10933","Haddathana Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith, haddathana Hammad from Suhayl from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every son of Adam has his share of zina: the zina of the two eyes is looking, the zina of the two hands is seizing, the zina of the two feet is walking, the zina of the mouth is kissing, the heart inclines and wishes, and the private part confirms that or denies it. And he formed a circle and then inserted his forefinger into it; Abu Hurayrah testifies to that by his flesh and blood."
"10934","Haddathana Zayd ibn al-Hubab, haddathani Musa ibn Ali he said: I heard my father say: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best women who rode camels are the women of Quraysh, most affectionate to a child in his smallness and most kind to a husband despite little means. Then Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew that the daughter of Imran did not ride a camel."
"10935","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, haddathana Yahya, meaning Ibn Ayyub, from the offspring of Jarir; he said: I heard Abu Zur'ah mentioned from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two parties to a sale do not part from a sale except by mutual consent."
"10936","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, haddathana Yahya ibn Ayyub from the offspring of Jarir; he said: I heard Abu Zur'ah mentioned from Abu Hurayrah he said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a sick child of hers, asking him to supplicate for healing and well-being, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, three have died for me. He said: In Islam? She said: In Islam; they did not reach puberty. He counts them as reward except he is fortified with a fortification from the Fire."
"10937","Haddathana Hasan ibn Musa, haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went to his bed, said: O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the earths, our Lord and Lord of everything, Splitter of the grain and the seed, Revealer of the Torah, the Gospel and the Qur'an, I seek refuge in You from the evil of every possessor of evil whose forelock You hold. You are the First, there is nothing before You; You are the Last, there is nothing after You; You are the Manifest, there is nothing above You; You are the Hidden, there is nothing beneath You. Settle my debt for me and enrich me from poverty."
"10938","Haddathana Hasan, haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah from Dawud ibn Abi Hind from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah from Habib ibn al-Shahid from al-Hasan, authentic from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: Three, whoever has them in him is a hypocrite even if he fasts and prays and claims he is a Muslim: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks, and when he is entrusted he betrays."
"10939","Haddathana Hasan and Hashim, they said: Haddathana Shayban from Asim from Yazid ibn Qays from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near: knowledge decreases and harj increases. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is harj? He said: Killing."
"10940","Haddathana Hasan and Hashim, they said: Haddathana Shayban from Asim from Yazid ibn Sharik al-Amiri he said: I heard Marwan saying to Abu Hurayrah: Narrate to me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man will soon wish he had fallen from al-Thurayya and that he had attained nothing of people's affairs. He said: And I heard him say: The destruction of the Arabs is at the hands of youths from Quraysh. Marwan said: What evil youths are those."
"10941","Haddathana Hasan, haddathana Shayban from Yahya he said: And akhbarani Abu Salamah that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty is jealous, and the believer is jealous, and Allah's jealousy is that the believer does what He forbade him."
"10942","Haddathana Affan from Aban, haddathana Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, haddathana Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is jealous, then he mentioned the like."
"10943","Haddathana Hasan, haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They lead you in prayer; if they are right, it is for you and them, and if they err, it is for you and against them."
"10944","Haddathana Hasan, haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: The molar tooth of the disbeliever is like Uhud, his thigh is like al-Bayda', his seat in the Fire is like between Qudayd to Makkah, and the thickness of his skin is forty-two cubits by the cubit of al-Jabbar."
"10945","Haddathana Hasan, haddathana Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz, haddathana al-Ash'ath al-Darir from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lowest of the people of Paradise in station has seven degrees, and he is upon the sixth, with the seventh above him; he has three hundred servants, and morning and evening brought to him every day three hundred dishes, of gold as I recall he said, in every dish a color not in the other; he enjoys its first as he enjoys its last; he says: O Lord, if You permitted me, I would feed the people of Paradise and give them drink, and nothing of what is with me would decrease; and he has of the houris seventy-two wives besides his wives from the world; the sitting place of one of them takes a mile of earth."
"10946","Haddathana Hashim, haddathana al-Mas'udi and Sharik from Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha' from his father from Abu Hurayrah he said: A man went out of the mosque after the mu'adhdhin called, so he said: As for this, he has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And in Sharik's hadith, then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us: When you are in the mosque and the call to prayer is made, let none of you go out until he prays. Haddathana Hashim, haddathana Sharik from al-Mas'udi he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us: When you are in the mosque and the call to prayer is made, let none of you go out until he prays."
"10947","Haddathana: source text truncated in the index; only this word is present."
"10948","Haddathana Hashim, haddathana Shayban from Asim from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the Isha prayer until the night deepened and a third of it or near it passed, then he went out to the mosque, and the people were in scattered small groups and few. He said: He became angry with an anger I do not know I ever saw him angry with anger more severe than it, then he said: If a man invited people to a bone with meat or two good hoof-pieces, they would come for that and not stay behind, yet they stay behind from this prayer. I have intended to command a man to lead the people in prayer and follow these houses whose people stayed behind from it and burn them over them with fire."
"10949","Haddathana Hashim, haddathana Sharik from al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Whoever is wounded in the path of Allah, and Allah knows who is wounded in His path, will come on the Day of Resurrection with the color of his wound the color of blood and its scent the scent of musk."
"10950","Haddathana Hashim, haddathana Sharik from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Ziyad al-Harithi he said: I heard a man asking Abu Hurayrah: Are you the one who forbids people to pray in their sandals? He said: Yes, by the Lord of this Sanctuary, yes, by the Lord of this Sanctuary, I saw Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying toward this Maqam in his sandals, then he left with them on him."
"10951","Haddathana Hashim from Ibn Abi Dhi'b from Abu al-Walid from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you lead people, lighten, for among them are the old, the weak, and the young."
"10952","Haddathana Hashim from Ibn Abi Dhi'b from al-Maqburi from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: None of you will be saved by his deed. They said: Nor you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Nor I, unless Allah covers me with mercy from Him. So be upright, draw near, go early and go late, and something of the night journey; and moderation, moderation, you will reach."
"10953","Haddathana Abu Kamil and Hashim, they said: Haddathana Zuhayr, haddathana Suhayl from his father from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sleeps with grease on his hand without washing it, and something befalls him, let him blame none but himself."
"10954","Haddathana Hashim and Abu Kamil, they said: Haddathana Zuhayr, haddathana Suhayl from his father from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a dog or a bell."
"10955","Haddathana Hashim and Abu Kamil, they said: Haddathana Zuhayr, haddathana Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man stands from his seat then returns to it, he has more right to it."
"10956","Haddathana Hashim, haddathana Zuhayr, haddathana Suhayl from his father from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until time draws near: the year becomes like the month, the month like the Friday, the Friday like the day, the day like the hour, and the hour like the burning of the palm frond; Suhayl claimed the dry frond."
"10957","Haddathana Hashim, haddathana Layth, haddathana Ibn Shihab from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the son of Maryam will soon descend among you as a just judge; he will break the cross, kill the pig, abolish the jizyah, and wealth will overflow until no one accepts it."
"10958","Haddathana Hashim, haddathana Layth, haddathani Sa'id al-Maqburi from Sa'id ibn Yasar the brother of Abu Marthad that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one gives charity from good, and Allah accepts only the good, except the Most Merciful Almighty takes it with His right hand, even if it is a date, and it grows for him in the palm of the Most Merciful until it becomes greater than the mountain, as one of you raises his foal or his weaned camel."
"10959","Haddathana Hashim, haddathana Shu'bah, haddathana Qatadah from Zurarah ibn Awfa al-Amiri from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: When a woman spends the night abandoning her husband's bed, the angels curse her until she returns."
"10960","Haddathana Hashim, haddathana Shu'bah he said: Qatadah informed me, he said: I heard Hilal ibn Zayd, a man from Banu Mazin ibn Shayban, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This black seed, meaning al-shuniz, is a healing from everything except al-sam. Qatadah said: Al-sam is death."
"10961","Haddathana Bahz and Hashim, they said: Haddathana Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah from Thabit; Hashim said: Haddathani Thabit al-Bunani, haddathana Abd Allah ibn Rabah he said: Delegations came to Mu'awiyah, I among them, and Abu Hurayrah, in Ramadan, and some of us used to make food for others. He said: Abu Hurayrah often invited us; Hashim said: he often invited us to his lodging. He said: I said: Shall I not make food and invite them to my lodging? He said: I ordered food to be made, and I met Abu Hurayrah in the evening. He said: I said: O Abu Hurayrah, the invitation is with me tonight. He said: Did you precede me? Hashim said: I said: Yes. He said: So I invited them, and they were with me. Abu Hurayrah said: Shall I not inform you of a hadith from your hadith, O company of Ansar? He said: Then he mentioned the conquest of Makkah. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and entered Makkah. He said: He sent al-Zubayr upon one flank and Khalid upon the other flank, and sent Abu Ubaydah upon the unarmed foot, and they took the belly of the valley, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his battalion. He said: Quraysh had gathered its rabble. He said: They said: We put these forward; if they have anything, we are with them, and if they are struck, we give what is asked of us. Abu Hurayrah said: He looked and saw me and said: O Abu Hurayrah. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Call the Ansar for me, and let none come to me except an Ansari. So I called them, and they came and surrounded the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Do you see the rabble of Quraysh and their followers? Then he said with his hands, one upon the other: Mow them down until you meet me at al-Safa. Abu Hurayrah said: We set out, and none of us wished to kill any of them he wished except he did, with none of them directing anything at us. He said: Abu Sufyan said: O Messenger of Allah, the green multitude of Quraysh is laid bare; there is no Quraysh after today. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever closes his door is safe, and whoever enters the house of Abu Sufyan is safe. He said: People closed their doors. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the Stone and touched it, then circumambulated the House. He said: In his hand was a bow, holding it by the curved end. He said: In his circumambulation he came upon an idol beside which they worshipped. He said: He began to stab it in its eye and say: Truth has come and falsehood has vanished. He said: Then he came to al-Safa and climbed it where the House is seen, raised his hands, and began to remember Allah with what He willed him to remember and supplicate Him. He said: The Ansar were beneath him. He said: Some of them said to others: As for the man, desire for his town and compassion for his kin have overtaken him. Abu Hurayrah said: Revelation came, and when it came it was not hidden from us; none of the people raises his glance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until it is completed. Hashim said: When the revelation was completed, he raised his head, then he said: O company of Ansar, did you say: As for the man, desire for his town and compassion for his kin have overtaken him? They said: We said that, O Messenger of Allah. He said: What would my name be then? Nay, I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger; I emigrated to Allah and to you; life is your life and death is your death. They came to him weeping and saying: By Allah, we said what we said only out of protectiveness for Allah and His Messenger. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah and His Messenger believe you and excuse you."
"10962","Haddathana Hashim, haddathana Abu Mu'awiyah, meaning Shayban, from Layth from Tawus from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of suspicion, for it is the most lying speech; do not eavesdrop, do not spy, do not envy, do not hate, do not compete, do not turn away from one another, and be servants of Allah, brothers, as Allah commanded you."
"10963","Haddathana Hashim, haddathana Abu Mu'awiyah, and he is Shayban, from Yahya from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is jealous, and the believer is jealous, and Allah's jealousy is that the believer does what He forbade him."
"10964","Haddathana Hashim, haddathana Abu Mu'awiyah from Mansur from Abu Uthman the mawla of the family of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah from Abu Hurayrah he said: I heard him say: Muhammad the Messenger of Allah, Abu al-Qasim, master of this chamber (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: Mercy is not stripped except from a wretched one."
"10965","Haddathana Hashim, haddathana Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, haddathani my father from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not fitting for a servant to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta."
"10966","Haddathana Hashim, haddathana Layth, haddathani Ibn Shihab from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged regarding the fetus of a woman from Banu Lihyan of Hudhayl, which fell dead, a ghurrah, a slave or a slave-girl. Then the woman against whom judgment of ghurrah was made died, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged that her inheritance is for her sons and her husband and that the blood-money is upon her clan."
"10967","Haddathana Ishaq ibn Isa, haddathana Layth, haddathani Ibn Shihab, and he mentioned the like, except he said: Then the woman against whom judgment of ghurrah was made died."
"10968","Haddathana Kathir ibn Hisham, haddathana Ja'far, haddathana Yazid ibn al-Asamm he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tribulations appear, harj increases. We said: What is harj? He said: Killing. And he said: Knowledge is taken away."
"10969","Haddathana Kathir, haddathana Ja'far, haddathana Yazid ibn al-Asamm from Abu Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Kathir once said: a hadith he raised it; he said: People are mines like the mines of silver and gold; the best of them in Jahiliyyah are the best in Islam when they understand; and souls are marshaled troops: those that recognize one another unite, and those that dislike one another differ."
"10970","Haddathana Kathir, haddathana Ja'far, haddathana Yazid ibn al-Asamm from Abu Hurayrah he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: People will ask you about everything until they say: Allah created everything, so who created Him? Yazid said: Najabah ibn Sabigh al-Sulami informed me that he saw riders come to Abu Hurayrah and ask him about that, and he said: Allah is Greater; my close friend did not narrate to me anything except I have seen it and I am awaiting it. Ja'far said: It reached me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When people ask you about this, say: Allah was before everything, Allah created everything, and Allah remains after everything."
"10971","Haddathana Kathir, haddathana Ja'far he said: I heard Yazid ibn al-Asamm say: Abu Hurayrah said: a hadith I deem he raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: Richness is not from abundance of goods, but richness is richness of soul. By Allah, I do not fear poverty for you, but I fear for you rivalry in increase, and I fear for you willful persistence."
"10972","Haddathana Ali ibn Thabit, haddathani Ja'far from Yazid ibn al-Asamm he said: It was said to Abu Hurayrah: You narrated much, much. He said: If I narrated to you all I heard from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), you would throw lumps at me and would not debate with me."
"10973","Haddathana Kathir, haddathana Ja'far, haddathana Yazid ibn al-Asamm from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty does not look at your forms and your wealth, but He looks at your hearts and your deeds."
"10974","Haddathana Kathir ibn Hisham, haddathana Ja'far ibn Burqan, haddathana Yazid ibn al-Asamm from Abu Hurayrah, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: Allah Almighty says: My servant is according to his opinion of Me, and I am with him when he supplicates Me."
"10975","Haddathana Kathir, haddathana Ja'far, haddathana Yazid ibn al-Asamm from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have intended to command prayer to be established, then go out with my youths with bundles of firewood and burn upon people in their houses who hear the call then do not come to prayer. Yazid asked: Is this about Friday or other than it? He said: I did not hear Abu Hurayrah mention Friday nor other than it, except thus."
"10976","Haddathana Kathir, haddathana Ja'far, haddathana Yazid ibn al-Asamm from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: My likeness and yours, O Ummah, is like a man who kindled a fire at night, so these moths and creatures that hover over the fire came to it; he kept driving them away but they overcome him, plunging into the fire; and I hold your waist-wrappers, calling you to Paradise, but you overcome me, plunging into the Fire."
"10977","Haddathana Ali ibn Thabit, haddathana Ja'far from Yazid ibn al-Asamm he said: Abu Hurayrah said: They say: You narrated much; if I narrated to you all I heard from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), you would throw lumps at me and would not debate with me."
"10978","Haddathana Umar ibn Ayyub al-Mawsili from Ja'far from Yazid from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Richness is not from abundance of goods, but richness is richness of soul."
"10979","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Mus'ab, haddathana al-Awza'i from al-Zuhri from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The right of the Muslim upon the Muslim is five: he greets him when he meets him, says Yarhamuk Allah to him when he sneezes, visits him when he is ill, attends his funeral when he dies, and answers him when he invites him. My father said: Strange, meaning this hadith."
"10980","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Mus'ab, haddathana al-Awza'i from al-Zuhri from Sa'id from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque while the Abyssinians were playing, so Umar rebuked them, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave them, O Umar, for they are the sons of Arfidah."
"10981","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Mus'ab and Abu al-Mughirah, they said: Haddathana al-Awza'i from Isma'il ibn Ubayd Allah from Umm al-Darda' from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Allah Almighty says: I am with My servant when he remembers Me and his lips move."
"10982","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Mus'ab, haddathana al-Awza'i from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wanted to depart from Mina, said: Tomorrow, Allah willing, we camp at al-Muhassab, at Khayf of Banu Kinanah, where they divided upon disbelief; that Quraysh divided against Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib that they would not intermarry with them nor mix with them until they hand over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to them."
"10983","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Mus'ab, haddathana al-Awza'i from Abu Ammar from Abd Allah ibn Farrukh from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: The best day on which the sun rose is Friday: in it Adam was created, in it he was admitted to Paradise, in it he was taken out of it, and in it the Hour comes."
"10984","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Mus'ab, haddathana al-Awza'i from Yahya from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh of the jar, the gourd, the varnished vessel, and all vessels."
"10985","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Mus'ab, haddathana al-Awza'i from Yahya from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: I am the master of the children of Adam, the first for whom the earth splits, the first intercessor and the first whose intercession is accepted."
"10986","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Mus'ab, haddathana al-Awza'i from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah, meaning Ibn Abi Talhah, from Ja'far ibn Iyad from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek refuge in Allah from poverty, scarcity, humiliation, and that you wrong or be wronged."
"10987","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Mus'ab, haddathana al-Awza'i from al-Zuhri from Hanzalah ibn Ali from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the son of Maryam will surely raise his voice with talbiyah at Fajj al-Rawha' as a pilgrim or an umrah performer."
"10988","Haddathana Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi, haddathana al-Walid ibn Muslim from Ibn Jabir, haddathani Isma'il ibn Abd Allah from Karimah the daughter of al-Hashas al-Muzaniyyah she said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say in the house of Umm al-Darda': The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty said: I am with My servant when he remembers Me and his lips move with Me."
"10989","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq, akhbarana Abd Allah, akhbarana Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, haddathana Isma'il ibn Ubayd Allah from Karimah the daughter of al-Hashas al-Muzaniyyah that she narrated to him, she said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to us, while we were in the house of this one, meaning Umm al-Darda', that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) transmitting from his Lord Almighty that He said: I am with My servant as long as he remembers Me and his lips move with Me."
"10990","Haddathana Isma'il ibn Ibrahim from Sa'id al-Jurayri from Abu Nadrah from a man of al-Tufawah he said: I stayed with Abu Hurayrah. He said: I never met among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a man more diligent nor more caring for a guest than him. While I was with him, he upon a bed of his, beneath him a black slave girl of his, with him a bag containing pebbles and date-stones, saying: Subhan Allah, Subhan Allah, until when what was in the bag was exhausted, he threw it to her, so she gathered it and put it in the bag, then handed it to him. He said to me: Shall I not narrate to you about me and about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: Yes. He said: While I was suffering fever in the mosque of Madinah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and said: Who feels the Daws youth? Who feels the Daws youth? A speaker said to him: He is there suffering fever in the side of the mosque where you see, O Messenger of Allah. He came and placed his hand upon me and spoke kindly to me, so I stood. He went until he stood in his station in which he prays, with him that day two rows of men and a row of women, or two rows of women and a row of men. He turned to them and said: If Satan makes me forget something of my prayer, let the men say Subhan Allah and the women clap. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed and did not forget anything of his prayer. When he gave salam, he turned to them with his face and said: Stay in your seats. Is there among you, when he comes to his wife, one who closes his door and lowers his curtain, then goes out and speaks, saying: I did with my wife such-and-such, and I did with my wife such-and-such? They were silent. He turned to the women and said: Is there among you one who speaks? A young buxom girl knelt upon one of her knees and stretched to be seen by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and to hear his speech, and said: Yes, by Allah, they speak and they speak. He said: Do you know the likeness of one who does that? The likeness of one who does that is a male devil and a female devil meeting in the road, fulfilling his need from her while people look on. Then he said: No man should lie intimately with a man, nor a woman with a woman, except to a child or a parent. He said: And he mentioned a third and I forgot it. The perfume of men is what its scent is found and its color not seen; the perfume of women is what its color appears and its scent not found."
"10991","Haddathana Isam ibn Khalid, haddathana Hariz from Shabib Abu Rawh that a Bedouin came to Abu Hurayrah and said: O Abu Hurayrah, narrate to us from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He mentioned the hadith and said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith is Yemeni, wisdom is Yemeni, and I find the breath of your Lord from the direction of Yemen. Abu al-Mughirah said: From the direction of the west. Disbelief, immorality and hardness of heart are among the loud-voiced owners of hair and wool, over whose camel rumps the devils whisper."
"10992","Haddathana Ahmad Abu Salih, haddathana Muhammad ibn Muslim, meaning Ibn Abi al-Waddah, Abu Sa'id al-Mu'addib, in Dhu al-Qa'dah in the year seventy, and he mentioned a hadith and mentioned this from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man gives a date in charity from the good, and Allah accepts only the good, it falls in the Hand of Allah, and He raises it for him as one of you raises his foal or his weaned camel until it returns in his hand like the mountain."
"10993","Haddathana Husayn ibn Muhammad, haddathana Ibn Abi al-Zinad from his father from al-A'raj from Abu Hurayrah he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No one enters the Fire except he is shown his seat in Paradise, had he done good, to be regret upon him; and no one enters Paradise except he is shown his seat in the Fire, had he done evil, to increase in gratitude."
"10994","Haddathana Husayn ibn Muhammad, haddathana Ibn Abi al-Zinad from his father from al-A'raj from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the most entitled of people to Isa son of Maryam in this world and the Hereafter; the prophets are brothers, sons of different mothers, their mothers different, and there is no prophet between us."
"10995","Haddathana Husayn, haddathana Ibn Abi al-Zinad from his father from al-A'raj from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Yemen have come to you; they are weakest in hearts and softest in minds; understanding is Yemeni and wisdom is Yemeni."
"10996","Haddathana Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il, haddathana Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, haddathana Hisham and Habib ibn al-Shahid from Ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith is Yemeni, understanding is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni."
"10997","Haddathana Hasan and Hashim, they said: Haddathana Shayban from Asim from Ziyad ibn Qays from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near: knowledge decreases and harj increases. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is harj? He said: Killing, killing. This is the end of the Musnad of Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him."
